('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:19:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','he','הָרַחֲמָן הַנִּקְדָּשׁ יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִתְעַלֶּה','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:19:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','en','The Merciful One, the Sanctified One, blessed and exalted,','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','transliteration','Harachaman hanikdash yitbarach ve yitaleh','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:20:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','he','עַל כּוֹס יַֽיִן מָלֵא כְּבִרְכַּת יְהֹוָה׃','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:20:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','en','over a full cup of wine, the bounty of Adonoy.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','transliteration','Al kos yayin maleh k''virkat Adonai','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:21:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','he','צוּר מִשֶּׁלּוֹ אָכַֽלְנוּ בָּרְכוּ אֱמוּנַי שָׂבַֽעְנוּ וְהוֹתַֽרְנוּ כִּדְבַר יְהֹוָה׃','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:21:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','en','The Rock—from His [store] we have eaten—Bless [Him] my faithful ones. We have satisfied ourselves and we have left over [some food] according to the word of Adonoy.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shabbat-evening-zemirot-for-shabbat-evening-tzur-mishelo','transliteration','Tzur mishelo achalenu barechu emunai savaenu ve hotarenu kidvar Adonai','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shabbat Evening, Zemirot for Shabbat Evening, Tzur Mishelo'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach','he','יִשְׁתַּבַּח שִׁמְךָ לָעַד מַלְכֵּנוּ. הָאֵל הַמֶּלֶךְ הַגָּדול וְהַקָּדושׁ בַּשָּׁמַיִם וּבָאָרֶץ. כִּי לְךָ נָאֶה ה'' אֱלהֵינוּ וֵאלהֵי אֲבותֵינוּ שִׁיר וּשְׁבָחָה. הַלֵּל וְזִמְרָה. עוז וּמֶמְשָׁלָה. נֶצַח גְּדֻלָּה וּגְבוּרָה. תְּהִלָּה וְתִפְאֶרֶת. קְדֻשָּׁה וּמַלְכוּת: בְּרָכות וְהודָאות מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עולָם: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה ה''. אֵל מֶלֶךְ גָּדול בַּתִּשְׁבָּחות אֵל הַהודָאות. אֲדון הַנִּפְלָאות. הַבּוחֵר בְּשִׁירֵי זִמְרָה. מֶלֶךְ אֵל חֵי הָעולָמִים:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Pesukei Dezimra, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach','en','May your name be praised forever, O our king. Great and holy god-emperor over the heavens and the earth! For songs of praise are pleasant to you, O LORD our god and god of our forefathers, and hymns of exaltation, and power and sovereignty, great and powerful victory, awesome wonder, and holy kingship, and blessings and thanks, from now until forever. Blessed are you O LORD, great god-emperor of praises, god of thanks, master of wonders, who chose hymnal songs, king and living god of all the world.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Pesukei Dezimra, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-pesukei-dezimra-yishtabach','transliteration','Yishtabach shimcha la''ad malkenu.
Hael hamelech hagadvl ve hakadvsh bashamayim uva''aretz.
Ki lecha naeh h'' elheinu velhei avvteinu shir ushevacha.
Halel ve zimra.
Vz umemshala.
Netzach gedula ugevura.
Tehila ve tiferet.
K''dusha umalchut.
B''rachvt ve hvdavt meatah ve ad -vlam.
Baruch atah h''.
El melech gadvl batishbachvt el hahvdavt.
Advn haniflavt.
Habvcher b''shirei zimra.
Melech el chei ha--vlamim.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Pesukei Dezimra, Yishtabach'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema','he','אַהֲבָה רַבָּה אֲהַבְתָּנוּ ה'' אֱלהֵינוּ. חֶמְלָה גְּדולָה וִיתֵרָה חָמַלְתָּ עָלֵינוּ: אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ. בַּעֲבוּר אֲבותֵינוּ שֶׁבָּטְחוּ בְךָ. וַתְּלַמְּדֵם חֻקֵּי חַיִּים כֵּן תְּחָנֵּנוּ וּתְלַמְּדֵנוּ: אָבִינוּ הָאָב הָרַחֲמָן. הַמְרַחֵם. רַחֵם עָלֵינוּ. וְתֵן בְּלִבֵּנוּ לְהָבִין וּלְהַשכִּיל. לִשְׁמעַ. לִלְמד וּלְלַמֵּד. לִשְׁמר וְלַעֲשות וּלְקַיֵּם אֶת כָּל דִּבְרֵי תַלְמוּד תּורָתֶךָ בְּאַהֲבָה: וְהָאֵר עֵינֵינוּ בְּתורָתֶךָ. וְדַבֵּק לִבֵּנוּ בְּמִצְותֶיךָ. וְיַחֵד לְבָבֵנוּ לְאַהֲבָה וּלְיִרְאָה אֶת שְׁמֶךָ. וְלא נֵבושׁ לְעולָם וָעֶד: כִּי בְשֵׁם קָדְשְׁךָ הַגָּדול וְהַנּורָא בָּטָחְנוּ. נָגִילָה וְנִשמְחָה בִּישׁוּעָתֶךָ: וַהֲבִיאֵנוּ לְשָׁלום מֵאַרְבַּע כַּנְפות הָאָרֶץ. וְתולִיכֵנוּ קומְמִיּוּת לְאַרְצֵנוּ: כִּי אֵל פּועֵל יְשׁוּעות אָתָּה. וּבָנוּ בָחַרְתָּ מִכָּל עַם וְלָשׁון.וְקֵרַבְתָּנוּ לְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדול סֶלָה בֶּאֱמֶת: לְהודות לְךָ וּלְיַחֶדְךָ בְּאַהֲבָה: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה ה''. הַבּוחֵר בְּעַמּו יִשרָאֵל בְּאַהֲבָה:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Blessings of the Shema, Second Blessing before Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema','en','(1) [With] great love You have loved us, Lord, our God; [with] great and abundant compassion have You had compassion upon us. Our Parent, our Sovereign — for the sake of our ancestors who trusted in You, and whom You taught laws of life, so [too] be gracious to us and teach us. Our Parent, merciful Parent, Who acts with compassion, have compassion on us and put into our hearts [comprehension] to understand and to discern, to listen, to learn and to teach, to keep, to practice, and to fulfill all the words of the teachings in Your Torah with love. And enlighten our eyes with Your Torah, and attach our hearts to Your mitzvot, and unify our hearts to love and revere Your Name; and may we never be embarrassed, for in Your holy Name— [which is] great and awe-inspiring— have we trusted; may we delight and rejoice in Your deliverance. Bring us in peace [wholeness] from the four corners of the earth; and lead us upright to our land. Because, You are the Almighty, Who performs acts of deliverance, and You have chosen us from among all peoples and languages, and You have brought us close to Your great Name in truth; to thank You and unify You with love. Blessed are You, Lord, Who chooses the people Israel with love.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Blessings of the Shema, Second Blessing before Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-blessings-of-the-shema-second-blessing-before-shema','transliteration','Ahava rabah ahavtanu h'' elheinu.
Chemla gedvla vitera chamalta aleinu.
Avinu malkenu.
Ba''avur avvteinu shebatechu ve cha.
Vatelamedem chukei chayim ken techanenu utelamedenu.
Avinu ha''av harachaman.
Hamerachem.
Rachem aleinu.
Ve ten b''libenu lehavin ulehashkil.
Lishma.
Lilmd ulelamed.
Lishmr ve la''ashvt ulekayem et kol divrei talmud tvratecha b''ahava.
Ve haer eineinu b''tvratecha.
Ve dabek libenu b''mitzvteicha.
Ve yached levavenu leahava uleyira et shemecha.
Vel nevvsh leh--vlam vaed.
Ki ve shem kodshecha hagadvl ve hanvra batachenu.
Nagila ve nishmcha bishuatecha.
Vahavienu leshalvm mearba kanfvt ha''aretz.
Ve tvlichenu kvmemiyut leartzenu.
Ki el pvel yeshuvt atah.
Uvanu vacharta mikol am ve lashvnvekeravtanu.
Leshimcha hagadvl sela be''emet.
Lhvdvt lecha uleyachedcha b''ahava.
Baruch atah h''.
Habvcher b''amv yishrael b''ahava.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Blessings of the Shema, Second Blessing before Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','מִי שֶׁבֵּרַךְ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','May He who blessed our fathers, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Mi sheberach avoteinu Avraham Yitzchak ve Yaakov','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:1:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','הוּא יְבָרֵךְ אֶת חַיָּלֵי צְבָא הֲגַנָּה לְיִשְׂרָאֵל','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:1:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','bless the soldiers of the Israel Defense Forces,','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Hu yevarech et chayalei tzeva hagana leYisrael','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:2:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','הָעוֹמְדִים עַל מִשְׁמַר אַרְצֵנוּ וְעָרֵי אֱלֹהֵינוּ','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:2:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','who are standing guard over our land and over the cities of our God,','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Haomedim al mishmar artzenu ve arei Eloheinu','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:3:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','מִגְּבוּל הַלְּבָנוֹן וְעַד מִדְבַּר מִצְרַיִם','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:3:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','from the border of Lebanon to the Wilderness of Egypt,','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Migevul halevanon ve ad midbar mitzrayim','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:4:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','וּמִן הַיָּם הַגָּדוֹל עַד לְבוֹא הָעֲרָבָה בַּיַּבָּשָׁה בָּאֲוִיר וּבַיָּם','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:4:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','and from the Great Sea to the Approach of the Aravah — on land, in the air, and in the sea.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Umin hayam hagadol ad levo ha''arava bayabasha ba''avir uvayam','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:5:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','יִתֵּן ה'' אֶת אוֹיְבֵינוּ הַקָּמִים עָלֵינוּ נִגָּפִים לִפְנֵיהֶם','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:5:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','May the Lord give plagues before our enemies who arise against us.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Yiten h'' et oyeveinu hakamim aleinu nigafim lifneihem','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:6:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא יִשְׁמֹר וְיַצִּיל אֶת חַיָלֵינוּ מִכָּל צָרָה וְצוּקָה וּמִכָּל נֶגַע וּמַחֲלָה','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:6:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','May the Holy One, blessed be He, guard and rescue our soldiers from all trouble and distress, and from all affliction and illness;','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Hakadosh baruch hu yishmor ve yatzil et chayaleinu mikol tzara ve tzuka umikal nega umachala','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:7:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','וְיִשְׁלַח בְּרָכָה וְהַצְלָחָה בְּכָל מַעֲשֵׂה יְדֵיהֶם','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:7:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','and may He grant blessing and success to all the acts of their hands.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Ve yishlach b''racha ve hatzlacha b''chol ma''aseh yedeihem','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:8:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','יַדְבֵּר שׂוֹנְאֵינוּ תַּחְתֵּיהֶם וִיעַטְרֵם בְּכֶתֶר יְשׁוּעָה וּבְעֲטֶרֶת נִצָּחוֹן','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:8:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','May He crush beneath them those who hate us and crown our soldiers with the crown of salvation and with the crown of victory.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Yadber sone''einu tachteihem viatrem b''cheter yeshua uveateret nitzachon','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:9:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','וִיקֻיַּם בָּהֶם הַכָּתוּב:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:9:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','And may the verse be fulfilled through them:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Vikuyam bahem hakatuv.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:10:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','כִּי ה'' אֱלֹהֵיכֶם הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּכֶם לְהִלָּחֵם לָכֶם עִם אֹיְבֵיכֶם לְהוֹשִׁיעַ אֶתְכֶם','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:10:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','For it is the Lord, your God, who walks with you to fight for you against your enemies to save you (Deuteronomy 20:4).','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Ki h'' Elohechem haholech imachem lehilachem lachem im oyeveichem lehoshia etchem','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:11:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','he','וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:11:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','en','And let us say, Amen.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-israeli-soldiers','transliteration','Ve nomar amen','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Israeli Soldiers'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity','he','מִי שֶׁבֵּרַךְ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב יוֹסֵף מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן דָּוִד וּשְׁלֹמֹה, הוּא יְבָרֵךְ וְיִשְׁמֹר וְיִנְצֹר אֶת כָּל הַחֲטוּפִים, הַשְּׁבוּיִים וְהַנֶּעֱדָרִים בְּתוֹךְ שְׁאָר אֲחֵינוּ בֵּית יִשְֹרָאֵל הַנְּתוּנִים בְּצָרָה וּבְשִׁבְיָה. בַּעֲבוּר שֶׁהַקָּהָל מִתְפַּלֵּל בַּעֲבוּרָם, הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא יִמָּלֵא רַחֲמִים עֲלֵיהֶם, וְיוֹצִיאֵם מֵחֹשֶׁךְ וְצַלְמָוֶת, וּמוֹסְרוֹתֵיהֶם יְנַתֵּק, וּמִמְּצוּקוֹתֵיהֶם יוֹשִׁיעֵם, וִישִׁיבֵם מְהֵרָה לְחֵיק מִשְׁפְּחוֹתֵיהֶם. יוֹדוּ לַה'' חַסְדּוֹ וְנִפְלְאוֹתָיו לִבְנֵי אָדָם. וִיקֻיַּם בָּהֶם מִקְרָא שֶׁכָּתוּב: וּפְדוּיֵי ה'' יְשׁוּבוּן וּבָאוּ צִיּוֹן בְּרִנָּה וְשִׂמְחַת עוֹלָם עַל רֹאשָׁם. שָׂשׂוֹן וְשִׂמְחָה יַשִּׂיגוּ וְנָסוּ יָגוֹן וַאֲנָחָה. וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Those Being Held in Captivity'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity','en','May the One who blessed Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, Joseph, Moses, Aaron, David and Solomon bless, watch and guard those missing from the Israel Defense Forces and the captives, among others of our brethren of the House of Israel that are situated in distress and in captivity. On account of the congregation''s praying for them, may the Holy One, blessed be He, grant mercy upon them, take them out from darkness and gloom, break their chains, redeem them from their ordeals and return them quickly to the comfort of their families. "Let them praise the Lord for His kindness, and His wondrous deeds for the children of man" (Psalms 107:8). And through them, let the verse (Isaiah 35:10) be fulfilled, "And the Lord’s ransomed shall return, and come with shouting to Zion, crowned with joy everlasting; they shall attain joy and gladness, while sorrow and sighing flee." And let us say, Amen!','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Those Being Held in Captivity'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-shabbat-shacharit-communal-prayers-prayer-for-those-being-held-in-captivity','transliteration','Mi sheberach avoteinu Avraham Yitzchak ve Yaakov yosef Moshe ve aharon David ushelomoh,
hu yevarech ve yishmor ve yintzor et kol hachatufim,
hashevuyim ve hane''edarim b''toch shear acheinu beit yishorael hanetunim b''tzara uveshivya.
Ba''avur shehakahal mitpalel ba''avuram,
hakadosh baruch hu yimaleh rachamim aleihem,
ve yotziem mechoshech ve tzalmavet,
umoseroteihem yenatek,
umimetzukoteihem yoshiem,
vishivem mehera lecheik mishpechoteihem.
Yodu lah'' chasdo ve nifleotav livnei adam.
Vikuyam bahem mikra shekatuv.
Ufeduyei h'' yeshuvun uvau tziyon b''rina ve simchat olam al rosham.
Sason ve simcha yasigu ve nasu yagon va''anacha.
Ve nomar amen.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Shabbat, Shacharit, Communal Prayers, Prayer for Those Being Held in Captivity'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','he','הֲרֵינִי מוּכָן וּמְזוּמָן לְקַיֵּים מִצְוַת סֻכָּה כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוַּנִי הַבּורֵא יִתְבָּרַךְ שְׁמו בַּסֻּכּות תֵּשְׁבוּ שִׁבְעַת יָמִים כָּל הָאֶזְרָח בְּיִשרָאֵל יֵשְׁבוּ בַּסֻּכּות:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','en','Behold, I am ready and prepared to fulfill the commandment of the sukkah (hut), as the Creator, may his Name be blessed, commanded me - as is written (Leviticus 23:43-44), "You shall live in huts seven days; all citizens in Israel shall live in huts.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','transliteration','Hareini muchan umezuman lekayeim mitzvat suka ka''asher tzivani habvreh yitbarach shmv basukvt teshevu shivat yamim kol haezrach b''yishrael yeshevu basukvt.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:1:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','he','לְמַעַן יֵדְעוּ דרתֵיכֶם כִּי בַסֻּכּות הושַׁבְתִּי אֶת בְּנֵי יִשרָאֵל בְּהוצִיאִי אותָם מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:1:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','en','In order that future generations may know that I made the Israelite people live in huts when I brought them out of the land of Egypt."','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-entering-the-sukkah','transliteration','Lema''an yedeu drteichem ki vasukvt hvshavti et b''nei yishrael b''hvtzi''i -vtam me''eretz mitzrayim.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Entering the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah','he','יְהִי רָצון מִלְּפָנֶיךָ ה'' אֱלהֵינוּ וֵאלהֵי אֲבותֵינוּ כְּשֵׁם שֶׁקִיַּמְתִּי וְיָשַׁבְתִּי בְּסוּכָּה זוּ כֵּן אֶזְכֶּה לְשָׁנָה הַבָּאָה לֵישֵׁב בְּסוּכָּה שֶׁל לִוְיָתָן:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Leaving the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah','en','May it be Your will in front of You, Lord, our God and God of our fathers - in the same way that I have fulfilled [the commandment] and dwelt in this sukkah, so may I merit next year to dwell in the sukkah (made from the skin) of the Leviathan.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Leaving the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-sukkot-prayers-in-the-sukkah-leaving-the-sukkah','transliteration','Yehi ratzvn milefaneicha h'' elheinu velhei avvteinu k''shem shekiyamti ve yashavti b''suka zu ken ezkeh leshana haba''a leishev b''suka shel livyatan.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Sukkot, Prayers in the Sukkah, Leaving the Sukkah'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu','he','הַנֵּרוֹת הַלָּלוּ שֶׁאָנוּ מַדְלִיקִין, עַל הַנִּסִּים וְעַל הַנִּפְלָאוֹת וְעַל הַתְּשׁוּעוֹת וְעַל הַמִּלְחָמוֹת, שֶׁעָשִׂיתָ לַאֲבוֹתֵינוּ בַּיָּמִים הָהֵם בַּזְּמַן הַזֶּה, עַל יְדֵי כֹּהֲנֶיךָ הַקְּדוֹשִׁים. וְכָל שְׁמוֹנַת יְמֵי הַחֲנֻכָּה הַנֵּרוֹת הַלָּלוּ קֹדֶשׁ הֵם וְאֵין לָנוּ רְשׁוּת לְהִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בָּהֶם, אֶלָּא לִרְאוֹתָם בִּלְבָד, כְּדֵי לְהוֹדוֹת וּלְהַלֵּל לְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל עַל נִסֶּיךָ וְעַל נִפְלְאוֹתֶיךָ וְעַל יְשׁוּעָתֶךָ.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Chanukah, Service for Lighting Chanukah Candles, Hanerot Hallalu'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu','en','We kindle these lights on account of the miracles, the deliverances and the wonders which thou didst work for our fathers, by means of thy holy priests. During all the eight days of Chanukah these lights are sacred, neither is it permitted us to make any profane use of them; but we are only to look at them, in order that we may give thanks unto thy name for thy miracles, thy deliverances and thy wonders.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Chanukah, Service for Lighting Chanukah Candles, Hanerot Hallalu'),
('sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-ashkenaz-festivals-chanukah-service-for-lighting-chanukah-candles-hanerot-hallalu','transliteration','Hanerot halalu sheanu madlikin,
al hanisim ve al haniflaot ve al hateshuot ve al hamilchamot,
sheasita la''avoteinu bayamim hahem bazeman hazeh,
al yedei kohaneicha hakedoshim.
Ve chol shemonat yemei hachanuka hanerot halalu kodesh hem ve ein lanu reshut lehishtamesh bahem,
ela lirotam bilvad,
k''dei lehodot ulehalel leshimcha hagadol al niseicha ve al nifleoteicha ve al yeshuatecha.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Festivals, Chanukah, Service for Lighting Chanukah Candles, Hanerot Hallalu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','מיד כשיעור משנתו, בעודו על משכבו, יאמר:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','Upon waking in the morning, even before washing your hands, say:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','מוֹדֶה אֲנִי לְפָנֶֽיךָ מֶֽלֶךְ חַי וְקַיָּם שֶׁהֶחֱזַֽרְתָּ בִּי נִשְׁמָתִי בְּחֶמְלָה, רַבָּה אֱמוּנָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','I give thanks to You living and everlasting King for You have restored my soul with mercy. Great is Your faithfulness.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','transliteration','Modeh Ani Lefanecha,
melech chai ve kayam,
shehech-zarta bee, nishmati, b''chemla,
Rabah Emunatecha','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','לאחר שנטל ידיו יאמר:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','After washing your hands, say:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','רֵאשִׁית חָכְמָה יִרְאַת יְהֹוָה, שֵֽׂכֶל טוֹב לְכָל עֹשֵׂיהֶם, תְּהִלָּתוֹ עוֹמֶֽדֶת לָעַד: בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','The beginning of wisdom is fear of Adonoy, good understanding to all who perform [His commandments], His praise endures forever. Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','transliteration','Reshit chochma yirat Adonai,
sechel tov lechol oseihem,
tehilato omedet la''ad.
Baruch shem k''vod malchuto le''olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','לפני עטיפת הטלית קטן, יברך:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','Before putting on your tallis katan say:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּ֒שָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ עַל מִצְוַת צִיצִית:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us concerning the mitzva of tzitzis (fringes).','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu al mitzvat tzitzit.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא חֲשׁוּבָה מִצְוַת צִיצִית לְפָנֶֽיךָ כְּאִלּוּ קִיַּמְתִּֽיהָ בְּכָל פְּרָטֶֽיהָ וְדִקְדּוּקֶֽיהָ וְכַוָּנוֹתֶֽיהָ וְתַרְיַ"ג מִצְווֹת הַתְּ֒לוּיוֹת בָּהּ, אָמֵן סֶלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, my God, and God of my fathers, to consider [my fulfillment of] the mitzva of tzitzis before You as though I had fulfilled it in every detail, accurately and with full intent, and the 613 commandments that depend on it. Amein, Selah.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-modeh-ani','transliteration','Yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai sheteheh chashuva mitzvat tzitzit lefanecha k''ilu kiyamtiha b''chol perateiha ve dikdukeiha ve chavanoteiha ve taryag" mitzvot hateluyot bah,
amen sela.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Modeh Ani'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','נכון לומר בבוקר קודם התפילה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','Before beginning the Morning Prayers you should say the following:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','הֲרֵינִי מְקַבֵּל עָלַי מִצְוַת עֲשֵׂה שֶׁל וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמֽוֹךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','I hereby accept upon myself the positive commandment to love my fellow Jew.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Hareini mekabel alai mitzvat aseh shel ve''ahavta lereacha kamocha.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','כשיכנס לבית הכנסת, יאמר:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','The following verses from Scriptures are recited upon entering the synagogue, as though asking permission of God to enter and pray in His Holy place.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','מַה טֹּֽבוּ אֹהָלֶֽיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִשְׁכְּ֒נֹתֶֽיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל: וַאֲנִי בְּרֹב חַסְדְּ֒ךָ אָבוֹא בֵיתֶֽךָ אֶשְׁתַּחֲוֶה אֶל הֵיכַל־קָדְשְׁ֒ךָ בְּיִרְאָתֶֽךָ: יְהֹוָה אָהַֽבְתִּי מְעוֹן בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּמְקוֹם מִשְׁכַּן כְּבוֹדֶֽךָ: וַאֲנִי אֶשְׁתַּחֲוֶה וְאֶכְרָֽעָה אֶבְרְ֒כָה לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה עֹשִׂי: וַאֲנִי תְפִלָּתִי־לְךָ יְהֹוָה עֵת רָצוֹן אֱלֹהִים בְּרָב־חַסְדֶּֽךָ עֲנֵֽנִי בֶּאֱמֶת יִשְׁעֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','How good are your tents, Jacob: your dwelling places, Israel. As for me, through Your abundant kindness I will enter Your House; I will prostrate myself toward Your Holy Sanctuary in awe of You. Adonoy, I love the Dwelling, Your House, and the place where Your glory resides. I will prostrate myself, and bow, I will kneel before Adonoy, my Maker. May my prayer to You Adonoy be at a favorable time; God, in the abundance of Your kindness answer me with the truth of Your deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Mah tovu ohaleicha Yaakov mishkenoteicha Yisrael.
Va''ani b''rov chasdecha avo veitecha eshtachaveh el heichal kodshecha b''yiratecha.
Adonai ahaveti meon beitecha umekom mishkan k''vodecha.
Va''ani eshtachaveh ve echra''a evrecha lifnei Adonai osi.
Va''ani tefilati lecha Adonai et ratzon Elohim b''rov chasdecha aneni be''emet yishecha.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','ויאמר פיוט ״אדון עולם״ המדבר ביחוד השם והשגחתו:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','This hymn has been attributed to R'' Shlomo ibn Gabirol who lived in Spain during the eleventh century. While praising God''s omnipotence and providence, it clarifies the meaning of the name Adonoy so that before proceeding to pray, each worshiper understands the significance of the God he is addressing.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','אֲדוֹן עוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר מָלַךְ, בְּטֶֽרֶם כָּל יְצִיר נִבְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','Master of the Universe Who reigned before any creature was created.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Adon olam asher malach,
b''terem kol yetzir nivra.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','לְעֵת נַעֲשָׂה בְחֶפְצוֹ כֹּל, אֲזַי מֶֽלֶךְ שְׁמוֹ נִקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','At the time when all was made by His will, then was His Name proclaimed King.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Le''et na''asa ve cheftzo kol,
azai melech shemo nikra.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְאַחֲרֵי כִּכְ֒לוֹת הַכֹּל, לְבַדּוֹ יִמְלֹךְ נוֹרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','And after all things shall cease to be the Awesome One will reign alone.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve acharei kichlot hakol,
levado yimloch nora.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְהוּא הָיָה וְהוּא הֹוֶה, וְהוּא יִהְיֶה בְּתִפְאָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He was, He is, and He shall be in glory.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve hu haya ve hu hoveh,
ve hu yihyeh b''tifara.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְהוּא אֶחָד וְאֵין שֵׁנִי, לְהַמְשִׁיל לוֹ לְהַחְבִּֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is One, and there is no second to compare to Him, to associate [with Him].','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve hu echad ve ein sheni,
lehameshil lo lehachbira.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','בְּלִי רֵאשִׁית בְּלִי תַכְלִית, וְלוֹ הָעֹז וְהַמִּשְׂרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','Without beginning, without end, power and dominion are His.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','B''li reshit b''li tachlit,
ve lo haoz ve hamisra.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְהוּא אֵלִי וְחַי גּוֹאֲלִי, וְצוּר חֶבְלִי בְּעֵת צָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is my God and my ever-living Redeemer, the Rock of my destiny in times of distress.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve hu eli ve chai goali,
ve tzur chevli b''et tzara.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְהוּא נִסִּי וּמָנוֹס לִי, מְנָת כּוֹסִי בְּיוֹם אֶקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is my flag and my refuge; He is the portion of my cup on the day I call.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve hu nisi umanos li,
menat kosi b''yom ekra.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','בְּיָדוֹ אַפְקִיד רוּחִי, בְּעֵת אִישַׁן וְאָעִֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','Into His hand I entrust my spirit [both] when I sleep and when I awaken.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','B''yado afkid ruchi,
b''et ishan ve aira.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','וְעִם רוּחִי גְּוִיָּתִי, יְהֹוָה לִי וְלֹא אִירָא:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','And with my spirit my body [too], Adonoy is with me, I shall not fear.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ve im ruchi geviyati,
Adonai li ve lo ira.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','פיוט המיוסד על שלושה עשר עקרי האמונה. מיוחס לר'' דניאל בן יהודה הרומי','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','This hymn, written by Daniel ben Yehuda, who was a Dayan in Rome about 1300, is based on Maimonides'' 13 principles of Judaism. According to Maimonides, failure to believe in a single one of these principles places one outside the pale of Judaism.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','מציאות השם','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','1) the existence of God','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','יִגְדַּל אֱלֹהִים חַי וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח, נִמְצָא וְאֵין עֵת אֶל מְצִיאוּתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','Exalted is the living God, and praised He exists, and His existence transcends time.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Yigdal Elohim chai ve yishtabach,
nimtza ve ein et el metziuto.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','אחדות השם','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','2) God is One','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','אֶחָד וְאֵין יָחִיד כְּיִחוּדוֹ, נֶעְלָם וְגַם אֵין סוֹף לְאַחְדּוּתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is One, and there is no unity like His, He is invisible, His unity is infinitive.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Echad ve ein yachid k''yichudo,
nelam ve gam ein sof leachduto.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','שאינו גוף','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','3) God is uncorporeal','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','אֵין לוֹ דְמוּת הַגּוּף וְאֵינוֹ גוּף, לֹא נַעֲרֹךְ אֵלָיו קְדֻשָּׁתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is unlike the corporeal or even the non-corporeal, His holiness is beyond comparison.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Ein lo demut haguf ve eino guf,
lo na''aroch elav k''dushato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','קדמות השם','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','4) God is Eternal','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','קַדְמוֹן לְכָל דָּבָר אֲשֶׁר נִבְרָא, רִאשׁוֹן וְאֵין רֵאשִׁית לְרֵאשִׁיתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He preceded every being that was created, He was First, and there was no genesis to His beginning.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Kadmon lechol davar asher nivra,
rishon ve ein reshit lereshito.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','שרק אותו ראוי לעבוד','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','5) God alone must be worshipped','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','הִנּוֹ אֲדוֹן עוֹלָם לְכָל נוֹצָר, יוֹרֶה גְדֻלָּתוֹ וּמַלְכוּתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He is Master of the Universe to every creature, (all) proclaim His greatness and His majesty.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Hino adon olam lechol notzar,
yoreh gedulato umalchuto.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','נבואה','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','6) Truth of Divine Prophecy','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','שֶֽׁפַע נְבוּאָתוֹ נְתָנוֹ, אֶל אַנְשֵׁי סְגֻלָּתוֹ וְתִפְאַרְתּוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','The fullness of His prophecy, He bestowed on those He treasured, and in whom He gloried.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Shefa nevuato netano,
el anshei segulato ve tifarto.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','נבואת משה אמיתית','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','7) Moses was the greatest of all prophets','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','לֹא קָם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל כְּמשֶׁה עוֹד, נָבִיא וּמַבִּיט אֶת תְּמוּנָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','There never arose in Israel another like Moses, a prophet who beheld God''s image.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Lo kam b''Yisrael k''Moshe od,
navi umabit et temunato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','תורה מן השמים','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','8) Divine revelation of the Torah','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','תּוֹרַת אֱמֶת נָתַן לְעַמּוֹ אֵל, עַל יַד נְבִיאוֹ נֶאֱמַן בֵּיתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','The Torah of truth the Almighty gave to His people through His prophet, the trusted one of His house.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Torat emet natan leamo el,
al yad nevio ne''eman beito.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','נצחיות התורה','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','9) The Torah is immutable','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','לֹא יַחֲלִיף הָאֵל וְלֹא יָמִיר דָּתוֹ, לְעוֹלָמִים לְזוּלָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','The Almighty will not exchange nor alter His Law. Never will He offer any alternative.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Lo yachalif hael ve lo yamir dato,
leolamim lezulato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','השגחה','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','10) God knows the acts and thoughts of man','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','צוֹפֶה וְיוֹדֵֽעַ סְתָרֵֽינוּ, מַבִּיט לְסוֹף דָּבָר בְּקַדְמָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He scrutinizes and knows our secrets. He beholds the end of a thing at its beginning.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Tzofeh ve yodea setareinu,
mabit lesof davar b''kadmato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','שכר ועונש','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','11) Divine reward and punishment','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:37:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','גּוֹמֵל לְאִישׁ חֶֽסֶד כְּמִפְעָלוֹ, נוֹתֵן לְרָשָׁע רָע כְּרִשְׁעָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:37:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He rewards man with kindness according to his deeds. He sends evil to the wicked according to his wickedness.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:37:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Gomel leish chesed k''mifalo,
noten lerasha ra k''rishato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:38:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','ביאת המשיח','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:38:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','12) Belief in the coming of the Messiah','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:39:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','יִשְׁלַח לְקֵץ הַיָּמִין מְשִׁיחֵֽנוּ, לִפְדּוֹת מְחַכֵּי קֵץ יְשׁוּעָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:39:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','He will send our Messiah at the end of days, to redeem all who await His final deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:39:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Yishlach leketz hayamin meshichenu,
lifdot mechakei ketz yeshuato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:40:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','תחיית המתים','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:40:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','13) Divine resurrection of the dead','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:41:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','he','מֵתִים יְחַיֶּה אֵל בְּרֹב חַסְדּוֹ, בָּרוּךְ עֲדֵי עַד שֵׁם תְּהִלָּתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:41:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','en','The Almighty will revive the dead because of His abundant kindness: Blessed forever is His praised Name.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue:41:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-upon-arising-upon-entering-synagogue','transliteration','Metim yechayeh el b''rov chasdo,
baruch adei ad shem tehilato.','Siddur Sefard, Upon Arising, Upon Entering Synagogue'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּ֒שָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ עַל נְטִילַת יָדָֽיִם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us concerning the washing of hands.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu al netilat yadayim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר יָצַר אֶת הָאָדָם בְּחָכְמָה וּבָֽרָא בוֹ נְקָבִים נְקָבִים חֲלוּלִים חֲלוּלִים גָּלוּי וְיָדֽוּעַ לִפְנֵי כִסֵּא כְבוֹדֶֽךָ שֶׁאִם יִפָּתֵֽחַ אֶחָד מֵהֶם אוֹ יִסָּתֵם אֶחָד מֵהֶם אִי אֶפְשַׁר לְהִתְקַיֵּם וְלַעֲמֹד לְפָנֶֽיךָ אֲפִילוּ שָׁעָה אֶחָת. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה רוֹפֵא כָל בָּשָׂר וּמַפְלִיא לַעֲשׂוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who formed man with wisdom and created within him openings and hollows. It is obvious and known in the presence of Your glorious throne that if one of them were ruptured, or if one of them were blocked, it would be impossible to exist and stand in Your Presence even for a short while. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who heals all flesh and performs wonders.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher yatzar et ha''adam b''chochma uvara vo nekavim nekavim chalulim chalulim galuy ve yadua lifnei chiseh chevodecha she''im yipateach echad mehem o yisatem echad mehem ee efshar lehitkayem ve la''amod lefanecha afilu sha''a echat.
Baruch atah Adonai rofeh chol basar umafli la''asot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','he','אֱלֹהַי, נְשָׁמָה שֶׁנָּתַֽתָּ בִּי טְהוֹרָה הִיא אַתָּה בְרָאתָהּ אַתָּה יְצַרְתָּהּ אַתָּה נְפַחְתָּהּ בִּי וְאַתָּה מְשַׁמְּ֒רָהּ בְּקִרְבִּי וְאַתָּה עָתִיד לִטְּ֒לָהּ מִמֶּֽנִּי וּלְהַחֲזִירָהּ בִּי לֶעָתִיד לָבֹא, כָּל זְמַן שֶׁהַנְּ֒שָׁמָה בְקִרְבִּי מוֹדֶה אֲנִי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי רִבּוֹן כָּל הַמַּעֲשִׂים אֲדוֹן כָּל הַנְּ֒שָׁמוֹת: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמַּחֲזִיר נְשָׁמוֹת לִפְגָרִים מֵתִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','en','My God! the soul which You bestowed in me is pure; You created it, You formed it, You breathed it into me and You preserve it within me. You will eventually take it from me, and restore it in me in the time to come. So long as the soul is within me I give thanks to You, Adonoy my God, and God of my fathers, Lord of all creatures, Master of all souls. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who restores souls to dead bodies.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-morning-blessings','transliteration','Elohai,
neshama shenatata bee tehora hi atah ve ratah atah yetzartah atah nefachtah bee ve atah meshamerah b''kirbi ve atah atid litelah mimeni ulehachazirah bee leatid lavo,
kol zeman shehaneshama ve kirbi modeh ani lefanecha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai ribon kol hama''asim adon kol haneshamot.
Baruch atah Adonai hamachazir neshamot lifgarim metim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Morning Blessings'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּ֒שָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ לַעֲסֹק בְּדִבְרֵי תוֹרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us to be engrossed in the words of Torah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu la''asok b''divrei torah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','וְהַעֲרֶב נָא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֶת דִּבְרֵי תוֹרָתְ֒ךָ בְּפִֽינוּ וּבְפִי עַמְּ֒ךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִהְיֶה אֲנַחְנוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵינוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵי צֶאֱצָאֵינוּ עַמְּ֒ךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל כֻּלָּֽנוּ יוֹדְ֒עֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ וְלוֹמְ֒דֵי תוֹרָתֶֽךָ לִשְׁמָהּ: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמְלַמֵּד תּוֹרָה לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Adonoy our God, please make pleasant the words of Your Torah in our mouths and in the mouths of Your people Israel. And may we and our descendants and the descendants of Your people the House of Israel, all be perceivers of Your Name and students of Your Torah for its own sake. Blessed are You, Adonoy Who teaches Torah to His people, Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Ve ha''arev na Adonai Eloheinu et divrei toratecha b''finu uvefi amecha beit Yisrael ve nihyeh anachnu ve tze''etzaeinu ve tze''etzaei tze''etzaeinu amecha beit Yisrael kulanu yode''ei shemecha ve lomedei toratecha lishmah.
Baruch atah Adonai hamelamed torah leamo Yisrael.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר בָּֽחַר בָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ אֶת תּוֹרָתוֹ: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה נוֹתֵן הַתּוֹרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe Who chose us from among all the peoples and gave us His Torah. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Giver of the Torah!','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher bachar banu mikol ha''amim ve natan lanu et torato.
Baruch atah Adonai noten hatora.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר דַבֵּר אֶל אַהֲרֹן וְאֶל בָּנָיו לֵאמֹר כֹּה תְבָרְכוּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אָמוֹר לָהֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','And Adonoy spoke to Moses, saying, Speak to Aaron and to his sons, saying, thus shall you bless the Children of Israel, say to them:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Vayedaber Adonai el Moshe lemor daber el aharon ve el banav lemor koh tevarechu et b''nei Yisrael amor lahem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','יְבָרֶכְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶֽךָ: יָאֵר יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וִיחֻנֶּֽךָּ: יִשָּׂא יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וְיָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','May Adonoy bless you and guard you. May Adonoy shine His countenance upon you and be gracious unto you. May Adonoy turn His countenance toward you and grant you peace.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Yevarechcha Adonai ve yishmerecha.
Yaer Adonai panav eleicha vichuneka.
Yisa Adonai panav eleicha ve yasem lecha shalom.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','וְשָׂמוּ אֶת שְׁמִי עַל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וַאֲנִי אַבָרְכֵם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','And they shall set My Name upon the Children of Israel, and I shall bless them.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Ve samu et shemi al b''nei Yisrael va''ani avarechem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','אֵֽלּוּ דְבָרִים שֶׁאֵין לָהֶם שִׁעוּר הַפֵּאָה וְהַבִּכּוּרִים וְהָרְ֒אָיוֹן וּגְמִילוּת חֲסָדִים וְתַלְמוּד תּוֹרָה: אֵֽלּוּ דְבָרִים שֶׁאָדָם אוֹכֵל פֵּרוֹתֵיהֶם בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְהַקֶּֽרֶן קַיֶּֽמֶת לָעוֹלָם הַבָּא, וְאֵֽלּוּ הֵן כִּבּוּד אָב וָאֵם וּגְמִילוּת חֲסָדִים וְהַשְׁכָּמַת בֵּית הַמִּדְרָשׁ שַׁחֲרִית וְעַרְבִית וְהַכְנָסַת אוֹרְ֒חִים וּבִקּוּר חוֹלִים וְהַכְנָסַת כַּלָּה וּלְוָיַת הַמֵּת וְעִיּוּן תְּפִלָּה וַהֲבָאַת שָׁלוֹם בֵּין אָדָם לַחֲבֵרוֹ ובֵין אִישׁ לְאִשְׁתּוֹ וְתַלְמוּד תּוֹרָה כְּנֶֽגֶד כֻּלָּם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','These are precepts for which no fixed measure is prescribed: [leaving] the corner [of a field unharvested], [the offering of] the first fruits, the appearance-offering, [performing] deeds of kindness, and the study of Torah. These are precepts, the fruits of which man enjoys in this world, [while] the principal [reward] is preserved for him in the World-to-Come. They are: honoring father and mother, [performing] deeds of kindness, early attendance in the House of Study morning and evening, providing hospitality to guests, visiting the sick, participating in making a wedding, accompanying the dead [to the grave], concentrating on the meaning of prayers, making peace between fellow men and between husband and wife— and the study of Torah is equal to them all.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Elu devarim she''ein lahem shiur hapea ve habikurim ve hareayon ugemilut chasadim ve talmud torah.
Elu devarim sheadam ochel peroteihem baolam hazeh ve hakeren kayemet laolam haba,
ve elu hen kibud av vaem ugemilut chasadim ve hashkamat beit hamidrash shacharit ve arvit ve hachnasat orechim uvikur cholim ve hachnasat kala ulevayat hamet ve iyun tefilah vahava''at shalom bein adam lachavero vvein ish leishto ve talmud torah k''neged kulam.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הַּנוֹתֵן לַשֶּֽׂכְוִי בִינָה לְהַבְחִין בֵּין יוֹם וּבֵין לָֽיְלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who gives the rooster understanding to distinguish between day and night.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam hanoten lasechevi vina lehavchin bein yom uvein layela.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם שֶׁלֹּא עָשַֽׂנִי גּוֹי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who did not make me a gentile.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam shelo asani goy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם שֶׁלֹּא עָשַֽׂנִי עָֽבֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-blessings-on-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who did not make me a slave.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Blessings on Torah'),
