('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכוֹר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember, that we are dust.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:42:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zachor ki afar anachenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נָא אַל תְּשִׁיבֵֽנוּ רֵיקָם מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! Please do not turn us away empty-handed from You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:43:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu na al teshivenu reikam milefaneicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ תְּהֵא הַשָּׁעָה הַזֹּאת שְׁעַת רַחֲמִים וְעֵת רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! let this hour be an hour of compassion and a time of favor before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:44:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu teheh hasha''a hazot sheat rachamim ve et ratzon milefaneicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חֲמוֹל עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל עוֹלָלֵֽינוּ וְטַפֵּֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! have compassion upon us, and upon our children and infants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:45:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chamol aleinu ve al olaleinu ve tapenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן הֲרוּגִים עַל שֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slain for Your holy Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:46:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an harugim al shem kodshecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן טְבוּחִים עַל יִחוּדֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slaughtered for [proclaiming] Your Unity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:47:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an tevuchim al yichudecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן בָּאֵי בָאֵשׁ וּבַמַּֽיִם עַל קִדּוּשׁ שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who went through fire and water for the sanctification of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:48:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an baei vaesh uvamayim al kidush shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נְקוֹם לְעֵינֵֽינוּ נִקְ֒מַת דַּם עֲבָדֶֽיךָ הַשָּׁפוּךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! avenge before our eyes the spilled blood of Your servants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:49:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu nekom le''eineinu nikmat dam avadeicha hashafuch.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אִם לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake if not for ours.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:50:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''ancha im lo lema''anenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:51:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''ancha ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great mercy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:52:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an rachameicha harabim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא שֶׁנִּקְרָא עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great, mighty, and awesome Name which is proclaimed upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:53:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an shimcha hagadol hagibor ve hanora shenikra aleinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! favor us and answer us for we have no accomplishments; deal with us charitably and kindly with us and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu:54:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chanenu va''anenu ki ein banu ma''asim aseh imanu tzedaka vachesed ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','בשני וחמישי יאמר והוא רחום. בשאר ימים שאומרים בהם תחנון יאמר שומר ישראל.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','The following prayers are added on Mondays and Thursday. On other days, continue "Guardian of Israel. . .":','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','נוהגים להרבות בתחנונים בשני וחמישי משום דאמרינן במדרש דמרע"ה עלה בחמישי לקבל לוחות אחרונות וירד בשני. ואומרים והוא רחום. ויש במדרש דג'' זקנים תקנוהו. שתפשם מלך אחד ונתנם בג'' ספינות בלא מנהיג. ושלחם לים ונתפזרו למרחקים. ולמקום שבאו הציר להם מאד ועמדו בתפלה וכל אחד יסד מקצת. ובכל חלק י"ח שמות כנגד תפלת י"ח. וימת אותו מלך שהציר להם בתחלואים רעים. ושלחו תפלתם בכל תפוצות ישראל לאמרה בשני וחמישי (ע"פ מחזור מכל השנה)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','This group of somber plaints, known as the "long Vehu Rachum" is recited in the morning service on Mondays and Thursdays, except on days when Tachanun is omitted. The origin of these seven prayers is shrouded in legend. It has been suggested that they were composed during the terrible persecutions at the hands of the Goths in seventh-century Spain. It has been said, "Whoever can read this ‘long Vehu Rachum'' prayer without emotion has lost all feeling for what is great and noble." Despite all the repetition in these cries for forgiveness, mercy, help, and protection, the effect is not tiring; because here it is not merely an individual soul, but the soul of an entire people that utters these laments and supplications, that gives voice to this woe of nearly two thousand years. Moses ascended Mount Sinai to receive the Second Tablets on the fifth day of the week, and he returned to the people on the second day of the week, bringing them the new tablets as a security for the Divine covenant and as confirmation of God''s atonement for their transgression. Ever since, the second and fifth day of each week, Monday and Thursday, have been days of summons to the Jewish people to assemble anew before God and to reaffirm their sincere "return" to the Law of God. Our regular service is therefore augmented on these days by these additional supplications.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֺן וְלֹא־יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא־יָעִיר כָּל־חֲמָתוֹ: אַתָּה יְהֹוָה לֺא תִכְלָא רַחֲמֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנּוּ חַסְדְּ֒ךָ וַאֲמִתְּ֒ךָ תָּמִיד יִצְ֒רֽוּנוּ: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְ֒הִלָּתֶֽךָ: אִם־עֲוֺנוֹת תִּשְׁמָר־יָהּ אֲדֹנָי מִי יַעֲמֹד: כִּי־עִמְּ֒ךָ הַסְּ֒לִיחָה לְמַֽעַן תִּוָּרֵא: לֺא כַחֲטָאֵֽינוּ תַּעֲשֶׂה־לָּֽנוּ וְלֹא כַעֲוֺנֹתֵֽינוּ תִּגְמֹל עָלֵֽינוּ: אִם־עֲוֺנֵֽינוּ עָֽנוּ בָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: זְכָר־רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: יַעֲנֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה בְּיוֹם צָרָה יְשַׂגְּ֒בֵֽנוּ שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ: אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה כְּרוֹב רַחֲמֶֽיךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: אֲדוֹנֵֽינוּ אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שְׁמַע קוֹל תַּחֲנוּנֵֽינוּ וּזְ֒כָר־לָֽנוּ אֶת־בְּרִית אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','And He, the merciful One, will atone iniquity, and will not destroy, He frequently withdraws His anger, and does not arouse all His rage. You, Adonoy, do not withhold Your mercy from us; may Your kindness and truth always protect us. Deliver us, Adonoy, our God, and gather us from among the nations to give thanks to Your holy Name to be extolled in Your praise. If You, God, should preserve iniquities, my Master, who could survive? But with You there is forgiveness, [in order] that You may be feared. Do not deal with us according to our sins nor repay us according to our iniquities. If our iniquities testify against us, Adonoy, act [mercifully] for Your Name''s sake. Remember Your mercies Adonoy, and Your kindnesses, for they are from the beginning of the world. Adonoy will answer us on the day of distress, the Name of the God of Jacob will fortify us. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call. Our Father, our King, favor us and answer us, for we have no [good] deeds; deal charitably with us according to Your abundant mercy and deliver us for the sake of Your Name. Our Master, our God, heed our supplications; and remember unto us the covenant of our fathers, and deliver us for Your Name''s sake.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Ve hu rachum yechaper avon ve lo yashchit ve hirba lehashiv apo ve lo yair kol chamato.
Atah Adonai lo tichla rachameicha mimenu chasdecha va''amitecha tamid yitzrunu.
Hoshienu Adonai Eloheinu ve kabetzenu min hagoyim lehodot leshem kodshecha lehishtabeach bithilatecha.
Im avonot tishmor yah adonai mi ya''amod.
Ki imecha haselicha lema''an tivareh.
Lo chachataeinu ta''aseh lanu ve lo cha''avonoteinu tigmol aleinu.
Im avoneinu anu vanu Adonai aseh lema''an shemecha.
Zechar rachameicha Adonai vachasadeicha ki meolam hema.
Ya''anenu Adonai b''yom tzara yesagevenu shem Elohei Yaakov.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.
Avinu malkenu chanenu va''anenu ki ein banu ma''asim aseh imanu tzedaka k''rov rachameicha ve hoshienu lema''an shemecha.
Adoneinu Eloheinu shema kol tachanuneinu uzechar lanu et b''rit avoteinu ve hoshienu lema''an shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וְעַתָּה אֲדֹנָי אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵֽאתָ אֶת־עַמְּ֒ךָ מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרַֽיִם בְּיָד חֲזָקָה וַתַּֽעַשׂ־לְךָ שֵׁם כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה חָטָֽאנוּ רָשָֽׁעְנוּ: אֲדֹנָי כְּכָל־צִדְ֒קֹתֶֽיךָ יָֽשָׁב־נָא אַפְּ֒ךָ וַחֲמָתְ֒ךָ מֵעִירְ֒ךָ יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ הַר־קָדְשֶֽׁךָ כִּי בַחֲטָאֵֽינוּ וּבַעֲוֺנוֹת אֲבֹתֵֽינוּ יְרוּשָׁלַֽםִ וְעַמְּ֒ךָ לְחֶרְפָּה לְכָל־סְבִיבֹתֵֽינוּ: וְעַתָּה שְׁמַע אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֶל־תְּפִלַּת עַבְדְּךָ וְאֶל־תַּחֲנוּנָיו וְהָאֵר פָּנֶֽיךָ עַל־מִקְדָּשְׁ֒ךָ הַשָּׁמֵם לְמַֽעַן אֲדֹנָי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','And now, my Master, our God, who brought out Your people, from the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and made for Yourself a name to this day;'' we have sinned, we have acted wickedly. My Master, with all Your righteousness turn away Your anger and Your rage from Your city, Jerusalem, Your holy mountain; for because of our sins and the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and Your people are [held] in contempt by all who surround us. And now, listen our God, to the prayers of Your servant and to his supplications; and let Your radiant countenance shine upon Your desolate Sanctuary for Your sake, my Master.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Ve atah adonai Eloheinu asher hotzeta et amecha me''eretz mitzrayim b''yad chazaka vata''as lecha shem kayom hazeh chatanu rashaenu.
Adonai k''chol tzidkoteicha yashav na apecha vachamatecha meirecha yerushalami har kodshecha ki vachataeinu uva''avonot avoteinu yerushalami ve amecha lecherpa lechol sevivoteinu.
Ve atah shema Eloheinu el tefilat avdecha ve el tachanunav ve haer paneicha al mikdashecha hashamem lema''an adonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַטֵּה אֱלֺהַי אָזְנְךָ וּשְׁ֒מָע פְּקַח עֵינֶֽיךָ וּרְ֒אֵה שֹׁמְ֒מוֹתֵֽינוּ וְהָעִיר אֲשֶׁר־נִקְרָא שִׁמְךָ עָלֶֽיהָ כִּי לֺא עַל־צִדְ֒קֹתֵֽינוּ אֲנַֽחְנוּ מַפִּילִים תַּחֲנוּנֵֽינוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ כִּי עַל־רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים: אֲדֹנָי שְׁמָֽעָה אֲדֹנָי סְלָֽחָה אֲדֹנָי הַקְשִֽׁיבָה וַעֲשֵׂה אַל־תְּאַחַר: לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אֱלֺהַי כִּי־שִׁמְךָ נִקְרָא עַל־עִירְ֒ךָ וְעַל־עַמֶּֽךָ: אָבִֽינוּ אָב הָרַחֲמָן הַרְאֵֽנוּ אוֹת לְטוֹבָה וְקַבֵּץ נְפוּצוֹתֵֽינוּ מֵאַרְבַּע כַּנְ֒פוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ: יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל־הַגּוֹיִם כִּי אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ: וְעַתָּה יְהֹוָה אָבִֽינוּ אָֽתָּה אֲנַֽחְנוּ הַחֹֽמֶר וְאַתָּה יֹצְ֒רֵֽנוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדְ֒ךָ כֻּלָּֽנוּ: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ צוּרֵֽנוּ וְגוֹאֲלֵֽנוּ: חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עַל־עַמֶּֽךָ וְאַל־תִּתֵּן נַחֲלָתְ֒ךָ לְחֶרְפָּה לִמְשָׁל־בָּם גּוֹיִם: לָֽמָּה יֹאמְ֒רוּ בָעַמִּים אַיֵּה (נָא) אֱלֺהֵיהֶם: יָדַֽעְנוּ יְהֺוָה כִּי חָטָֽאנוּ וְאֵין מִי יַעֲמֹד בַּעֲדֵֽנוּ אֶלָּא שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל יַעֲמָד־לָֽנוּ בְּעֵת צָרָה: יָדַֽעְנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים צְדָקָה עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: כְּרַחֵם אָב עַל־בָּנִים כֵּן תְּרַחֵם יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: חֲמוֹל עַל עַמֶּֽךָ רַחֵם עַל נַחֲלָתֶֽךָ חֽוּסָה־נָּא כְּרוֹב רַחֲמֶֽיךָ חָנֵּֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַצְּ֒דָקָה עֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת בְּכָל עֵת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Incline Your ear, my God, and hear; open Your eyes and behold our desolate places and the city which is called by Your Name, for it is not on account of our righteousness that we let fall our supplications before You, but because of Your great mercy. My Master, hear! my Master, forgive! my Master, listen and take action, do not delay! For Your sake, my God, for Your Name is proclaimed over Your city and Your people. Our Father, merciful Father, show us a sign for good and gather our dispersed [people] from the four corners of the earth, [so that] all nations will recognize and know that You, Adonoy, are our God. And now, Adonoy, You are our Father; we are the clay and You are our Former; and we are all the work of Your hand. Deliver us, for Your Name''s sake our Father, our King, our Rock and our Redeemer. Adonoy, spare Your people, and let not Your heritage be [an object] of contempt for nations to rule over. Why should they say among the peoples, Where is their God? Adonoy, we know that we have sinned, and there is none to stand up in our behalf; let Your great Name, then, stand up for us at the time of distress. We know that we have no [good] deeds, [therefore] deal charitably with us for Your Name''s sake. As a father has compassion on his children, so do You have compassion on us, Adonoy, and [therefore] deliver us for Your Name''s sake. Have pity on Your people, have compassion on Your heritage, spare us with Your great mercy; favor us. our King, and answer us, for righteousness is Yours, Adonoy, Who performs wonders at all times.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Hateh Elohai oznecha ushema pekach eineicha ure''eh shomemoteinu ve hair asher nikra shimcha aleiha ki lo al tzidkoteinu anachenu mapilim tachanuneinu lefanecha ki al rachameicha harabim.
Adonai shema''a adonai selacha adonai hakshiva va''aseh al teachar.
Lema''ancha Elohai ki shimcha nikra al irecha ve al amecha.
Avinu av harachaman harenu ot letova ve kabetz nefutzoteinu mearba kanfot ha''aretz.
Yakiru ve yedeu kol hagoyim ki atah Adonai Eloheinu.
Ve atah Adonai avinu atah anachenu hachomer ve atah yotzerenu uma''aseh yadecha kulanu.
Hoshienu lema''an shemecha avinu malkenu tzurenu ve goalenu.
Chusa Adonai al amecha ve al titen nachalatecha lecherpa limshal bam goyim.
Lama yomeru va''amim ayeh (na) eloheihem.
Yadaenu Adonai ki chatanu ve ein mi ya''amod ba''adenu ela shimcha hagadol ya''amad lanu b''et tzara.
Yadaenu ki ein banu ma''asim tzedaka aseh imanu lema''an shemecha.
K''rachem av al banim ken terachem Adonai aleinu ve hoshienu lema''an shemecha.
Chamol al amecha rachem al nachalatecha chusa na k''rov rachameicha chanenu malkenu va''anenu ki lecha Adonai hatzedaka oseh niflaot b''chol et.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַבֶּט־נָא רַחֶם־נָא וְהוֹשִֽׁיעָה־נָא צֹאן מַרְעִיתֶֽךָ וְאַל יִמְשָׁל־בָּֽנוּ קֶֽצֶף כִּי לְךָ יְהֹוָה הַיְ֒שׁוּעָה: בְּךָ תוֹחַלְתֵּֽנוּ אֱלֽוֹהַּ סְלִיחוֹת אָנָּא סְלַח־נָא כִּי אֵל טוֹב וְסַלָּח אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Look, we beseech You, speedily have compassion and deliver the sheep of Your pasture; let wrath not prevail over us, for, Adonoy, deliverance is Yours. Our hope rests with You, God of forgiveness; please forgive [us], for You Almighty, are good, and forgiving.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Habet na rachem na ve hoshia na tzon maritecha ve al yimshal banu ketzef ki lecha Adonai hayeshua.
B''cha tochaltenu eloah selichot ana selach na ki el tov ve salach atah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אָנָּא מֶֽלֶךְ חַנוּן וְרַחוּם זְכוֹר וְהַבֵּט לִבְ֒רִית בֵּין הַבְּ֒תָרִים וְתֵרָאֶה לְפָנֶֽיךָ עֲקֵדַת יָחִיד וּלְ֒מַֽעַן יִשְׂרָאֵל אָבִֽינוּ: אַל־תַּעַזְ֒בֵֽנוּ אָבִֽינוּ וְאַל־תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ וְאַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ יוֹצְ֒רֵֽנוּ וְאַל־תַּֽעַשׁ עִמָּֽנוּ כָּלָה בְּגָלוּתֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','We beseech You, gracious and compassionate King, remember and look to the Covenant between the divided pieces, and let appear before You the binding [upon the Altar] of the only son, and for the sake of Israel, our father. Do not abandon us our father, do not cast us off our King, do not forget us our Creator, and do not bring destruction upon us in our exile for You are the Almighty who is King, gracious and merciful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Ana melech chanun ve rachum zechor ve habet livrit bein habetarim ve teraeh lefanecha akedat yachid ulema''an Yisrael avinu.
Al ta''azvenu avinu ve al titeshenu malkenu ve al tishkachenu yotzerenu ve al ta''ash imanu kala b''galutenu ki el melech chanun ve rachum atah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אֵין כָּמֽוֹךָ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֵין כָּמֽוֹךָ אֵל אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וְרַב חֶֽסֶד וֶאֱמֶת: הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ וְרַחֲמֵֽנוּ בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים מֵרַֽעַשׁ וּמֵרֺֽגֶז הַצִּילֵֽנוּ: זְכֺר לַעֲבָדֶֽיךָ לְאַבְרָהָם לְיִצְחָק וּלְ֒יַעֲקֹב אַל־תֵּֽפֶן אֶל־קְשִׁי הָעָם הַזֶּה וְאֶל־רִשְׁעוֹ וְאֶל־חַטָּאתוֹ: שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ: וְהָסֵר מִמֶּֽנּוּ מַכַּת הַמָּֽוֶת כִּי רַחוּם אָֽתָּה: כִּי כֵן דַּרְכֶּֽךָ עֹשֶׂה חֶֽסֶד חִנָּם בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדוֹר: חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עַל־עַמֶּֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ מִזַּעְמֶֽךָ: וְהָסֵר מִמֶּֽנּוּ מַכַּת הַמַּגֵּפָה וּגְ֒זֵרָה קָשָׁה כִּי אַתָּה שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל: לְךָ אֲדֹנָי הַצְּ֒דָקָה וְלָֽנוּ בּֽשֶׁת הַפָּנִים: מַה־נִּתְאוֹנֵן וּמַה־נֹּאמַר מַה־נְּדַבֵּר וּמַה־נִּצְטַּדָּק: נַחְפְּשָׂה דְרָכֵֽינוּ וְנַחְקֺֽרָה וְנָשֽׁוּבָה אֵלֶֽיךָ כִּי יְמִינְ֒ךָ פְשׁוּטָה לְקַבֵּל שָׁבִים: אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה נָּא אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה הַצְלִיחָה נָא: אָֽנָּא יְהֹוָה עֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: לְךָ יְהֹוָה חִכִּֽינוּ לְךָ יְהֹוָה קִוִּינוּ לְךָ יְהֹוָה נְיַחֵל אַל תֶּחֱשֶׁה וּתְ֒עַנֵּֽנוּ כִּי נָאֲמוּ גוֹיִם אָבְ֒דָה תִקְוָתָם: כָּל־בֶּֽרֶךְ לְךָ תִכְרַע וְכָל־קוֹמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ לְבַד תִּשְׁתַּחֲוֶה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','There is none like You, gracious and merciful Adonoy, our God; there is none like You, Almighty, slow to anger, abundant in kindliness and truth. Deliver us, and have mercy on us with Your great mercy, save us from storm and rage. Remember Your servants, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob; do not consider the stubbornness of this people, their wickedness, and their sinfulness. Turn from Your fierce anger and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil [intended] for Your people. Remove from us the scourge of death, for You are merciful; for such is Your way— to bestow undeserved kindness in every generation. Spare Your people, Adonoy, and save us from Your wrath; remove from us the scourge of plague, and harsh decree, for You are the Guardian of Israel. Righteousness is Yours, my Master, while shame is ours. How can we complain? What can we say? What can we speak? and how can we justify ourselves? Let us search into our ways and examine them, and return to You; for Your right hand is extended to receive those who repent. We beseech You Adonoy!—deliver us. We beseech You Adonoy!—grant us success; We beseech You Adonoy! — answer us on the day we call. For You, Adonoy, we have waited, For You, Adonoy, we have hoped, For You, Adonoy, we yearn. Do not be silent, and do not allow us to be tormented; for the nations have said, "Their hope is lost." Let every knee bend to You and all who stand erect prostrate themselves before You','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Ein kamocha chanun ve rachum Adonai Eloheinu ein kamocha el erech apayim ve rav chesed ve''emet.
Hoshienu ve rachamenu b''rachameicha harabim mera''ash umerogez hatzilenu.
Zechor la''avadeicha leAvraham leYitzchak uleya''akov al tefen el k''shi ha''am hazeh ve el risho ve el chatato.
Shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.
Ve haser mimenu makat hamavet ki rachum atah.
Ki chen darkecha oseh chesed chinam b''chol dor vador.
Chusa Adonai al amecha ve hatzilenu mizamecha.
Ve haser mimenu makat hamagefa ugezera kasha ki atah shomer Yisrael.
Lecha adonai hatzedaka ve lanu bshet hapanim.
Mah nitonen umah nomar mah nedaber umah nitztadak.
Nachpesa deracheinu ve nachkora ve nashuva eleicha ki yeminecha feshuta lekabel shavim.
Ana Adonai hoshia na ana Adonai hatzlicha na.
Ana Adonai anenu ve yom kare''enu.
Lecha Adonai chikinu lecha Adonai kivinu lecha Adonai neyachel al techesheh uteanenu ki na''amu goyim aveda tikvatam.
Kol berech lecha tichra ve chol koma lefanecha levad tishtachaveh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַפּוֹתֵֽחַ יָד בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה לְקַבֵּל פּוֹשְׁ֒עִים וְחַטָּאִים נִבְהֲלָה נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ מֵרוֹב עִצְּ֒בוֹנֵֽנוּ אַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ נֶֽצַח קֽוּמָה וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ: אַל־תִּשְׁפּוֹךְ חֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ עָלֵֽינוּ כִּי אֲנַֽחְנוּ עַמְּ֒ךָ בְּנֵי בְרִיתֶֽךָ: אֵל הַבִּֽיטָה דַּל כְּבוֹדֵֽנוּ בַּגּוֹיִם וְשִׁקְּ֒צֽוּנוּ כְּטֻמְאַת הַנִּדָּה: עַד־מָתַי עֻזְּ֒ךָ בַּשְּׁ֒בִי וְתִפְאַרְתְּ֒ךָ בְּיַד־צָר: עוֹרְ֒רָה גְבוּרָתְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁעֵֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ: אַל־יִמְעֲטוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ תְּלָאוֹתֵֽינוּ: מַהֵר יְקַדְּ֒מֽוּנוּ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ בְּעֵת צָרוֹתֵֽינוּ, לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ אֶלָּא לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ פְעַל, וְאַל תַּשְׁחִית אֶת־זֵֽכֶר שְׁאֵרִיתֵֽנוּ, כִּי לְךָ מְיַחֲלוֹת עֵינֵֽינוּ כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה: וּזְ֒כוֹר עֵדוּתֵֽנוּ בְּכָל־יוֹם תָּמִיד אוֹמְ֒רִים פַּעֲמַֽיִם בְּאַהֲבָה: שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','You Who opens Your hand to [accept] repentance, to receive transgressors and sinners: our soul is terrified from our great sorrow— forget us not forever; arise and deliver us. Do not pour out Your wrath upon us, for we are Your people, the children of Your covenant. Almighty, look! Our glory has sunk low among the nations, and they abominate us like the impurity of the nidah. How long will Your strength be in captivity, and Your glory, in the hand of the foe? Arouse Your might and deliver us for the sake of Your Name, let our sufferings not seem trivial to You. May Your mercy come swiftly toward us in time of our distress; not for our sake, but do it for Your sake, and do not obliterate the remembrance of our remnant, for our eyes look hopefully to You, for You are the Almighty Who is King, Gracious, and Merciful. Remember our testimony every day we proclaim twice a day with love: Hear Israel, Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Hapoteach yad bitshuva lekabel posheim ve chataim nivhala nafshenu merov itzevonenu al tishkachenu netzach kuma ve hoshienu.
Al tishpoch charonecha aleinu ki anachenu amecha b''nei ve ritecha.
El habita dal k''vodenu bagoyim ve shiketzunu k''tumat hanida.
Ad matai uzecha bashevi ve tifartecha b''yad tzar.
Orera gevuratecha ve hoshienu lema''an shemecha.
Al yimatu lefanecha telaoteinu.
Maher yekademunu rachameicha b''et tzaroteinu,
lo lema''anenu ela lema''ancha feal,
ve al tashchit et zecher she''eritenu,
ki lecha meyachalot eineinu ki el melech chanun ve rachum atah.
Uzechor edutenu b''chol yom tamid omerim pa''amayim b''ahava.
Shema Yisrael Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','הַבֵּט מִשָּׁמַֽיִם וּרְ֒אֵה כִּי הָיִֽינוּ לַֽעַג וָקֶֽלֶס בַּגּוֹיִם: נֶחְשַֽׁבְנוּ כַּצֹּאן לָטֶֽבַח יוּבָל, לַהֲרוֹג וּלְ֒אַבֵּד וּלְ֒מַכָּה וּלְ֒חֶרְפָּה: וּבְכָל־זֹאת שִׁמְךָ לֺא שָׁכָֽחְנוּ נָא אַל־תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Look from heaven and behold that we have become [an object] of scorn and derision among the nations; we are considered as the sheep led to the slaughter to be slain and destroyed, tortured and humiliated. And yet despite all this, we have not forgotten Your Name; please, do not forget us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Habet mishamayim ure''eh ki hayinu la''ag vakeles bagoyim.
Nechshavenu katzon latevach yuval,
laharog uleabed ulemaka ulecherpa.
Uvechol zot shimcha lo shachachenu na al tishkachenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','זָרִים אוֹמְ֒רִים אֵין תּוֹחֶֽלֶת וְתִקְוָה: חוֹן אוֹם לְשִׁמְךָ מְקַוֶּה: טָהוֹר, יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ קָרְ֒בָה, יָגַֽעְנוּ וְלֺא הֽוּנַח־לָֽנוּ: רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יִכְבְּ֒שׁוּ אֶת־כַּעַסְ֒ךָ מֵעָלֵֽינוּ: אָנָּא שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ וְרַחֵם סְגֻלָּה אֲשֶׁר בָּחָֽרְתָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Strangers say: there is no hope or expectation [for us.] Be gracious to the people who place their hope in Your Name. Pure One, bring our deliverance near; we are weary and no relief is granted us. May Your mercy suppress Your anger from us. We beseech You, turn from Your anger, and have compassion on the treasured people whom You have chosen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Zarim omerim ein tochelet ve tikva.
Chon om leshimcha mekaveh.
Tahor,
yeshuatenu kareva,
yagaenu ve lo hunach lanu.
Rachameicha yichbeshu et ka''ascha mealeinu.
Ana shuv mecharonecha ve rachem segula asher bachareta.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','חֽוּסָה יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ, וְאַל תִּתְּ֒נֵֽנוּ בִּידֵי אַכְזָרִים: לָֽמָּה יֹאמְ֒רוּ הַגּוֹיִם אַיֵּה־נָא אֱלֺהֵיהֶם לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ חֶֽסֶד וְאַל תְּאַחַר: אָנָּא שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹנְ֒ךָ וְרַחֵם סְגֻלָּה אֲשֶׁר בָּחָֽרְתָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, in Your mercy, spare us, do not discard us in the hands of cruel foes. Why should the nations say: Where now is their God? For Your sake, deal kindly with us and do not delay. We beseech You, turn from Your anger, and have compassion on the treasured people whom You have chosen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Chusa Adonai aleinu b''rachameicha,
ve al titenenu bidei achzarim.
Lama yomeru hagoyim ayeh na eloheihem lema''ancha aseh imanu chesed ve al teachar.
Ana shuv mecharonecha ve rachem segula asher bachareta.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','קוֹלֵֽנוּ תִשְׁמַע וְתָחוֹן וְאַל־תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנוּ בְּיַד אֹיְ֒בֵֽינוּ לִמְחוֹת אֶת־שְׁמֵֽנוּ: זְכוֹר אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ, כְּכוֹכְ֒בֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם אַרְבֶּה אֶת־זַרְעֲכֶם וְעַתָּה נִשְׁאַֽרְנוּ מְעַט מֵהַרְבֵּה: וּבְכָל־זֹאת שִׁמְךָ לֺא שָׁכָֽחְנוּ נָא אַל תִּשְׁכָּחֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Hear our voice and be gracious, do not cast us off into the hands of our enemies to obliterate our name. Remember what You have sworn to our fathers: Like the stars of the heavens will I multiply your descendants, and now, we are left only a few out of many. And yet despite all this, we have not forgotten Your Name; please, do not forget us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Kolenu tishma ve tachon ve al titeshenu b''yad oyeveinu limchot et shemenu.
Zechor asher nishbaeta la''avoteinu,
k''chochevei hashamayim arbeh et zarachem ve atah nisharenu meat meharbeh.
Uvechol zot shimcha lo shachachenu na al tishkachenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','עָזְ֒רֵֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ עַל־דְּבַר כְּבוֹד־שְׁמֶֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ וְכַפֵּר עַל־חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Help us, God of our deliverance for the sake of the glory of Your Name; save us and atone our sins for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Azerenu Elohei yishenu al devar k''vod shemecha ve hatzilenu ve chaper al chatoteinu lema''an shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שׁוּב מֵחֲרוֹן אַפֶּֽךָ וְהִנָּחֵם עַל־הָרָעָה לְעַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Adonoy, God of Israel, turn from Your fierce anger, and let Your mind be changed concerning the evil intended for Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael shuv mecharon apecha ve hinachem al hara''a leamecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאַל יֹאבַד יִשְׂרָאֵל הָאֹמְ֒רִים שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of Israel, guard the remnant of Israel, and let not Israel perish, who say, "Hear Israel."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Shomer Yisrael shemor she''erit Yisrael ve al yovad Yisrael haomerim shema Yisrael.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי אֶחָד שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם אֶחָד וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי אֶחָד הַמְ֒יַחֲדִים שִׁמְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of the unique nation, guard the remnant of the unique people, and let not the unique nation perish, who proclaim the Oneness of Your Name, [saying:] Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Shomer goy echad shemor she''erit am echad ve al yovad goy echad hameyachadim shimcha Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם קָדוֹשׁ וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ הַמְ֒שַׁלְּ֒שִׁים בְּשָׁלשׁ קְדֻשּׁוֹת לְקָדוֹשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Guardian of the holy nation, guard the remnant of the holy people and let not the holy nation perish who repeat the threefold sanctification to the Holy One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Shomer goy kadosh shemor she''erit am kadosh ve al yovad goy kadosh hameshaleshim b''shalsh k''dushot lekadosh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','מִתְרַצֶּה בְּרַחֲמִים וּמִתְפַּיֵּס בְּתַחֲנוּנִים הִתְרַצֶּה וְהִתְפַּיֵּס לְדוֹר עָנִי כִּי אֵין עוֹזֵר: אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','You Who are appeased by pleas for mercy, and conciliated by supplications, be appeased and conciliated to an afflicted generation, for there is none else to help. Our Father, our King! be gracious to us and answer us for we have no [good] deeds, deal with us charitably and kindly and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Mitratzeh b''rachamim umitpayes b''tachanunim hitratzeh ve hitpayes ledor ani ki ein ozer.
Avinu malkenu chanenu va''anenu ki ein banu ma''asim aseh imanu tzedaka vachesed ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ לֺא נֵדַע מַה נַּעֲשֶׂה כִּי עָלֶֽיךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ: זְכֹר רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: יְהִי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר יִחַֽלְנוּ לָךְ: אַל תִּזְכָּר לָֽנוּ עֲוֹנוֹת רִאשׁוֹנִים מַהֵר יְקַדְּ֒מֽוּנוּ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ כִּי דַלּֽוֹנוּ מְאֹד: עֶזְרֵֽנוּ בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה עֹשֵׂה שָׁמַֽיִם וְאָֽרֶץ: חָנֵּֽנוּ יְהֹוָה חָנֵּֽנוּ כִּי־רַב שָׂבַֽעְנוּ בוּז: בְּרֺֽגֶז רַחֵם תִּזְכּוֹר: בְּרֹֽגֶז עַקֵדָה תִּזְכּוֹר, בְּרֹֽגֶז תְּמִימוֹת תִּזְכּוֹר: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה, הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: כִּי הוּא יָדַע יִצְרֵֽנוּ זָכוּר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ: עָזְ֒רֵֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ עַל־דְּבַר כְּבוֹד־שְׁמֶֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ וְכַפֵּר עַל־חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','As for us, we know not what to do; but our eyes are upon You. Remember Your mercies, Adonoy, and kindnesses for they are from the beginning of the world. Adonoy! may Your kindness be upon us, as we have waited for You. Remember not the sins of our ancestors; let Your mercy come swiftly toward us, for we have been brought very low. Help us for the Name of Adonoy Creator of Heaven and earth. Be gracious to us, Adonoy, be gracious to us for we are saturated with humiliation. [Even] in anger remember to have compassion. [Even] in anger remember the binding of Isaac. Even in anger remember the uprightness of Jacob Adonoy deliver [us] the King will answer us on the day we call. For He knows of what we are made; He is mindful that we are but dust. Help us, God of our deliverance, for the sake of the glory of Your Name; save us and atone our sins, for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Va''anachenu lo neda mah na''aseh ki aleicha eineinu.
Zechor rachameicha Adonai vachasadeicha ki meolam hema.
Yehi chasdecha Adonai aleinu ka''asher yichalenu lach.
Al tizkar lanu avonot rishonim maher yekademunu rachameicha ki dalonu meod.
Ezrenu b''shem Adonai oseh shamayim ve aretz.
Chanenu Adonai chanenu ki rav savaenu vuz.
B''rogez rachem tizkor.
B''rogez akeda tizkor,
b''rogez temimot tizkor.
Adonai hoshia,
hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.
Ki hu yada yitzrenu zachur ki afar anachenu.
Azerenu Elohei yishenu al devar k''vod shemecha ve hatzilenu ve chaper al chatoteinu lema''an shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','ש"ץ אומר חצי קדיש:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','The Chazzan recites the Half Kaddish','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','transliteration','Le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','he','אשרי ובא לציון. כשמכריזים דבר יש להכריז קודם שיתחיל החזן אשרי (מגן אברהם סי'' קלב)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-for-monday-thursday','en','On days when the Torah is not read continue with Ashrei.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, For Monday & Thursday'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','אַשְׁרֵי יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ עוֹד יְהַלְ֒לֽוּךָ סֶּֽלָה: אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּֽכָה לּוֹ אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיְהֹוָה אֱלֺהָיו: תְּהִלָּה לְדָוִד אֲרוֹמִמְךָ אֱלוֹהַי הַמֶּֽלֶךְ וַאֲבָרְ֒כָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: בְּכָל־יוֹם אֲבָרְ֒כֶֽךָ וַאֲהַלְ֒לָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד וְלִגְ֒דֻלָּתוֹ אֵין חֵֽקֶר: דּוֹר לְדוֹר יְשַׁבַּח מַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּגְ֒בוּרֹתֶֽיךָ יַגִּֽידוּ: הֲדַר כְּבוֹד הוֹדֶֽךָ וְדִבְרֵי נִפְלְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ אָשִֽׂיחָה: וֶעֱזוּז נוֹרְ֒אוֹתֶֽיךָ יֹאמֵֽרוּ וּגְ֒דֻלָּתְ֒ךָ אֲסַפְּ֒רֶֽנָּה: זֵֽכֶר רַב־טוּבְ֒ךָ יַבִּֽיעוּ וְצִדְ֒קָתְ֒ךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וּגְ֒דָל־חָֽסֶד: טוֹב־יְהֹוָה לַכֹּל וְרַחֲמָיו עַל־כָּל־מַעֲשָׂיו: יוֹדֽוּךָ יְהֹוָה כָּל־מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְבָרְ֒כֽוּכָה: כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ יֹאמֵֽרוּ וּגְ֒בוּרָתְ֒ךָ יְדַבֵּֽרוּ: לְהוֹדִֽיעַ לִבְנֵי הָאָדָם גְּבוּרֹתָיו וּכְ֒בוֹד הֲדַר מַלְכוּתוֹ: מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ מַלְכוּת כָּל־עֹלָמִים וּמֶמְשַׁלְתְּ֒ךָ בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדֹר: סוֹמֵךְ יְהֹוָה לְכָל־הַנֹּפְ֒לִים וְזוֹקֵף לְכָל־הַכְּ֒פוּפִים: עֵינֵי־כֹל אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּֽרוּ וְאַתָּה נוֹתֵן־לָהֶם אֶת־אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: פּוֹתֵֽחַ אֶת־יָדֶֽךָ וּמַשְׂבִּֽיעַ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן: צַדִּיק יְהֹוָה בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו וְחָסִיד בְּכָל־מַעֲשָׂיו: קָרוֹב יְהֹוָה לְכָל־קֹרְ֒אָיו לְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָאֻֽהוּ בֶאֱמֶת: רְצוֹן־יְרֵאָיו יַעֲשֶׂה וְאֶת־שַׁוְעָתָם יִשְׁמַע וְיוֹשִׁיעֵם: שׁוֹמֵר יְהֹוָה אֶת־כָּל־אֹהֲבָיו וְאֵת כָּל־הָרְ֒שָׁעִים יַשְׁמִיד: תְּהִלַּת יְהֹוָה יְדַבֶּר פִּי וִיבָרֵךְ כָּל־בָּשָׂר שֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ נְבָרֵךְ יָהּ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Fortunate are those who dwell in Your house; may they continue to praise You, Selah. Fortunate is the people whose lot is thus; Fortunate is the people for whom Adonoy is their God. A praise by David! I will exalt You, my God, the King, and bless Your Name forever and ever. Every day I will bless You and extol Your Name forever and ever. Adonoy is great and highly extolled, and His greatness is unfathomable. One generation to another will praise Your works and Your mighty acts they will declare. The splendor of Your glorious majesty, and the words of Your wonders I will speak. Of Your awesome might, they will speak, and Your greatness I will recount. Mention of Your bountifulness they will express, and in Your righteousness joyfully exult. Adonoy is gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and great in kindliness. Adonoy is good to all, His mercy encompasses all His works. All Your works will thank You, Adonoy, and Your pious ones will bless You. Of the honor of Your kingship, they will speak and Your might they will declare. To reveal to men His mighty acts, and the glorious splendor of His kingship. Your kingship is the kingship for all times, and Your dominion is in every generation. Adonoy supports all the fallen, and straightens all the bent. The eyes of all look expectantly to You, and You give them their food at its proper time. You open Your hand and satisfy the desire of every living being. Adonoy is just in all His ways, and benevolent in all His deeds. Adonoy is near to all who call upon Him, to all who call upon Him in truth. The will of those who fear Him He fulfills; He hears their cry and delivers them. Adonoy watches over all those who love Him, and will destroy all the wicked. Praise of Adonoy, my mouth will declare, and all flesh will bless His holy Name forever and ever. And we will bless God from now on forever. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Ashrei yoshevei veitecha od yehalelucha sela.
Ashrei ha''am shekacha lo ashrei ha''am sheyadonai elohav.
Tehila leDavid aromimcha Elohai hamelech va''avarecha shimcha le''olam vaed.
B''chol yom avarechecha va''ahalela shimcha le''olam vaed.
Gadol Adonai umehulal meod ve ligdulato ein cheker.
Dor ledor yeshabach ma''aseicha ugevuroteicha yagidu.
Hadar k''vod hodecha ve divrei nifleoteicha asicha.
Ve''ezuz noreoteicha yomeru ugedulatecha asaperena.
Zecher rav tuvecha yabiu ve tzidkatecha yeranenu.
Chanun ve rachum Adonai erech apayim ugedal chased.
Tov Adonai lakol ve rachamav al kol ma''asav.
Yoducha Adonai kol ma''aseicha vachasideicha yevarechucha.
K''vod malchutecha yomeru ugevuratecha yedaberu.
Lehodia livnei ha''adam gevurotav uchevod hadar malchuto.
Malchutecha malchut kol olamim umemshaltecha b''chol dor vador.
Somech Adonai lechol hanofelim ve zokef lechol hakefufim.
Einei chol eleicha yesaberu ve atah noten lahem et ochlam b''ito.
Poteach et yadecha umasbia lechol chai ratzon.
Tzadik Adonai b''chol derachav ve chasid b''chol ma''asav.
Karov Adonai lechol koreav lechol asher yikrauhu ve''emet.
Retzon yereav ya''aseh ve et shavatam yishma ve yoshiem.
Shomer Adonai et kol ohavav ve et kol hareshaim yashmid.
Tehilat Adonai yedaber pi vivarech kol basar shem kodsho le''olam vaed.
Va''anachenu nevarech yah meatah ve ad olam haleluyah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','אלו ימים שאין אומרים בהם למנצח ואל ארך אפים. ר"ח חנוכה ופורים ערב פסח וערב יו"כ ותשעה באב. והוא הדין ביום י"ד וט"ו באדר ראשון. גם אין אומרים אותם בבית האבל דכללא הוא דאא"א ולמנצח דינם שוה. (דה"ח)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Psalm 20 is omitted on the following days: Rosh Chodesh, the day before Yom Kippur, Chanukah, both days of Purim, the day before Passover, the intermediate days of the Festivals (Chol HaMoed), and Tisha b''Av. It is also omitted when prayers are recited in the house of a mourner, the entire month of Nisssan, Pesach Sheni (14th of Iyar) Lag-b''omer, from Rosh Codesh Sivan through the twelfth of the month i.e., 5 days after Shavuoth, the Fifteenth of av, from Erev Yom Kippur until the end of Tishre, the Fifteenth of Shevat, when there is a circumcision in the Synagogue, or when a bride groom during the seven days of his wedding celebration is present.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','מה שתקנו לאומרו בסוף התפלה מפני שאומר במדרש תלים אמר ר'' שמעון בר אבא אתה מוצא י"ח מזמורים מראש הספר ועד פסוק זה ואשרי האיש ולמה רגשו גוים חד הוא כנגד י"ח ברכות שאדם מתפלל בכל יום. אדם אומר לחבירו תתעני צלותך כך דוד המלך לאחר ששר י"ח שירות ותושבחות אמר יענך ה'' ביום צרה והכי איתא בירושלמי. ובשבתות ובימים טובים אין אומרים אותו מפני שהוא מזמור של תחנה וגם הוא מתחיל יענך ה'' ביום צרה ושבתות וימים טובים אינם ימי צרה אלא ימי שמחה. (אבודרהם)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','According to Rabbi S.R. Hirsch, this psalm is addressed to David by the people of Israel. It is a testimonial of trust that the people have in the Divinely-appointed king, who is accustomed to victory and triumph. At the same time, it proclaims the eternal truth that the victories which our king wins for our people are to be attributed not to his bravery, nor to his sword, nor to his soldiers, but solely to his relationship with God, His Sanctuary, and His Law.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ מִזְמוֹר לְדָוִד: יַעַנְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה בְּיוֹם צָרָה יְשַׂגֶּבְ֒ךָ שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: יִשְׁלַח עֶזְרְךָ מִקֹּֽדֶשׁ וּמִצִּיּוֹן יִסְעָדֶֽךָּ: יִזְכֹּר כָּל מִנְחֹתֶֽיךָ וְעוֹלָתְ֒ךָ יְדַשְּׁ֒נֶה סֶּֽלָה: יִתֶּן לְךָ כִלְ֒בָבֶֽךָ וְכָל עֲצָתְ֒ךָ יְמַלֵּא: נְרַנְּ֒נָה בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ וּבְ֒שֵׁם אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ נִדְגֹּל יְמַלֵּא יְהֹוָה כָּל מִשְׁאֲלוֹתֶֽיךָ: עַתָּה יָדַֽעְתִּי כִּי הוֹשִֽׁיעַ יְהֹוָה מְשִׁיחוֹ יַעֲנֵֽהוּ מִשְּׁ֒מֵי קָדְשׁוֹ בִּגְ֒בוּרוֹת יֵֽשַׁע יְמִינוֹ: אֵֽלֶּה בָרֶֽכֶב וְאֵֽלֶּה בַסּוּסִים וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ נַזְכִּיר: הֵֽמָּה כָּרְ֒עוּ וְנָפָֽלוּ וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ קַֽמְנוּ וַנִּתְעוֹדָד: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','To Him Who grants victory, a Psalm of David May Adonoy answer you on the day of distress; May the Name of Jacob''s God fortify you. May He send your help from the Sanctuary, and support you from Zion. May He remember all your meal-offerings, and accept your burnt sacrifices, Selah. May He grant you what your heart desires, and fulfill all your plans. We will sing at Your deliverance, and in the Name of our God, raise our banners; May Adonoy fulfill all your wishes. Now I know that Adonoy has delivered His anointed one, He will answer him from His holy heavens with the mighty deliverance of His right hand. Some [rely] upon chariots and some upon horses, but as for us, upon the Name of Adonoy, our God, we call. They have bowed down and fallen, but we have risen and stand firm. Adonoy, deliver [us], the King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Lamnatzeach mizmor leDavid.
Ya''ancha Adonai b''yom tzara yesagevcha shem Elohei Yaakov.
Yishlach ezrecha mikodesh umitziyon yisadeka.
Yizkor kol minchoteicha ve olatecha yedasheneh sela.
Yiten lecha chilvavecha ve chol atzatecha yemaleh.
Neranena bishuatecha uveshem Eloheinu nidgol yemaleh Adonai kol mishaloteicha.
Atah yadaeti ki hoshia Adonai meshicho ya''anehu mishemei kodsho bigvurot yesha yemino.
Eleh varechev ve eleh vasusim va''anachenu b''shem Adonai Eloheinu nazkir.
Hema kareu ve nafalu va''anachenu kamenu vanitodad.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','מה שתקנו סדר קדושה בסוף התפלה בעבור עמי הארץ המאחרים לבא לתפלה שלא יפסידו שמיעת הקדושה. דאמרינן בשלהי סוטה אמאי קאי עלמא אסדרא דקדושה ואיהא שמיה רבה דאגדתא. ולכך תקנו לתרגם סדר קדושה זה כדי שיבינו עמי הארץ שאין מכירים לדבר בלשון הקדש אלא בלשון תרגום שהיו רגילין לדבר בו באותו זמן. (אבודרהם)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','This portion, known as Kedushas d''Sidra, was introduced at the conclusion of the morning service to accomodate those who came to the synagogue too late to hear the Kedushah in Shemoneh Esrei. The Talmud (Maseches Sotah 49a) declares that the world is preserved solely by virtue of this Kedushah, and by the virtue of our answering, "May His great Name," which is part of the Kaddish recited following the study of the Aggadah. Because of its importance, a vernacular translation in Aramaic was added, so that even those ignorant of Hebrew would understand the sacred words.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּבָא לְצִיּוֹן גּוֹאֵל וּלְ֒שָׁבֵי פֶֽשַׁע בְּיַעֲקֹב נְאֻם יְהֹוָה: וַאֲנִי זֹאת בְּרִיתִי אֹתָם אָמַר יְהֹוָה רוּחִי אֲשֶׁר עָלֶֽיךָ וּדְ֒בָרַי אֲשֶׁר שַֽׂמְתִּי בְּפִֽיךָ לֺא יָמֽוּשׁוּ מִפִּֽיךָ וּמִפִּי זַרְעֲךָ וּמִפִּי זֶֽרַע זַרְעֲךָ אָמַר יְהֹוָה מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','The Redeemer shall come to Zion and to those of Jacob who repent from sin, says Adonoy. As for Me, this is My covenant with them, said Adonoy: My spirit which is upon you, and My words which I have put in your mouth shall not depart from your mouth, nor from the mouth of your children, nor from the mouth of your children''s children, said Adonoy— from now to eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Uva letziyon goel uleshavei fesha b''Yaakov neum Adonai.
Va''ani zot b''riti otam amar Adonai ruchi asher aleicha udevarai asher sameti b''ficha lo yamushu mipicha umipi zaracha umipi zera zaracha amar Adonai meatah ve ad olam.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וְאַתָּה קָדוֹשׁ יוֹשֵׁב תְּהִלּוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל: וְקָרָא זֶה אֶל זֶה וְאָמַר קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת מְלֺא כָל הָאָֽרֶץ כְּבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','(This next section is the actual Kedushah d''Sidra) And You, Holy One, are enthroned upon the praises of Israel. And [the angels] call one to another and say: Holy, holy, holy is Adonoy of Hosts: the fullness of all the earth is His glory."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Ve atah kadosh yoshev tehilot Yisrael.
Ve kara zeh el zeh ve amar kadosh kadosh kadosh Adonai tzevaot melo chol ha''aretz k''vodo.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּמְ֒קַבְּ֒לִין דֵּין מִן דֵּין וְאָמְ֒רִין קַדִּישׁ בִּשְׁ֒מֵי מְרוֹמָא עִלָּאָה בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ עַל אַרְעָא עוֹבַד גְּבוּרְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת, מַלְיָא כָל אַרְעָא זִיו יְקָרֵהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And they receive [sanction] one from another, and say, Holy in the highest heights of heaven, the abode of His Divine Presence; holy upon earth, the work of His mighty power; holy forever and to all eternity— is Adonoy of hosts; the whole earth is filled with the radiance of His glory.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Umekabelin dein min dein ve amerin kadish bishmei meroma ila''a beit shechineteh kadish al ara ovad gevureteh kadish lealam ulealemei alemaya Adonai tzevaot,
malya chol ara ziv yekareh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וַתִּשָּׂאֵֽנִי רֽוּחַ וָאֶשְׁמַע אַחֲרַי קוֹל רַֽעַשׁ גָּדוֹל בָּרוּךְ כְּבוֹד יְהֹוָה מִמְּ֒קוֹמוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And a wind lifted me; and I heard behind me the sound of a great rushing; Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from His place.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Vatisaeni ruach vaeshma acharai kol ra''ash gadol baruch k''vod Adonai mimekomo.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּנְ֒טָלַתְנִי רוּחָא וּשְׁמָעִית בַּתְרַי קָל זִֽיעַ סַגִּיא דִּמְ֒שַׁבְּ֒חִין וְאָמְ֒רִין בְּרִיךְ יְקָרָא דַיהוָֹה מֵאֲתַר בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And a wind lifted me and I heard behind me a sound of a great rushing of those who uttered praises and said, ‘Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from the place, the abode of His Divine Presence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Unetalatni rucha ushemait batrai kal zia sagi dimshabechin ve amerin b''rich yekara da''adonai meatar beit shechineteh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה יִמְלֺךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy will reign forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה מַלְכוּתֵהּ קָאֵים לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy, His kingdom is established forever and to all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Adonai malchuteh kaeim lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שָׁמְ֒רָה זֹאת לְעֹלָם לְיֵֽצֶר מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת לְבַב עַמֶּֽךָ וְהָכֵן לְבָבָם אֵלֶֽיךָ: וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֺא יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֺא יָעִיר כָּל חֲמָתוֹ: כִּי אַתָּה אֲדֹנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב חֶֽסֶד לְכָל קֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ: צִדְ֒קָתְ֒ךָ צֶֽדֶק לְעוֹלָם וְתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ אֱמֶת: תִּתֵּן אֱמֶת לְיַעֲקֹב חֶֽסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ מִֽימֵי קֶֽדֶם: בָּרוּךְ אֲדֹנָי יוֹם יוֹם יַעֲמָס לָֽנוּ הָאֵל יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגָּב לָֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Adonoy, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, our fathers, keep this forever as the intention of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts to You. And He, the merciful One, atones iniquity and does not destroy; He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You. Your righteousness is everlasting and Your Torah is truth. You will grant truth to Jacob, kindliness to Abraham, as You have sworn to our fathers from the days of old. Blessed is my Master day by day; He loads us [with blessings], the Almighty Who is our deliverance, forever. Adonoy of Hosts is with us a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah. Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Avraham Yitzchak ve Yisrael avoteinu shamera zot le''olam leyetzer machshevot levav amecha ve hachen levavam eleicha.
Ve hu rachum yechaper avon ve lo yashchit ve hirba lehashiv apo ve lo yair kol chamato.
Ki atah adonai tov ve salach ve rav chesed lechol kore''eicha.
Tzidkatecha tzedek le''olam ve toratecha emet.
Titen emet leYaakov chesed leAvraham asher nishbaeta la''avoteinu mimei kedem.
Baruch adonai yom yom ya''amas lanu hael yeshuatenu sela.
Adonai tzevaot imanu misgav lanu Elohei Yaakov sela.
Adonai tzevaot ashrei adam boteach bach.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בָּרוּךְ הוּא אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבְּ֒רָאָֽנוּ לִכְ֒בוֹדוֹ וְהִבְדִּילָֽנוּ מִן הַתּוֹעִים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ תּוֹרַת אֱמֶת וְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם נָטַע בְּתוֹכֵֽנוּ הוּא יִפְתַּח לִבֵּֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָשֵׂם בְּלִבֵּֽנוּ אַהֲבָתוֹ וְיִרְאָתוֹ וְלַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנוֹ וּלְ֒עָבְ֒דוֹ בְּלֵבָב שָׁלֵם לְמַֽעַן לֺא נִיגַע לָרִיק וְלֺא נֵלֵד לַבֶּהָלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Blessed is He, our God, Who created us for His glory, and set us apart from those who go astray; and gave us the Torah of truth, and eternal life He implanted within us. May He open our heart to His Torah, and instill in our heart love and awe of Him, to do His will and serve Him with a perfect heart, so that we shall not labor in vain nor bring forth that which causes dismay.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Baruch hu Eloheinu shebera''anu lichvodo ve hivdilanu min hatoim ve natan lanu torat emet ve chayei olam nata b''tochenu hu yiftach libenu b''torato ve yasem b''libenu ahavato ve yirato ve la''asot retzono uleavedo b''levav shalem lema''an lo niga larik ve lo neled labehala.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁנִּשְׁמֹר חֻקֶּֽיךָ בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְנִזְכֶּה וְנִחְיֶה וְנִרְאֶה וְנִירַשׁ טוֹבָה וּבְ֒רָכָה לִשְׁ֒נֵי יְמוֹת הַמָּשִֽׁיחַ וּלְ֒חַיֵּי הָעוֹלָם הַבָּא: לְמַֽעַן יְזַמֶּרְ֒ךָ כָבוֹד וְלֺא יִדֹּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי לְעוֹלָם אוֹדֶֽךָּ: בָּרוּךְ הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר יִבְטַח בַּיהוָֹה וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה מִבְטַחוֹ: בִּטְ֒חוּ בַיהוָֹה עֲדֵי עַד כִּי בְּיָהּ יְהֹוָה צוּר עוֹלָמִים: וְיִבְטְחוּ בְךָ יוֹדְ֒עֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ כִּי לֺא עָזַֽבְתָּ דֹרְ֒שֶֽׁיךָ יְהֹוָה: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַֽעַן צִדְקוֹ יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, that we keep Your statutes in this world, and [thus] be privileged to live and behold, and to inherit the goodness and blessing of the Messianic days, and in the life of the World to Come. In order that my soul sing to You and not be stilled; Adonoy, my God, forever will I thank You. Blessed is the man who trusts in Adonoy, so that Adonoy is his security. Trust in Adonoy until the end of days, for in God, Adonoy, is the strength of the worlds. And they will trust in You— those who know your Name, for You have never forsaken those who seek You, Adonoy. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Eloheinu velohei avoteinu shenishmor chukeicha baolam hazeh ve nizkeh ve nichyeh ve nireh ve nirash tova uveracha lishnei yemot hamashiach ulechayei ha''olam haba.
Lema''an yezamercha chavod ve lo yidom Adonai Elohai le''olam odeka.
Baruch hagever asher yivtach ba''adonai ve haya Adonai mivtacho.
Bitchu va''adonai adei ad ki b''yah Adonai tzur olamim.
Ve yivtechu ve cha yode''ei shemecha ki lo azaveta doresheicha Adonai.
Adonai chafetz lema''an tzidko yagdil torah ve yadir.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','(יְהֺוָה אֲדוֹנֵֽינוּ, מָה אַדִּיר שִׁמְךָ בְּכָל הָאָֽרֶץ: חִזְ֒קוּ וְיַאֲמֵץ לְבַבְ֒כֶם כָּל הַמְ֒יַחֲלִים לַיהֹוָה:)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','(Adonoy, our Master, how mighty is Your Name over all the earth. Be strong and take courage, all who wait for Adonoy.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','(Adonai adoneinu,
ma adir shimcha b''chol ha''aretz.
Chizku ve ya''ametz levavchem kol hameyachalim laAdonai)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','כל ימות השנה כשאין מוסף אומר הש"ץ קדיש תתקבל אחר ובא לציון. אבל כשיש מוסף אומר הש"ץ רק חצי קדיש על סדר קדושה ומתפללין מוסף. ובר"ח חולצין התפילין קודם תפלת מוסף.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','On Rosh Chodesh the Chazzan recites the half-Kaddish, the Tefillin are then removed and the congregation says the Musaf Amidah; and on Chol Hamoed the Chazzan recites the half-Kaddish, and the congregation says the Mussaf Amidah. On regular weekdays the Chazzan recites the following Kaddish:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','תִּתְקַבֵּל צְלוֹתְ֒הוֹן וּבָעוּתְ֒הוֹן דְּכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דִּי בִשְׁ֒מַיָּא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May there be acceptance of the prayers and supplications of the entire House of Israel before their Father in heaven. And say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Titkabel tzelotehon uvautehon dechal beit Yisrael kodam avuhon di vishmaya ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בשני ובחמישי ושאר ימים שמוציאין ספר תורה אומרים יהללו כשמחזירים הס"ת למקומו. ואומר החזן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','On Mondays, Thursdays and other days when the Torah is read, as the Sefer Torah is returned to the Ark the Chazzan takes the Torah and says:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','יְהַלְ֒לוּ אֶת־שֵׁם יְהֹוָה כִּי־נִשְׂגָּב שְׁמוֹ לְבַדּוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','They will praise the Name of Adonoy for His Name alone is exalted.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Yehalelu et shem Adonai ki nisgav shemo levado.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','קהל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','Chazzan and congregation:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','הוֹדוֹ עַל־אֶֽרֶץ וְשָׁמָֽיִם: וַיָּֽרֶם קֶֽרֶן לְעַמּוֹ תְּהִלָּה לְכָל־חֲסִידָיו לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַם קְרֹבוֹ הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','His majesty is over the earth and the skies. He will raise the might of His people, [which is] praise for all His pious ones, for the children of Israel, the people near to Him. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Hodo al eretz ve shamayim.
Vayarem keren leamo tehila lechol chasidav livnei Yisrael am k''rovo haleluyah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר לַיהוָֹה הָאָֽרֶץ וּמְ֒לוֹאָהּ תֵּבֵל וְיֽשְׁ֒בֵי בָהּ: כִּי־הוּא עַל־יַמִּים יְסָדָהּ וְעַל־נְהָרוֹת יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ: מִי־יַעֲלֶה בְהַר־יְהֹוָה וּמִי יָקוּם בִּמְ֒קוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ: נְקִי כַפַּֽיִם וּבַר־לֵבָב אֲשֶׁר לֺא־נָשָׂא לַשָּׁוְא נַפְשִׁי וְלֺא נִשְׁבַּע לְמִרְמָה: יִשָּׂא בְרָכָה מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה וּצְ֒דָקָה מֵאֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעוֹ: זֶה דּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שָׁיו מְבַקְ֒שֵׁי פָנֶֽיךָ יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וְהִנָּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה עִזּוּז וְגִבּוֹר יְהֹוָה גִּבּוֹר מִלְחָמָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי הוּא זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת הוּא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','A psalm of David: the earth is Adonoy''s and the fullness thereof, the inhabited world and those who dwell in it. For He founded it upon the seas, and established it upon rivers. Who may ascend the mountain of Adonoy, and who may stand in the place of His holiness? The clean of hands and the pure of heart, who has not borne My soul in vain, and has not sworn deceitfully. He will bear Adonoy''s blessing and righteousness from the God of his deliverance. This is the generation of those who seek Him, and seekers of Your Presence, [God of] Jacob, selah. Lift up your heads, gates, and be uplifted [you] entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is this King of Glory? Adonoy, strong and mighty; Adonoy, the Mighty One in battle. Lift up your heads, gates, and lift, entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is He, this King of Glory? Adonoy of hosts, He is the King of Glory, selah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','LeDavid mizmor laAdonai ha''aretz umeloah tevel ve yshevei vah.
Ki hu al yamim yesadah ve al neharot yechoneneha.
Mi ya''aleh ve har Adonai umi yakum bimkom kodsho.
Neki chapayim uvar levav asher lo nasa lashav nafshi ve lo nishba lemirma.
Yisa ve racha me''et Adonai utzedaka meElohei yisho.
Zeh dor doreshav mevakshei faneicha Yaakov sela.
Seu shearim rasheichem ve hinaseu pitchei olam ve yavo melech hakavod.
Mi zeh melech hakavod Adonai izuz ve gibor Adonai gibor milchama.
Seu shearim rasheichem useu pitchei olam ve yavo melech hakavod.
Mi hu zeh melech hakavod Adonai tzevaot hu melech hakavod sela.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','בשעת הכנסת ס"ת להיכל אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','As the Torah is returned to the Ark the following is said:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','he','וּבְ֒נֻחֹה יֹאמַר שׁוּבָה יְהֹוָה רִבְ֒בוֹת אַלְ֒פֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל: קוּמָה יְהֹוָה לִמְ֒נוּחָתֶֽךָ אַתָּה וַאֲרוֹן עֻזֶּֽךָ: כֹּהֲנֶֽיךָ יִלְבְּ֒שׁוּ צֶֽדֶק וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: בַּעֲבוּר דָּוִד עַבְדֶּֽךָ אַל תָּשֵׁב פְּנֵי מְשִׁיחֶֽךָ: כִּי לֶֽקַח טוֹב נָתַֽתִּי לָכֶם תּוֹרָתִי אַל תַּעֲזֹֽבוּ: עֵץ חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ וְתוֹמְ֒כֶֽיהָ מְאֻשָּׁר: דְּרָכֶֽיהָ דַּרְ֒כֵי נֹֽעַם וְכָל נְתִיבוֹתֶֽיהָ שָׁלוֹם: הֲשִׁיבֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֵלֶֽיךָ וְנָשׁוּבָה חַדֵּשׁ יָמֵֽינוּ כְּקֶֽדֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','en','And when it rested, he would say: Return, Adonoy, to the myriads and thousands of Israel. Arise, Adonoy unto Your resting place, You and the Ark of Your strength. Let Your priests clothe themselves in righteousness, and let Your devoted ones sing in joy. For the sake of David, Your servant, do not reject Your anointed. For I have given you good instruction, do not forsake My Torah. It is a tree of life to those who grasp it, and those who support it are fortunate. Its ways are ways of pleasantness and all its paths are peace. Cause us to return to you, Adonoy, and we shall return; renew our days as of old.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-ashrei','transliteration','Uvenuchoh yomar shuva Adonai rivvot alfei Yisrael.
Kuma Adonai limnuchatecha atah va''aron uzecha.
Kohaneicha yilbeshu tzedek vachasideicha yeranenu.
Ba''avur David avdecha al tashev penei meshichecha.
Ki lekach tov natati lachem torati al ta''azovu.
Etz chayim hi lamachazikim bah ve tomecheiha meushar.
Deracheiha darchei noam ve chol netivoteiha shalom.
Hashivenu Adonai eleicha ve nashuva chadesh yameinu k''kedem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Ashrei'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','נהגו לומר בכל ימי השבוע השיר שהיו הלוים אומרים במקדש. ומקורו במס'' סופרים (מס'' סופרים י"ח, א) לפיכך נהגו העם לומר מזמורים בעונתן. דתנינן תמן (תמיד פ"ז מ"ד) השיר שהיו הלוים אומרים בביהמ"ק וכו''. שכל המזכיר פסוק בעונתו מעלה עליו כאילו בונה מזבח חדש ומקריב עליו קרבן. ע"כ. (עץ יוסף)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','The custom of reciting a different psalm each day of the week originated in the Temple. The Mishnah (Maseches Tamid 7:4) describes the psalms which were chanted by the Levites each day during the service.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בראשון בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Sunday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם רִאשׁוֹן בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the first day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom rishon bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר לַיהוָֹה הָאָֽרֶץ וּמְ֒לוֹאָהּ תֵּבֵל וְיֽשְׁ֒בֵי בָהּ: כִּי הוּא עַל יַמִּים יְסָדָהּ וְעַל נְהָרוֹת יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ: מִי יַעֲלֶה בְהַר יְהֹוָה וּמִי יָקוּם בִּמְ֒קוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ: נְקִי כַפַּֽיִם וּבַר לֵבָב אֲשֶׁר לֺא נָשָׂא לַשָּׁוְא נַפְשִׁי וְלֺא נִשְׁבַּע לְמִרְמָה: יִשָּׂא בְרָכָה מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה וּצְ֒דָקָה מֵאֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעוֹ: זֶה דּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שָׁיו מְבַקְ֒שֵׁי פָנֶֽיךָ יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וְהִנָּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה עִזּוּז וְגִבּוֹר יְהֹוָה גִּבּוֹר מִלְחָמָה: שְׂאוּ שְׁעָרִים רָאשֵׁיכֶם וּשְׂ֒אוּ פִּתְ֒חֵי עוֹלָם וְיָבוֹא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד: מִי הוּא זֶה מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת הוּא מֶֽלֶךְ הַכָּבוֹד סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A psalm of David: the earth is Adonoy''s and the fullness thereof, the inhabited world and those who dwell in it. For He founded it upon the seas, and established it upon rivers. Who may ascend the mountain of Adonoy, and who may stand in the place of His holiness? The clean of hands and the pure of heart, who has not borne My soul in vain, and has not sworn deceitfully. He will bear Adonoy''s blessing and righteousness from the God of his deliverance. This is the generation of those who seek Him, the seekers of Your Presence, [God of] Jacob, Selah. Lift up your heads, gates, and be uplifted [you] entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is this King of Glory? Adonoy, strong and mighty; Adonoy, the Mighty One in battle. Lift up your heads, gates, and lift, entranceways to eternity, so that the King of Glory may enter. Who is He, this King of Glory? Adonoy of hosts, He is the King of Glory, Selah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','LeDavid mizmor laAdonai ha''aretz umeloah tevel ve yshevei vah.
Ki hu al yamim yesadah ve al neharot yechoneneha.
Mi ya''aleh ve har Adonai umi yakum bimkom kodsho.
Neki chapayim uvar levav asher lo nasa lashav nafshi ve lo nishba lemirma.
Yisa ve racha me''et Adonai utzedaka meElohei yisho.
Zeh dor doreshav mevakshei faneicha Yaakov sela.
Seu shearim rasheichem ve hinaseu pitchei olam ve yavo melech hakavod.
Mi zeh melech hakavod Adonai izuz ve gibor Adonai gibor milchama.
Seu shearim rasheichem useu pitchei olam ve yavo melech hakavod.
Mi hu zeh melech hakavod Adonai tzevaot hu melech hakavod sela.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשני בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Monday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שֵׁנִי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the second day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom sheni bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','שִׁיר מִזְמוֹר לִבְנֵי קֹֽרַח: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד בְּעִיר אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ הַר קָדְשׁוֹ: יְפֵה נוֹף מְשׂוֹשׂ כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ הַר צִיּוֹן יַרְכְּתֵי צָפוֹן קִרְיַת מֶֽלֶךְ רָב: אֱלֺהִים בְּאַרְמְנוֹתֶֽיהָ נוֹדַע לְמִשְׂגָּב: כִּי הִנֵּה הַמְּ֒לָכִים נוֹעֲדוּ עָבְ֒רוּ יַחְדָּו: הֵֽמָּה רָאוּ כֵּן תָּמָֽהוּ נִבְהֲלוּ נֶחְפָּֽזוּ: רְעָדָה אֲחָזָֽתַם שָׁם חִיל כַּיּוֹלֵדָה: בְּרֽוּחַ קָדִים תְּשַׁבֵּר אֳנִיּוֹת תַּרְשִׁישׁ: כַּאֲשֶׁר שָׁמַֽעְנוּ כֵּן רָאִֽינוּ בְּעִיר יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת בְּעִיר אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֱלֺהִים יְכוֹנְ֒נֶֽהָ עַד עוֹלָם סֶֽלָה: דִּמִּֽינוּ אֱלֺהִים חַסְדֶּֽךָ בְּקֶֽרֶב הֵיכָלֶֽךָ: כְּשִׁמְךָ אֱלֺהִים כֵּן תְּהִלָּתְ֒ךָ עַל קַצְוֵי אֶֽרֶץ צֶֽדֶק מָלְ֒אָה יְמִינֶֽךָ: יִשְׂמַח הַר צִיּוֹן תָּגֵֽלְנָה בְּנוֹת יְהוּדָה לְמַֽעַן מִשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ: סֹֽבּוּ צִיּוֹן וְהַקִּיפֽוּהָ סִפְ֒רוּ מִגְדָּלֶֽיהָ: שִֽׁיתוּ לִבְּ֒כֶם לְחֵילָה פַּסְּ֒גוּ אַרְמְ֒נוֹתֶֽיהָ לְמַֽעַן תְּסַפְּ֒רוּ לְדוֹר אַחֲרוֹן: כִּי זֶה אֱלֺהִים אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ עוֹלָם וָעֶד הוּא יְנַהֲגֵֽנוּ עַל מוּת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A song, a psalm by the sons of Korach. Adonoy is great and highly extolled in the city of our God, the mountain of His Sanctuary. Beautiful in its panoramic vista, the joy of all the earth is Mount Zion, on the northern extremities (of Jerusalem); the city of the great King. God, in its palaces, has become known as a Stronghold. For behold, the kings assembled, they passed by together. They saw and were astounded, they panicked and fled in haste. Trembling siezed them there, like the pangs of a woman in labor. With an east wind You smashed the ships of Tarshish. As we heard, so we saw in the city of Adonoy of hosts, in the city of our God; may God establish it for eternity, Selah. We hoped, God, for Your lovingkindness in the midst of Your Sanctuary. As Your Name, God, so is Your praise— to the ends of the earth; Your right hand is full of righteousness. Let Mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah exult, because of Your judgments. Rally around Zion and encircle her, count her towers. Consider well her ramparts, raise high her citadels, that you may recount it to future generations. That this is God, our God forever and ever, He will lead us like children.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Shir mizmor livnei korach.
Gadol Adonai umehulal meod b''ir Eloheinu har kodsho.
Yefeh nof mesos kol ha''aretz har tziyon yarketei tzafon kiryat melech rav.
Elohim b''armenoteiha noda lemisgav.
Ki hineh hamelachim noadu averu yachdav.
Hema rau ken tamahu nivhalu nechpazu.
Reada achazatam sham chil kayoleda.
B''ruach kadim teshaber oniyot tarshish.
Ka''asher shamaenu ken rainu b''ir Adonai tzevaot b''ir Eloheinu Elohim yechoneneha ad olam sela.
Diminu Elohim chasdecha b''kerev heichalecha.
K''shimcha Elohim ken tehilatecha al katzvei eretz tzedek malea yeminecha.
Yismach har tziyon tagelena b''not Yehudah lema''an mishpateicha.
Sobu tziyon ve hakifuha sifru migdaleiha.
Shitu libechem lecheila pasegu armenoteiha lema''an tesaperu ledor acharon.
Ki zeh Elohim Eloheinu olam vaed hu yenahagenu al mut.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשלישי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Tuesday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שְׁלִישִׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the third day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom shelishi bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף אֱלֺהִים נִצָּב בַּעֲדַת אֵל בְּקֶֽרֶב אֱלֺהִים יִשְׁפֹּט: עַד מָתַי תִּשְׁפְּטוּ עָֽוֶל וּפְ֒נֵי רְשָׁעִים תִּשְׂ֒אוּ סֶֽלָה: שִׁפְ֒טוּ דָל וְיָתוֹם עָנִי וָרָשׁ הַצְדִּֽיקוּ: פַּלְּ֒טוּ דַל וְאֶבְיוֹן מִיַּד רְשָׁעִים הַצִּֽילוּ: לֺא יָדְ֒עוּ וְלֺא יָבִֽינוּ בַּחֲשֵׁכָה יִתְהַלָּֽכוּ יִמּֽוֹטוּ כָּל מֽוֹסְ֒דֵי אָֽרֶץ: אֲנִי אָמַֽרְתִּי אֱלֺהִים אַתֶּם וּבְ֒נֵי עֶלְיוֹן כֻּלְּ֒כֶם: אָכֵן כְּאָדָם תְּמוּתוּן וּכְ֒אַחַד הַשָּׂרִים תִּפֹּֽלוּ: קוּמָה אֱלֺהִים שָׁפְ֒טָה הָאָרֶץ כִּי אַתָּה תִנְחַל בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','A psalm of Assaf God stands in the congregation of the Almighty, in the midst of the judges He gives judgement. How long will you judge lawlessly and show partiality to the wicked forever? Render justice to the lowly and the orphan, deal righteously with the poor and destitute. Rescue the lowly and the needy, save them from the hand of the wicked. They neither know nor understand, they walk along in darkness, all the foundations of the earth are shaken. I had said "You are godlike beings, all of you, sons of the Most High." Nevertheless, you shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes. Arise, God, judge the earth, for You will inherit all the nations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Mizmor leasaf Elohim nitzav ba''adat el b''kerev Elohim yishpot.
Ad matai tishpetu avel ufenei reshaim tisu sela.
Shiftu dal ve yatom ani varash hatzdiku.
Paletu dal ve evyon miyad reshaim hatzilu.
Lo yadeu ve lo yavinu bachashecha yithalachu yimotu kol mosedei aretz.
Ani amareti Elohim atem uvenei elyon kulechem.
Achen k''adam temutun ucheachad hasarim tipolu.
Kuma Elohim shafeta ha''aretz ki atah tinchal b''chol hagoyim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','ברביעי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Wednesday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם רְבִיעִי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the fourth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom revi''i bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','אֵל נְקָמוֹת יְהֹוָה אֵל נְקָמוֹת הוֹפִֽיעַ: הִנָּשֵׂא שֹׁפֵט הָאָֽרֶץ הָשֵׁב גְּמוּל עַל גֵּאִים: עַד מָתַי רְשָׁעִים יְהֹוָה עַד מָתַי רְשָׁעִים יַעֲלֺֽזוּ: יַבִּֽיעוּ יְדַבְּ֒רוּ עָתָק יִתְאַמְּ֒רוּ כָּל פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן: עַמְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה יְדַכְּ֒אוּ וְנַחֲלָתְ֒ךָ יְעַנּוּ: אַלְמָנָה וְגֵר יַהֲרֹֽגוּ וִיתוֹמִים יְרַצֵּֽחוּ: וַיֹּאמְ֒רוּ לֺא יִרְאֶה יָהּ וְלֺא יָבִין אֱלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: בִּֽינוּ בֹּעֲרִים בָּעָם וּכְ֒סִילִים מָתַי תַּשְׂכִּֽילוּ: הֲנֹֽטַע אֹֽזֶן הֲלֺא יִשְׁמָע אִם יוֹצֵר עַֽיִן הֲלֺא יַבִּיט: הֲיֹסֵר גּוֹיִם הֲלֺא יוֹכִֽיחַ הַמְ֒לַמֵּד אָדָם דָּֽעַת: יְהֹוָה יֹדֵֽעַ מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת אָדָם כִּי הֵֽמָּה הָֽבֶל: אַשְׁרֵי הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר תְּיַסְּ֒רֶֽנּוּ יָהּ וּמִתּוֹרָתְ֒ךָ תְלַמְּ֒דֶֽנּוּ: לְהַשְׁקִיט לוֹ מִֽימֵי רָע עַד יִכָּרֶה לָרָשָׁע שָֽׁחַת: כִּי לֺא יִטּשׁ יְהֹוָה עַמּוֹ וְנַחֲלָתוֹ לֺא יַעֲזֹב: כִּי עַד צֶֽדֶק יָשׁוּב מִשְׁפָּט וְאַחֲרָיו כָּל יִשְׁ֒רֵי לֵב: מִי יָקוּם לִי עִם מְרֵעִים מִי יִתְיַצֵּב לִי עִם פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן: לוּלֵי יְהֹוָה עֶזְרָֽתָה לִּי כִּמְ֒עַט שָׁכְ֒נָה דוּמָה נַפְשִׁי: אִם אָמַֽרְתִּי מָֽטָה רַגְלִי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה יִסְעָדֵֽנִי: בְּרֹב שַׂרְעַפַּי בְּקִרְבִּי תַּנְחוּמֶֽיךָ יְשַׁעַשְׁ֒עוּ נַפְשִׁי: הַיְ֒חָבְרְךָ כִּסֵּא הַוָּוֹת יֹצֵר עָמָל עֲלֵי חֹק: יָגֽוֹדּוּ עַל נֶֽפֶשׁ צַדִּיק וְדָם נָקִי יַרְשִֽׁיעוּ: וַיְ֒הִי יְהֹוָה לִי לְמִשְׂגָּב וֵאלֺהַי לְצוּר מַחְסִי: וַיָּֽשֶׁב עֲלֵיהֶם אֶת אוֹנָם וּבְ֒רָעָתָם יַצְמִיתֵם יַצְמִיתֵם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ: לְכוּ נְרַנְּ֒נָה לַיהוָֹה נָרִֽיעָה לְצוּר יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ: נְקַדְּ֒מָה פָנָיו בְּתוֹדָה בִּזְמִרוֹת נָרִֽיעַ לוֹ: כִּי אֵל גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמֶֽלֶךְ גָּדוֹל עַל כָּל אֱלֺהִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Almighty of vengeance, Adonoy, Almighty of vengeance, reveal Yourself. Arise Judge of the earth, repay the arrogant their just reward. How long shall the wicked— Adonoy— how long shall the wicked exult? They express, they speak with arrogance; all the evildoers are boastful. Adonoy, they crush Your people and Your heritage they oppress. The widow and stranger they kill, and orphans they murder. And they say, "God does not see, the God of Jacob is not concerned." Consider, [you] stupid [ones] among the people,— and you fools when will you become wise? He Who implanted the ear, does He not hear? He Who formed the eye, does He not see? He Who chastises nations, does He not reprove— He that teaches man knowledge? Adonoy knows the thoughts of men, that they are vanity. Fortunate is the man whom You chastise, God, and whom You instruct from Your Torah. To grant him tranquility from days of evil, until the pit is dug for the wicked. for Adonoy will not abandon His people and His inheritance, He will not forsake. For justice shall return unto righteousness, and all the upright in heart will follow it. Who will rise up for me against the wicked, who will stand up for me against the evildoers? Had Adonoy not been my help, in an instant my soul would have dwelt in the silent grave. If [Whenever] I said, my foot has slipped, Your kindliness, Adonoy upheld me. When (worrisome) thoughts multiply within me, Your consolations soothe my soul. Can a tribunal of evil have accord with You— [a tribunal] that makes iniquity into law? They gang up against the life of the righteous, and blood of the innocent they condemn. Adonoy has been my stronghold, my God the Rock of my refuge. He turns their violence against them, and with their own wickedness destroys them; Adonoy, my God, destroys them. Come let us sing to Adonoy; let us shout for joy to the Rock of our Deliverance. Let us greet Him with thanksgiving; with song let us shout for joy to Him. for a great Almighty is Adonoy; a great King over all godlike beings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','El nekamot Adonai el nekamot hofia.
Hinaseh shofet ha''aretz hashev gemul al geim.
Ad matai reshaim Adonai ad matai reshaim ya''alozu.
Yabiu yedaberu atak yitameru kol poalei aven.
Amecha Adonai yedakeu ve nachalatecha yeanu.
Almana ve ger yaharogu vitomim yeratzechu.
Vayomeru lo yireh yah ve lo yavin Elohei Yaakov.
Binu boarim ba''am uchesilim matai taskilu.
Hanota ozen halo yishma im yotzer ayin halo yabit.
Hayoser goyim halo yochiach hamelamed adam da''at.
Adonai yodea machshevot adam ki hema havel.
Ashrei hagever asher teyaserenu yah umitoratecha telamedenu.
Lehashkit lo mimei ra ad yikareh larasha shachat.
Ki lo yitzh Adonai amo ve nachalato lo ya''azov.
Ki ad tzedek yashuv mishpat ve acharav kol yishrei lev.
Mi yakum li im mereim mi yityatzev li im poalei aven.
Lulei Adonai ezrata li kimat shachena duma nafshi.
Im amareti mata ragli chasdecha Adonai yisadeni.
B''rov sarapai b''kirbi tanchumeicha yesha''ashu nafshi.
Hayechaverecha kiseh havavot yotzer amal alei chok.
Yagodu al nefesh tzadik ve dam naki yarshiu.
Vayehi Adonai li lemisgav velohai letzur machsi.
Vayashev aleihem et onam uvera''atam yatzmitem yatzmitem Adonai Eloheinu.
Lechu neranena laAdonai naria letzur yishenu.
Nekadema fanav b''toda bizmirot naria lo.
Ki el gadol Adonai umelech gadol al kol Elohim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בחמישי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Thursday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם חֲמִישִׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the fifth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom chamishi bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ עַל הַגִּתִּית לְאָסָף: הַרְנִֽינוּ לֵאלֺהִים עֻזֵּנוּ הָרִֽיעוּ לֵאלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: שְׂאוּ זִמְרָה וּתְ֒נוּ תֹף כִּנּוֹר נָעִים עִם נָֽבֶל: תִּקְ֒עוּ בַחֹֽדֶשׁ שׁוֹפָר בַּכֶּֽסֶה לְיוֹם חַגֵּֽנוּ: כִּי חֹק לְיִשְׂרָאֵל הוּא מִשְׁפָּט לֵאלֺהֵי יַעֲקֹב: עֵדוּת בִּיהוֹסֵף שָׂמוֹ בְּצֵאתוֹ עַל אֶֽרֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם שְׂפַת לֺא יָדַֽעְתִּי אֶשְׁמָע: הֲסִירֽוֹתִי מִסֵּֽבֶל שִׁכְמוֹ כַּפָּיו מִדּוּד תַּעֲבֹֽרְ֒נָה: בַּצָּרָה קָרָֽאתָ וָאֲחַלְּ֒צֶֽךָ אֶעֶנְךָ בְּסֵֽתֶר רַֽעַם אֶבְחָנְ֒ךָ עַל מֵי מְרִיבָה סֶֽלָה: שְׁמַע עַמִּי וְאָעִֽידָה בָּךְ יִשְׂרָאֵל אִם תִּשְׁמַע לִי: לֺא יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֵל זָר וְלֺא תִשְׁתַּחֲוֶה לְאֵל נֵכָר: אָנֹכִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֶֽיךָ הַמַּעַלְ֒ךָ מֵאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם הַרְחֶב פִּֽיךָ וַאֲמַלְ֒אֵֽהוּ: וְלֺא שָׁמַע עַמִּי לְקוֹלִי וְיִשְׂרָאֵל לֺא אָֽבָה לִי: וָאֲשַׁלְּ֒חֵֽהוּ בִּשְׁרִירוּת לִבָּם יֵלְ֒כוּ בְּמוֹעֲצוֹתֵיהֶם: לוּ עַמִּי שֹׁמֵֽעַ לִי יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּדְ֒רָכַי יְהַלֵּֽכוּ: כִּמְ֒עַט אוֹיְ֒בֵיהֶם אַכְנִֽיעַ וְעַל צָרֵיהֶם אָשִׁיב יָדִי: מְשַׂנְ֒אֵי יְהֹוָה יְכַחֲשׁוּ לוֹ וִיהִי עִתָּם לְעוֹלָם: וַיַּאֲכִילֵֽהוּ מֵחֵֽלֶב חִטָּה וּמִצּוּר דְּבַשׁ אַשְׂבִּיעֶֽךָּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','To Him Who grants victory— upon the Gittis, a psalm of Assaf: Sing joyously to God, our strength, shout for joy to the God of Jacob. Take up the hymn, sound the drum, the pleasant harp and the lute. Blow the shofar on the Rosh Chodesh, at the appointed time for our festive day. For it is a statute for Israel, a [day of] judgement of the God of Jacob. As a testimony for Yehosef, He ordained it when he went out over the land of Egypt, [where] an unfamiliar language I heard. From the burden, I removed his shoulder, his hands were removed from the cauldron. In distress you called out, and I released you, I answered you [though you called] in secret [I answered you] thunderously; I tested you at the waters of Merivah. Selah. Hear, My people, I will testify about you, Israel, if you would just listen to Me. Let no strange god be within you, nor bow before a foreign god. I am Adonoy, your God, Who brought you up from the land of Egypt, open your mouth wide, and I will fill it. But My people did not heed My voice, and Israel did not want Me. So I sent them to follow their heart''s desires, let them follow their own devices. If only My people would heed Me, if Israel would walk in My ways. I would immediately subdue their enemies, and turn My hand against their tormentors. Those who cause hate of Adonoy deceive [pretend obedience to] Him, but their time (of punishment) will be forever. But He would feed him (Israel) from the cream of the wheat, and from the rock, I would sate you with honey.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Lamnatzeach al hagitit leasaf.
Harninu lelohim uzenu hariu lelohei Yaakov.
Seu zimra utenu tof kinor naim im navel.
Tiku vachodesh shofar bakeseh leyom chagenu.
Ki chok leYisrael hu mishpat lelohei Yaakov.
Edut bihosef samo b''tzeto al eretz mitzrayim sefat lo yadaeti eshma.
Hasiroti misevel shichmo kapav midud ta''avorena.
Batzara karata va''achaletzecha e''encha b''seter ra''am evchanecha al mei meriva sela.
Shema ami ve aida bach Yisrael im tishma li.
Lo yihyeh ve cha el zar ve lo tishtachaveh le''el nechar.
Anochi Adonai Elohecha hama''alcha me''eretz mitzrayim harchev picha va''amalehu.
Ve lo shama ami lekoli ve Yisrael lo ava li.
Va''ashalechehu bishrirut libam yelechu b''moatzoteihem.
Lu ami shomea li Yisrael bidrachai yehalechu.
Kimat oyeveihem achnia ve al tzareihem ashiv yadi.
Mesanei Adonai yechachashu lo vihi itam le''olam.
Vaya''achilehu mechelev chita umitzur devash asbieka.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','בשישי בשבת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','On Friday:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הַיּוֹם יוֹם שִׁשִּׁי בַּשַּׁבָּת שֶׁבּוֹ הָיוּ הַלְ֒וִיִּם אוֹמְ֒רִים בְּבֵית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Today is the sixth day of the week, on which the Levites used to recite in the Holy Temple:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hayom yom shishi bashabat shebo hayu haleviyim omerim b''veit hamikdash.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ גֵּאוּת לָבֵשׁ לָבֵשׁ יְהֹוָה עֹז הִתְאַזָּר אַף תִּכּוֹן תֵּבֵל בַּל תִּמּוֹט: נָכוֹן כִּסְאֲךָ מֵאָז מֵעוֹלָם אָֽתָּה: נָשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת יְהֹוָה נָשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת קוֹלָם יִשְׂ֒אוּ נְהָרוֹת דָּכְיָם: מִקֹּלוֹת מַֽיִם רַבִּים אַדִּירִים מִשְׁבְּ֒רֵי יָם אַדִּיר בַּמָּרוֹם יְהֹוָה: עֵדֹתֶֽיךָ נֶאֶמְ֒נוּ מְאֹד לְבֵיתְ֒ךָ נָאֲוָה קֹֽדֶשׁ יְהֹוָה לְאֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Adonoy has begun His reign, with majesty He has clothed Himself; Adonoy clothed Himself, with strength He has girded Himself; He has firmly established the world, so that it cannot be moved. Your throne stands firm from of old, You are from eternity. The rivers have raised—Adonoy— the rivers have raised their voice, the rivers raise their raging waves. More than the roar of many waters, mightier than the breakers of the sea, mighty on high are You "Adonoy." Your testimonies are extremely faithful; holiness is becoming to Your House, Adonoy,—for the length of days.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Adonai malach geut lavesh lavesh Adonai oz hitazar af tikon tevel bal timot.
Nachon kisacha meaz meolam atah.
Naseu neharot Adonai naseu neharot kolam yisu neharot dochyam.
Mikolot mayim rabim adirim mishberei yam adir bamarom Adonai.
Edoteicha ne''emnu meod leveitecha na''ava kodesh Adonai leorech yamim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','he','הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ וְקַבְּ֒צֵֽנוּ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ מִן־הַגּוֹיִם לְהוֹדוֹת לְשֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּֽחַ בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִן־הָעוֹלָם וְעַד הָעֹלָם וְאָמַר כָל־הָעָם אָמֵן הַלְ֒לוּיָה. בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה מִצִּיּוֹן שֹׁכֵן יְרוּשָׁלָֽיִם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ: בְּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהִים אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת לְבַדּוֹ: וּבָרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹדוֹ לְעוֹלָם וְיִמָּלֵא כְבוֹדוֹ אֶת־כָּל־הָאָרֶץ אָמֵן וְאָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','en','Deliver us, God of our deliverance; gather us and save us from the nations to give thanks to Your holy Name, to be extolled in Your praise. Blessed is Adonoy, the God of Israel for all eternity, and all the people said: "Amen" Praise God. Blessed is Adonoy from Zion, Who dwells in Jerusalem. Praise God. Blessed is Adonoy, God, God of Israel Who alone performs wonders. And blessed is the Name of His glory forever, and may His glory fill the whole earth. Amen and Amen!','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-song-of-the-day','transliteration','Hoshienu Elohei yishenu ve kabetzenu ve hatzilenu min hagoyim lehodot leshem kodshecha lehishtabeach bithilatecha.
Baruch Adonai Elohei Yisrael min ha''olam ve ad ha''olam ve amar chol ha''am amen haleluya.
Baruch Adonai mitziyon shochen Yerushalayim haleluyah.
B''ruch Adonai Elohim Elohei Yisrael oseh niflaot levado.
Uvaruch shem k''vodo le''olam ve yimaleh chevodo et kol ha''aretz amen ve amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Song of the Day'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','נוהגין בספרד לומר מזמור ברכי נפשי בראש חדש לפי שיש בו עשה ירח למועדים (טור אורח חיים תכג)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The following psalm (104) is recited in many synagogues on Rosh Chodesh days, following the daily psalm.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','בָּרְ֒כִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי גָּדַֽלְתָּ מְאֹד, הוֹד וְהָדָר לָבָֽשְׁתָּ: עֹֽטֶה אוֹר כַּשַּׂלְמָה, נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם כַּיְ֒רִיעָה: הַמְ֒קָרֶה בַמַּֽיִם עֲלִיּוֹתָיו הַשָּׂם־עָבִים רְכוּבוֹ, הַמְ֒הַלֵּךְ עַל־כַּנְ֒פֵי־רֽוּחַ: עֹשֶׂה מַלְאָכָיו רוּחוֹת, מְשָׁרְ֒תָיו אֵשׁ לֺהֵט: יָסַד אֶֽרֶץ עַל־מְכוֹנֶֽיהָ, בַּל־תִּמּוֹט עוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','My soul, bless Adonoy; Adonoy, my God, You are greatly exalted; with beauty and splendor are You clothed. Enwrapped in light, garment-like, He spreads out the heavens like a curtain. He Who covers His upper chambers with water, He Who makes clouds His chariot, He Who walks upon wings of wind. He Who makes winds His messengers, flaming fires His servants. He Who established the earth upon its foundations, [so] that it shall never be moved.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Barechi nafshi et Adonai Adonai Elohai gadaleta meod,
hod ve hadar lavasheta.
Oteh or kasalma,
noteh shamayim kayria.
Hamekareh vamayim aliyotav hasam avim rechuvo,
hamehalech al kanfei ruach.
Oseh malachav ruchot,
mesharetav esh lohet.
Yasad eretz al mechoneiha,
bal timot olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','תְּהוֹם כַּלְּ֒בוּשׁ כִּסִּיתוֹ, עַל־הָרִים יַֽעַמְ֒דוּ מָֽיִם: מִן־גַּעֲרָתְ֒ךָ יְנוּסוּן, מִן־קוֹל רַעַמְ֒ךָ יֵחָפֵזוּן: יַעֲלוּ הָרִים יֵרְ֒דוּ בְקָעוֹת, אֶל־מְקוֹם זֶה יָסַֽדְתָּ לָהֶם: גְּבוּל־שַֽׂמְתָּ בַּל־יַעֲבֹרוּן, בַּל־יְשֻׁבוּן לְכַסּוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The deep, He covered as with a garment; the waters remain on mountains. At Your shout they retreated, at Your thunderous voice they hastened away. They go up mountains, down into valleys, to the specific place You founded for them. You set a boundary [which] they may not cross, lest they return to cover the earth.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Tehom kalevush kisito,
al harim ya''amdu mayim.
Min ga''aratecha yenusun,
min kol ra''amcha yechafezun.
Ya''alu harim yeredu ve kaot,
el mekom zeh yasadeta lahem.
Gevul sameta bal ya''avorun,
bal yeshuvun lechasot ha''aretz.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','הַמְ֒שַׁלֵּֽחַ מַעְיָנִים בַּנְּ֒חָלִים, בֵּין הָרִים יְהַלֵּכוּן: יַשְׁקוּ כָּל־חַיְ֒תוֹ שָׂדָי, יִשְׁבְּרוּ פְרָאִים צְמָאָם: עֲלֵיהֶם עוֹף־הַשָּׁמַֽיִם יִשְׁכּוֹן, מִבֵּין עֳפָאִים יִתְּ֒נוּ־קוֹל: מַשְׁקֶה הָרִים מֵעֲלִיּוֹתָיו, מִפְּ֒רִי מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ תִּשְׂבַּע הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','He Who sends springs into streams to flow between the mountains; to water all the beasts of the fields; the wild ones quench their thirst. Over them dwell the birds of the sky, from among the branches, they give voice. [You] Who waters the mountains from His upper chambers, from the fruit of Your works the earth is sated.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Hameshaleach mayanim banechalim,
bein harim yehalechun.
Yashku kol chayto sadai,
yishberu feraim tzema''am.
Aleihem of hashamayim yishkon,
mibein ofaim yitenu kol.
Mashkeh harim mealiyotav,
miperi ma''aseicha tisba ha''aretz.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','מַצְמִֽיחַ חָצִיר לַבְּ֒הֵמָה וְעֵֽשֶׂב לַעֲבֹדַת הָאָדָם, לְהוֹצִיא לֶֽחֶם מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ: וְיַֽיִן יְשַׂמַּח לְבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ לְהַצְהִיל פָּנִים מִשָּֽׁמֶן, וְלֶֽחֶם לְבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ יִסְעָד: יִשְׂבְּ֒עוּ עֲצֵי יְהֹוָה אַרְ֒זֵי לְבָנוֹן אֲשֶׁר נָטָע: אֲשֶׁר־שָׁם צִפֳּרִים יְקַנֵּֽנוּ, חֲסִידָה בְּרוֹשִׁים בֵּיתָהּ: הָרִים הַגְּ֒בֹהִים לַיְּ֒עֵלִים, סְלָעִים מַחְסֶה לַשְּׁ֒פַנִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','[You] Who causes grass to sprout for cattle, and vegetation for the labor of man, to bring forth bread from the earth; wine to cheer the heart of man, to make [his] face shine from oil, and bread to sustain the heart of man. Adonoy''s trees are sated, the cedars of Lebanon that He planted; where birds make their nests, the stork—the firs are her home. The high mountains [are] for the wild goats, the rocks a refuge for the rabbits.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Matzmiach chatzir labehema ve esev la''avodat ha''adam,
lehotzi lechem min ha''aretz.
Ve yayin yesamach levav enosh lehatzhil panim mishamen,
ve lechem levav enosh yisad.
Yisbeu atzei Adonai arzei levanon asher nata.
Asher sham tziporim yekanenu,
chasida b''roshim beitah.
Harim hagevohim laye''elim,
selaim machseh lashefanim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','עָשָׂה יָרֵֽחַ לְמוֹעֲדִים שֶֽׁמֶשׁ יָדַע מְבוֹאוֹ: תָּֽשֶׁת חֽשֶׁךְ וִיהִי לָֽיְלָה, בּוֹ־תִרְמֹשׂ כָּל־חַֽיְ֒תוֹ־יָֽעַר: הַכְּ֒פִירִים שֹׁאֲגִים לַטָּֽרֶף, וּלְ֒בַקֵּשׁ מֵאֵל אָכְלָם: תִּזְרַח הַשֶּֽׁמֶשׁ יֵאָסֵפוּן, וְאֶל־מְעוֹנֹתָם יִרְבָּצוּן: יֵצֵא אָדָם לְפָעֳלוֹ, וְלַעֲבֹדָתוֹ עֲדֵי־עָֽרֶב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','He made the moon to fix seasons the sun knows its place to set. You make darkness and night comes, in which move about all the beasts of the forest. —The young lions roar for prey, and seek their food from the Almighty. [When] the sun rises, they gather and come into their dens to lie. Man goes out to his work, to his labor until evening.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Asa yareach lemoadim shemesh yada mevo''o.
Tashet chshech vihi layela,
bo tirmos kol chayeto ya''ar.
Hakefirim shoagim lataref,
ulevakesh me''el ochlam.
Tizrach hashemesh yeasefun,
ve el meonotam yirbatzun.
Yetzeh adam lefo''olo,
ve la''avodato adei arev.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','מָה־רַבּוּ מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ יְהֹוָה כֻּלָּם בְּחָכְמָה עָשִֽׂיתָ, מָלְ֒אָה הָאָֽרֶץ קִנְיָנֶֽךָ: זֶה הַיָּם גָּדוֹל וּרְ֒חַב יָדָֽיִם שָׁם־רֶֽמֶשׂ וְאֵין מִסְפָּר, חַיּוֹת קְטַנּוֹת עִם־גְּדֹלוֹת: שָׁם אֳנִיּוֹת יְהַלֵּכוּן, לִוְיָתָן זֶה יָצַֽרְתָּ לְשַֽׂחֶק־בּוֹ: כֻּלָּם אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּרוּן, לָתֵת אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: תִּתֵּן לָהֶם יִלְקֹטוּן, תִּפְתַּח יָדְ֒ךָ יִשְׂבְּעוּן טוֹב: תַּסְתִּיר פָּנֶֽיךָ יִבָּהֵלוּן תֹּסֵף רוּחָם יִגְוָעוּן, וְאֶל־עֲפָרָם יְשׁוּבוּן: תְּשַׁלַּח רוּחֲךָ יִבָּרֵאוּן, וּתְ֒חַדֵּשׁ פְּנֵי אֲדָמָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','How many are Your works, Adonoy! You made them all with wisdom; the earth is full of Your possessions! This sea, great and wide— therein are innumerable creeping things, animals small and great. There ships travel; this Leviathan You formed to frolic with. They all look to You expectantly, to provide their food in its time. [When] You give it to them, they gather it in; [when] You open Your hand, they are sated with goodness. Whey You hide Your face, they are panic-stricken; When You gather in their breath, they perish, and to their dust they return. When You send Your spirit, they will be created [anew]; and You will renew the face of the earth.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Ma rabu ma''aseicha Adonai kulam b''chochma asita,
malea ha''aretz kinyanecha.
Zeh hayam gadol urechav yadayim sham remes ve ein mispar,
chayot k''tanot im gedolot.
Sham oniyot yehalechun,
livyatan zeh yatzareta lesachek bo.
Kulam eleicha yesaberun,
latet ochlam b''ito.
Titen lahem yilkotun,
tiftach yadecha yisbeun tov.
Tastir paneicha yibahelun tosef rucham yigvaun,
ve el afaram yeshuvun.
Teshalach ruchacha yibareun,
utechadesh penei adama.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','יְהִי כְבוֹד יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם, יִשְׂמַח יְהֹוָה בְּמַעֲשָׂיו: הַמַּבִּיט לָאָֽרֶץ וַתִּרְעָד, יִגַּע בֶּהָרִים וְיֶעֱשָֽׁנוּ: אָשִֽׁירָה לַּיהוָֹה בְּחַיָּי, אֲזַמְּ֒רָה לֵאלֺהַי בְּעוֹדִי: יֶעֱרַב עָלָיו שִׂיחִי, אָנֹכִי אֶשְׂמַח בַּיהוָֹה: יִתַּֽמּוּ חַטָּאִים מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ וּרְ֒שָׁעִים עוֹד אֵינָם בָּרְ֒כִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָה הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','The glory of Adonoy will endure forever, Adonoy will rejoice in His works— Who gazes upon the earth and it trembles; Who touches the mountains and they erupt. I will sing to Adonoy with my life; I will offer hymns to my God as long as I am alive. May my words be pleasant to Him; I will rejoice in Adonoy. Sin will be excised from the earth, and the wicked will be no more; My soul bless Adonoy, Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','transliteration','Yehi chevod Adonai le''olam,
yismach Adonai b''ma''asav.
Hamabit la''aretz vatirad,
yiga beharim ve ye''eshanu.
Ashira laAdonai b''chayai,
azamera lelohai b''odi.
Ye''erav alav sichi,
anochi esmach ba''adonai.
Yitamu chataim min ha''aretz ureshaim od einam barechi nafshi et Adonai haleluyah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','he','(הושיענו וכו''. קדיש יתום.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-barchi-nafshi','en','(Deliver us...; Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Barchi Nafshi'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','מנהג טוב לומר אחר כל תפלה מזמור לדוד ה׳‬ אורי וישעי. ובפרט מר״ח אלול עד הושענא רבא (מורה באצבע סי'' לז).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','The following psalm (27) is recited at the conclusion of services, morning and evenings, from the first day of Elul, through Shemini Atzeres. Others say only until Hoasha''na Rabbah. The psalm voices our prayer that God will be our light on Rosh Hashana enabling us to repel the darkness of sin through true repentance, and that He will be our salvation on Yom Kippur, through His compassionate atonement of our sins.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','לְדָוִד יְהֹוָה אוֹרִי וְיִשְׁעִי מִמִּי אִירָא יְהֹוָה מָעוֹז חַיַּי מִמִּי אֶפְחָד: בִּקְ֒רֹב עָלַי מְרֵעִים לֶאֱכֹל אֶת בְּשָׂרִי צָרַי וְאֹיְ֒בַי לִי הֵֽמָּה כָשְׁ֒לוּ וְנָפָֽלוּ: אִם תַּחֲנֶה עָלַי מַחֲנֶה לֺא יִירָא לִבִּי אִם תָּקוּם עָלַי מִלְחָמָה בְּזֹאת אֲנִי בוֹטֵֽחַ: אַחַת שָׁאַֽלְתִּי מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה אוֹתָהּ אֲבַקֵּשׁ שִׁבְתִּי בְּבֵית יְהֹוָה כָּל יְמֵי חַיַּי לַחֲזוֹת בְּנֹֽעַם יְהֹוָה וּלְ֒בַקֵּר בְּהֵיכָלוֹ: כִּי יִצְפְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּסֻכֹּה בְּיוֹם רָעָה יַסְתִּרֵֽנִי בְּסֵֽתֶר אָהֳלוֹ בְּצוּר יְרוֹמְ֒מֵֽנִי: וְעַתָּה יָרוּם רֹאשִׁי עַל אֹיְ֒בַי סְבִיבוֹתָי וְאֶזְבְּחָה בְאָהֳלוֹ זִבְחֵי תְרוּעָה אָשִֽׁירָה וַאֲזַמְּ֒רָה לַיהוָֹה: שְׁמַע יְהֹוָה קוֹלִי אֶקְרָא וְחָנֵּֽנִי וַעֲנֵֽנִי: לְךָ אָמַר לִבִּי בַּקְּ֒שׁוּ פָנָי אֶת פָּנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֲבַקֵּשׁ: אַל תַּסְתֵּר פָּנֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנִּי אַל תַּט בְּאַף עַבְדֶּֽךָ עֶזְרָתִי הָיִֽיתָ אַל תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנִי וְאַל תַּעַזְ֒בֵֽנִי אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעִי: כִּי אָבִי וְאִמִּי עֲזָבֽוּנִי וַיהוָֹה יַאַסְ֒פֵֽנִי: הוֹרֵֽנִי יְהֹוָה דַּרְכֶּֽךָ וּנְ֒חֵֽנִי בְּאֹֽרַח מִישׁוֹר לְמַֽעַן שׁוֹרְ֒רָי: אַל תִּתְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּנֶֽפֶשׁ צָרָי כִּי קָֽמוּ בִי עֵֽדֵי שֶֽׁקֶר וִיפֵֽחַ חָמָס: לוּלֵא הֶאֱמַֽנְתִּי לִרְאוֹת בְּטוּב יְהֹוָה בְּאֶֽרֶץ חַיִּים: קַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה חֲזַק וְיַאֲמֵץ לִבֶּךָ וְקַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','By David: Adonoy is my light and my salvation, whom shall I fear? Adonoy is the strength of my life, of whom shall I be afraid? When evildoers approach me to devour my flesh— my tormentors and my foes they stumble and fall. If an army should encamp against me, my heart would not fear; if war were to rise against me, in this I trust. One thing I request of Adonoy, [only] that shall I seek, that I may dwell in the House of Adonoy all the days of my life, to behold the pleasantness of Adonoy, and to meditate in His Sanctuary. For He will hide me in His Tabernacle on the day of distress, He will conceal me in the shelter of His Tent, upon a rock He will lift me. And now my head is raised high above my enemies around me; and I will offer in His Tent, sacrifices accompanied by trumpets of joy; I will sing and chant to Adonoy. Adonoy, hear my voice when I call; be gracious to me and answer me. Of You, my heart has said, Seek My Presence; Your Presence, Adonoy I will seek. Conceal not Your Presence from me, do not turn away Your servant in anger. You have been my help; neither cast me off nor abandon me, God of my deliverance. When my father and mother abandon me, Adonoy will gather me up. Adonoy, teach me Your way, and lead me in the path of uprightness, because of my watchers. Do not deliver me to the will of my tormentors, for false witnesses have risen against me, who breathe violence. Had I not believed that I would see the goodness of Adonoy in the land of living. Hope to Adonoy, be strong and He will give you courage; and hope to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','LeDavid Adonai ori ve yishi mimi ira Adonai maoz chayai mimi efchad.
Bikrov alai mereim le''echol et b''sari tzarai ve oyevai li hema chashelu ve nafalu.
Im tachaneh alai machaneh lo yira libi im takum alai milchama b''zot ani voteach.
Achat sha''aleti me''et Adonai otah avakesh shivti b''veit Adonai kol yemei chayai lachazot b''noam Adonai ulevaker b''heichalo.
Ki yitzpeneni b''sukoh b''yom ra''a yastireni b''seter oholo b''tzur yeromemeni.
Ve atah yarum roshi al oyevai sevivotai ve ezbecha ve oholo zivchei terua ashira va''azamera laAdonai.
Shema Adonai koli ekra ve chaneni va''aneni.
Lecha amar libi bakeshu fanai et paneicha Adonai avakesh.
Al taster paneicha mimeni al tat b''af avdecha ezrati hayita al titesheni ve al ta''azveni Elohei yishi.
Ki avi ve imi azavuni va''adonai ya''asfeni.
Horeni Adonai darkecha unecheni b''orach mishor lema''an shorerai.
Al titeneni b''nefesh tzarai ki kamu vi edei sheker vifeach chamas.
Luleh he''emaneti lirot b''tuv Adonai b''eretz chayim.
Kaveh el Adonai chazak ve ya''ametz libecha ve kaveh el Adonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','(קדיש יתום)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','(Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','בבית האבל בבוקר אחר שיר של יום ואחר מנחה בימים שיש בהם תחנון אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','It is customary to recite this psalm (49) in the house of a mourner during the week of mourning, following the morning and evening services. On weekdays when Tachanun is not said Psalm 16 (page 218) is substituted. This psalm, the final hymn of the psalms set down by the sons of Korach has significance for all mankind. Its message is that man must utilize all his material and physical resources to enhance his spiritual existence so that when his soul survives the body''s brief stay on earth it can ascend to immortality. If man fails to recognize his purpose in life and instead regards the acquisition of material wealth the primary aim of life, he forfeits his hope of immortality, and his existence will not continue beyond the grave.—S.R. Hirsch','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ לִבְנֵי קֹֽרַח מִזְמוֹר: שִׁמְ֒עוּ זֹאת כָּל־הָעַמִּים הַאֲזִֽינוּ כָּל יֽשְׁ֒בֵי חָֽלֶד: גַּם בְּנֵי אָדָם גַּם בְּנֵי אִישׁ יַֽחַד עָשִׁיר וְאֶבְיוֹן: פִּי יְדַבֵּר חָכְמוֹת וְהָגוּת לִבִּי תְבוּנוֹת: אַטֶּה לְמָשָׁל אָזְנִי אֶפְתַּח בְּכִנּוֹר חִידָתִי: לָֽמָּה אִירָא בִּֽימֵי רָע עֲוֹן עֲקֵבַי יְסוּבֵּֽנִי: הַבֹּטְ֒חִים עַל חֵילָם וּבְ֒רֹב עָשְׁרָם יִתְהַלָּֽלוּ: אָח לֺא פָדֹה יִפְדֶּה אִישׁ לֺא יִתֵּן לֵאלֺהִים כָּפְרוֹ: וְיֵקַר פִּדְיוֹן נַפְשָׁם וְחָדַל לְעוֹלָם: וִיחִי עוֹד לָנֶֽצַח לֺא יִרְאֶה הַשָּֽׁחַת: כִּי יִרְאֶה חֲכָמִים יָמֽוּתוּ יַֽחַד כְּסִיל וָבַֽעַר יֹאבֵֽדוּ וְעָזְ֒בוּ לַאֲחֵרִים חֵילָם: קִרְבָּם בָּתֵּֽימוֹ לְעוֹלָם מִשְׁכְּ֒נֹתָם לְדוֹר וָדֹר קָרְ֒אוּ בִשְׁמוֹתָם עֲלֵי אֲדָמוֹת: וְאָדָם בִּיקָר בַּל־יָלִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ: זֶה דַרְכָּם כֶּֽסֶל לָֽמוֹ וְאַחֲרֵיהֶם בְּפִיהֶם יִרְצוּ סֶֽלָה: כַּצֹּאן לִשְׁ֒אוֹל שַׁתּוּ מָֽוֶת יִרְעֵם וַיִּרְדּוּ בָם יְשָׁרִים לַבֹּֽקֶר וְצוּרָם לְבַלּוֹת שְׁאוֹל מִזְּ֒בֻל לוֹ: אַךְ־אֱלֺהִים יִפְדֶּה נַפְשִׁי מִיַּד שְׁאוֹל כִּי יִקָּחֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: אַל־תִּירָא כִּי־יַעֲשִׁר אִישׁ כִּי־יִרְבֶּה כְּבוֹד בֵּיתוֹ: כִּי לֺא בְמוֹתוֹ יִקַּח הַכֹּל לֺא־יֵרֵד אַחֲרָיו כְּבוֹדוֹ: כִּי־נַפְשׁוֹ בְּחַיָּיו יְבָרֵךְ וְיוֹדֻֽךָ כִּי־תֵיטִיב לָךְ: תָּבוֹא עַד־דּוֹר אֲבוֹתָיו עַד־נֵֽצַח לֺא יִרְאוּ אוֹר: אָדָם בִּיקָר וְלֺא־יָבִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','To Him Who grants victory, a psalm by the sons of Korach. Hear this all peoples, listen all inhabitants of the decaying world! Sons of Adam and sons of men, rich and poor together. My mouth shall speak wisdom, and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding. I will incline my ear to a parable, I will begin to solve, to the accompaniment of a harp, my riddle. Why should I fear in the days of evil? The iniquity I trod upon surrounds me. Those who trust in their wealth and take pride in their great riches. A man will not redeem his brother neither can he give to God his ransom. The redemption of their soul is too costly and it shall cease to be forever. Shall he then live forever, shall he never see the grave? For he sees that wise men die, the fools and senseless perish equally and leave their wealth to others. Their inner thoughts are that their houses [will last] forever, their homes for generation after generation; (for) they have proclaimed their names throughout the lands. But man does not endure in his splendor, he is likened to the silenced animals. This is their way— their folly remains with them, and [yet] their descendants take pleasure in their speech, Selah. Like sheep—they are destined for the grave; death shall be their shepherd, and the upright shall dominate them at morning, their form will be consumed in the grave; [it will not remain] their dwelling-place. But God will redeem my soul from the [grasp of] the grave, for He will take me [to Himself] Selah. Fear not when a man grows rich, when the glory of his house is increased. For when he dies, he shall carry nothing away, his glory will not descend after him. Because while he lived, he blessed his soul. (saying): they will praise you because you have done well for yourself. He will join the generation of his fathers, they shall not see light, for all eternity. Man with [all] his splendor, [but] without understanding is likened to the silenced animals.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Lamnatzeach livnei korach mizmor.
Shimu zot kol ha''amim ha''azinu kol yshevei chaled.
Gam b''nei adam gam b''nei ish yachad ashir ve evyon.
Pi yedaber chochmot ve hagut libi tevunot.
Ateh lemashal ozni eftach b''chinor chidati.
Lama ira bimei ra avon akevai yesubeni.
Habotechim al cheilam uverov oshram yithalalu.
Ach lo fadoh yifdeh ish lo yiten lelohim kafero.
Ve yekar pidyon nafsham ve chadal le''olam.
Vichi od lanetzach lo yireh hashachat.
Ki yireh chachamim yamutu yachad k''sil vava''ar yovedu ve azevu la''acherim cheilam.
Kirbam bateimo le''olam mishkenotam ledor vador kareu vishmotam alei adamot.
Ve adam bikar bal yalin nimshal kabehemot nidmu.
Zeh darkam kesel lamo ve achareihem b''fihem yirtzu sela.
Katzon lishol shatu mavet yirem vayirdu vam yesharim laboker ve tzuram levalot sheol mizevul lo.
Ach Elohim yifdeh nafshi miyad sheol ki yikacheni sela.
Al tira ki ya''ashir ish ki yirbeh k''vod beito.
Ki lo ve moto yikach hakol lo yered acharav k''vodo.
Ki nafsho b''chayav yevarech ve yoducha ki teitiv lach.
Tavo ad dor avotav ad netzach lo yiru or.
Adam bikar ve lo yavin nimshal kabehemot nidmu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','(קדיש יתום)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','(Mourner''s Kaddish.)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','ובימים שאין בהם תחנון אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','On weekdays when Tachanun is not said, the following is said in the house of a mourner.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','מִכְתָּם לְדָוִד שָׁמְרֵֽנִי אֵל כִּי־חָסִֽיתִי בָךְ: אָמַֽרְתְּ לַיהֺוָה אֲדֹנָי אָֽתָּה טוֹבָתִי בַּל־עָלֶֽיךָ: לִקְדוֹשִׁים אֲשֶׁר־בָּאָֽרֶץ הֵֽמָּה וְאַדִּירֵי כָּל־חֶפְצִי־בָם: יִרְבּוּ עַצְּבוֹתָם אַחֵר מָהָֽרוּ בַּל־אַסִּיךְ נִסְכֵּיהֶם מִדָּם וּבַל־אֶשָּׂא אֶת־שְׁמוֹתָם עַל־שְׂפָתָי: יְהֺוָה מְנָת־חֶלְקִי וְכוֹסִי אַתָּה תּוֹמִיךְ גּוֹרָלִי: חֲבָלִים נָֽפְלוּ־לִי בַּנְּעִמִים אַף־נַחֲלָת שָׁפְרָה עָלָי: אֲבָרֵךְ אֶת־יְהֺוָה אֲשֶׁר יְעָצָֽנִי אַף־לֵילוֹת יִסְּרֽוּנִי כִלְיוֹתָי: שִׁוִּיתִי יְהֺוָה לְנֶגְדִּי תָמִיד כִּי מִימִינִי בַּל־אֶמּוֹט: לָכֵן שָׂמַח לִבִּי וַיָּֽגֶל כְּבוֹדִי אַף־בְּשָׂרִי יִשְׁכֹּן לָבֶֽטַח: כִּי לֹא־תַעֲזֹב נַפְשִׁי לִשְׁאוֹל לֹא־תִתֵּן חֲסִידְךָ לִרְאוֹת שָֽׁחַת: תּוֹדִיעֵֽנִי אֹֽרַח חַיִּים שֽׂבַע שְׂמָחוֹת אֶת־פָּנֶֽיךָ נְעִימוֹת בִּימִינְךָ נֶֽצַח:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','A Michtam of David. Preserve me, Almighty, for I have taken refuge in You. You said to Adonoy, You are my Master, I have no well-being without You. Due to the holy that are in the earth, and the mighty, are all my desires [fulfilled]. Let their sufferings multiply, those who follow another [sovereignty]; I will not pour their libations of blood, nor carry their names upon my lips. Adonoy is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup; You guide my fate. The portions that have fallen to me are in pleasant places; a beautiful inheritance is mine. I will bless Adonoy Who has given me counsel; even for the nights in which my mind admonished me. I have set Adonoy before me always; for surely He is at my right hand, I will not be moved. Therefore my heart rejoiced and my soul exulted; also my flesh will dwell in safety. For You will not abandon my soul to the grave, nor will You allow Your devoted one to see the pit. You will make known to me the path of life; fullness of joy is in Your presence; pleasantness is at Your right hand, evermore.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Michtam leDavid shamereni el ki chasiti vach.
Amart laAdonai adonai atah tovati bal aleicha.
Likdoshim asher ba''aretz hema ve adirei kol cheftzi vam.
Yirbu atzevotam acher maharu bal asich niskeihem midam uval esa et shemotam al sefatai.
Adonai menat chelki ve chosi atah tomich gorali.
Chavalim nafelu li baneimim af nachalat shafera alai.
Avarech et Adonai asher yeatzani af leilot yiseruni chilyotai.
Shiviti Adonai lenegdi tamid ki mimini bal emot.
Lachen samach libi vayagel k''vodi af b''sari yishkon lavetach.
Ki lo ta''azov nafshi lishol lo titen chasidecha lirot shachat.
Todieni orach chayim sva semachot et paneicha neimot biminecha netzach.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','קדיש יתום יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','Mourner''s Kaddish Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Kdysh ytvm yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen,','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-l-david-hashem','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, L''David Hashem'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','קַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה חֲזַק וְיַאֲמֵץ לִבֶּךָ וְקַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה: אֵין קָדוֹשׁ כַּיהֹוָה כִּי אֵין בִּלְתֶּךָ וְאֵין צוּר כֵּאלֹהֵינוּ: כִּי מִי אֱלוֹהַּ מִבַּלְעֲדֵי יְהֹוָה וּמִי צוּר זוּלָתִי אֱלֹהֵינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Hope to Adonoy; be strong and He will give you courage and hope to Adonoy. There is none holy like Adonoy for there is none beside You and there is no stronghold like our God. For who is a god other than Adonoy and who is a stronghold beside our God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Kaveh el Adonai chazak ve ya''ametz libecha ve kaveh el Adonai.
Ein kadosh ka''adonai ki ein biltecha ve ein tzur keloheinu.
Ki mi eloah mibaladei Adonai umi tzur zulati Eloheinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אֵין כֵּאלֹהֵינוּ. אֵין כַּאדוֹנֵנוּ. אֵין כְּמַלְכֵּנוּ. אֵין כְּמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: מִי כֵאלֹהֵינוּ. מִי כַאדוֹנֵנוּ. מִי כְמַלְכֵּנוּ. מִי כְמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: נוֹדֶה לֵאלֹהֵינוּ. נוֹדֶה לַאדוֹנֵנוּ. נוֹדֶה לְמַלְכֵּנוּ. נוֹדֶה לְמוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: בָּרוּךְ אֱלֹהֵינוּ. בָּרוּךְ אֲדוֹנֵנוּ. בָּרוּךְ מַלְכֵּנוּ. בָּרוּךְ מוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ: אַתָּה הוּא אֱלֹהֵינוּ. אַתָּה הוּא אֲדוֹנֵנוּ. אַתָּה הוּא מַלְכֵּנוּ. אַתָּה הוּא מוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ. אַתָּה תוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ. אַתָּה תָקוּם תְּרַחֵם צִיוֹן כִּי עֵת לְחֶנְנָה כִּי בָא מוֹעֵד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','There is none like our God. There is none like our Master. There is none like our King. There is none like our Deliverer. Who is like our God? Who is like our Master? Who is like our King? Who is like our Deliverer? Let us thank our God. Let us thank our Master. Let us thank our King. Let us thank our deliverer. Blessed is our God. Blesed is our Master. Blessed is our King. Blessed is our Deliverer. You are our God. You are our Master. You are our King. You are our Deliverer. You will deliver us You will arise and have mercy on Zion, for it is time to be gracious to her, for the appointed time has come.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Ein keloheinu.
Ein kadonenu.
Ein k''malkenu.
Ein k''moshienu.
Mi cheloheinu.
Mi chadonenu.
Mi chemalkenu.
Mi chemoshienu.
Nodeh leloheinu.
Nodeh ladonenu.
Nodeh lemalkenu.
Nodeh lemoshienu.
Baruch Eloheinu.
Baruch adonenu.
Baruch malkenu.
Baruch moshienu.
Atah hu Eloheinu.
Atah hu adonenu.
Atah hu malkenu.
Atah hu moshienu.
Atah toshienu.
Atah takum terachem tziyon ki et lechenna ki va moed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','פִּטּוּם הַקְּ֒טֺרֶת הַצֳּרִי וְהַצִּפֹּרֶן הַחֶלְ֒בְּנָה וְהַלְּבוֹנָה מִשְׁקַל שִׁבְעִים שִׁבְעִים מָנָה. מוֹר וּקְ֒צִיעָה שִׁבֹּלֶת נֵרְדְּ וְכַרְכֹּם מִשְׁקַל שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר מָנֶה. הַקּשְׁטְ שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר וְקִלּוּפָה שְׁלֹשָׁה וְקִנָּמוֹן תִּשְׁעָה. בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה תִּשְׁעָה קַבִּין. יֵין קַפְרִיסִין סְאִין תְּלָתָא וְקַבִּין תְּלָתָא. וְאִם אֵין לוֹ יֵין קַפְרִיסִין מֵבִיא חֲמַר חִוַּרְיָן עַתִּיק. מֶלַח סְדוֹמִית רֹבַע הַקָב. מַעֲלֶה עָשָׁן כָּל שֶׁהוּא. רַבִּי נָתָן הַבַּבְלִי אוֹמֵר אַף כִּפַּת הַיַּרְדֵּן כָּל שֶׁהוּא. וְאִם נָתַן בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ פְּסָלָהּ וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','The composition of the incense consisted of balm, onycha, galbanum, and frankincense— by weight, seventy maneh of each; myrrh, cassia, spikenard and saffron by weight— sixteen maneh of each; twelve maneh of costus, three maneh of aromatic bark, and nine maneh of cinnamon. [Also used in compounding the incense were:] Nine kabin of Carshina lye, Cyprus wine [measuring] three s''in and three kabin— if he had no Cyprus wine, he could used strong white wine— a fourth of a kab of Sodom salt, and a minute quantity of maaleh ashan. Rabbi Nosson of Babylonia says, Add a minute quantity of Jordan amber. If one added honey, the incense became unfit; and if one omitted any of its spices he was liable to the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Pitum haketoret hatzori ve hatziporen hachelbena ve halevona mishkal shivim shivim mana.
Mor uketzia shibolet nerd ve charkom mishkal shisha asar shisha asar maneh.
Haksht sheneim asar ve kilufa shelosha ve kinamon tisha.
Borit karshina tisha kabin.
Yein kafrisin sein telata ve kabin telata.
Ve im ein lo yein kafrisin mevi chamar chivaryan atik.
Melach sedomit rova hakav.
Ma''aleh ashan kol shehu.
Rabi natan habavli omer af kipat hayarden kol shehu.
Ve im natan bah devash pesalah ve im chisar achat mikol samaneiha chayav mita.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר הַצֳּרִי אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא שְׂרָף הַנּוֹטֵף מֵעֲצֵי הַקְּ֒טָף. בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה לָמָּה הִיא בָאָה כְּדֵי לְיַפּוֹת בָּהּ אֶת הַצִּפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא נָאָה. יֵין קַפְרִיסִין לָמָּה הוּא בָא כְּדֵי לִשְׁרוֹת בּוֹ אֶת הַצִּפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא עַזָּה. וַהֲלֹא מֵי רַגְלַיִם יָפִין לָהּ אֶלָּא שֶׁאֵין מַכְנִיסִין מֵי רַגְלַיִם בַּמִּקְדָּשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי הַכָּבוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Rabbi Shimon ben Gamliel says: The balm is nothing but sap which drips from the balsam tree. the lye of Carshina was used for rubbing the onycha in order to refine its appearance. The Cyprus wine was used to soak the onycha to give it a pungent odor. Though the water of Raglayim was well suited for that purpose, they did not bring the water of Raglayim into the Temple because it would be disrespectful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Raban shimon ben gamliel omer hatzori eino ela seraf hanotef meatzei haketaf.
Borit karshina lama hi va''a k''dei leyapot bah et hatziporen k''dei sheteheh na''a.
Yein kafrisin lama hu va k''dei lishrot bo et hatziporen k''dei sheteheh aza.
Vahalo mei raglayim yafin lah ela she''ein machnisin mei raglayim bamikdash mipenei hakavod.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תַּנְיָא רַבִּי נָתָן אוֹמֵר כְּשֶׁהוּא שׁוֹחֵק אוֹמֵר הָדֵק הֵיטֵב הֵיטֵב הָדֵק מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַקּוֹל יָפֶה לַבְּ֒שָׂמִים, פִּטְּ֒מָהּ לַחֲצָאִין כְּשֵׁרָה לִשְׁלִישׁ וְלִרְבִֽיעַ לֹא שָׁמַֽעְנוּ: אָמַר רַבִּי יְהוּדָה זֶה הַכְּ֒לָל אִם כְּמִדָּתָהּ כְּשֵׁרָה לַחֲצָאִין וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Rabbi Nosson says, While [the Kohein] ground [the incense] he would say, ‘Hodeik heiteiv, heiteiv hodeik,'' because the sound is good for the spices. If half the quantity of incense was prepared it was acceptable, but if only a third or a fourth [of it was prepared] we have not heard [whether it was acceptable."] Rabbi Yehuda said, This is the general rule: If [it was prepared with all its ingredients] in the correct proportion, it is acceptable even if only half was prepared; but if he left out any of its spices, he was liable for the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Tanya rabi natan omer k''shehu shochek omer hadek heitev heitev hadek mipenei shehakol yafeh labesamim,
pitemah lachatzain k''shera lishlish ve lirvia lo shamaenu.
Amar rabi Yehudah zeh hakelal im k''midatah k''shera lachatzain ve im chisar achat mikol samaneiha chayav mita.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תַּנְיָא בַּר קַפָּרָא אוֹמֵר אַחַת לְשִׁשִּׁים אוֹ לְשִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה הָיְ֒תָה בָאָה שֶׁל שִׁירַֽיִם לַחֲצָאִין: וְעוֹד תָּנֵי בַּר קַפָּרָא אִלּוּ הָיָה נוֹתֵן בָּהּ קוֹרְ֒טוֹב שֶׁל דְּבַשׁ אֵין אָדָם יָכוֹל לַעֲמֹד מִפְּ֒נֵי רֵיחָהּ וְלָֽמָּה אֵין מְעָרְ֒בִין בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַתּוֹרָה אָמְ֒רָה כִּי כָל־שְׂאֹר וְכָל־דְּבַשׁ לֹא־תַקְטִֽירוּ מִמֶּֽנּוּ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Bar Kappara says, Once in sixty or seventy years the accumulated surplus was sufficient to provide half [the yearly quantity of incense."] Bar Kappara also taught, If he would have put into it a minute quantity of honey, no one could have withstood [resisted] the scent. Why was no honey mixed with it? Because the Torah says, (Leviticus 2:11) For any leaven or honey, do not burn from them, [as] a fire-offering to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Tanya bar kapara omer achat leshishim o leshivim shana hayeta va''a shel shirayim lachatzain.
Ve od tanei bar kapara ilu haya noten bah koretov shel devash ein adam yachol la''amod mipenei reichah ve lama ein mearevin bah devash mipenei shehatora amera ki chol seor ve chol devash lo taktiru mimenu isheh laAdonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אומר ג'' פעמים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Recite each of these verses three times:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגַּב־לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Adonoy of Hosts is with us, a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah! Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]! The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Adonai tzevaot imanu misgav lanu Elohei Yaakov sela.
Adonai tzevaot ashrei adam boteach bach.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אַתָּה סֵֽתֶר לִי מִצַּר תִּצְּ֒רֵֽנִי רָנֵּי פַלֵּט תְּסוֹבְ֒בֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: וְעָרְ֒בָה לַיהוָֹה מִנְחַת יְהוּדָה וִירוּשָׁלָֽםִ כִּימֵי עוֹלָם וּכְשָׁנִים קַדְמֹנִיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','You are my shelter; from distress You preserve me; with glad song of rescue, You envelop me, Selah! Let Adonoy be pleased with the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem, as in the days of old and in earlier years.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Atah seter li mitzar titzereni ranei falet tesoveveni sela.
Ve areva laAdonai minchat Yehudah virushalami kimei olam ucheshanim kadmoniyot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','תָּנָא דְבֵי אֵלִיָּֽהוּ כָּל הַשּׁוֹנֶה הֲלָכוֹת בְּכָל יוֹם מֻבְטָח לוֹ שֶׁהוּא בֶּן עוֹלָם הַבָּא שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר הֲלִיכוֹת עוֹלָם לוֹ אַל תִּקְרֵי הֲלִיכוֹת אֶלָּא הֲלָכוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','It was taught in the school of Elijah; Whoever studies halachos every day, he is assured of life in the World-to-Come, for it is said, The ways (halichos) of the world are His." Do not read halichos, but halachos:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Tana devei eliyahu kol hashoneh halachot b''chol yom muvtach lo shehu ben olam haba shene''emar halichot olam lo al tikrei halichot ela halachot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אָמַר רַבִּי חֲנִינָא. תַּלְמִידֵי חֲכָמִים מַרְבִּים שָׁלוֹם בָּעוֹלָם. שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר וְכָל בָּנַֽיִךְ לִמּוּדֵי יְהֹוָה וְרַב שְׁלוֹם בָּנָֽיךְ: אַל תִּקְרֵי בָּנָֽיךְ אֶלָּא בּוֹנָֽיךְ: שָׁלוֹם רָב לְאֹהֲבֵי תוֹרָתֶֽךָ וְאֵין לָֽמוֹ מִכְשׁוֹל: יְהִי שָׁלוֹם בְּחֵילֵךְ שַׁלְוָה בְּאַרְמְּנוֹתָֽיךְ לְמַֽעַן אַחַי וְרֵעָי אֲדַבְּרָה נָא שָׁלוֹם בָּךְ: לְמַֽעַן בֵּית יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֲבַקְ֒שָׁה טוֹב לָךְ: יְהֹוָה עֹז לְעַמּוֹ יִתֵּן יְהֹוָה יְבָרֵךְ אֶת עַמּוֹ בַשָּׁלוֹם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Rabbi Eliezer said on behalf of Rabbi Chanina: the disciples of the wise increase peace in the world, for it is said: ‘and all your children will be disciples of Adonoy''s [Torah]; and great will be the peace of your children.'' Do not read banayich [your children] but read bonayich [your builders]. Great is the peace of those who love Your Torah, and they will have no stumbling block [misfortune]. Let there be peace within your moats, serenity within your palaces. For the sake of my brethren and companions, I will say: ‘peace be with you.'' For the sake of the House of Adonoy, our God, I will seek [pray for] your good. Adonoy will give strength to His people, Adonoy will bless His people with peace.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Amar rabi elazar amar rabi chanina.
Talmidei chachamim marbim shalom baolam.
Shene''emar ve chol banayich limudei Adonai ve rav shelom banaych.
Al tikrei banaych ela bonaych.
Shalom rav leohavei toratecha ve ein lamo michshol.
Yehi shalom b''cheilech shalva b''armenotaych lema''an achai ve reai adabera na shalom bach.
Lema''an beit Adonai Eloheinu avaksha tov lach.
Adonai oz leamo yiten Adonai yevarech et amo vashalom.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','קדיש דרבנן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Mourners say the following Kaddish d''Rabanan','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh.
B''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','עַל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעַל רַבָּנָן וְעַל תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן וְעַל כָּל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן, וְעַל כָּל מָאן דְּעָסְ֒קִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא, דִּי בְאַתְרָא הָדֵין וְדִי בְכָל אֲתַר וַאֲתַר, יְהֵא לְהוֹן וּלְכוֹן שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמִין וְחַיִּין אֲרִיכִין וּמְזוֹנָא רְוִיחֵי וּפוּרְקָנָא מִן קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דְבִשְׁמַיָּא וְאַרְעָא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','Upon Israel, and upon our Sages, and upon their disciples, and upon all the disciples of their disciples, and upon all those who engage in Torah study in this land and in every land. May there be unto them and unto you abundant peace, favor, kindness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance and redemption from their Father Who is in heaven and on earth, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Al Yisrael ve al rabanan ve al talmideihon ve al kol talmidei talmideihon,
ve al kol man deasekin b''orayta,
di ve atra hadein ve di ve chal atar va''atar,
yeheh lehon ulechon shelama rabah china ve chisda ve rachamin ve chayin arichin umezona revichei ufurekana min kodam avuhon devishmaya ve ara ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and a good life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim tovim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא בְּרַחֲמָיו יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, in His mercy, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-kaveh','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu b''rachamav ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Kaveh'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','אחר כל התפלות אומר עלינו לשבח. בפרק ר׳ אליעזר אומר שבח גדול יש בעלינו לשבח על כן צריך לאומרו מעומד ותמצא עלינו עולה בגימטריא ומעומד. ושמעתי שיהושע תקנו בשעה שכבש יריחו וחתם בו שם קטנותו למפרע. (כל בו)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Kol Bo writes that Joshua authored this prayer when he captured Jericho. Taken from the Musaf service of Rosh Hashana, it serves as the closing prayer of all the daily services. As ruled by Tur (Orach Chaim 133), it is said while standing.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֺּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֺא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֺּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּ֒לִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְ֒עִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְ֒כֵי הַמְּ֒לָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁ֒כִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְ֒הֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֺהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of Kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: And You shall know this day and take into Your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia,
va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu,
shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz,
umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al,
ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim,
hu Eloheinu ein od,
emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','(וְ)עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁ֒מֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁ֒עֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְ֒בוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּ֒לוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֺךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְ֒כוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְ֒עֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֺךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: Adonoy will reign forever and ever. And it is said: And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','(ve al) ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha,
lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz,
yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu,
ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu,
vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha,
ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed,
ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod,
kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','אַל תִּירָא מִפַּחַד פִּתאֹם וּמִשֹׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹא עֻֽצוּ עֵצָה וְתֻפָר דַּבְּ֒רוּ דָבָר וְלֹא יָקוּם כִּי עִמָּנוּ אֵל: וְעַד זִקְנָה אֲנִי הוּא וְעַד שֵׂיבָה אֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל: אֲנִי עָשִֽׂיתִי וַאֲנִי אֶשָׂא וַאֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל וַאֲמַלֵּט:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Do not fear sudden terror nor the destruction of the wicked when it comes take counsel together but it will be foiled speak the word and it will not stand for God is with us. To Your old age I am [with You], to Your older years I will sustain You, I have made You, and I will carry You, I will sustain You and save You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Al tira mipachad pitom umishoat reshaim ki tavo utzu etza ve tufar daberu davar ve lo yakum ki imanu el.
Ve ad zikna ani hu ve ad seiva ani esbol.
Ani asiti va''ani esa va''ani esbol va''amalet.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','כתב הלבוש בסי קל"ג אחר עלינו אומרים קדיש יתום. ואפילו אין יתום של תוך י"ב חודש בבית הכנסת יאמר אותו אחר מי שאין לו אב ואם. והטעם שהרי לעולם צריכין לומר קדיש אחר שאמרו פסוקים. ובעלינו יש גם כן פסוקים וצריכים קדיש אחריו. אלא שנהגו בקדיש זה להניחו ליתום שמת אביו ואמו תוך שנה זו. מפני שיש יתומים קטנים או אפילו גדולים שאינם יכולין להיות שלוחי ציבור ולומר קדיש וברכו אחר אביו ואמו. וכבר ידענו ממעשה דרבי עקיבא [במס'' כלה רבתי פ"ב] תועלת הגדולה שיש למתים כשיש להם בן האומר קדיש וברכו ויותר בתוך שנה ראשונה. לכך תקנו והניחו קדיש זה. שאין צריך שום דבר יותר ליתומים הן קטנים הן גדולים. ומפני שתקנוהו ליתומים אין נוהגין לאמרו כלל מי שיש לו אב או אם שמא אביו או אמו יקפידו בכך משום אל יפתח אדם פיו לשטן ויאמר אתה מקוה למיתתנו. לפיכך אם אין אביו או אמו מקפידין בכך יכול לאומרו אפילו מי שיש לו אב ואם. ע"כ.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Although the Kaddish contains no reference to the dead, it has been recited by mourners for many centuries. The tradition of the mourner''s Kaddish began with the following incident: Once, while walking, Rabbi Akiva met a man who had died some time before and was suffering the torments of Purgatory. He pleaded with Rabbi Akiva to go to his home town and teach his son to recite the Kaddish and Borechu, for this would save him from the terrible punishments. Rabbi Akiva and his Court then instituted the practice of mourners reciting the Kaddish, for until then it had been limited to the Chazzan''s reciting it only after the services or after a sermon (See Tana D''vei Eliyahu Zuta, 17: Zohar Parshas Noach).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming if His Messiah in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן, יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen,
yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-shacharit-aleinu','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Shacharit, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','he','וְעַתָּה֙ יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל מָ֚ה יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ שֹׁאֵ֖ל מֵעִמָּ֑ךְ כִּ֣י אִם־לְ֠יִרְאָה אֶת־יְהוָ֨ה אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ לָלֶ֤כֶת בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו֙ וּלְאַהֲבָ֣ה אֹת֔וֹ וְלַֽעֲבֹד֙ אֶת־יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ֖ וּבְכָל־נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃ לִשְׁמֹ֞ר אֶת־מִצְוֺ֤ת יְהוָה֙ וְאֶת־חֻקֹּתָ֔יו אֲשֶׁ֛ר אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּ֑וֹם לְט֖וֹב לָֽךְ׃ הֵ֚ן לַיהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם וּשְׁמֵ֣י הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם הָאָ֖רֶץ וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר־בָּֽהּ׃ רַ֧ק בַּאֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ חָשַׁ֥ק יְהוָ֖ה לְאַהֲבָ֣ה אוֹתָ֑ם וַיִּבְחַ֞ר בְּזַרְעָ֣ם אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם בָּכֶ֛ם מִכָּל־הָעַמִּ֖ים כַּיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּה׃ וּמַלְתֶּ֕ם אֵ֖ת עָרְלַ֣ת לְבַבְכֶ֑ם וְעָ֨רְפְּכֶ֔ם לֹ֥א תַקְשׁ֖וּ עֽוֹד׃ כִּ֚י יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם ה֚וּא אֱלֹהֵ֣י הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים וַאֲדֹנֵ֖י הָאֲדֹנִ֑ים הָאֵ֨ל הַגָּדֹ֤ל הַגִּבֹּר֙ וְהַנּוֹרָ֔א אֲשֶׁר֙ לֹא־יִשָּׂ֣א פָנִ֔ים וְלֹ֥א יִקַּ֖ח שֹֽׁחַד׃ עֹשֶׂ֛ה מִשְׁפַּ֥ט יָת֖וֹם וְאַלְמָנָ֑ה וְאֹהֵ֣ב גֵּ֔ר לָ֥תֶת ל֖וֹ לֶ֥חֶם וְשִׂמְלָֽה׃ וַאֲהַבְתֶּ֖ם אֶת־הַגֵּ֑ר כִּֽי־גֵרִ֥ים הֱיִיתֶ֖ם בְּאֶ֥רֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם׃ אֶת־יְהוָ֧ה אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ תִּירָ֖א אֹת֣וֹ תַעֲבֹ֑ד וּב֣וֹ תִדְבָּ֔ק וּבִשְׁמ֖וֹ תִּשָּׁבֵֽעַ׃ ה֥וּא תְהִלָּתְךָ֖ וְה֣וּא אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ אֲשֶׁר־עָשָׂ֣ה אִתְּךָ֗ אֶת־הַגְּדֹלֹ֤ת וְאֶת־הַנּֽוֹרָאֹת֙ הָאֵ֔לֶּה אֲשֶׁ֥ר רָא֖וּ עֵינֶֽיךָ׃ בְּשִׁבְעִ֣ים נֶ֔פֶשׁ יָרְד֥וּ אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ מִצְרָ֑יְמָהּ וְעַתָּ֗ה שָֽׂמְךָ֙ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם לָרֹֽב׃ וְאָ֣הַבְתָּ֔ אֵ֖ת יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣ מִשְׁמַרְתּ֗וֹ וְחֻקֹּתָ֧יו וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֛יו וּמִצְוֺתָ֖יו כָּל־הַיָּמִֽים׃ וִֽידַעְתֶּם֮ הַיּוֹם֒ כִּ֣י ׀ לֹ֣א אֶת־בְּנֵיכֶ֗ם אֲשֶׁ֤ר לֹֽא־יָדְעוּ֙ וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר לֹא־רָא֔וּ אֶת־מוּסַ֖ר יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם אֶת־גָּדְל֕וֹ אֶת־יָדוֹ֙ הַחֲזָקָ֔ה וּזְרֹע֖וֹ הַנְּטוּיָֽה׃ וְאֶת־אֹֽתֹתָיו֙ וְאֶֽת־מַעֲשָׂ֔יו אֲשֶׁ֥ר עָשָׂ֖ה בְּת֣וֹךְ מִצְרָ֑יִם לְפַרְעֹ֥ה מֶֽלֶךְ־מִצְרַ֖יִם וּלְכָל־אַרְצֽוֹ׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשָׂה֩ לְחֵ֨יל מִצְרַ֜יִם לְסוּסָ֣יו וּלְרִכְבּ֗וֹ אֲשֶׁ֨ר הֵצִ֜יף אֶת־מֵ֤י יַם־סוּף֙ עַל־פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם בְּרָדְפָ֖ם אַחֲרֵיכֶ֑ם וַיְאַבְּדֵ֣ם יְהוָ֔ה עַ֖ד הַיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר עָשָׂ֛ה לָכֶ֖ם בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר עַד־בֹּאֲכֶ֖ם עַד־הַמָּק֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃ וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר עָשָׂ֜ה לְדָתָ֣ן וְלַאֲבִירָ֗ם בְּנֵ֣י אֱלִיאָב֮ בֶּן־רְאוּבֵן֒ אֲשֶׁ֨ר פָּצְתָ֤ה הָאָ֙רֶץ֙ אֶת־פִּ֔יהָ וַתִּבְלָעֵ֥ם וְאֶת־בָּתֵּיהֶ֖ם וְאֶת־אָהֳלֵיהֶ֑ם וְאֵ֤ת כָּל־הַיְקוּם֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר בְּרַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם בְּקֶ֖רֶב כָּל־יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ כִּ֤י עֵֽינֵיכֶם֙ הָֽרֹאֹ֔ת אֶת־כָּל־מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה יְהוָ֖ה הַגָּדֹ֑ל אֲשֶׁ֖ר עָשָֽׂה׃ וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙ אֶת־כָּל־הַמִּצְוָ֔ה אֲשֶׁ֛ר אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּ֑וֹם לְמַ֣עַן תֶּחֶזְק֗וּ וּבָאתֶם֙ וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם אֶת־הָאָ֔רֶץ אֲשֶׁ֥ר אַתֶּ֛ם עֹבְרִ֥ים שָׁ֖מָּה לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃ וּלְמַ֨עַן תַּאֲרִ֤יכוּ יָמִים֙ עַל־הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה אֲשֶׁר֩ נִשְׁבַּ֨ע יְהוָ֧ה לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶ֛ם לָתֵ֥ת לָהֶ֖ם וּלְזַרְעָ֑ם אֶ֛רֶץ זָבַ֥ת חָלָ֖ב וּדְבָֽשׁ׃','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','en','Deuteronomy 10:12-11:9 And now Israel, what does Adonoy, your God, require of you, but to fear Adonoy, your God, to walk in all His ways, and to love Him and to serve Adonoy, your God, with all your heart and with all your soul. To keep the commandments of Adonoy and His decrees, which I command you this day. Behold, the heaven and the highest of heavens belong to Adonoy, your God, the earth and all that is in it. Yet only in your fathers did Adonoy delight, to love them, and He chose their offspring after them, even you among all the peoples as [it is] this day. Circumcise the barrier of your heart, and be stiffnecked no longer. For Adonoy, your God, is God of all powers and the Master of all masters, the Almighty, the Great, the Powerful, the Awesome, Who has no regard for personages and takes no bribes. Who does justice for the orphan and the widow, and loves the stranger, giving him food and clothing. You must love the stranger for you were strangers in the land of Egypt. You must fear Adonoy, your God, serve Him, cleave to Him, and swear by His Name. He is your praise, and He is your God, Who did with you all these great and awesome things that your eyes have seen. With seventy people your fathers descended to Egypt, and now Adonoy, your God, has made you as abundant as the stars of heaven. [Therefore] you shall love Adonoy, your God, and keep His trust, His decrees, His statutes, and His commandments all the days. And you should know this day, that it is not with your children who have not known and who did not experience the chastisement of Adonoy, your God, His mighty hand, and His outstretched arm. His signs and His deeds that He performed in the midst of Egypt, to Pharaoh, the king of Egypt, and to all his land. And what He did to the army of Egypt, to their horses, and to their chariots; how He made the water of the Sea of Reeds drown them as they pursued you, and Adonoy destroyed them to this very day. And what He did for you in the wilderness, until you came into this place. And what He did unto Dathan and Aviram, the sons of Eliav, son of Reuben, when the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them, and their households, their tents and all the substance that was in their possession in the midst of all Israel. But your eyes have seen all the great deeds of Adonoy, that He performed. You should [therefore] keep all the commandments which I command you this day, so you will be strong, and go in and possess the land, to which you are passing over to possess it. And in order to prolong your days upon the land Adonoy swore to your fathers to give to them and to their offspring; a land flowing with milk and honey.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','transliteration','Ve atah Yisrael ma Adonai Elohecha shoel meimach ki im leyira et Adonai Elohecha lalechet b''chol derachav uleahava oto ve la''avod et Adonai Elohecha b''chol levavecha uvechol nafshecha lishmor et mitzvot Adonai ve et chukotav asher anochi metzavecha hayom letov lach hen laAdonai Elohecha hashamayim ushemei hashamayim ha''aretz ve chol asher bah rak ba''avoteicha chashak Adonai leahava otam vayivchar b''zaram achareihem bachem mikol ha''amim kayom hazeh umaltem et orlat levavchem ve orpechem lo takshu od ki Adonai Elohechem hu Elohei haelohim va''adonei ha''adonim hael hagadol hagibor ve hanora asher lo yisa fanim ve lo yikach shochad oseh mishpat yatom ve almana ve ohev ger latet lo lechem ve simla va''ahavtem et hager ki gerim heyitem b''eretz mitzrayim et Adonai Elohecha tira oto ta''avod uvo tidbak uvishmo tishavea hu tehilatecha ve hu Elohecha asher asa itecha et hagedolot ve et hanoraot haeleh asher rau eineicha b''shivim nefesh yaredu avoteicha mitzrayemah ve atah samecha Adonai Elohecha k''chochevei hashamayim larov ve''ahavta et Adonai Elohecha ve shamarta mishmarto ve chukotav umishpatav umitzvotav kol hayamim vidatem hayom ki lo et b''neichem asher lo yadeu va''asher lo rau et musar Adonai Elohechem et godlo et yado hachazaka uzero''o hanetuya ve et ototav ve et ma''asav asher asa b''toch mitzrayim lefaroh melech mitzrayim ulechol artzo va''asher asa lecheil mitzrayim lesusav ulerichbo asher hetzif et mei yam suf al peneihem b''radefam achareichem vayeabedem Adonai ad hayom hazeh va''asher asa lachem bamidbar ad boachem ad hamakom hazeh va''asher asa ledatan ve la''aviram b''nei eliav ben reuven asher patzeta ha''aretz et piha vativlaem ve et bateihem ve et oholeihem ve et kol hayekum asher b''ragleihem b''kerev kol Yisrael ki eineichem haro''ot et kol ma''aseh Adonai hagadol asher asa ushemartem et kol hamitzva asher anochi metzavecha hayom lema''an techezku uvatem virishtem et ha''aretz asher atem overim shama lerishtah ulema''an ta''arichu yamim al ha''adama asher nishba Adonai la''avoteichem latet lahem ulezaram eretz zavat chalav udevash','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','he','אין אומרים בשבת ויו"ט:','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','en','The following prayer is omitted on Shabbos and Yom Tov','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֺוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתִּטַּע אַהֲבָתְ֒ךָ וְיִרְאָתְ֒ךָ בְּלִבִּי וּבְלֵב כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל עַמֶּֽךָ לְיִרְאָה אֶת שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא בְּכָל לְבָבֵֽנוּ וּבְכָל נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ, יִרְאַת הָרוֹמְ֒מוּת שֶׁל אֵין סוֹֺף בָּרוּךְ וְיִתעַלֶּה שִׁמְךָ, כִּי גָדוֹל אַתָּה וְנוֹרָא שְׁמֶֽךָ. אָמֵן, סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, my God, and the God of my fathers, to implant Your love and fear of You in my heart and in the heart of all Israel, Your people, to fear Your Great, Mighty and Awesome Name with all our heart and with all our soul, for You are great and Your Name is awesome. Amein. Selah.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-fear-of-god','transliteration','Yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai shetita ahavatecha ve yiratecha b''libi uvelev kol Yisrael amecha leyira et shimcha hagadol hagivor ve hanora b''chol levavenu uvechol nafshenu,
yirat haromemut shel ein sovof baruch ve yitaleh shimcha,
ki gadol atah ve nora shemecha.
Amen,
sela.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Fear of God'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','he','וְהָיָה֩ כִֽי־יָבֹ֨אוּ עָלֶ֜יךָ כָּל־הַדְּבָרִ֣ים הָאֵ֗לֶּה הַבְּרָכָה֙ וְהַקְּלָלָ֔ה אֲשֶׁ֥ר נָתַ֖תִּי לְפָנֶ֑יךָ וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ֙ אֶל־לְבָבֶ֔ךָ בְּכָל־הַגּוֹיִ֔ם אֲשֶׁ֧ר הִדִּיחֲךָ֛ יְהוָ֥ה אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ שָֽׁמָּה׃ וְשַׁבְתָּ֞ עַד־יְהוָ֤ה אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙ וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֣ בְקֹל֔וֹ כְּכֹ֛ל אֲשֶׁר־אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּ֑וֹם אַתָּ֣ה וּבָנֶ֔יךָ בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ֖ וּבְכָל־נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃ וְשָׁ֨ב יְהוָ֧ה אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ אֶת־שְׁבוּתְךָ֖ וְרִחֲמֶ֑ךָ וְשָׁ֗ב וְקִבֶּצְךָ֙ מִכָּל־הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים אֲשֶׁ֧ר הֱפִֽיצְךָ֛ יְהוָ֥ה אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ שָֽׁמָּה׃ אִם־יִהְיֶ֥ה נִֽדַּחֲךָ֖ בִּקְצֵ֣ה הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם מִשָּׁ֗ם יְקַבֶּצְךָ֙ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ וּמִשָּׁ֖ם יִקָּחֶֽךָ׃ וֶהֱבִֽיאֲךָ֞ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ אֶל־הָאָ֛רֶץ אֲשֶׁר־יָרְשׁ֥וּ אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֑הּ וְהֵיטִֽבְךָ֥ וְהִרְבְּךָ֖ מֵאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃ וּמָ֨ל יְהוָ֧ה אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ אֶת־לְבָבְךָ֖ וְאֶת־לְבַ֣ב זַרְעֶ֑ךָ לְאַהֲבָ֞ה אֶת־יְהוָ֧ה אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ֥ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ֖ לְמַ֥עַן חַיֶּֽיךָ׃ וְנָתַן֙ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ אֵ֥ת כָּל־הָאָל֖וֹת הָאֵ֑לֶּה עַל־אֹיְבֶ֥יךָ וְעַל־שֹׂנְאֶ֖יךָ אֲשֶׁ֥ר רְדָפֽוּךָ׃ וְאַתָּ֣ה תָשׁ֔וּב וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֖ בְּק֣וֹל יְהוָ֑ה וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙ אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֺתָ֔יו אֲשֶׁ֛ר אָנֹכִ֥י מְצַוְּךָ֖ הַיּֽוֹם׃ וְהוֹתִֽירְךָ֩ יְהוָ֨ה אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ בְּכֹ֣ל ׀ מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה יָדֶ֗ךָ בִּפְרִ֨י בִטְנְךָ֜ וּבִפְרִ֧י בְהֶמְתְּךָ֛ וּבִפְרִ֥י אַדְמָתְךָ֖ לְטוֹבָ֑ה כִּ֣י ׀ יָשׁ֣וּב יְהוָ֗ה לָשׂ֤וּשׂ עָלֶ֙יךָ֙ לְט֔וֹב כַּאֲשֶׁר־שָׂ֖שׂ עַל־אֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃ כִּ֣י תִשְׁמַ֗ע בְּקוֹל֙ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ לִשְׁמֹ֤ר מִצְוֺתָיו֙ וְחֻקֹּתָ֔יו הַכְּתוּבָ֕ה בְּסֵ֥פֶר הַתּוֹרָ֖ה הַזֶּ֑ה כִּ֤י תָשׁוּב֙ אֶל־יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ֖ וּבְכָל־נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','en','Deuteronomy 30:1-11 And it will come to pass when all these things come upon you, the blessing and the curse which I have set before you, that you will take it to heart in the midst of all the nations to which Adonoy, your God, has driven you. Then you will return unto Adonoy, your God, and obey His voice according to everything that I command you this day, you and your children, with all your heart and with all your soul. And then Adonoy, your God, will return your captivity and have compassion upon you; and He will return and gather you from among all the peoples where Adonoy, your God, has scattered you. Even if your scattered ones will be dispersed unto the outermost parts of heaven, from there Adonoy, your God, will gather you, and from there, He will take you. And Adonoy, your God, will bring you into the land which your forefathers possessed, and you will possess it; and He will do good to you and increase you even more than your fathers. Adonoy, your God, will circumcise your heart, and the hearts of your descendants, to love Adonoy, your God, with all your heart and with all your soul, that you may live. Then Adonoy, your God, will set all these curses upon your enemies, and upon those who hate you, who have pursued you. But you will repent and listen to the voice of Adonoy, and perform all His commandments that I command you this day. And Adonoy, your God, will cause you to prosper in all your activities, in the fruit of your womb, in the fruit of your cattle, and the fruit of your soil, for good; for Adonoy will rejoice over you for goodness as He rejoiced over your fathers. For you will then obey the voice of Adonoy, your God, to observe His commandments and His decrees that are written in this Seifer Torah; for you will then return to Adonoy, your God, with all your heart and with all your soul.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','transliteration','Ve haya chi yavou aleicha kol hadevarim haeleh haberacha ve hakelala asher natati lefanecha vahashevota el levavecha b''chol hagoyim asher hidichacha Adonai Elohecha shama ve shavta ad Adonai Elohecha ve shamata ve kolo k''chol asher anochi metzavecha hayom atah uvaneicha b''chol levavecha uvechol nafshecha ve shav Adonai Elohecha et shevutecha ve richamecha ve shav ve kibetzcha mikol ha''amim asher hefitzecha Adonai Elohecha shama im yihyeh nidachacha biktzeh hashamayim misham yekabetzcha Adonai Elohecha umisham yikachecha veheviacha Adonai Elohecha el ha''aretz asher yareshu avoteicha virishtah ve heitivecha ve hirbecha meavoteicha umal Adonai Elohecha et levavecha ve et levav zarecha leahava et Adonai Elohecha b''chol levavecha uvechol nafshecha lema''an chayeicha ve natan Adonai Elohecha et kol ha''alot haeleh al oyeveicha ve al sone''eicha asher redafucha ve atah tashuv ve shamata b''kol Adonai ve asita et kol mitzvotav asher anochi metzavecha hayom ve hotirecha Adonai Elohecha b''chol ma''aseh yadecha bifri vitnecha uvifri ve hemtecha uvifri admatecha letova ki yashuv Adonai lasus aleicha letov ka''asher sas al avoteicha ki tishma b''kol Adonai Elohecha lishmor mitzvotav ve chukotav haketuva b''sefer hatora hazeh ki tashuv el Adonai Elohecha b''chol levavecha uvechol nafshecha','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','he','אין אומרים בשבת ויו"ט:','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','en','(The following prayer is not recited on Shabbos and Yom Tov.)','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֺוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתַּחְתּוֹר חֲתִּירָה מִתַּֽחַת כִּסֵּא כְבוֹדֶֽ֒ךָ לְהַחֲזִיר בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה שְׁלֵמָה לְכָל פּוֹשְׁ֒עֵי עַמְּ֒ךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל וּבִכְ֒לָלָם תַּחֲזִירֵֽנִי בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה שְׁלֵמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ כִּי יְמִינְ֒ךָ פְשׁוּטָה לְקַבֵּל שָׁבִים וְרוֹצֶה אַתָּה בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה. אָמֵן, סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','en','May it be Your will Adonoy, my God, and the God of my fathers, to construct a passage beneath Your Throne of Glory in order to bring back in perfect repentance all the transgressors of Your people, the House of Israel. And among them, bring me back unto You in perfect repentance, for Your right hand is outstretched to receive those who repent, for You desire repentance. Amein. Selah.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-additional-prayers-chapter-of-repentance','transliteration','Yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai shetachtor chatira mitachat kiseh chevodecha lehachazir bitshuva shelema lechol poshe''ei amecha beit Yisrael uvichlalam tachazireni bitshuva shelema lefanecha ki yeminecha feshuta lekabel shavim ve rotzeh atah bitshuva.
Amen,
sela.','Siddur Sefard, Additional Prayers , Chapter of Repentance'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: צַו אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם אֶת־קָרְבָּנִי לַחְמִי לְאִשַּׁי רֵֽיחַ נִיחֹחִי תִּשְׁמְ֒רוּ לְהַקְרִיב לִי בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ: וְאָמַרְתָּ לָהֶם זֶה הָאִשֶּׁה אֲשֶׁר תַּקְרִֽיבוּ לַיהוָֹה כְּבָשִׂים בְּנֵי־שָׁנָה תְמִימִם שְׁנַֽיִם לַיּוֹם עֹלָה תָמִיד: אֶת־הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ אֶחָד תַּעֲשֶׂה בַבֹּֽקֶר וְאֵת הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הַשֵּׁנִי תַּעֲשֶׂה בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם: וַֽעֲשִׂירִית הָאֵיפָה סֹֽלֶת לְמִנְחָה בְּלוּלָה בְּשֶֽׁמֶן כָּתִית רְבִיעִת הַהִין: עֹלַת תָּמִיד הָעֲשֻׂיָה בְּהַר סִינַי לְרֵֽיחַ נִיחֹֽחַ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה: וְנִסְכּוֹ רְבִיעִת הַהִין לַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הָאֶחָד בַּקֹּֽדֶשׁ הַסֵּךְ נֶֽסֶךְ שֵׁכָר לַיהוָֹה: וְאֵת הַכֶּֽבֶשׂ הַשֵּׁנִי תַּעֲשֶׂה בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם כְּמִנְחַת הַבֹּֽקֶר וּכְנִסְכּוֹ תַּעֲשֶׂה אִשֵּׁה רֵֽיחַ נִיחֹֽחַ לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','(Numbers 28:1-8) And Adonoy spoke to Moses to say: Command the Children of Israel, and say to them: My offering, My food, to be consumed by My fires, a pleasing odor to Me, You shall be diligent to bring unto Me, at its fixed time. And you will say to them: This is the fire-offering that you will bring unto Adonoy: [male] lambs, in their first year, without blemish, two [of them] each day, as a constant burnt-offering. Offer one lamb in the morning, and the second lamb, offer in the afternoon. And a tenth of an ephah of fine flour as a meal-offering, mixed with oil of crushed [olives] measuring one-fourth of a hin. [This is] a constant burnt-offering as offered at Mount Sinai for a pleasing odor, a fire-offering to Adonoy. And its libation will be a fourth of a hin for the one lamb; in the Holy [Sanctuary] you will pour out a drink-offering of strong wine to Adonoy. And the second lamb you will offer in the afternoon; as the meal-offering of the morning [together] with its libation, you shall offer a fire-offering of pleasing odor to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Vayedaber Adonai el Moshe lemor.
Tzav et b''nei Yisrael ve amarta alehem et korbani lachmi leishai reiach nichochi tishmeru lehakriv li b''moado.
Ve amarta lahem zeh haisheh asher takrivu laAdonai k''vasim b''nei shana temimim shenayim layom ola tamid.
Et hakeves echad ta''aseh vaboker ve et hakeves hasheni ta''aseh bein ha''arbayim.
Va''asirit haeifa solet lemincha b''lula b''shemen katit revi''it hahin.
Olat tamid ha''asuya b''har sinai lereiach nichoach isheh laAdonai.
Ve nisko revi''it hahin lakeves haechad bakodesh hasech nesech shechar laAdonai.
Ve et hakeves hasheni ta''aseh bein ha''arbayim k''minchat haboker uchenisko ta''aseh isheh reiach nichoach laAdonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','וְשָׁחַט אֹתוֹ עַל יֶֽרֶךְ הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ צָפֹֽנָה לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה וְזָרְקוּ בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן הַכֹּהֲנִים אֶת־דָּמוֹ עַל־הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ סָבִיב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','(Leviticus 1:11) And he will slaughter it on the north side of the Altar, before Adonoy; and Aaron''s sons, the Kohanim, will sprinkle its blood all around the Altar.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Ve shachat oto al yerech hamizbeach tzafona lifnei Adonai ve zareku b''nei aharon hakohanim et damo al hamizbeach saviv.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ, יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ, שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא אֲמִירָה זוּ, חֲשׁוּבָה וּמְקֻבֶּֽלֶת, וּמְרֻצָּה לְפָנֶֽיךָ, כְּאִלּוּ הִקְרַֽבְנוּ קָרְבַּן הַתָּמִיד בְּמוֹעֲדוֹ, וּבִמְ֒קוֹמוֹ וּכְהִלְכָתוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers, that this recitation be important, acceptable and desirable before You, as if we sacrificed the daily burnt-offering at its proper time, in its proper place and according to its laws.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Yehi ratzon milefaneicha,
Adonai Eloheinu velohei avoteinu,
sheteheh amira zu,
chashuva umekubelet,
umerutza lefanecha,
k''ilu hikravenu korban hatamid b''moado,
uvimkomo uchehilchato.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','אַתָּה הוּא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ שֶׁהִקְטִֽירוּ אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ אֶת קְטֹֽרֶת הַסַּמִּים בִּזְמַן שֶׁבֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ הָיָה קַיָּם כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתָ אוֹתָם עַל יְדֵי משֶׁה נְבִיאֶֽךָ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','You are Adonoy, our God, before Whom our fathers burned the incense of spices when the Holy Temple was standing, as You commanded them by the hand of Moses Your prophet, as it is written in Your Torah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Atah hu Adonai Eloheinu shehiktiru avoteinu lefanecha et k''toret hasamim bizman shebeit hamikdash haya kayam ka''asher tzivita otam al yedei Moshe neviecha kakatuv b''toratecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה קַח־לְךָ סַמִּים נָטָף וּשְׁחֵֽלֶת וְחֶלְבְּנָה סַמִּים וּלְבֹנָה זַכָּה בַּד בְּבַד יִהְיֶה: וְעָשִֽׂיתָ אֹתָהּ קְטֹֽרֶת רֹֽקַח מַעֲשֵׂה רוֹקֵֽחַ מְמֻלָּח טָהוֹר קֹֽדֶשׁ: וְשָׁחַקְתָּ מִמֶּֽנָּה הָדֵק וְנָתַתָּה מִמֶּֽנָּה לִפְנֵי הָעֵדֻת בְּאֹֽהֶל מוֹעֵד אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לְךָ שָֽׁמָּה קֹֽדֶשׁ קָדָשִׁים תִּהְיֶה לָכֶם: וְנֶאֱמַר','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','(Exodus 30:34-36) And Adonoy said to Moses, Take for yourself spices— stacte, onycha, and galbanum— spices, and pure frankincense, [they] shall be in equal weights. You will make it into incense, a compound mixed by a compounder, salted, undefiled, and holy. You will pulverize some of it very fine, and place it before the [Ark of] Testimony in the Tent of Meeting, where I will meet with you; it will be to you holy of holies." It is also written:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Vayomer Adonai el Moshe kach lecha samim nataf ushechelet ve chelbena samim ulevona zaka bad b''vad yihyeh.
Ve asita otah k''toret rokach ma''aseh rokeach memulach tahor kodesh.
Ve shachakta mimena hadek ve natata mimena lifnei haedut b''ohel moed asher ivaed lecha shama kodesh kadashim tihyeh lachem.
Ve ne''emar','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','וְהִקְטִיר עָלָיו אַהֲרֹן קְטֹֽרֶת סַמִּים בַּבֹּֽקֶר בַּבֹּֽקֶר בְּהֵיטִיבוֹ אֶת־הַנֵּרֹת יַקְטִירֶֽנָּה: וּבְהַעֲלֹת אַהֲרֹן אֶת־הַנֵּרֹת בֵּין הָֽעַרְבַּֽיִם יַקְטִירֶֽנָּה קְטֹֽרֶת תָּמִיד לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','(Exodus 30:7-8) And Aaron shall burn upon it [the Altar] incense of spices every morning; when he cleans the lamps he will burn it. And when Aaron lights the lamps in the afternoon, he will burn it; a constant incense-offering before Adonoy throughout your generations.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Ve hiktir alav aharon k''toret samim baboker baboker b''heitivo et hanerot yaktirena.
Uveha''alot aharon et hanerot bein ha''arbayim yaktirena k''toret tamid lifnei Adonai ledoroteichem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','תָּנוּ רַבָּנָן פִּטּוּם הַקְּ֒טֹֽרֶת כֵּיצַד שְׁלֹש מֵאוֹת וְשִׁשִּׁים וּשְׁמוֹנָה מָנִים הָיוּ בָהּ, שְׁלֹש מֵאוֹת וְשִׁשִּׁים וַחֲמִשָּׁה כְּמִנְיַן יְמוֹת הַחַמָּה מָנֶה לְכָל יוֹם, פְּרַס בַּשַּׁחֲרִית וּפְרַס בֵּין הָעַרְבָּֽיִם, וּשְׁלשָׁה מָנִים יְתֵרִים שֶׁמֵּהֶם מַכְנִיס כֹּהֵן גָּדוֹל מְלֹא חָפְנָיו בְּיוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים, וּמַחֲזִירָן לְמַכְתֶּֽשֶׁת בְּעֶֽרֶב יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים, וְשׁוֹחֲקָן יָפֶה יָפֶה כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא דַקָּה מִן הַדַּקָּה, וְאַחַד עָשָׂר סַמָּנִים הָֽיוּ בָהּ, וְאֵֽלּוּ הֵן הַצֳּרִי וְהַצִּפֹּֽרֶן הַחֶלְבְּנָה וְהַלְּ֒בוֹנָה מִשְׁקַל שִׁבְעִים שִׁבְעִים מָנֶה, מוֹר וּקְצִיעָה שִׁבֹּֽלֶת נֵרְדְּ וְכַרְכֹּם מִשְׁקַל שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר שִׁשָּׁה עָשָׂר מָנֶה, הַקּשְׁטְ שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר וְקִלּוּפָה שְׁלשָׁה וְקִנָּמוֹן תִּשְׁעָה, בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה תִּשְׁעָה קַבִּין, יֵין קַפְרִיסִין סְאִין תְּלָתָא וְקַבִּין תְּלָתָא, וְאִם אֵין לוֹ יֵין קַפְרִיסִין מֵבִיא חֲמַר חִוַּרְיָן עַתִּיק, מֶֽלַח סְדוֹמִית רֹֽבַע הַקָּב, מַעֲלֶה עָשָׁן כָּל שֶׁהוּא, רַבִּי נָתָן הַבַּבְלִי אוֹמֵר אַף כִּפַּת הַיַּרְדֵּן כָּל שֶׁהוּא, וְאִם נָֽתַן בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ פְּסָלָהּ וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','(Maseches Kreisos 6a; Jerusalem Talmud, Maseches Yoma 4:5) The Rabbis taught: How was the incense compounded? Three hundred and sixty-eight manim were comprised therein, three hundred and sixty-five corresponding to the number of days in the solar year, one maneh for each day— half in the morning and half in the afternoon. From the three remaining manim the Kohein Gadol brought two handfuls [into the Holy of Holies] on Yom Kippur; [for which purpose] they were put back into the mortar on the eve of Yom Kippur, and ground [again] very thoroughly, in order to make them very fine. Eleven kinds of spices were used for it. They were: 1) balm, 2) onycha, 3) galbanum, 4) frankincense— by weight, seventy maneh of each; 5) myrrh, 6) cassia, 7) spikenard and 8) saffron— in weight sixteen maneh of each; 9) twelve maneh of costus, 10) three of aromatic bark, and 11) nine of cinnamon. [Also used in the incense compound were:] Nine kabin of Carshina lye, Cyprus wine [measuring] three s''in and three kabin— if he had no Cyprus wine, he could use strong white wine— a fourth of a kab of Sodom salt, and a minute quantity of maaleh ashan. Rabbi Nosson of Babylonia says, Jordan amber was added of a minute quantity, and if one added honey, it (the incense) became unfit; and if one omitted any of its spices he was liable to the death penalty."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Tanu rabanan pitum haketoret keitzad shelosh meot ve shishim ushemona manim hayu vah,
shelosh meot ve shishim vachamisha k''minyan yemot hachama maneh lechol yom,
peras bashacharit uferas bein ha''arbayim,
ushelsha manim yeterim shemehem machnis kohen gadol melo chofnav b''yom hakipurim,
umachaziran lemachteshet b''erev yom hakipurim,
ve shochakan yafeh yafeh k''dei sheteheh daka min hadaka,
ve achad asar samanim hayu vah,
ve elu hen hatzori ve hatziporen hachelbena ve halevona mishkal shivim shivim maneh,
mor uketzia shibolet nerd ve charkom mishkal shisha asar shisha asar maneh,
haksht sheneim asar ve kilufa shelsha ve kinamon tisha,
borit karshina tisha kabin,
yein kafrisin sein telata ve kabin telata,
ve im ein lo yein kafrisin mevi chamar chivaryan atik,
melach sedomit rova hakav,
ma''aleh ashan kol shehu,
rabi natan habavli omer af kipat hayarden kol shehu,
ve im natan bah devash pesalah ve im chisar achat mikol samaneiha chayav mita.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר הַצֳּרִי אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא שְׂרָף הַנּוֹטֵף מֵעֲצֵי הַקְּ֒טָף, בֹּרִית כַּרְשִׁינָה שֶׁשָׁפִין בָּה אֶת הַצִפֹּרֶן כִּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא נָאָה יֵין קַפְרִיסִין שֶׁשׁוֹרִין בּוֹ אֶת הַצִפֹּרֶן כְּדֵי שֶׁתְּ֒הֵא עַזָּה, וַהֲלֹא מֵי רַגְלַֽיִם יָפִין לָהּ אֶלָּא שֶׁאֵין מַכְנִיסִין מֵי רַגְלַֽיִם בַּמִּקְדָּשׁ מִפְּנֵי הַכָּבוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Rabbi Shimon ben Gamliel says: The balm is nothing but sap which drips from the balsam tree. the lye of Carshina was used for rubbing the onycha in order to refine its appearance. The Cyprus wine was used to soak the onycha to give it a pungent odor. Though the water of Raglayim was well suited for that purpose, they did not bring the water of Raglayim into the Temple because it would be disrespectful.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Raban shimon ben gamliel omer hatzori eino ela seraf hanotef meatzei haketaf,
borit karshina sheshafin ba et hatziporen kidei sheteheh na''a yein kafrisin sheshorin bo et hatziporen k''dei sheteheh aza,
vahalo mei raglayim yafin lah ela she''ein machnisin mei raglayim bamikdash mipenei hakavod.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','תַּנְיָא רַבִּי נָתָן אוֹמֵר כְּשֶׁהוּא שׁוֹחֵק אוֹמֵר הָדֵק הֵיטֵב הֵיטֵב הָדֵק מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַקּוֹל יָפֶה לַבְּ֒שָׂמִים, פִּטְּ֒מָהּ לַחֲצָאִין כְּשֵׁרָה לִשְׁלִישׁ וְלִרְבִֽיעַ לֹא שָׁמַֽעְנוּ: אָמַר רַבִּי יְהוּדָה זֶה הַכְּ֒לָל אִם כְּמִדָּתָהּ כְּשֵׁרָה לַחֲצָאִין וְאִם חִסַּר אַחַת מִכָּל סַמָּנֶֽיהָ חַיָּב מִיתָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Rabbi Nosson says, While [the Kohein] ground [the incense] he would say, ‘Hodeik heiteiv, heiteiv hodeik,'' because the sound is good for the spices. If half the quantity of incense was prepared it was acceptable, but if only a third or a fourth [of it was prepared] we have not heard [whether it was acceptable."] Rabbi Yehuda said, This is the general rule: If [it was prepared with all its ingredients] in the correct proportion, it is acceptable even if only half was prepared; but if he left out any of its spices, he was liable for the death penalty.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Tanya rabi natan omer k''shehu shochek omer hadek heitev heitev hadek mipenei shehakol yafeh labesamim,
pitemah lachatzain k''shera lishlish ve lirvia lo shamaenu.
Amar rabi Yehudah zeh hakelal im k''midatah k''shera lachatzain ve im chisar achat mikol samaneiha chayav mita.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','תַּנְיָא בַּר קַפָּרָא אוֹמֵר אַחַת לְשִׁשִּׁים אוֹ לְשִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה הָיְ֒תָה בָאָה שֶׁל שִׁירַֽיִם לַחֲצָאִין: וְעוֹד תָּנֵי בַּר קַפָּרָא אִלּוּ הָיָה נוֹתֵן בָּהּ קוֹרְ֒טוֹב שֶׁל דְּבַשׁ אֵין אָדָם יָכוֹל לַעֲמֹד מִפְּ֒נֵי רֵיחָהּ וְלָֽמָּה אֵין מְעָרְ֒בִין בָּהּ דְּבַשׁ מִפְּ֒נֵי שֶׁהַתּוֹרָה אָמְ֒רָה כִּי כָל־שְׂאֹר וְכָל־דְּבַשׁ לֹא־תַקְטִֽירוּ מִמֶּֽנּוּ אִשֶּׁה לַיהוָֹה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','It was taught in a Boraysa: Bar Kappara says, Once in sixty or seventy years the accumulated surplus was sufficient to provide half [the yearly quantity of incense."] Bar Kappara also taught, If he would have put into it a minute quantity of honey, no one could have withstood [resisted] the scent. Why was no honey mixed with it? Because the Torah says, (Leviticus 2:11) For any leaven or honey, do not burn from them, [as] a fire-offering to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Tanya bar kapara omer achat leshishim o leshivim shana hayeta va''a shel shirayim lachatzain.
Ve od tanei bar kapara ilu haya noten bah koretov shel devash ein adam yachol la''amod mipenei reichah ve lama ein mearevin bah devash mipenei shehatora amera ki chol seor ve chol devash lo taktiru mimenu isheh laAdonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','אומר ג'' פעמים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Recite each of these verses three times:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגַּב־לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם־קָרְאֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Adonoy of Hosts is with us, a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, Selah! Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]! The King will answer us on the day we call.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Adonai tzevaot imanu misgav lanu Elohei Yaakov sela.
Adonai tzevaot ashrei adam boteach bach.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','אַתָּה סֵֽתֶר לִי מִצַּר תִּצְּ֒רֵֽנִי רָנֵּי פַלֵּט תְּסוֹבְ֒בֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: וְעָרְ֒בָה לַיהוָֹה מִנְחַת יְהוּדָה וִירוּשָׁלָֽםִ כִּימֵי עוֹלָם וּכְשָׁנִים קַדְמֹנִיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','You are my shelter; from distress You preserve me; with glad song of rescue, You envelop me, Selah! Let Adonoy be pleased with the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem, as in the days of old and in earlier years.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Atah seter li mitzar titzereni ranei falet tesoveveni sela.
Ve areva laAdonai minchat Yehudah virushalami kimei olam ucheshanim kadmoniyot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','ואח"כ יאמר תפלת רבי נחוניא בן הקנה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','The following is the prayer of Rabbi Nechunya ben Hakanah:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','אָֽנָּא בְּכֹֽחַ גְּדֻלַּת יְמִינְ֒ךָ תַּתִּיר צְרוּרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Please, by the force of Your great right hand, release the bound one.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Ana b''choach gedulat yeminecha tatir tzerura.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','קַבֵּל רִנַּת עַמְּ֒ךָ שַׂגְּ֒בֵֽנוּ טַהֲרֵֽנוּ נוֹרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Accept the prayer of Your people; strengthen us, purify us, Awesome One!','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Kabel rinat amecha sagevenu taharenu nora.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','נָא גִבּוֹר דּוֹרְ֒שֵׁי יִחוּדְ֒ךָ כְּבָבַת שָׁמְ֒רֵם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Please! Mighty One, those who seek Your Unity, preserve them like the pupil [of Your eye].','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Na gibor doreshei yichudecha k''vavat shamerem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','בָּרְ֒כֵם טַהֲרֵם רַחֲמֵם צִדְקָתְ֒ךָ תָּמִיד גָּמְ֒לֵם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Bless them, purify them, have compassion on them; Your benevolent righteousness [may You] always bestow upon them.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Barechem taharem rachamem tzidkatecha tamid gamelem.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','חֲסִין קָדוֹשׁ בְּרֹב טוּבְ֒ךָ נַהֵל עֲדָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Mighty, Holy One, in Your abundant goodness, lead Your community.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Chasin kadosh b''rov tuvecha nahel adatecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יָחִיד גֵּאֶה לְעַמְּ֒ךָ פְּנֵה, זוֹכְ֒רֵי קְדֻשָּׁתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Unique One, Exalted, turn to Your people who are mindful of Your holiness.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Yachid ge''eh leamecha peneh,
zocherei k''dushatecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','שַׁוְעָתֵֽנוּ קַבֵּל וּשְׁמַע צַעֲקָתֵֽנוּ יוֹדֵֽעַ תַּעֲלוּמוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Accept our prayer and hear our cry, [You] Who knows hidden thoughts.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Shavatenu kabel ushema tza''akatenu yodea ta''alumot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Baruch shem k''vod malchuto le''olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','אַשְׁרֵי יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ עוֹד יְהַלְ֒לֽוּךָ סֶּֽלָה: אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּֽכָה לּוֹ אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיְהֹוָה אֱלֹהָיו: תְּהִלָּה לְדָוִד אֲרוֹמִמְךָ אֱלוֹהַי הַמֶּֽלֶךְ וַאֲבָרְ֒כָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: בְּכָל־יוֹם אֲבָרְ֒כֶֽךָ וַאֲהַלְ֒לָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: גָּדוֹל יְהֹוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד וְלִגְ֒דֻלָּתוֹ אֵין חֵֽקֶר: דּוֹר לְדוֹר יְשַׁבַּח מַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּגְ֒בוּרֹתֶֽיךָ יַגִּֽידוּ: הֲדַר כְּבוֹד הוֹדֶֽךָ וְדִבְרֵי נִפְלְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ אָשִֽׂיחָה: וֶעֱזוּז נוֹרְ֒אֹתֶֽיךָ יֹאמֵרוּ וּגְ֒דֻלָּתְ֒ךָ אֲסַפְּ֒רֶֽנָּה: זֵֽכֶר רַב־טוּבְ֒ךָ יַבִּֽיעוּ וְצִדְ֒קָתְ֒ךָ יְרַנֵּֽנוּ: חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם יְהֹוָה אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וּגְ֒דָל־חָֽסֶד: טוֹב־יְהֹוָה לַכֹּל וְרַחֲמָיו עַל־כָּל־מַעֲשָׂיו: יוֹדֽוּךָ יְהֹוָה כָּל־מַעֲשֶֽׂיךָ וַחֲסִידֶֽיךָ יְבָרְ֒כֽוּכָה: כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ יֹאמֵרוּ וּגְ֒בוּרָתְ֒ךָ יְדַבֵּֽרוּ: לְהוֹדִֽיעַ לִבְנֵי הָאָדָם גְּבוּרֹתָיו וּכְ֒בוֹד הֲדַר מַלְכוּתוֹ: מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ מַלְכוּת כָּל־עֹלָמִים וּמֶמְשַׁלְתְּךָ בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדֹר: סוֹמֵךְ יְהֹוָה לְכָל־הַנֹּפְ֒לִים וְזוֹקֵף לְכָל־הַכְּ֒פוּפִים: עֵינֵי־כֹל אֵלֶֽיךָ יְשַׂבֵּֽרוּ וְאַתָּה נוֹתֵן־לָהֶם אֶת־אָכְלָם בְּעִתּוֹ: פּוֹתֵֽחַ אֶת־יָדֶֽךָ וּמַשְׂבִּֽיעַ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן: צַדִּיק יְהֹוָה בְּכָל־דְּרָכָיו וְחָסִיד בְּכָל־מַעֲשָׂיו: קָרוֹב יְהֹוָה לְכָל־קֹרְ֒אָיו לְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָאֻֽהוּ בֶאֱמֶת: רְצוֹן־יְרֵאָיו יַעֲשֶׂה וְאֶת־שַׁוְעָתָם יִשְׁמַע וְיוֹשִׁיעֵם: שׁוֹמֵר יְהֹוָה אֶת־כָּל־אֹהֲבָיו וְאֵת כָּל־הָרְ֒שָׁעִים יַשְׁמִיד: תְּהִלַּת יְהֹוָה יְדַבֶּר פִּי וִיבָרֵךְ כָּל־בָּשָׂר שֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ נְבָרֵךְ יָהּ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם הַלְ֒לוּיָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Fortunate are those who dwell in Your house; may they continue to praise You, Selah. Fortunate is the people whose lot is thus; fortunate is the people for whom Adonoy is their God. A praise by David! I will exalt You, my God, the King, and bless Your Name forever and ever. Every day I will bless You and extol Your Name forever and ever. Adonoy is great and highly extolled, and His greatness is unfathomable. One generation to another will praise Your works, and Your mighty acts they will declare. The splendor of Your glorious majesty, and the words of Your wonders I will speak. Of Your awesome might, they will speak, and Your greatness I will recount. Mention of Your bountifulness they will express, and in Your righteousness joyfully exult. Adonoy is gracious and merciful, slow to anger and great in kindliness. Adonoy is good to all, His mercy encompasses all His works. All Your works will thank You, Adonoy, and Your pious ones will bless You. Of the honor of Your kingship, they will speak, and Your might they will declare. To reveal to men His mighty acts, and the glorious splendor of His kingship. Your kingship is the kingship for all times, and Your dominion is in every generation. Adonoy supports all the fallen, and straightens all the bent. The eyes of all look expectantly to You, and You give them their food at its proper time. You open Your hand and satisfy the desire of every living being. Adonoy is just in all His ways and benevolent in all His deeds. Adonoy is near to all who call upon Him, to all who call upon Him in truth. The will of those who fear Him, He fulfills; He hears their cry and delivers them. Adonoy watches over all those who love Him, and will destroy all the wicked. Praise of Adonoy, my mouth will declare and all flesh will bless His holy Name forever and ever. And we will bless God from now forever. Praise God.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Ashrei yoshevei veitecha od yehalelucha sela.
Ashrei ha''am shekacha lo ashrei ha''am sheyadonai elohav.
Tehila leDavid aromimcha Elohai hamelech va''avarecha shimcha le''olam vaed.
B''chol yom avarechecha va''ahalela shimcha le''olam vaed.
Gadol Adonai umehulal meod ve ligdulato ein cheker.
Dor ledor yeshabach ma''aseicha ugevuroteicha yagidu.
Hadar k''vod hodecha ve divrei nifleoteicha asicha.
Ve''ezuz noreoteicha yomeru ugedulatecha asaperena.
Zecher rav tuvecha yabiu ve tzidkatecha yeranenu.
Chanun ve rachum Adonai erech apayim ugedal chased.
Tov Adonai lakol ve rachamav al kol ma''asav.
Yoducha Adonai kol ma''aseicha vachasideicha yevarechucha.
K''vod malchutecha yomeru ugevuratecha yedaberu.
Lehodia livnei ha''adam gevurotav uchevod hadar malchuto.
Malchutecha malchut kol olamim umemshaltecha b''chol dor vador.
Somech Adonai lechol hanofelim ve zokef lechol hakefufim.
Einei chol eleicha yesaberu ve atah noten lahem et ochlam b''ito.
Poteach et yadecha umasbia lechol chai ratzon.
Tzadik Adonai b''chol derachav ve chasid b''chol ma''asav.
Karov Adonai lechol koreav lechol asher yikrauhu ve''emet.
Retzon yereav ya''aseh ve et shavatam yishma ve yoshiem.
Shomer Adonai et kol ohavav ve et kol hareshaim yashmid.
Tehilat Adonai yedaber pi vivarech kol basar shem kodsho le''olam vaed.
Va''anachenu nevarech yah meatah ve ad olam haleluyah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','החזן אומר חצי קדיש:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','The Chazzan recites the following half-Kaddish','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh.
B''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','he','לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','en','above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-korbanot','transliteration','Le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Korbanot'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','אין נופלין על פניהם בבית האבל או בבית הכנסת שמלין בו התינוק או שבעל ברית או סנדק והמוהל מתפללין שם, ולא כשיש שם חתן כל ז'' ימי המשתה, ולא בט"ו באב, ובט"ו בשבט, ר"ח, חנוכה, פורים קטן, ופורים גדול ב'' ימים, ול"ג בעומר, ועיו"כ וערב ראש השנה, ולא בכל חודש ניסן ולא בתשעה באב, ומערב יום הכיפורים עד אחר ראש חודש חשון, ומתחלת ר"ח סיון עד י"ג סיון, וכל אלו הימים אין אומרים במנחה שלפניהם זולת עיו"כ וער"ה שאומרים במנחה שלפניהם. (מדה"ח):','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','On days when Tachanun is omitted (see below) the chazzan continues with Kaddish. (14 and 15 Adar Rishon in a leap year); the entire month of Nissan; Pesach Sheini (14 Iyar); Lag BaOmer; 1-8 Sivan; 9 and 15 Av; and 29 Elul. When Tachanun is omitted on these days, it is also omitted at the preceding Mincha (afternoon service). Tachanun is also omitted in the presence of a bridegroom, in the house of a mourner during the week of mourning, and on the occasion of a circumcision if the father, the sandak or the mohel is present. The worshipper recites the Tachanun in a sitting position, while resting his brow on his arm. During the morning service, when the hand-tefillin is on the left arm, he leans his brow on his right arm, but at the Mincha service he leans his brow on his left arm. This "falling on one''s face" symbolizes complete submission to God and the committing of our destinies into His hands. It is mentioned in the Talmud (Maseches Megillah 22b), and originates with Moses, who "Fell down before God" (Deuteronomy 9:18) and was followed by Joshua, who "Fell on the earth upon his face before the Ark of God" (Joshua 7:6)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ תָּבֹא לְפָנֶֽיךָ תְּפִלָּֽתֵֽנוּ, וְאַל תִּתְעַלַּם מִתְּ֒חִנָּתֵֽנוּ שֶׁאֵין אָֽנוּ עַזֵּי פָנִים וּקְ֒שֵׁי עֹֽרֶף לוֹמַר לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ צַדִּיקִים אֲנַֽחְנוּ וְלֺא חָטָֽאנוּ אֲבָל אֲנַֽחְנוּ וַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ חָטָֽאנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Our God and God of our fathers, let our prayer come before you and do not ignore our supplication. For we are not so brazen-faced and stiff-necked to say to you, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, We are righteous and have not sined. But, indeed, we and our fathers have sinned.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Eloheinu velohei avoteinu tavo lefanecha tefilatenu,
ve al titalam mitechinatenu she''ein anu azei fanim ukeshei oref lomar lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu velohei avoteinu tzadikim anachenu ve lo chatanu aval anachenu va''avoteinu chatanu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','אָשַֽׁמְנוּ. בָּגַֽדְנוּ. גָּזַֽלְנוּ. דִּבַּֽרְנוּ דֹּֽפִי. הֶעֱוִֽינוּ. וְהִרְשַֽׁעְנוּ. זַֽדְנוּ. חָמַֽסְנוּ. טָפַֽלְנוּ שֶֽׁקֶר. יָעַֽצְנוּ רָע. כִּזַּֽבְנוּ. לַֽצְנוּ. מָרַֽדְנוּ. נִאַֽצְנוּ. סָרַֽרְנוּ. עָוִֽינוּ. פָּשַֽׁעְנוּ. צָרַֽרְנוּ. קִשִּֽׁינוּ עֹֽרֶף. רָשַֽׁעְנוּ. שִׁחַֽתְנוּ. תִּעַֽבְנוּ. תָּעִֽינוּ. תִּעְתָּֽעְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','We have trespassed [against God and man, and we are devastated by our guilt]; We have betrayed [God and man, we have been ungrateful for the good done to us]; We have stolen; We have slandered. We have caused others to sin; We have caused others to commit sins for which they are called רְשָׁעִים, wicked; We have sinned with malicious intent; We have forcibly taken other''s possessions even though we paid for them; We have added falsehood upon falsehood; we have joined with evil individuals or groups. We have given harmful advice; We have deceived; We have mocked; We have rebelled against God and His Torah; We have caused God to be angry with us; We have turned away from God''s Torah; We have sinned deliberately; We have been negligent in our performance of the commandments; We have caused our friends grief; We have been stiff-necked, refusing to admit that the cause of our suffering is our own sins. We have committed sins for which we are called רָשָׁע [raising a hand to hit someone]. We have committed sins which are the result of moral corruption; We have committed sins which the Torah refers to as abominations; We have gone astray; We have led others astray.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Ashamenu.
Bagadenu.
Gazalenu.
Dibarenu dofi.
He''evinu.
Ve hirshaenu.
Zadenu.
Chamasenu.
Tafalenu sheker.
Ya''atzenu ra.
Kizavenu.
Latzenu.
Maradenu.
Niatzenu.
Sararenu.
Avinu.
Pashaenu.
Tzararenu.
Kishinu oref.
Rashaenu.
Shichatenu.
Tiavenu.
Tainu.
Titaenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','סַֽרְנוּ מִמִּצְוֹתֶֽיךָ וּמִמִּשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ הַטּוֹבִים וְלֺא שָֽׁוָה לָֽנוּ. וְאַתָּה צַדִּיק עַל כָּל הַבָּא עָלֵֽינוּ. כִּי אֱמֶת עָשִֽׂיתָ וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ הִרְשָֽׁעְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','We have turned away from Your commandments and from Your good laws, and we have gained nothing from it. And You are the Righteous One in all [punishment] that has come upon us; for You have acted truthfully and we have acted wickedly.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Sarenu mimitzvoteicha umimishpateicha hatovim ve lo shava lanu.
Ve atah tzadik al kol haba aleinu.
Ki emet asita va''anachenu hirshaenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','אֵל אֶֽרֶךְ־אַפַּֽיִם אַתָּה. וּבַֽעַל הָרַחֲמִים נִקְרֵֽאתָ. וְדֶֽרֶךְ תְּשׁוּבָה הוֹרֵֽיתָ: גְּדֻלַּת רַחֲמֶֽיךָ וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ. תִּזְכֺּר הַיּוֹם וּבְכָל־יוֹם לְזֶֽרַע יְדִידֶֽיךָ: תֵּֽפֶן אֵלֵֽינוּ בְּרַחֲמִים. כִּי אַתָּה הוּא בַּֽעַל הָרַחֲמִים: בְּתַחֲנוּן וּבִתְ֒פִלָּה פָּנֶֽיךָ נְקַדֵּם. כְּהוֹדַֽעְתָּ לֶעָנָיו מִקֶּֽדֶם: מֵחֲרוֹן אַפְּ֒ךָ שׁוּב. כְּמוֹ בְּתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ כָּתוּב: וּבְ֒צֵל כְּנָפֶֽיךָ נֶחֱסֶה וְנִתְלוֹנָן. כְּיוֹם וַיֵֽרֶד יְהֺוָה בֶּעָנָן: תַּעֲבֺר עַל־פֶּֽשַׁע וְתִמְחֶה אָשָׁם. כְּיוֹם וַַיִּתְיַצֵּב עִמּוֹ שָׁם: תַּאֲזִין שַׁוְעָתֵֽנוּ וְתַקְשִׁיב מֶֽנוּ מַאֲמַר. כְּיוֹם וַיִּקְרָא בְשֵׁם יְהֹוָה, וְשָׁם נֶאֱמַר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','You are Almighty, Slow to anger, Lord of Mercy, You are called, and the way of repentance, You have taught us. The greatness of Your mercy and kindness, remember this day and every day for the descendants of Your loved ones. Turn to us with compassion for You are the Lord of Mercy. With supplication and prayer we approach Your Presence, as You made know to [Moses,] the modest one of old. From Your fierce anger turn, as it is written in Your Torah: In the shadow of Your wings, may we be sheltered and lodged, as on the day [of which it is said:] When Adonoy descended in the cloud. Remove [our] transgression, and blot out [our] iniquity, as on the day [of which it is said:] And He stood with him there. Give ear to our cry and listen to our speech, as on the day [of which it is said:] And He proclaimed in the Name, Adonoy And there it is said:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','El erech apayim atah.
Uva''al harachamim nikreta.
Ve derech teshuva horeita.
Gedulat rachameicha vachasadeicha.
Tizkor hayom uvechol yom lezera yedideicha.
Tefen eleinu b''rachamim.
Ki atah hu ba''al harachamim.
B''tachanun uvitfila paneicha nekadem.
K''hodaeta leanav mikedem.
Mecharon apecha shuv.
K''mo b''toratecha katuv.
Uvetzel k''nafeicha necheseh ve nitlonan.
K''yom vayered Adonai beanan.
Ta''avor al pesha ve timcheh asham.
K''yom va''ayityatzev imo sham.
Ta''azin shavatenu ve takshiv menu ma''amar.
K''yom vayikra ve shem Adonai,
ve sham ne''emar.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','קהל וש"ץ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Congregation and Chazzan:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהֺוָה עַל פָּנָיו וַיִּקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','And Adonoy passed before him [Moses] and proclaimed:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Vaya''avor Adonai al panav vayikra.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֺוָה יְהֺוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן אֶֽרֶךְ אַפַּֽיִם וְרַב־חֶֽסֶד וֶאֱמֶת: נֹצֵר חֶֽסֶד לָאֲלָפִים נֹשֵׂא עָוֹן וָפֶֽשַׁע וְחַטָּאָה וְנַקֵּה: וְסָלַחְתָּ לַעֲוֺנֵֽנוּ וּלְ֒חַטָּאתֵֽנוּ וּנְ֒חַלְתָּֽנוּ: סְלַח־לָֽנוּ אָבִֽינוּ כִּי־חָטָֽאנוּ. מְחַל־לָֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כִּי־פָשָֽׁעְנוּ: כִּי־אַתָּה אֲדֺנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב־חֶֽסֶד לְכָל־קוֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Adonoy, Adonoy, Almighty, Merciful, Gracious, Slow to Anger, and Abundant in Kindness and Truth. Keeper of kindness for thousands of generations, Endurer of iniquity and transgression, and sin, and Acquitter of those who repent. And pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for Your inheritance. Pardon us, our Father, for we have sinned, forgive us, our King, for we have transgressed. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Adonai Adonai el rachum ve chanun erech apayim ve rav chesed ve''emet.
Notzer chesed la''alafim noseh avon vafesha ve chata''a ve nakeh.
Ve salachta la''avonenu ulechatatenu unechaltanu.
Selach lanu avinu ki chatanu.
Mechal lanu malkenu ki fashaenu.
Ki atah adonai tov ve salach ve rav chesed lechol kore''eicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','כשנופל על פניו יש נוהגים להטות על צד ימין משום דכתיב שויתי ה'' לנגדי תמיד. ויש נוהגים להטות על צד שמאל משום דהסבת שמאל שמה הסבה הלכך באותו צד שהוא נראה כבן מלך צריך ליכנע לפני המקום. וכבר נהגו ליפול בשחרית על צד ימין ובמנחה על צד שמאל.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','The following supplication is recited while resting your brow on your arm.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר דָּוִד אֶל־גָּד צַר־לִי מְאֹד נִפְּ֒לָה־נָּא בְיַד־יְהֹוָה כִּי־רַבִּים רַחֲמָיו וּבְ֒יַד־אָדָם אַל־אֶפֹּֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','And David said to Gad (II Samuel 24:14), I am greatly distressed; let us fall into the hand of Adonoy for His mercies are great, but into the hand of man let me not fall.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Vayomer David el gad tzar li meod nipela na ve yad Adonai ki rabim rachamav uveyad adam al epola.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן חָטָֽאתִי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה מָלֵא רַחֲמִים רַחֵם עָלַי וְקַבֵּל תַּחֲנוּנָי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Merciful and gracious One, I have sinned before You; Adonoy, full of mercy, have compassion upon me and accept my supplications.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Rachum ve chanun chatati lefanecha Adonai maleh rachamim rachem alai ve kabel tachanunai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֹוָה אַל־בְּאַפְּ֒ךָ תוֹכִיחֵֽנִי וְאַל־בַּחֲמָתְ֒ךָ תְיַסְּ֒רֵֽנִי: חָנֵּֽנִי יְהֹוָה כִּי אֻמְלַל אָֽנִי רְפָאֵֽנִי יְהֹוָה כִּי נִבְהֲלוּ עֲצָמָי: וְנַפְשִׁי נִבְהֲלָה מְאֹד וְאַתָּה יְהֹוָה עַד־מָתָי: שׁוּבָה יְהֹוָה חַלְּ֒צָה נַפְשִׁי הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי לְמַֽעַן חַסְדֶּֽךָ: כִּי אֵין בַּמָּֽוֶת זִכְרֶךָ בִּשְׁ֒אוֹל מִי־יוֹדֶה לָּךְ: יָגַֽעְתִּי־בְּאַנְחָתִי אַשְׂחֶה בְכָל־לַֽיְלָה מִטָּתִי בְּדִמְעָתִי עַרְשִׂי אַמְסֶה: עָשְׁ֒שָׁה מִכַּֽעַס עֵינִי עָתְ֒קָה בְּכָל־צוֹרְ֒רָי: סֽוּרוּ מִמֶּֽנִּי כָּל־פֹּֽעֲלֵי אָוֶן כִּי־שָׁמַע יְהֹוָה קוֹל בִּכְיִי: שָׁמַע יְהֹוָה תְּחִנָּתִי יְהֹוָה תְּפִלָּתִי יִקָּח: יֵבֽשׁוּ וְיִבָּהֲלוּ מְאֹד כָּל־אֹיְ֒בָי יָשֻֽׁבוּ יֵבֽשׁוּ רָֽגַע:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Adonoy, do not rebuke me with Your anger, nor chastise me with Your rage. Be gracious unto me, Adonoy, for I am desolate, heal me Adonoy, for my bones are terrified. My soul, [too,] is utterly terrified, and You Adonoy, how long? Return Adonoy, free my soul, deliver me for the sake of Your lovingkindness. For in death there is no mention of You; in the lower world who will thank You. I am worn out with my sighing, every night I cause my bed to float; with my tears, I melt my couch. My eye is dimmed from anger, it has aged because of my tormentors. Depart from me, all you evildoers, for Adonoy has heard the voice of my weeping. Adonoy has heard my supplication, Adonoy will (also) accept my prayer. Ashamed and utterly terrified will all my foes be, they will return and be instantaneously ashamed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Adonai al b''apecha tochicheni ve al bachamatecha teyasereni.
Chaneni Adonai ki umlal ani refaeni Adonai ki nivhalu atzamai.
Ve nafshi nivhala meod ve atah Adonai ad matai.
Shuva Adonai chaletza nafshi hoshieni lema''an chasdecha.
Ki ein bamavet zichrecha bishol mi yodeh lach.
Yagaeti b''anchati ascheh ve chol layela mitati b''dimati arsi amseh.
Ashesha mika''as eini ateka b''chol tzorerai.
Suru mimeni kol poalei aven ki shama Adonai kol bichyi.
Shama Adonai techinati Adonai tefilati yikach.
Yevshu ve yibahalu meod kol oyevai yashuvu yevshu raga.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאַל יֹאבַד יִשְׂרָאֵל הָאֹמְ֒רִים שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Guardian of Israel, guard the remnant of Israel, and let not Israel perish, who say, "Hear Israel."','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Shomer Yisrael shemor she''erit Yisrael ve al yovad Yisrael haomerim shema Yisrael.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי אֶחָד שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם אֶחָד וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי אֶחָד הַמְ֒יַחֲדִים שִׁמְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Guardian of the unique nation, guard the remnant of the unique people, and let not the unique nation perish, who proclaim the Oneness of Your Name, [saying:] Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Shomer goy echad shemor she''erit am echad ve al yovad goy echad hameyachadim shimcha Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ שְׁמוֹר שְׁאֵרִית עַם קָדוֹשׁ וְאַל יֹאבַד גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ הַמְ֒שַׁלְּ֒שִׁים בְּשָׁלשׁ קְדֻשּׁוֹת לְקָדוֹשׁ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Guardian of the holy nation, guard the remnant of the holy people and let not the holy nation perish who repeat the threefold sanctification to the Holy One.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Shomer goy kadosh shemor she''erit am kadosh ve al yovad goy kadosh hameshaleshim b''shalsh k''dushot lekadosh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','מִתְרַצֶּה בְּרַחֲמִים וּמִתְפַּיֵּס בְּתַחֲנוּנִים הִתְרַצֶּה וְהִתְפַּיֵּס לְדוֹר עָנִי כִּי אֵין עוֹזֵר: אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','You Who are appeased by pleas for mercy, and conciliated by supplications, be appeased and conciliated to an afflicted generation, for there is none else to help. Our Father, our King! be gracious to us and answer us for we have no [good] deeds, deal with us charitably and kindly and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Mitratzeh b''rachamim umitpayes b''tachanunim hitratzeh ve hitpayes ledor ani ki ein ozer.
Avinu malkenu chanenu va''anenu ki ein banu ma''asim aseh imanu tzedaka vachesed ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ לֺא נֵדַע מַה נַּעֲשֶׂה כִּי עָלֶֽיךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ: זְכֹר רַחֲמֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה וַחֲסָדֶֽיךָ כִּי מֵעוֹלָם הֵֽמָּה: יְהִי חַסְדְּ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה עָלֵֽינוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר יִחַֽלְנוּ לָךְ: אַל תִּזְכָּר לָֽנוּ עֲוֹנוֹת רִאשׁוֹנִים מַהֵר יְקַדְּ֒מֽוּנוּ רַחֲמֶֽיךָ כִּי דַלּֽוֹנוּ מְאֹד: עֶזְרֵֽנוּ בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה עֹשֵׂה שָׁמַֽיִם וְאָֽרֶץ: חָנֵּֽנוּ יְהֹוָה חָנֵּֽנוּ כִּי־רַב שָׂבַֽעְנוּ בוּז: בְּרֺֽגֶז רַחֵם תִּזְכּוֹר: בְּרֹֽגֶז עַקֵדָה תִּזְכּוֹר, בְּרֹֽגֶז תְּמִימוֹת תִּזְכּוֹר: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה, הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: כִּי הוּא יָדַע יִצְרֵֽנוּ זָכוּר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ: עָזְ֒רֵֽנוּ אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ עַל־דְּבַר כְּבוֹד־שְׁמֶֽךָ וְהַצִּילֵֽנוּ וְכַפֵּר עַל־חַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','As for us, we know not what to do; but our eyes are upon You. Remember Your mercies, Adonoy, and kindnesses for they are from the beginning of the world. Adonoy! may Your kindness be upon us, as we have waited for You. Remember not the sins of our ancestors; let Your mercy come swiftly toward us, for we have been brought very low. Help us for the Name of Adonoy Creator of Heaven and earth. Be gracious to us, Adonoy, be gracious to us for we are saturated with humiliation. [Even] in anger remember to have compassion. [Even] in anger remember the binding of Isaac. Even in anger remember the uprightness of Jacob Adonoy deliver [us] the King will answer us on the day we call. For He knows of what we are made; He is mindful that we are but dust. Help us, God of our deliverance, for the sake of the glory of Your Name; save us and atone our sins, for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Va''anachenu lo neda mah na''aseh ki aleicha eineinu.
Zechor rachameicha Adonai vachasadeicha ki meolam hema.
Yehi chasdecha Adonai aleinu ka''asher yichalenu lach.
Al tizkar lanu avonot rishonim maher yekademunu rachameicha ki dalonu meod.
Ezrenu b''shem Adonai oseh shamayim ve aretz.
Chanenu Adonai chanenu ki rav savaenu vuz.
B''rogez rachem tizkor.
B''rogez akeda tizkor,
b''rogez temimot tizkor.
Adonai hoshia,
hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.
Ki hu yada yitzrenu zachur ki afar anachenu.
Azerenu Elohei yishenu al devar k''vod shemecha ve hatzilenu ve chaper al chatoteinu lema''an shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','הש"ץ אומר קדיש שלם:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','The Chazzan recites the following Kaddish','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','תִּתְקַבֵּל צְלוֹתְ֒הוֹן וּבָעוּתְ֒הוֹן דְּכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דִּי בִשְׁ֒מַיָּא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','May there be acceptance of the prayers and supplications of the entire House of Israel before their Father in heaven. And say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Titkabel tzelotehon uvautehon dechal beit Yisrael kodam avuhon di vishmaya ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and good life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim tovim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּ֒לִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְ֒עִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְ֒כֵי הַמְּ֒לָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁ֒כִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְ֒הֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of Kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And You shall know this day and take into Your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia,
va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu,
shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz,
umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al,
ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim,
hu Eloheinu ein od,
emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','(וְ)עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁ֒מֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁ֒עֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְ֒בוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּ֒לוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְ֒כוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְ֒עֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','(ve al) ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha,
lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz,
yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu,
ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu,
vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha,
ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed,
ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod,
kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','אַל תִּירָא מִפַּֽחַד פִּתְאֹם וּמִשֹּׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹא: עֻֽצוּ עֵצָה וְתֻפָר דַּבְּ֒רוּ דָבָר וְלֹא יָקוּם כִּי עִמָּֽנוּ אֵל: וְעַד זִקְנָה אֲנִי הוּא וְעַד שֵׂיבָה אֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל: אֲנִי עָשִֽׂיתִי וַאֲנִי אֶשָּׂא וַאֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל וַאֲמַלֵּט:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Do not fear sudden terror nor the destruction of the wicked when it comes. Take counsel together and it will be foiled speak the word and it will not stand for God is with us. To your old age I am [with you], to your older years I will sustain you, I have made you, and I will carry you, I will sustain you and save you.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Al tira mipachad pitom umishoat reshaim ki tavo.
Utzu etza ve tufar daberu davar ve lo yakum ki imanu el.
Ve ad zikna ani hu ve ad seiva ani esbol.
Ani asiti va''ani esa va''ani esbol va''amalet.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְ֒מָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְ֒עֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and good life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim tovim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם (בעשי"ת הַשָּׁלוֹם) בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','He Who makes peace (Ten Days of Penitence: the peace) in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Oseh shalom (vshyt" hashalom) bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','מנהג טוב לומר אחר כל תפלה מזמור לדוד ה׳‬ אורי וישעי. ובפרט מר״ח אלול עד הושענא רבא (מורה באצבע סי'' לז).','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','The following is recited here by some congregations from the first day of Elul, through Shemini Atzeres. Others recite it at the end of the Maariv (Evening) Service.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','לְדָוִד יְהֹוָה אוֹרִי וְיִשְׁעִי מִמִּי אִירָא יְהֹוָה מָעוֹז חַיַּי מִמִּי אֶפְחָד: בִּקְ֒רֹב עָלַי מְרֵעִים לֶאֱכֹל אֶת בְּשָׂרִי צָרַי וְאֹיְ֒בַי לִי הֵֽמָּה כָשְׁ֒לוּ וְנָפָֽלוּ: אִם תַּחֲנֶה עָלַי מַחֲנֶה לֹא יִירָא לִבִּי אִם תָּקוּם עָלַי מִלְחָמָה בְּזֹאת אֲנִי בוֹטֵֽחַ: אַחַת שָׁאַֽלְתִּי מֵאֵת יְהֹוָה אוֹתָהּ אֲבַקֵּשׁ שִׁבְתִּי בְּבֵית יְהֹוָה כָּל יְמֵי חַיַּי לַחֲזוֹת בְּנֹֽעַם יְהֹוָה וּלְ֒בַקֵּר בְּהֵיכָלוֹ: כִּי יִצְפְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּסֻכֹּה בְּיוֹם רָעָה יַסְתִּרֵֽנִי בְּסֵֽתֶר אָהֳלוֹ בְּצוּר יְרוֹמְ֒מֵֽנִי: וְעַתָּה יָרוּם רֹאשִׁי עַל אֹיְ֒בַי סְבִיבוֹתָי וְאֶזְבְּחָה בְאָהֳלוֹ זִבְחֵי תְרוּעָה אָשִֽׁירָה וַאֲזַמְּ֒רָה לַיהֹוָה: שְׁמַע יְהֹוָה קוֹלִי אֶקְרָא וְחָנֵּֽנִי וַעֲנֵֽנִי: לְךָ אָמַר לִבִּי בַּקְּ֒שׁוּ פָנָי אֶת פָּנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֲבַקֵּשׁ: אַל תַּסְתֵּר פָּנֶֽיךָ מִמֶּֽנִּי אַל תַּט בְּאַף עַבְדֶּֽךָ עֶזְרָתִי הָיִֽיתָ אַל תִּטְּ֒שֵֽׁנִי וְאַל תַּעַזְ֒בֵֽנִי אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעִי: כִּי אָבִי וְאִמִּי עֲזָבֽוּנִי וַיהֹוָה יַאַסְ֒פֵֽנִי: הוֹרֵֽנִי יְהֹוָה דַּרְכֶּֽךָ וּנְ֒חֵֽנִי בְּאֹֽרַח מִישׁוֹר לְמַֽעַן שׁוֹרְ֒רָי: אַל תִּתְּ֒נֵֽנִי בְּנֶֽפֶשׁ צָרָי כִּי קָֽמוּ בִי עֵֽדֵי שֶֽׁקֶר וִיפֵֽחַ חָמָס: לוּלֵא הֶאֱמַֽנְתִּי לִרְאוֹת בְּטוּב יְהֹוָה בְּאֶֽרֶץ חַיִּים: קַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה חֲזַק וְיַאֲמֵץ לִבֶּךָ וְקַוֵּה אֶל יְהֹוָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','By David: Adonoy is my light and my salvation, whom shall I fear? Adonoy is the strength of my life, of whom shall I be afraid? When evildoers approach me to devour my flesh— my tormentors and my foes they stumble and fall. If an army should encamp against me, my heart would not fear; if war were to rise against me, in this I trust. One thing I request of Adonoy, [only] that shall I seek, that I may dwell in the House of Adonoy all the days of my life, to behold the pleasantness of Adonoy, and to meditate in His Sanctuary. For He will hide me in His Tabernacle on the day of distress, He will conceal me in the shelter of His Tent, upon a rock He will lift me. And now my head is raised high above my enemies around me; and I will offer in His Tent, sacrifices accompanied by trumpets of joy; I will sing and chant to Adonoy. Adonoy, hear my voice when I call; be gracious to me and answer me. Of You, my heart has said, “Seek My Presence”; Your Presence, Adonoy I will seek. Conceal not Your Presence from me, do not turn away Your servant in anger. You have been my help; neither cast me off nor abandon me, God of my deliverance. When my father and mother abandon me, Adonoy will gather me up. Adonoy, teach me Your way, and lead me in the path of uprightness, because of my watchers. Do not deliver me to the will of my tormentors, for false witnesses have risen against me, who breathe violence. Had I not believed that I would see the goodness of Adonoy in the land of living. Hope to Adonoy, be strong and He will give you courage; and hope to Adonoy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','LeDavid Adonai ori ve yishi mimi ira Adonai maoz chayai mimi efchad.
Bikrov alai mereim le''echol et b''sari tzarai ve oyevai li hema chashelu ve nafalu.
Im tachaneh alai machaneh lo yira libi im takum alai milchama b''zot ani voteach.
Achat sha''aleti me''et Adonai otah avakesh shivti b''veit Adonai kol yemei chayai lachazot b''noam Adonai ulevaker b''heichalo.
Ki yitzpeneni b''sukoh b''yom ra''a yastireni b''seter oholo b''tzur yeromemeni.
Ve atah yarum roshi al oyevai sevivotai ve ezbecha ve oholo zivchei terua ashira va''azamera laAdonai.
Shema Adonai koli ekra ve chaneni va''aneni.
Lecha amar libi bakeshu fanai et paneicha Adonai avakesh.
Al taster paneicha mimeni al tat b''af avdecha ezrati hayita al titesheni ve al ta''azveni Elohei yishi.
Ki avi ve imi azavuni va''adonai ya''asfeni.
Horeni Adonai darkecha unecheni b''orach mishor lema''an shorerai.
Al titeneni b''nefesh tzarai ki kamu vi edei sheker vifeach chamas.
Luleh he''emaneti lirot b''tuv Adonai b''eretz chayim.
Kaveh el Adonai chazak ve ya''ametz libecha ve kaveh el Adonai.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','(קדיש יתום)','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','Mourner''s Kaddish is said here:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','בבית האבל בבוקר אחר שיר של יום ואחר מנחה בימים שיש בהם תחנון אומרים זה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','It is customary to recite this psalm (49) in the house of a mourner during the week of mourning, following the morning and evening services. On weekdays when Tachanun is not said Psalm 16 (page 218) is substituted. This psalm, the final hymn of the psalms set down by the sons of Korach has significance for all mankind. Its message is that man must utilize all his material and physical resources to enhance his spiritual existence so that when his soul survives the body''s brief stay on earth it can ascend to immortality. If man fails to recognize his purpose in life and instead regards the acquisition of material wealth the primary aim of life, he forfeits his hope of immortality, and his existence will not continue beyond the grave.—S.R. Hirsch','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','he','לַמְנַצֵּֽחַ לִבְנֵי קֹֽרַח מִזְמוֹר: שִׁמְ֒עוּ זֹאת כָּל־הָעַמִּים הַאֲזִֽינוּ כָּל יֽשְׁ֒בֵי חָֽלֶד: גַּם בְּנֵי אָדָם גַּם בְּנֵי אִישׁ יַֽחַד עָשִׁיר וְאֶבְיוֹן: פִּי יְדַבֵּר חָכְמוֹת וְהָגוּת לִבִּי תְבוּנוֹת: אַטֶּה לְמָשָׁל אָזְנִי אֶפְתַּח בְּכִנּוֹר חִידָתִי: לָֽמָּה אִירָא בִּֽימֵי רָע עֲוֹן עֲקֵבַי יְסוּבֵּֽנִי: הַבֹּטְ֒חִים עַל חֵילָם וּבְ֒רֹב עָשְׁרָם יִתְהַלָּֽלוּ: אָח לֺא פָדֹה יִפְדֶּה אִישׁ לֺא יִתֵּן לֵאלֺהִים כָּפְרוֹ: וְיֵקַר פִּדְיוֹן נַפְשָׁם וְחָדַל לְעוֹלָם: וִיחִי עוֹד לָנֶֽצַח לֺא יִרְאֶה הַשָּֽׁחַת: כִּי יִרְאֶה חֲכָמִים יָמֽוּתוּ יַֽחַד כְּסִיל וָבַֽעַר יֹאבֵֽדוּ וְעָזְ֒בוּ לַאֲחֵרִים חֵילָם: קִרְבָּם בָּתֵּֽימוֹ לְעוֹלָם מִשְׁכְּ֒נֹתָם לְדוֹר וָדֹר קָרְ֒אוּ בִשְׁמוֹתָם עֲלֵי אֲדָמוֹת: וְאָדָם בִּיקָר בַּל־יָלִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ: זֶה דַרְכָּם כֶּֽסֶל לָֽמוֹ וְאַחֲרֵיהֶם בְּפִיהֶם יִרְצוּ סֶֽלָה: כַּצֹּאן לִשְׁ֒אוֹל שַׁתּוּ מָֽוֶת יִרְעֵם וַיִּרְדּוּ בָם יְשָׁרִים לַבֹּֽקֶר וְצוּרָם לְבַלּוֹת שְׁאוֹל מִזְּ֒בֻל לוֹ: אַךְ־אֱלֺהִים יִפְדֶּה נַפְשִׁי מִיַּד שְׁאוֹל כִּי יִקָּחֵֽנִי סֶֽלָה: אַל־תִּירָא כִּי־יַעֲשִׁר אִישׁ כִּי־יִרְבֶּה כְּבוֹד בֵּיתוֹ: כִּי לֺא בְמוֹתוֹ יִקַּח הַכֹּל לֺא־יֵרֵד אַחֲרָיו כְּבוֹדוֹ: כִּי־נַפְשׁוֹ בְּחַיָּיו יְבָרֵךְ וְיוֹדֻֽךָ כִּי־תֵיטִיב לָךְ: תָּבוֹא עַד־דּוֹר אֲבוֹתָיו עַד־נֵֽצַח לֺא יִרְאוּ אוֹר: אָדָם בִּיקָר וְלֺא־יָבִין נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּ֒הֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','en','To Him Who grants victory, a psalm by the sons of Korach. Hear this all peoples, listen all inhabitants of the decaying world! Sons of Adam and sons of men, rich and poor together. My mouth shall speak wisdom, and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding. I will incline my ear to a parable, I will begin to solve, to the accompaniment of a harp, my riddle. Why should I fear in the days of evil? The iniquity I trod upon surrounds me. Those who trust in their wealth and take pride in their great riches. A man will not redeem his brother neither can he give to God his ransom. The redemption of their soul is too costly and it shall cease to be forever. Shall he then live forever, shall he never see the grave? For he sees that wise men die, the fools and senseless perish equally and leave their wealth to others. Their inner thoughts are that their houses [will last] forever, their homes for generation after generation; (for) they have proclaimed their names throughout the lands. But man does not endure in his splendor, he is likened to the silenced animals. This is their way— their folly remains with them, and [yet] their descendants take pleasure in their speech, Selah. Like sheep—they are destined for the grave; death shall be their shepherd, and the upright shall dominate them at morning, their form will be consumed in the grave; [it will not remain] their dwelling-place. But God will redeem my soul from the [grasp of] the grave, for He will take me [to Himself] Selah. Fear not when a man grows rich, when the glory of his house is increased. For when he dies, he shall carry nothing away, his glory will not descend after him. Because while he lived, he blessed his soul. (saying): they will praise you because you have done well for yourself. He will join the generation of his fathers, they shall not see light, for all eternity. Man with [all] his splendor, [but] without understanding is likened to the silenced animals.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun:36:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-tachanun','transliteration','Lamnatzeach livnei korach mizmor.
Shimu zot kol ha''amim ha''azinu kol yshevei chaled.
Gam b''nei adam gam b''nei ish yachad ashir ve evyon.
Pi yedaber chochmot ve hagut libi tevunot.
Ateh lemashal ozni eftach b''chinor chidati.
Lama ira bimei ra avon akevai yesubeni.
Habotechim al cheilam uverov oshram yithalalu.
Ach lo fadoh yifdeh ish lo yiten lelohim kafero.
Ve yekar pidyon nafsham ve chadal le''olam.
Vichi od lanetzach lo yireh hashachat.
Ki yireh chachamim yamutu yachad k''sil vava''ar yovedu ve azevu la''acherim cheilam.
Kirbam bateimo le''olam mishkenotam ledor vador kareu vishmotam alei adamot.
Ve adam bikar bal yalin nimshal kabehemot nidmu.
Zeh darkam kesel lamo ve achareihem b''fihem yirtzu sela.
Katzon lishol shatu mavet yirem vayirdu vam yesharim laboker ve tzuram levalot sheol mizevul lo.
Ach Elohim yifdeh nafshi miyad sheol ki yikacheni sela.
Al tira ki ya''ashir ish ki yirbeh k''vod beito.
Ki lo ve moto yikach hakol lo yered acharav k''vodo.
Ki nafsho b''chayav yevarech ve yoducha ki teitiv lach.
Tavo ad dor avotav ad netzach lo yiru or.
Adam bikar ve lo yavin nimshal kabehemot nidmu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Tachanun'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור ובעשי"ת אומרים כאן אבינו מלכנו. גודל מעלת אבינו מלכנו הובא בספרים. ויסדה רבי עקיבא. ונתקן כנגד ברכות אמצעיות דתפלת י"ח דחול. ולפי שיש בו מעין י"ח אין אומרים בשבת.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','During the Ten Days of Penitence, Avinu Malkeinu is recited here during Shacharis—the morning service, and Mincha—the afternoon service. It is also said by some congregations on public Fast Days. The number of petitions in this prayer varies with custom, but in our rite, Avinu Malkeinu consists of 44 petitions. Since many of them are similar to the petitions of Shemoneh Esrei, Avinu Malkeinu is never recited on Shabbos, when the petitions of Shemoneh Esrei are also omitted. This unique and moving prayer is recorded as having been recited by Rabbi Akiva. The Talmud (Maseches Taanis 25b) relates that Rabbi Eliezer once stepped down before the Ark and recited the 24 benedictions for fast days and his prayers were not answered. Rabbi Akiva stepped down after him and exclaimed, "Our Father, our King, we have no king except You. Our Father, our King, for Your sake have mercy on us," and rain fell.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָטָֽאנוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! we have sinned before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chatanu lefanecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֵין לָֽנוּ מֶֽלֶךְ אֶלָּא אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father our King! we have no King except You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu ein lanu melech ela atah.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! deal with us [kindly] for the sake of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh imanu lema''an shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','בעשי"ת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','During the Ten Days of Penitence, say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חַדֵּשׁ עָלֵֽינוּ שָׁנָה טוֹבָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! renew for us a good year.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chadesh aleinu shana tova.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','On public fast-days, say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בָּרֵךְ עָלֵֽינוּ שָׁנָה טוֹבָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! bless us with a good year.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu barech aleinu shana tova.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בַּטֵּל מֵעָלֵֽינוּ כָּל גְּזֵרוֹת קָשׁוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! annul all harsh decrees concerning us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu batel mealeinu kol gezerot kashot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בַּטֵּל מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת שׂוֹנְ֒אֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! annul the designs of those who hate us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu batel machshevot sone''einu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָפֵר עֲצַת אוֹיְ֒בֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, our King! thwart the plans of our enemies.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu hafer atzat oyeveinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כַּלֵּה כָּל צַר וּמַשְׂטִין מֵעָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! rid us of every oppressor and adversary.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu kaleh kol tzar umastin mealeinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ סְתוֹם פִּיּוֹת מַשְׂטִינֵֽנוּ וּמְ֒קַטְרִיגֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! seal the mouths of our adversaries and accusers.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu setom piyot mastinenu umekatrigenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כַּלֵּה דֶּֽבֶר וְחֶֽרֶב וְרָעָב וּשְׁ֒בִי וּמַשְׁחִית וְעָוֹן וּשְׁ֒מַד מִבְּ֒נֵי בְרִיתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remove pestilence, sword, famine, captivity, destruction, [the burden of] iniquity and religious persecution from the members of Your covenant.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu kaleh dever ve cherev ve ra''av ushevi umashchit ve avon ushemad mibenei ve ritecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְנַע מַגֵּפָה מִנַּחֲלָתֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! withhold the plague from Your inheritance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu mena magefa minachalatecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ סְלַח וּמְ֒חַל לְכָל עֲוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! forgive and pardon all our iniquities.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu selach umechal lechol avonoteinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְחֵה וְהַעֲבֵר פְּשָׁעֵֽינוּ וְחַטֹּאתֵֽינוּ מִנֶּֽגֶד עֵינֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! blot out and remove our transgressions and sins from before Your eyes.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu mecheh ve ha''aver peshaeinu ve chatoteinu mineged eineicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מְחוֹק בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים כָּל שִׁטְ֒רֵי חוֹבוֹתֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! erase in Your abundant mercy all records of our liabilities.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu mechok b''rachameicha harabim kol shitrei chovoteinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הַחֲזִירֵֽנוּ בִּתְ֒שׁוּבָה שְׁלֵמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! bring us back in wholehearted repentance before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu hachazirenu bitshuva shelema lefanecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ שְׁלַח רְפוּאָה שְׁלֵמָה לְחוֹלֵי עַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! send complete healing to the sick among Your people.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu shelach refua shelema lecholei amecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ קְרַע רֹֽעַ גְּזַר דִּינֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! tear up the evil [parts] of our sentence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu k''ra roa gezar dinenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ בְּזִכָּרוֹן טוֹב לְפָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us favorably before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu b''zikaron tov lefanecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','בעשרת ימי תשובה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','The following five prayers are said during the Ten Days of Penitence.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר חַיִּים טוֹבִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of the Good Life.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu katevenu b''sefer chayim tovim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר גְּאֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Redemption and Deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu katevenu b''sefer geula vishua.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר פַּרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Maintenance and Sustenance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu katevenu b''sefer parnasa ve chalkala.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר זְכֻיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Merits.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu katevenu b''sefer zechuyot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ כָּתְ֒בֵֽנוּ בְּסֵֽפֶר סְלִיחָה וּמְ֒חִילָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! inscribe us in the Book of Pardon and Forgiveness.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu katevenu b''sefer selicha umechila.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','בתענית ציבור','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','The following five prayers are said on public fast-days.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לְחַיִּים טוֹבִים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for a good life.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu lechayim tovim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִגְ֒אֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for redemption and deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu ligula vishua.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לְפַרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for maintenance and sustenance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu lefarnasa ve chalkala.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִזְ֒כֻיּוֹת:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for merit.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu lizchuyot.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכְ֒רֵֽנוּ לִסְ֒לִיחָה וּמְ֒חִילָה:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember us for pardon and forgiveness.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zacherenu lislicha umechila.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הַצְמַח לָֽנוּ יְשׁוּעָה בְּקָרוֹב:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! cause deliverance to spring forth for us soon.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu hatzmach lanu yeshua b''karov.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָרֵם קֶֽרֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל עַמֶּֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! raise up the might of Your people Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu harem keren Yisrael amecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:36:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ הָרֵם קֶֽרֶן מְשִׁיחֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:36:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! raise up the might of Your anointed.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:36:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu harem keren meshichecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:37:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מַלֵּא יָדֵֽינוּ מִבִּרְ֒כוֹתֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:37:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! fill our hands with Your blessings.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:37:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu maleh yadeinu mibirchoteicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:38:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ מַלֵּא אֲסָמֵֽינוּ שָׂבָע:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:38:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! fill our storehouses with abundance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:38:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu maleh asameinu sava.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:39:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ שְׁמַע קוֹלֵֽנוּ חוּס וְרַחֵם עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:39:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! hear our voice, spare us and have compassion upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:39:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu shema kolenu chus ve rachem aleinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:40:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ קַבֵּל בְּרַחֲמִים וּבְ֒רָצוֹן אֶת תְּפִלָּתֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:40:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! accept our prayer with compassion and favor.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:40:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu kabel b''rachamim uveratzon et tefilatenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:41:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ פְּתַח שַׁעֲרֵי שָׁמַֽיִם לִתְ֒פִלָּתֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:41:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! open the gates of heaven to our prayer.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:41:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu petach sha''arei shamayim litfilatenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:42:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ זָכוֹר כִּי עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:42:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! remember, that we are dust.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:42:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu zachor ki afar anachenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נָא אַל תְּשִׁיבֵֽנוּ רֵיקָם מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! Please do not turn us away empty-handed from You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:43:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu na al teshivenu reikam milefaneicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ תְּהֵא הַשָּׁעָה הַזֹּאת שְׁעַת רַחֲמִים וְעֵת רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! let this hour be an hour of compassion and a time of favor before You.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:44:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu teheh hasha''a hazot sheat rachamim ve et ratzon milefaneicha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חֲמוֹל עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל עוֹלָלֵֽינוּ וְטַפֵּֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! have compassion upon us, and upon our children and infants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:45:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chamol aleinu ve al olaleinu ve tapenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן הֲרוּגִים עַל שֵׁם קָדְשֶֽׁךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slain for Your holy Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:46:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an harugim al shem kodshecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן טְבוּחִים עַל יִחוּדֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who were slaughtered for [proclaiming] Your Unity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:47:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an tevuchim al yichudecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן בָּאֵי בָאֵשׁ וּבַמַּֽיִם עַל קִדּוּשׁ שְׁמֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of those who went through fire and water for the sanctification of Your Name.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:48:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an baei vaesh uvamayim al kidush shemecha.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ נְקוֹם לְעֵינֵֽינוּ נִקְ֒מַת דַּם עֲבָדֶֽיךָ הַשָּׁפוּךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! avenge before our eyes the spilled blood of Your servants.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:49:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu nekom le''eineinu nikmat dam avadeicha hashafuch.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ אִם לֺא לְמַעֲנֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake if not for ours.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:50:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''ancha im lo lema''anenu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַעַנְ֒ךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for Your sake and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:51:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''ancha ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן רַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great mercy.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:52:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an rachameicha harabim.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ עֲשֵׂה לְמַֽעַן שִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא שֶׁנִּקְרָא עָלֵֽינוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! do it for the sake of Your great, mighty, and awesome Name which is proclaimed upon us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:53:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu aseh lema''an shimcha hagadol hagibor ve hanora shenikra aleinu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','he','אָבִֽינוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ חָנֵּֽנוּ וַעֲנֵֽנוּ כִּי אֵין בָּֽנוּ מַעֲשִׂים עֲשֵׂה עִמָּֽנוּ צְדָקָה וָחֶֽסֶד וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','en','Our Father, Our King! favor us and answer us for we have no accomplishments; deal with us charitably and kindly with us and deliver us.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu:54:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-mincha-avinu-malkeinu','transliteration','Avinu malkenu chanenu va''anenu ki ein banu ma''asim aseh imanu tzedaka vachesed ve hoshienu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Mincha, Avinu Malkeinu'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach. In your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh.
B''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael.
Ba''agala uvizman kariv.
Ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְ֒מֵי עָלְ֒מַיָּא','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְ֒מָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וִיהִי נֹֽעַם אֲדֹנָי אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנָה עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנֵֽהוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May the pleasantness of my Master our God be upon us, and the work of our hands established for us, and the work of our hands—establish it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Vihi noam adonai Eloheinu aleinu uma''aseh yadeinu konena aleinu uma''aseh yadeinu konenehu.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','ישֵׁב בְּסֵֽתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן: אֹמַר לַיהֹוָה מַחְסִי וּמְצוּדָתִי אֱלֹהַי אֶבְטַח־בּוֹ: כִּי הוּא יַצִּילְךָ מִפַּח יָקוּשׁ מִדֶּֽבֶר הַוּֽוֹת: בְּאֶבְרָתוֹ יָֽסֶךְ לָךְ וְתַֽחַת־כְּנָפָיו תֶּחְסֶה צִנָּה וְסֹחֵרָה אֲמִתּוֹ: לֹא־תִירָא מִפַּֽחַד לָֽיְלָה מֵחֵץ יָעוּף יוֹמָם: מִדֶּֽבֶר בָּאֹֽפֶל יַהֲלֹךְ מִקֶּֽטֶב יָשׁוּד צָהֳרָֽיִם: יִפֹּל מִצִּדְּךָ אֶֽלֶף וּרְבָבָה מִימִינֶֽךָ אֵלֶֽיךָ לֹא יִגָּשׁ: רַק בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ תַבִּיט וְשִׁלֻּמַת רְשָׁעִים תִּרְאֶה: כִּי־אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מַחְסִי עֶלְיוֹן שַֽׂמְתָּ מְעוֹנֶֽךָ: לֹא־תְאֻנֶּה אֵלֶֽיךָ רָעָה וְנֶֽגַע לֹא־יִקְרַב בְּאָהֳלֶֽךָ: כִּי מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה־לָּךְ לִשְׁמָרְךָ בְּכָל־דְּרָכֶֽיךָ: עַל־כַּפַּֽיִם יִשָּׂאֽוּנְךָ פֶּן־תִּגֹּף בָּאֶֽבֶן רַגְלֶֽךָ: עַל־שַֽׁחַל וָפֶֽתֶן תִּדְרֹךְ תִּרְמֹס כְּפִיר וְתַנִּין: כִּי בִי חָשַׁק וַאֲפַלְּטֵֽהוּ אֲשַׂגְּבֵֽהוּ כִּי־יָדַע שְׁמִי: יִקְרָאֵֽנִי וְאֶעֱנֵֽהוּ עִמּוֹ־אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה אֲחַלְּצֵֽהוּ וַאֲכַבְּדֵֽהוּ: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He who dwells in the shelter of the Supreme One, under the protection of Shadai he will abide. I say of Adonoy, [He is] my refuge and my stronghold, my God in Whom I trust. For He will save you from the snare-trap, from destructive pestilence. With His wings He will cover you and beneath His wings, you will find refuge; His truth is a shield, a full shield. You will not fear the terror of night, nor the arrow that flies by day. The pestilence that prowls in darkness, nor the deadly plague that ravages at noon. A thousand will fall at your [left] side, and ten thousand at your [right] side but it shall not come near you. Only with your eyes will you behold and see the punishment of the wicked. For you [have proclaimed]: “Adonoy is my refuge,” the Supreme One you have made your dwelling. No evil shall befall you, and no plague shall come near your tent. For His angels He will command on your behalf— to guard you in all your ways. They will carry you upon their hands, lest you hurt your foot on a rock. You will tread upon lion and snake, you will trample young lion and serpent. Because he clings to Me with desire, I will save him; I will strengthen him, for he knows My Name. When he calls upon Me, I will answer him; I am with him in distress, I will free him and honor him. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yshev b''seter elyon b''tzel shadai yitlonan.
Omar laAdonai machsi umetzudati Elohai evtach bo.
Ki hu yatzilecha mipach yakush midever havot.
B''evrato yasech lach ve tachat k''nafav techseh tzina ve sochera amito.
Lo tira mipachad layela mechetz yauf yomam.
Midever baofel yahaloch miketev yashud tzohorayim.
Yipol mitzidecha elef urevava miminecha eleicha lo yigash.
Rak b''eineicha tabit ve shilumat reshaim tireh.
Ki atah Adonai machsi elyon sameta meonecha.
Lo teuneh eleicha ra''a ve nega lo yikrav b''oholecha.
Ki malachav yetzaveh lach lishmarecha b''chol deracheicha.
Al kapayim yisaunecha pen tigof baeven raglecha.
Al shachal vafeten tidroch tirmos k''fir ve tanin.
Ki vi chashak va''afaletehu asagevehu ki yada shemi.
Yikraeni ve e''enehu imo anochi ve tzara achaletzehu va''achabedehu.
Orech yamim asbiehu ve arehu bishuati.
Orech yamim asbiehu ve arehu bishuati.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וְאַתָּה קָדוֹשׁ יוֹשֵׁב תְּהִלּוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל: וְקָרָא זֶה אֶל זֶה וְאָמַר','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And You, Holy One, are enthroned upon the praises of Israel. And [the angels] call one to another and say:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Ve atah kadosh yoshev tehilot Yisrael.
Ve kara zeh el zeh ve amar','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת מְלֹא כָל הָאָֽרֶץ כְּבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“Holy, holy, holy is Adonoy of Hosts: the fullness of all the earth is His glory.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Kadosh kadosh kadosh Adonai tzevaot melo chol ha''aretz k''vodo.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וּמְקַבְּ֒לִין דֵּין מִן דֵּין וְאָמְרִין קַדִּישׁ בִּשְׁמֵי מְרוֹמָא עִלָּאָה בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ עַל אַרְעָא עוֹבַד גְּבוּרְתֵּהּ קַדִּישׁ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת. מַלְיָא כָל אַרְעָא זִיו יְקָרֵהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And they receive [sanction] one from another, and say, “Holy in the highest heights of heaven, the abode of His Divine Presence; holy upon earth, the work of His mighty power; holy forever and to all eternity— is Adonoy of Hosts; the whole earth is filled with the radiance of His glory.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Umekabelin dein min dein ve amerin kadish bishmei meroma ila''a beit shechineteh kadish al ara ovad gevureteh kadish lealam ulealemei alemaya Adonai tzevaot.
Malya chol ara ziv yekareh.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וַתִּשָּׂאֵֽנִי רֽוּחַ וָאֶשְׁמַע אַחֲרַי קוֹל רַֽעַשׁ גָּדוֹל','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','And a wind lifted me; and I heard behind me the sound of a great rushing;','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Vatisaeni ruach vaeshma acharai kol ra''ash gadol','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','בָּרוּךְ כְּבוֹד יְהֹוָה מִמְּ֒קוֹמוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from His place.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Baruch k''vod Adonai mimekomo.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','וּנְטָלַתְנִי רוּחָא וּשְׁמָעִית בַּתְרַי קָל זִֽיעַ סַגִּיא דִּמְשַׁבְּ֒חִין וְאָמְרִין בְּרִיךְ יְקָרָא דַיהֹוָה מֵאֲתַר בֵּית שְׁכִינְתֵּהּ: יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: יְהֹוָה מַלְכוּתֵהּ קָאֵים לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שָׁמְרָה זֹאת לְעֹלָם לְיֵֽצֶר מַחְשְׁ֒בוֹת לְבַב עַמֶּֽךָ וְהָכֵן לְבָבָם אֵלֶֽיךָ: וְהוּא רַחוּם יְכַפֵּר עָוֹן וְלֹא יַשְׁחִית וְהִרְבָּה לְהָשִׁיב אַפּוֹ וְלֹא יָעִיר כָּל חֲמָתוֹ: כִּי אַתָּה אֲדֹנָי טוֹב וְסַלָּח וְרַב חֶֽסֶד לְכָל קֹרְ֒אֶֽיךָ: צִדְקָתְ֒ךָ צֶֽדֶק לְעוֹלָם וְתוֹרָתְ֒ךָ אֱמֶת: תִּתֵּן אֱמֶת לְיַעֲקֹב חֶֽסֶד לְאַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּֽעְתָּ לַאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ מִֽימֵי קֶֽדֶם: בָּרוּךְ אֲדֹנָי יוֹם יוֹם יַעֲמָס לָֽנוּ הָאֵל יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת עִמָּֽנוּ מִשְׂגָּב לָֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב סֶֽלָה: יְהֹוָה צְבָאוֹת אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם בֹּטֵֽחַ בָּךְ: יְהֹוָה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יַעֲנֵֽנוּ בְיוֹם קָרְאֵֽנוּ: בָּרוּךְ הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבְּ֒רָאָֽנוּ לִכְבוֹדוֹ וְהִבְדִּילָֽנוּ מִן הַתּוֹעִים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ תּוֹרַת אֱמֶת וְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם נָטַע בְּתוֹכֵֽנוּ הוּא יִפְתַּח לִבֵּֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָשֵׂם בְּלִבֵּֽנוּ אַהֲבָתוֹ וְיִרְאָתוֹ וְלַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנוֹ וּלְעָבְדוֹ בְּלֵבָב שָׁלֵם לְמַֽעַן לֹא נִיגַע לָרִיק וְלֹא נֵלֵד לַבֶּהָלָה: יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ שֶׁנִּשְׁמֹר חֻקֶּֽיךָ בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְנִזְכֶּה וְנִחְיֶה וְנִרְאֶה וְנִירַשׁ טוֹבָה וּבְרָכָה לִשְׁנֵי יְמוֹת הַמָּשִֽׁיחַ וּלְחַיֵּי הָעוֹלָם הַבָּא: לְמַֽעַן יְזַמֶּרְךָ כָבוֹד וְלֹא יִדֹּם יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי לְעוֹלָם אוֹדֶֽךָ: בָּרוּךְ הַגֶּֽבֶר אֲשֶׁר יִבְטַח בַּיהֹוָה וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה מִבְטַחוֹ: בִּטְחוּ בַיהֹוָה עֲדֵי עַד כִּי בְּיָהּ יְהֹוָה צוּר עוֹלָמִים: וְיִבְטְ֒חוּ בְךָ יוֹדְ֒עֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ כִּי לֹא עָזַֽבְתָּ דֹרְ֒שֶֽׁיךָ יְהֹוָה: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַֽעַן צִדְקוֹ יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','“And a wind lifted me and I heard behind me a sound of a great rushing of those who uttered praises and said, “Blessed is the glory of Adonoy from the place, the abode of His Divine Presence.” Adonoy will reign forever and ever. Adonoy, His kingdom is established forever and to all eternity. Adonoy, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, our fathers, keep this forever as the intention of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts to You. And He, the merciful One, atons iniquity and does ot destroy; He frequently withdraws His anger and does not arouse all His rage. For You, my Master, are good and forgiving, and abounding in kindness to all who call upon You. Your righteousness is everlasting and Your Torah is truth. You will grant truth to Jacob kindliness to Abraham, as You have sworn to our fathers from the days of old. Blessed is my Master day by day; He loads us, the Almighty Who is our deliverance, forever. Adonoy of Hosts is with us a stronghold for us is the God of Jacob, selah. Adonoy of Hosts, fortunate is the man who trusts in You. Adonoy, deliver [us]; the King will answer us on the day we call. Blessed is He, our God, Who created us for His glory, and set us apart from those who go astray; and gave us the Torah of truth, and eternal life He implanted within us. May He open our heart to His Torah, and instill in our heart love and awe of Him, to do His will and serve Him with a perfect heart, so that we shall not labor in vain nor bring forth that which causes dismay. May it be Your will, Adonoy, our God, and God of our fathers, that we keep Your statutes in this world, and [thus] be privileged to live and behold, and to inherit the goodness and blessing of the Messianic days and in the life of the World to Come. In order that my soul sing to You and not be stilled; Adonoy, my God, forever will I thank You. Blessed is the man who trusts in Adonoy, so that Adonoy is his security. Trust in Adonoy until the end of days, for in God, Adonoy, is the strength of the worlds. Those who know your Name will trust in You, for You have never forsaken those who seek You, Adonoy. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Unetalatni rucha ushemait batrai kal zia sagi dimshabechin ve amerin b''rich yekara da''adonai meatar beit shechineteh.
Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Adonai malchuteh kaeim lealam ulealemei alemaya.
Adonai Elohei Avraham Yitzchak ve Yisrael avoteinu shamera zot le''olam leyetzer machshevot levav amecha ve hachen levavam eleicha.
Ve hu rachum yechaper avon ve lo yashchit ve hirba lehashiv apo ve lo yair kol chamato.
Ki atah adonai tov ve salach ve rav chesed lechol kore''eicha.
Tzidkatecha tzedek le''olam ve toratecha emet.
Titen emet leYaakov chesed leAvraham asher nishbaeta la''avoteinu mimei kedem.
Baruch adonai yom yom ya''amas lanu hael yeshuatenu sela.
Adonai tzevaot imanu misgav lanu Elohei Yaakov sela.
Adonai tzevaot ashrei adam boteach bach.
Adonai hoshia hamelech ya''anenu ve yom kare''enu.
Baruch hu Eloheinu shebera''anu lichvodo ve hivdilanu min hatoim ve natan lanu torat emet ve chayei olam nata b''tochenu hu yiftach libenu b''torato ve yasem b''libenu ahavato ve yirato ve la''asot retzono uleavedo b''levav shalem lema''an lo niga larik ve lo neled labehala.
Yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Eloheinu velohei avoteinu shenishmor chukeicha baolam hazeh ve nizkeh ve nichyeh ve nireh ve nirash tova uveracha lishnei yemot hamashiach ulechayei ha''olam haba.
Lema''an yezamercha chavod ve lo yidom Adonai Elohai le''olam odecha.
Baruch hagever asher yivtach ba''adonai ve haya Adonai mivtacho.
Bitchu va''adonai adei ad ki b''yah Adonai tzur olamim.
Ve yivtechu ve cha yode''ei shemecha ki lo azaveta doresheicha Adonai.
Adonai chafetz lema''an tzidko yagdil torah ve yadir.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְקָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh.
B''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael.
Ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקֻדְשָׁא. בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא. תֻּשְׁבְּ֒חָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא. דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudsha.
B''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata.
Tushbechata ve nechemata.
Da''amiran b''alema.
Ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','תִּתְקַבֵּל צְלוֹתְ֒הוֹן וּבָעוּתְ֒הוֹן דְּכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דִּי בִשְׁמַיָּא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be acceptance of the prayers and supplications of the entire House of Israel before their Father in heaven. And say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Titkabel tzelotehon uvautehon dechal beit Yisrael kodam avuhon di vishmaya ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He Who makes peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Oseh shalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּ֒חוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לַהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּ֒לִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ. וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְ֒עִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּ֒לָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא. שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ. וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל. וּשְׁכִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְהֵי מְרוֹמִים. הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד. אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the Seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And you shall know this day and take into your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia.
Va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu.
Shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz.
Umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al.
Ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim.
Hu Eloheinu ein od.
Emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְ֒אוּ בִשְׁמֶֽךָ. לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁעֵי אָֽרֶץ. יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְ֒עוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁ֒בֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְ֒עוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ. וְלִכְבוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ. וִיקַבְּ֒לוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ. וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד. כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד. כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Al ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha.
Lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz.
Yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu.
Ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu.
Vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha.
Ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed.
Ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod.
Kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','אַל תִּירָא מִפַּֽחַד פִּתְאֹם וּמִשֹּׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹא: עֻֽצוּ עֵצָה וְתֻפָר דַּבְּ֒רוּ דָבָר וְלֹא יָקוּם כִּי עִמָּֽנוּ אֵל: וְעַד זִקְנָה אֲנִי הוּא וְעַד שֵׂיבָה אֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל: אֲנִי עָשִֽׂיתִי וַאֲנִי אֶשָּׂא וַאֲנִי אֶסְבֹּל וַאֲמַלֵּט:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Do not fear sudden terror nor the destruction of the wicked when it comes. Take counsel together and it will be foiled speak the word and it will not stand for God is with us. To your old age I am [with you], to your older years I will sustain you, I have made you, and I will carry you, I will sustain you and save you.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Al tira mipachad pitom umishoat reshaim ki tavo.
Utzu etza ve tufar daberu davar ve lo yakum ki imanu el.
Ve ad zikna ani hu ve ad seiva ani esbol.
Ani asiti va''ani esa va''ani esbol va''amalet.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ וְיַצְמַח פּוּרְ֒קָנֵהּ וִיקָרֵב (קֵץ) מְשִׁיחֵהּ. בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will and may He rule His kingdom bring forth His redemption and hasten the coming of His Mashiach in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Israel, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh ve yatzmach purekaneh vikarev (ketz) meshicheh.
B''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael.
Ba''agala uvizman kariv.
Ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקֻדְשָׁא. בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵלָּא (בעשי"ת וּלְעֵלָּא מִכָּל) מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא. תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא. דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above (Ten Days of Penitence: far above) all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudsha.
B''rich hu le''ela (vshyt" ule''ela mikal) min kol birchata ve shirata.
Tushbechata ve nechemata.
Da''amiran b''alema.
Ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל. וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael.
Ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','he','עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','en','He Who makes peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and for all Israel, —and say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-weekday-maariv-motzaei-shabbat','transliteration','Oseh shalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Siddur Sefard, Weekday Maariv, Motzaei Shabbat'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל־עוֹלָם הֲרֵינִי מוֹחֵל לְכָל־מִי שֶׁהִכְעִיס וְהִקְנִיט אוֹתִי אוֹ שֶׁחָטָא כְּנֶגְדִי בֵּין בְּגוּפִי בֵּין בְּמֶמוֹנִי בֵין בִּכְבוֹדִי בֵין בְכָל אֲשֶׁר לִי בֵין בְּאוֹנֶס בֵּין בְּרָצוֹן בֵּין בְּשׁוֹגֵג בֵּין בְּמֵזִיד בֵין בְּדִבּוּר בֵּין בְּמַעֲשֶׂה בֵּין בְּגִלְגוּל זֶה בֵּין בְּגִלְגּוּל אַחֵר לְכָל־בַּר יִשְׂרָאֵל וְלֹא יֵעָנֵשׁ שׁוּם אָדָם בְסִבָּתִי יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁלֹּא אֶחְטֶא עוֹד וְלֹא אֶחֱזוֹר בָּהֶם וְלֹא אָשׁוּב עוֹד לְהַכְעִיסֶךָ וְלֹא אֶעֱשֶׂה הָרַע בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ וּמַה־שֶׁחָטָֽאתִי מְחוֹק בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ הָרַבִּים וְלֹא עַל יְדֵי יִסּוּרִים וָחֳלֶיִם רָעִים: יִהְיוּ לְרָצוֹן אִמְרֵי־פִי וְהֶגְיוֹן לִבִּי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה צוּרִי וְגֹאֲלִי:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Master of the universe! I hearby forgive anyone who has angered me, or sinned against me, either physically or financially, against my honor or anything that is mine, whether accidentally or intentionally, inadvertently or deliberately, by speech or by deed, in this incarnation or in any other any Israelite [is forgiven], may no man be punished on my account. May it be Your will, Adonoy, my God and God of my fathers, that I shall sin no more nor repeat my sins, neither shall I again anger You nor do what is wrong in Your eyes. The sins I have committed, erase in your abounding mercies, but not through suffering or severe illnesses. May they be acceptable the words of my mouth and the thoughts of my heart, before You Adonoy, my Rock and my Redeemer.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ribono shel olam hareini mochel lechol mi shehichis ve hiknit oti o shechata k''negdi bein b''gufi bein b''memoni vein bichvodi vein ve chal asher li vein b''ones bein b''ratzon bein b''shogeg bein b''mezid vein b''dibur bein b''ma''aseh bein b''gilgul zeh bein b''gilgul acher lechol bar Yisrael ve lo yeanesh shum adam ve sibati yehi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai shelo echteh od ve lo echezor bahem ve lo ashuv od lehachisecha ve lo e''eseh hara b''eineicha umah shechatati mechok b''rachameicha harabim ve lo al yedei yisurim vocholeyim raim.
Yihyu leratzon imrei fi ve hegyon libi lefanecha Adonai tzuri ve goali.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם הַמַּפִּיל חֶבְלֵי שֵׁנָה עַל עֵינָי וּתְנוּמָה עַל עַפְעַפָּי: וּמֵאִיר לְאִישׁוֹן בַּת עָיִן. וִיהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהַי וֵאלֺהֵי אֲבוֹתַי שֶׁתַּשְׁכִּיבֵֽנִי לְשָׁלוֹם וְתַעֲמִידֵֽנִי לְחַיִים טוֹבִים וּלְשָׁלוֹם וְתֵן חֶלְקֵי בְּתוֹרָתֶךָ וְתַרְגִילֵנוּ לִדְבַר מִצְוָה וְאַל תַּרְגִילֵנוּ לִדְבַר עַבֵרָה וְאַל תְּבִיאֵֽנוּ לֹא לִידֵי חֵטְא וְלֹא לִידֵי נִסָּיוֹן וְלֹא לִידֵי בִזָּיוֹן וְיִשְׁלֹט בִּי יֵצֵר הַטוֹב וְאַל יִשְׁלֹט בִּי יֵֽצֶר הָרָע וְתַצִילֵנוּ מִשָׂטָן וּמִפֶגַע רָע וּמֵחָלָיִם רָעִים וְאַל יְבַהֲלֽוּנִי רַעְיוֹנַי וַחֲלוֹמוֹת רָעִים וְהַרְהוֹרִים רָעִים וּתְהֵא מִטָּתִי שְׁלֵמָה לְפָנֶֽיךָ: וְהָאֵר עֵינַי פֶּן אִישַׁן הַמָּֽוֶת. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמֵּאִיר לָעוֹלָם כֻּלּוֹ בִּכְבוֹדוֹ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy, our God, King of the Universe, Who causes the fetters of sleep to fall upon my eyes, and slumber upon my eyelids. And illuminates the pupil of the eye. May it be Your will, Adonoy, my God and God of my fathers to make me lie down in peace, and to raise me (again) to good life and peace, and grant me my portion in Your Torah, make us accustomed to do Your commands, and let us not become accustomed to sin, Do not bring us into the grasp of sin, Do not cause us to be tested, or brought to disgrace. May I be ruled by the Good Inclination and let me not be ruled over by the Evil Inclination. Protect me from Satan, from an evil mishap and from illnesses. Let my thoughts not terrify me— nor evil dreams or evil fancies (disturb me), and may my bed be perfect before You. And light up my eyes lest I sleep the sleep of death, Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who illuminates the whole world with His glory.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam hamapil chevlei shena al einai utenuma al afapai.
Umeir leishon bat ayin.
Vihi ratzon milefaneicha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai shetashkiveni leshalom ve ta''amideni lechayim tovim uleshalom ve ten chelkei b''toratecha ve targilenu lidvar mitzvah ve al targilenu lidvar avera ve al tevienu lo lidei chet ve lo lidei nisayon ve lo lidei vizayon ve yishlot bee yetzer hatov ve al yishlot bee yetzer hara ve tatzilenu misatan umifega ra umechalayim raim ve al yevahaluni rayonai vachalomot raim ve harhorim raim uteheh mitati shelema lefanecha.
Ve haer einai pen ishan hamavet.
Baruch atah Adonai hameir laolam kulo bichvodo.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','מי שאינו מדקדק לקרות ק"ש בבהכ"נ בזמנה צריך לקרות ק"ש על מטתו שתי פרשיות שמע והיה אם שמוע. אבל פ'' ויאמר שהוא משום הזכרת יצ"מ אין צריך לחזור ולקרות על מטתו כיון שכבר הזכיר בבהכ"נ. אבל מי שקורא ק"ש בזמנה אין צריך לקרות על מטתו רק פרשה ראשונה לבד. ורי"ו כתב על פי המדרש לומר כל שלש פרשיות על מטתו משום שהוא רמ"ח תיבות לשמור רמ"ח איבריו. (דה"ח ומ"א)','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','If one has prayed Ma''ariv and with it recited Sh''ma earlier than the ideal time for the evening Sh''ma, he should repeat all of it here. Some people have the custom of reciting all three paragraphs here every night.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ נֶאֱמָן:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Almighty, faithful King','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','El melech ne''eman.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Hear, Israel Adonoy is our God Adonoy is One','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Shema Yisrael Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echad.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יש להפסיק מעט בין אחד לברוך כי עיקר קבול עול מלכות שמים היא פסוק ראשון. ויאמר בלחש:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','The following three lines are to be said silently:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious Kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Baruch shem k''vod malchuto le''olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ בְּכָל֯־לְ֯בָבְ֒ךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְכָל־מְאֹדֶֽךָ: וְהָיוּ הַדְּ֒בָרִים הָאֵֽלֶּה אֲשֶׁר֯ אָ֯נֹכִי מְצַוְּ֒ךָ הַיּוֹם עַל֯־לְ֯בָבֶֽךָ: וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶֽיךָ וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ וּבְ֒לֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּֽרֶךְ וּבְ֒שָׁכְבְּךָ וּבְ֒קוּמֶֽךָ: וּקְ֒שַׁרְתָּם לְאוֹת עַל֯־יָ֯דֶֽךָ וְהָיוּ לְטֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ: וּכְ֒תַבְתָּם עַל־מְזֻזוֹת בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּבִשְׁ֒עָרֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And you shall love Adonoy, your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your possessions. And these words which I command you today shall be upon your heart. And you shall teach them sharply to your children, and you shall discuss them when you sit in your house, and when you travel on the road, and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand, and they shall be for totafos between your eyes. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve''ahavta et Adonai Elohecha b''chal levavecha uvechol nafshecha uvechol meodecha.
Ve hayu hadevarim haeleh asher anochi metzavecha hayom al levavecha.
Ve shinantam levaneicha ve dibarta bam b''shivtecha b''veitecha uvelechtecha vaderech uveshachebecha uvekumecha.
Ukeshartam leot al yadecha ve hayu letotafot bein eineicha.
Uchetavtam al mezuzot beitecha uvishareicha.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וִיהִי נֹֽעַם אֲדֹנָי אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנָה עָלֵֽינוּ וּמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֵֽינוּ כּוֹנְנֵֽהוּ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','May the pleasantness of my Master, our God, be upon us, and the work of our hands establish for us and the work of our hands may He establish.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Vihi noam adonai Eloheinu aleinu uma''aseh yadeinu konena aleinu uma''aseh yadeinu konenehu.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','ישֵׁב בְּסֵֽתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן: אֹמַר לַיהֹוָה מַחְסִי וּמְצוּדָתִי אֱלֹהַי אֶבְטַח־בּוֹ: כִּי הוּא יַצִּילְךָ מִפַּח יָקוּשׁ מִדֶּֽבֶר הַוָּוֹת: בְּאֶבְרָתוֹ יָֽסֶךְ לָךְ וְתַֽחַת־כְּנָפָיו תֶּחְסֶה צִנָּה וְסֹחֵרָה אֲמִתּוֹ: לֹא־תִירָא מִפַּֽחַד לָֽיְלָה מֵחֵץ יָעוּף יוֹמָם: מִדֶּֽבֶר בָּאֹֽפֶל יַהֲלֹךְ מִקֶּֽטֶב יָשׁוּד צָהֳרָֽיִם: יִפֹּל מִצִּדְּךָ אֶֽלֶף וּרְבָבָה מִימִינֶֽךָ אֵלֶֽיךָ לֹא יִגָּשׁ: רַק בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ תַבִּיט וְשִׁלֻּמַת רְשָׁעִים תִּרְאֶה: כִּי־אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מַחְסִי עֶלְיוֹן שַֽׂמְתָּ מְעוֹנֶֽךָ: לֹא־תְאֻנֶּה אֵלֶֽיךָ רָעָה וְנֶֽגַע לֹא־יִקְרַב בְּאָהֳלֶֽךָ: כִּי מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה־לָּךְ לִשְׁמָרְךָ בְּכָל־דְּרָכֶֽיךָ: עַל־כַּפַּֽיִם יִשָּׂאֽוּנְךָ פֶּן־תִּגֹּף בָּאֶֽבֶן רַגְלֶֽךָ: עַל־שַֽׁחַל וָפֶֽתֶן תִּדְרֹךְ תִּרְמֹס כְּפִיר וְתַנִּין: כִּי בִי חָשַׁק וַאֲפַלְּטֵֽהוּ אֲשַׂגְּבֵֽהוּ כִּי־יָדַע שְׁמִי: יִקְרָאֵֽנִי וְאֶעֱנֵֽהוּ עִמּוֹ־אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה אֲחַלְּצֵֽהוּ וַאֲכַבְּדֵֽהוּ: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי: אֹֽרֶךְ יָמִים אַשְׂבִּיעֵֽהוּ וְאַרְאֵֽהוּ בִּישׁוּעָתִי:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He who dwells in the shelter of the Supreme One, under the protection of Shadai He will abide. I say of Adonoy, [He is] my refuge and my stronghold, my God in Whom I trust. For He will save you from the snare-trap, from destructive pestilence. With His wings He will cover you and beneath His wings, you will find refuge; His truth is a shield, a full shield. You will not fear the terror of night, nor the arrow that flies by day, the pestilence that prowls in darkness, nor the deadly plague that ravages at noon. A thousand will fall at your [left] side, and ten thousand at your [right] side but it shall not come near you. Only with your eyes will you behold and see the punishment of the wicked. For you [have proclaimed]: Adonoy is my refuge, the Supreme One you have made your dwelling No evil shall befall you, and no plague shall come near your tent. For His angels He will command on your behalf— to guard you in all your ways. They will carry you upon their hands, lest you hurt your foot on a rock. You will tread upon lion and snake, you will trample young lion and serpent. Because he clings to Me with desire, I will save him; I will strengthen him, for he knows My Name. When he calls upon Me, I will answer him; I am with him in distress, I will free him and honor him. I will satiate him with longevity, and will let him see My deliverance. I will satiate him with longevity and will let him see My deliverance.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Yshev b''seter elyon b''tzel shadai yitlonan.
Omar laAdonai machsi umetzudati Elohai evtach bo.
Ki hu yatzilecha mipach yakush midever havavot.
B''evrato yasech lach ve tachat k''nafav techseh tzina ve sochera amito.
Lo tira mipachad layela mechetz yauf yomam.
Midever baofel yahaloch miketev yashud tzohorayim.
Yipol mitzidecha elef urevava miminecha eleicha lo yigash.
Rak b''eineicha tabit ve shilumat reshaim tireh.
Ki atah Adonai machsi elyon sameta meonecha.
Lo teuneh eleicha ra''a ve nega lo yikrav b''oholecha.
Ki malachav yetzaveh lach lishmarecha b''chol deracheicha.
Al kapayim yisaunecha pen tigof baeven raglecha.
Al shachal vafeten tidroch tirmos k''fir ve tanin.
Ki vi chashak va''afaletehu asagevehu ki yada shemi.
Yikraeni ve e''enehu imo anochi ve tzara achaletzehu va''achabedehu.
Orech yamim asbiehu ve arehu bishuati.
Orech yamim asbiehu ve arehu bishuati.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יְהֹוָה מָה־רַבּוּ צָרָי רַבִּים קָמִים עָלָי: רַבִּים אֹמְ֒רִים לְנַפְשִׁי אֵין יְשׁוּעָֽתָה לוֹ בֵאלֺהִים סֶֽלָה: וְאַתָּה יְהֹוָה מָגֵן בַּעֲדִי כְּבוֹדִי וּמֵרִים רֹאשִׁי: קוֹלִי אֶל־יְהֹוָה אֶקְרָא וַיַּעֲנֵֽנִי מֵהַר קָדְשׁוֹ סֶֽלָה: אֲנִי שָׁכַֽבְתִּי וָאִישָֽׁנָה הֱקִיצֽוֹתִי כִּי יְהֹוָה יִסְמְ֒כֵֽנִי: לֺא אִירָא מֵרִבְבוֹת עָם אֲשֶׁר סָבִיב שָֽׁתוּ עָלָי: קוּמָה יְהֹוָה הוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי אֱלֺהַי כִּי־הִכִּֽיתָ אֶת־כָּל אֹיְ֒בַי לֶֽחִי שִׁנֵּי רְשָׁעִים שִׁבַּֽרְתָּ: לַיהוָֹה הַיְ֒שׁוּעָה עַל־עַמְּ֒ךָ בִרְכָתֶֽךָ סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','(Psalms 3:2-9) Adonoy, how many are my tormentors; many rise up against me. Many say of my soul: There is no deliverance for him through God, forever. But You, Adonoy, are a shield for me; my glory and Raiser of my head. With my voice, I call out to Adonoy, and He answers me from His holy mountain, forever. I lay down and slept; I awake for Adonoy supports me. I fear not the tens of thousands of people deployed against me from every side. Rise Adonoy, deliver me, my God, for You have struck all my enemies on the cheek; You have broken the teeth of the wicked. Deliverance is Adonoy''s; upon Your people is Your blessing, selah.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Adonai ma rabu tzarai rabim kamim alai.
Rabim omerim lenafshi ein yeshuata lo velohim sela.
Ve atah Adonai magen ba''adi k''vodi umerim roshi.
Koli el Adonai ekra vaya''aneni mehar kodsho sela.
Ani shachaveti vaishana hekitzoti ki Adonai yismecheni.
Lo ira merivvot am asher saviv shatu alai.
Kuma Adonai hoshieni Elohai ki hikita et kol oyevai lechi shinei reshaim shibareta.
LaAdonai hayeshua al amecha virchatecha sela.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הַשְׁכִּיבֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ לְשָׁלוֹם וְהַעֲמִידֵֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ לְחַיִּים טוֹבִים וּלשָׁלוֹם. וּפְרוֹשׂ עָלֵֽינוּ סֻכַּת שְׁלוֹמֶֽךָ וְתַקְּ֒נֵֽנוּ בְּעֵצָה טוֹבָה מִלְּ֒פָנֶֽיךָ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ מְהֵרָה לְמַֽעַן שְׁמֶֽךָ. וְהָגֵן בַּעֲדֵֽנוּ וְהָסֵר מֵעָלֵֽינוּ אוֹיֵב דֶּֽבֶר וְחֶֽרֶב וְרָעָב וְיָגוֹן וְהָסֵר שָׂטָן מִלְּ֒פָנֵֽינוּ וּמֵאַחֲרֵֽינוּ וּבְצֵל כְּנָפֶֽיךָ תַּסְתִּירֵֽנוּ. כִּי אֵל שׁוֹמְ֒רֵֽנוּ וּמַצִּילֵֽנוּ אָֽתָּה כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה. וּשְׁמוֹר צֵאתֵֽנוּ וּבוֹאֵֽנוּ לְחַיִּים וּלְשָׁלוֹם מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Adonoy, our God, make us lie down in peace, our King, raise us [again] to good life and peace. Spread over us the shelter of Your peace, and direct us to better ourselves through Your good counsel; and deliver us speedily for Your Name''s sake. Shield us, and remove from us enemies, pestilence, sword, famine and sorrow. Remove the adversary from before us and from behind us, and in the shadow of Your wings shelter us. For You are the Almighty Who is our protector and rescuer. For You are the Almighty Who is King, Gracious, and Merciful. Guard our going out and our coming in for life and peace from now, forever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Hashkivenu Adonai Eloheinu leshalom ve ha''amidenu malkenu lechayim tovim ulshalom.
Uferos aleinu sukat shelomecha ve takenenu b''etza tova milefaneicha ve hoshienu mehera lema''an shemecha.
Ve hagen ba''adenu ve haser mealeinu oyev dever ve cherev ve ra''av ve yagon ve haser satan milefaneinu umeachareinu uvetzel k''nafeicha tastirenu.
Ki el shomerenu umatzilenu atah ki el melech chanun ve rachum atah.
Ushemor tzetenu uvoenu lechayim uleshalom meatah ve ad olam.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בַּיּוֹם בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בַּלָּֽיְלָה בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בְּשָׁכְבֵֽנוּ בָּרוּךְ יְהֹוָה בְּקוּמֵֽנוּ. כִּי בְיָדְ֒ךָ נַפְשׁוֹת הַחַיִּים וְהַמֵּתִים אֲשֶׁר בְּיָדוֹ נֶֽפֶשׁ כָּל חָי וְרֽוּחַ כָּל בְּשַׂר אִישׁ. בְּיָדְ֒ךָ אַפְקִיד רוּחִי פָּדִֽיתָה אוֹתִי יְהֹוָה אֵל אֱמֶת. אֱלֺהֵֽינוּ שֶׁבַּשָּׁמַֽיִם יַחֵד שִׁמְךָ וְקַיֵּם מַלְכוּתְ֒ךָ תָּמִיד וּמְלֺךְ עָלֵֽינוּ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Blessed is Adonoy by day, Blessed is Adonoy by night. Blessed is Adonoy when we lie down Blessed is Adonoy when we rise. For in Your hand are the souls of the living and the dead, (as it is written): For in His hand is the soul of every living thing and the spirit of every human being. In Your hand, I commit my spirit; You have liberated me, Adonoy, Almighty of truth. Our God in heaven, reveal the unity of Your Name, preserve Your kingdom always, and reign over us forever and ever.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Baruch Adonai bayom baruch Adonai balayela baruch Adonai b''shachevenu baruch Adonai b''kumenu.
Ki ve yadecha nafshot hachayim ve hametim asher b''yado nefesh kol chai ve ruach kol b''sar ish.
B''yadecha afkid ruchi padita oti Adonai el emet.
Eloheinu shebashamayim yached shimcha ve kayem malchutecha tamid umeloch aleinu le''olam vaed.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יִרְאוּ עֵינֵֽינוּ וְיִשְׂמַח לִבֵּֽנוּ וְתָגֵל נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ בִּישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ בֶּאֱמֶת בֶּאֱמוֹר לְצִיּוֹן מָלַךְ אֱלֺהָֽיִךְ. יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ יְהֹוָה מָלָךְ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד: כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּ֒ךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְ֒מֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד כִּי אֵין לָֽנוּ מֶֽלֶךְ אֶלָּא אָֽתָּה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','May our eyes behold, may our heart rejoice and our soul exalt in Your true deliverance, when it will be said to Zion: Your God has begun His reign Adonoy is King, Adonoy was King, Adonoy will reign forever and ever For the Kingdom is Yours and to all eternity, You will reign in glory, for we have no king except You.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Yiru eineinu ve yismach libenu ve tagel nafshenu bishuatecha be''emet be''emor letziyon malach elohayich.
Adonai melech Adonai malach Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod ki ein lanu melech ela atah.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הַמַּלְאָךְ הַגֹּאֵל אֹתִי מִכָּל רָע יְבָרֵךְ אֶת הַנְּ֒עָרִים וְיִקָּרֵא בָהֶם שְׁמִי וְשֵׁם אֲבוֹתַי אַבְרָהָם וְיִצְחָק וְיִדְגּוּ לָרֹב בְּקֶֽרֶב הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','The angel who redeemed me from all evil May he bless the lads; and may they be called by my name and the names of my fathers, Abraham and Isaac; and may they multiply like fish within the land.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Hamalach hagoel oti mikol ra yevarech et hanearim ve yikareh vahem shemi ve shem avotai Avraham ve Yitzchak ve yidgu larov b''kerev ha''aretz.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר אִם שָׁמֽוֹעַ תִּשְׁמַע לְקוֹל יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֶֽיךָ וְהַיָּשָׁר בְּעֵינָיו תַּעֲשֶׂה וְהַאֲזַנְתָּ לְמִצְוֹתָיו וְשָׁמַרְתָּ כָּל חֻקָּיו כָּל הַמַּחֲלָה אֲשֶׁר שַֽׂמְתִּי בְמִצְרַֽיִם לֺא אָשִׂים עָלֶֽיךָ כִּי אֲנִי יְהֹוָה רֹפְ֒אֶֽךָ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And He said, "If you will diligently heed the voice of Adonoy, your God, and do what is upright in His eyes, and listen carefully to His commandments, and guard all His statutes— [then] every sickness that I put in Egypt, I will not put upon you, for I am Adonoy, your Healer.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Vayomer im shamoa tishma lekol Adonai Elohecha ve hayashar b''einav ta''aseh ve ha''azanta lemitzvotav ve shamarta kol chukav kol hamachala asher sameti ve mitzrayim lo asim aleicha ki ani Adonai rofe''echa.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וַיֹּֽאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל הַשָּׂטָן יִגְעַר יְהֹוָה בְּךָ הַשָּׂטָן וְיִגְעַר יְהֹוָה בְּךָ הַבֹּחֵר בִּירוּשָׁלָֽםִ הֲלֺא זֶה אוּד מֻצָּל מֵאֵשׁ','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And Adonoy said to Satan: Adonoy rebukes you, Satan, Adonoy rebukes you, He Who chose Jerusalem; for is this one not a firebrand plucked out of the fire?','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Vayomer Adonai el hasatan yigar Adonai b''cha hasatan ve yigar Adonai b''cha habocher birushalami halo zeh ud mutzal me''esh','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הִנֵּה מִטָּתוֹ שֶׁלִּשְׁלֺמֹה שִׁשִּׁים גִּבֹּרִים סָבִיב לָהּ מִגִּבֹּרֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כֻּלָּם אֲחֻֽזֵי חֶֽרֶב מְלֻמְּ֒דֵי מִלְחָמָה אִישׁ חַרְבּוֹ עַל יְרֵכוֹ מִפַּֽחַד בַּלֵּילוֹת','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Behold the bed of Solomon! Sixty mighty men [are set] around it, of the mighty men of Israel. All of them armed with swords, trained in warfare; each man has his sword at his side, because of the dread of the night.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Hineh mitato shelishlomoh shishim giborim saviv lah migiborei Yisrael kulam achuzei cherev melumedei milchama ish charbo al yerecho mipachad baleilot','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יאמר כל פסוק ג"פ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Each unit is said three times:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהֹוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶֽךָ יָאֵר יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וִיחֻנֶּֽךָּ: יִשָּׂא יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וְיָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Adonoy bless you and guard you! Adonoy shine His countenance upon you and be gracious unto You! Adonoy turn His countenance toward you and grant you peace!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Yevarechcha Adonai ve yishmerecha yaer Adonai panav eleicha vichuneka.
Yisa Adonai panav eleicha ve yasem lecha shalom.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','הִנֵּה לֺא יָנוּם וְלֺא יִישָׁן שׁוֹמֵר יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Behold, He neither slumbers nor sleeps! the Guardian of Israel.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Hineh lo yanum ve lo yishan shomer Yisrael.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ קִוִּיתִי יְהֹוָה קִוִּיתִי יְהֹוָה לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ יְהֹוָה לִישׁוּעָתְ֒ךָ קִוִּיתִי','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','For your deliverance, I hope, Adonoy; I hope, Adonoy, for Your deliverance; Adonoy, for Your deliverance I hope.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Lishuatecha kiviti Adonai kiviti Adonai lishuatecha Adonai lishuatecha kiviti','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּשֵׁם יְהֹוָה אֱלֺהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִימִינִי מִיכָאֵל וּמִשְּׂ֒מֹאלִי גַבְרִיאֵל וּמִלְּ֒פָנַי אוֹרִיאֵל וּמֵאֲחוֹרַי רְפָאֵל וְעַל רֹאשִי שְׁכִינַת אֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','In the Name of Adonoy, God of Israel: at my right [hand] Michael, at my left [hand] Gabriel, before me Uriel, behind me Raphael, and above my head, the Presence of Almighty.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','B''shem Adonai Elohei Yisrael mimini michael umisemoli gavriel umilefanai oriel umeachorai refael ve al roshi shechinat el.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','שִׁיר הַמַּעֲלוֹת אַשְׁרֵי כָּל־יְרֵא יְהֹוָה הַהֹלֵךְ בִּדְרָכָיו: יְגִֽיעַ כַּפֶּֽיךָ כִּי תֹאכֵל אַשְׁרֶֽיךָ וְטוֹב לָךְ: אֶשְׁתְּ֒ךָ כְּגֶֽפֶן פֹּרִיָּה בְּיַרְכְּ֒תֵי בֵיתֶֽךָ בָּנֶֽיךָ כִּשְׁתִלֵי זֵיתִים סָבִיב לְשֻׁלְחָנֶֽךָ: הִנֵּה כִי־כֵן יְבֹֽרַךְ גָּֽבֶר יְרֵא יְהֹוָה: יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהֹוָה מִצִּיּוֹן וּרְאֵה בְּטוּב יְרוּשָׁלָֽםִ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּֽיךָ: וּרְאֵה־ בָנִים לְבָנֶֽיךָ שָׁלוֹם עַל־יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','A song of ascents Fortunate are all who fear Adonoy, who walk in His ways. When you eat of the toil of your hands you are fortunate and it is good with you. Your wife will be like a fruitful vine in the innermost parts of your house; your children like olive plants around your table. Behold! thus shall be blessed the man who fears Adonoy. Adonoy bless you from Zion! and [may you] see the good of Jerusalem all the days of your life! May you [live to] see your children''s children! Peace upon Israel!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Shir hama''alot ashrei kol yereh Adonai haholech bidrachav.
Yegia kapeicha ki tochel ashreicha ve tov lach.
Eshtecha k''gefen poriya b''yarketei veitecha baneicha kishtilei zeitim saviv leshulchanecha.
Hineh chi chen yevorach gaver yereh Adonai.
Yevarechcha Adonai mitziyon ure''eh b''tuv yerushalami kol yemei chayeicha.
Ure''eh vanim levaneicha shalom al Yisrael.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','יאמר כל פסוק ג"פ:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','To be said three times:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','רִגְזוּ וְאַל תֶּחֱטָֽאוּ אִמְרוּ בִלְבַבְכֶם עַל מִשְׁכַּבְכֶם וְדֹֽמּוּ סֶֽלָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Tremble and do not sin; commune with your hearts upon your bed, and be silent, selah!','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Rigzu ve al techetau imru vilvavchem al mishkavchem ve domu sela.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','אֲדוֹן עוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר מָלַךְ, בְּטֶֽרֶם כָּל יְצִיר נִבְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Master of the Universe Who reigned before any creature was created.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:26:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Adon olam asher malach,
b''terem kol yetzir nivra.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','לְעֵת נַעֲשָׂה בְחֶפְצוֹ כֹּל, אֲזַי מֶֽלֶךְ שְׁמוֹ נִקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','At the time when all was made by His will, then was His Name proclaimed King.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Le''et na''asa ve cheftzo kol,
azai melech shemo nikra.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְאַחֲרֵי כִּכְ֒לוֹת הַכֹּל, לְבַדּוֹ יִמְלֹךְ נוֹרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And after all things shall cease to be the Awesome One will reign alone.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve acharei kichlot hakol,
levado yimloch nora.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא הָיָה וְהוּא הֹוֶה, וְהוּא יִהְיֶה בְּתִפְאָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He was, He is, and He shall be in glory.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve hu haya ve hu hoveh,
ve hu yihyeh b''tifara.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא אֶחָד וְאֵין שֵׁנִי, לְהַמְשִׁיל לוֹ לְהַחְבִּֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is One, and there is no second to compare to Him, to associate [with Him].','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve hu echad ve ein sheni,
lehameshil lo lehachbira.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּלִי רֵאשִׁית בְּלִי תַכְלִית, וְלוֹ הָעֹז וְהַמִּשְׂרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Without beginning, without end, power and dominion are His.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:31:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','B''li reshit b''li tachlit,
ve lo haoz ve hamisra.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא אֵלִי וְחַי גּוֹאֲלִי, וְצוּר חֶבְלִי בְּעֵת צָרָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is my God and my ever-living Redeemer, the Rock of my destiny in times of distress.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve hu eli ve chai goali,
ve tzur chevli b''et tzara.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְהוּא נִסִּי וּמָנוֹס לִי, מְנָת כּוֹסִי בְּיוֹם אֶקְרָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','He is my flag and my refuge; He is the portion of my cup on the day I call.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve hu nisi umanos li,
menat kosi b''yom ekra.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','בְּיָדוֹ אַפְקִיד רוּחִי, בְּעֵת אִישַׁן וְאָעִֽירָה:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','Into His hand I entrust my spirit [both] when I sleep and when I awaken.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:34:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','B''yado afkid ruchi,
b''et ishan ve aira.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','he','וְעִם רוּחִי גְּוִיָּתִי, יְהֹוָה לִי וְלֹא אִירָא:','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','en','And with my spirit my body [too], Adonoy is with me, I shall not fear.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema:35:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-bedtime-shema','transliteration','Ve im ruchi geviyati,
Adonai li ve lo ira.','Siddur Sefard, Bedtime Shema'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','אֵשֶׁת חַיִל מִי יִמְצָא וְרָחֹק מִפְּנִינִים מִכְרָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Whoever finds a valorous wife— far greater than that of pearls is her value.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:0:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Eshet chayil mi yimtza ve rachok mipeninim michrah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','בָּטַח בָּהּ לֵב בַּעְלָהּ וְשָׁלָל לֹא יֶחְסָר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','The heart of her husband trusts in her, and he lacks no gain.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Batach bah lev balah ve shalal lo yechsar.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','גְּמָלַתְהוּ טוֹב וְלֹא רָע כָּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She repays him good and not evil all the days of her life.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Gemalathu tov ve lo ra kol yemei chayeih.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','דָּרְשָׁה צֶמֶר וּפִשְׁתִּים וַתַּעַשׂ בְּחֵפֶץ כַּפֶּיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She seeks wool and linen, and works them willingly with her hands.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Daresha tzemer ufishtim vata''as b''chefetz kapeiha.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','הָיְתָה כָּאֳנִיּוֹת סוֹחֵר מִמֶּרְחָק תָּבִיא לַחְמָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She is like the merchant ships; from afar, she brings her food.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Hayeta ko''oniyot socher mimerchak tavi lachmah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','וַתָּקָם בְּעוֹד לַיְלָה וַתִּתֵּן טֶרֶף לְבֵיתָהּ וְחֹק לְנַעֲרֹתֶיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She rises while it is still night and gives food to her household, and tasks to her maids.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Vatakom b''od layla vatiten teref leveitah ve chok lena''aroteiha.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','זָמְמָה שָׂדֶה וַתִּקָּחֵהוּ מִפְּרִי כַפֶּיהָ נָטְעָה כָּרֶם:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She considers a field and buys it; from the fruit of her hand, she plants a vineyard.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:6:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Zamema sadeh vatikachehu miperi chapeiha natea karem.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','חָגְרָה בְעוֹז מָתְנֶיהָ וַתְּאַמֵּץ זְרֹעוֹתֶיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She girds herself with might and strengthens her arms.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Chagera ve oz motneiha vateametz zero''oteiha.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','טָעֲמָה כִּי טוֹב סַחְרָהּ לֹא יִכְבֶּה בַלַּיְלָה נֵרָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She senses that her business is good, [so] her lamp is not extinguished at night.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Ta''ama ki tov sachrah lo yichbeh valayla nerah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','יָדֶיהָ שִׁלְּחָה בַכִּישׁוֹר וְכַפֶּיהָ תָּמְכוּ פָלֶךְ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She puts her hand to the spindle, and her palms support the distaff.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Yadeiha shilecha vakishor ve chapeiha tamechu falech.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','כַּפָּהּ פָּרְשָׂה לֶעָנִי וְיָדֶיהָ שִׁלְּחָה לָאֶבְיוֹן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her palm she spreads out to the poor and her hands she extends to the needy.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Kapah paresa leani ve yadeiha shilecha laevyon.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','לֹא תִירָא לְבֵיתָהּ מִשָּׁלֶג כִּי כָל בֵּיתָהּ לָבֻשׁ שָׁנִים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She has no fear for her household because of snow, for her entire household is clothed with scarlet [wool].','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:11:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Lo tira leveitah mishaleg ki chol beitah lavush shanim.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','מַרְבַדִּים עָשְׂתָה לָּהּ שֵׁשׁ וְאַרְגָּמָן לְבוּשָׁהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Bedspreads, she makes herself fine linen and purple [wool] are her clothing.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Marvadim aseta lah shesh ve argaman levushah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','נוֹדָע בַּשְּׁעָרִים בַּעְלָהּ בְּשִׁבְתּוֹ עִם זִקְנֵי אָרֶץ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Well-known at the gates is her husband as he sits among the elders of the land.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Noda bashearim balah b''shivto im ziknei aretz.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','סָדִין עָשְׂתָה וַתִּמְכֹּר וַחֲגוֹר נָתְנָה לַכְּנַעֲנִי:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Garments she makes and sells them, and belts, she provides for the merchants.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:14:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Sadin aseta vatimkor vachagor natena lakena''ani.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','עֹז וְהָדָר לְבוּשָׁהּ וַתִּשְׂחַק לְיוֹם אַחֲרוֹן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Strength and splendor are her clothing, and smilingly [she awaits her] last day.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Oz ve hadar levushah vatischak leyom acharon.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','פִּיהָ פָּתְחָה בְחָכְמָה וְתוֹרַת חֶסֶד עַל לְשׁוֹנָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her mouth she opens with wisdom, and the teaching of kindness is on her tongue.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:16:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Piha patecha ve chochma ve torat chesed al leshonah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','צוֹפִיָּה הֲלִיכוֹת בֵּיתָהּ וְלֶחֶם עַצְלוּת לֹא תֹאכֵל:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','She anticipates the ways of her household, and the bread of idleness, she does not eat.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Tzofiya halichot beitah ve lechem atzlut lo tochel.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','קָמוּ בָנֶיהָ וַיְאַשְּׁרוּהָ בַּעְלָהּ וַיְהַלְלָהּ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Her children rise16 and make her fortunate; her husband—and he praises her:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Kamu vaneiha vayeasheruha balah vayehalelah.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','רַבּוֹת בָּנוֹת עָשׂוּ חָיִל וְאַתְּ עָלִית עַל כֻּלָּנָה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Many daughters have attained valor but you surpassed them all.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Rabot banot asu chayil ve at alit al kulana.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','שֶׁקֶר הַחֵן וְהֶבֶל הַיֹּפִי אִשָּׁה יִרְאַת יְהֹוָה הִיא תִתְהַלָּל:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Favor is deceptive and beauty is vain; a God-fearing woman— —she should be praised.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Sheker hachen ve hevel hayofi isha yirat Adonai hi tithalal.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','he','תְּנוּ לָהּ מִפְּרִי יָדֶיהָ וִיהַלְלוּהָ בַשְּׁעָרִים מַעֲשֶׂיהָ:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','en','Give her the fruit of her hand, and let her deeds praise her in the gates.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil:21:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-evening-meal-eishet-chayil','transliteration','Tenu lah miperi yadeiha vihaleluha vashearim ma''aseiha.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Evening Meal, Eishet Chayil'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','he','אם קראו לספר תורה נער שנעשה בר מצוה אחר שבירך ברכה אחרונה. יאמר אביו:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','en','The following blessing is said by the father of a Bar Mitzvah, after the lad has been called to the Torah and has recited the blessing following the reading:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','he','בָּרוּךְ שֶׁפְּטָרַנִי מֵעָנְשׁוֹ שֶׁלָזֶה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who has released me from the punishment of this [boy].','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-bar-mitzva','transliteration','Baruch shepetarani meanesho shelazeh.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Bar Mitzva'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','he','מגביהין את הספר ואומרים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','en','When the reading of the Torah is concluded, the Half Kaddish is recited by the Reader. The Maftir is read and then the Torah is raised so that the congregation can see the script, and the congregation exclaims:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','he','וְזֹאת הַתּוֹרָה אֲשֶׁר שָׂם מֹשֶׁה לִפְנֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל: עַל פִּי יְהֹוָה בְּיַד מֹשֶׁה: תּוֹרָה צִוָה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה מוֹרָשָׁה קְהִלַּת יַעֲקֹב: עֵץ חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ וְתוֹמְכֶיהָ מְאֻשָּׁר: דְּרָכֶיהָ דַרְכֵי נֹעַם וְכָל נְתִיבוֹתֶיהָ שָׁלוֹם: אֹרֶךְ יָמִים בִּימִינָה, בִּשְׂמֹאלָה עֹשֶׁר וְכָבוֹד: יְהֹוָה חָפֵץ לְמַעַן צִדְקוֹ, יַגְדִּיל תּוֹרָה וְיַאְדִּיר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','en','This is the Torah which Moses placed before the children of Israel. at Adonoy''s command by the hand of Moses. It is a tree of life to those who grasp to it, and those who support it are fortunate. Its ways are ways of pleasantness, and all its paths are peace. Long life is at its right, at its left, riches and honor. Adonoy desired, for the sake of His righteousness, to make the Torah great and to glorify it.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-hagbahah','transliteration','Ve zot hatora asher sam Moshe lifnei b''nei Yisrael.
Al pi Adonai b''yad Moshe.
Torah tziva lanu Moshe morasha k''hilat Yaakov.
Etz chayim hi lamachazikim bah ve tomecheiha meushar.
Deracheiha darchei noam ve chol netivoteiha shalom.
Orech yamim bimina,
bismola osher ve chavod.
Adonai chafetz lema''an tzidko,
yagdil torah ve yadir.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Hagbahah'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','נהגו להזכיר נשמות המת אחר קריאת התורה בכל שבת שאומרים אב הרחמים:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','Yizkor may be recited following the Torah reading.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','לזכר:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','In memory of a father:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','אֵל מָלֵא רַחֲמִים שׁוֹכֵן בַּמְּרוֹמִים הַמְצֵא מְנוּחָה נְכוֹנָה עַל כַּנְפֵי הַשְּׁכִינָה בְּמַעֲלוֹת קְדוֹשִׁים וּטְהוֹרִים כְּזֹהַר הָרָקִיעַ מַזְהִירִים אֶת נִשְׁמַת (פב"פ) שֶׁהָלַךְ לְעוֹלָמוֹ בַּעֲבוּר (שפלוני) נָדַב לִצְדָקָה בְּעַד הַזְכָּרַת נִשְׁמָתוֹ, לָכֵן בַּעַל הָרַחֲמִים יַסְתִּירֵהוּ בְּסֵתֶר כְּנָפָיו לְעוֹלָמִים וְיִצְרֹר בִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים אֶת נִשְׁמָתוֹ יְהֹוָה הוּא נַחֲלָתוֹ וְיָנוּחַ בְּשָּׁלוֹם עַל מִשְׁכָּבוֹ וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','May God remember the soul of my father, my teacher, (Mention his Hebrew name and that of his father) son of who has gone to his world, because I pledge [without vowing] to donate charity for his sake In this merit, may his soul be bound up in the bond of life, with the souls of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov, Sarah, Rivkah, Rachel, and Leah, and with the other righteous men and women who are in the Gan Eden (Paradise) and let us say Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','transliteration','El maleh rachamim shochen bameromim hametzeh menucha nechona al kanfei hashechina b''ma''alot k''doshim utehorim k''zohar harakia mazhirim et nishmat (fvf") shehalach leolamo ba''avur (shflvny) nadav litzdaka b''ad hazkarat nishmato,
lachen ba''al harachamim yastirehu b''seter k''nafav leolamim ve yitzror bitzror hachayim et nishmato Adonai hu nachalato ve yanuach b''shalom al mishkavo ve nomar amen.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','לנקבה:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','In memory of a mother:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','he','אֵל מָלֵא רַחֲמִים שׁוֹכֵן בַּמְּרוֹמִים הַמְצֵא מְנוּחָה נְכוֹנָה עַל כַּנְפֵי הַשְּׁכִינָה בְּמַעֲלוֹת קְדוֹשִׁים וּטְהוֹרִים כְּזֹהַר הָרָקִיעַ מַזְהִירִים אֶת נִשְׁמַת (פב"פ) שֶׁהָלְכָה לְעוֹלָמָהּ בַּעֲבוּר (שפלוני) נָדַב לִצְדָקָה בְּעַד הַזְכָּרַת נִשְׁמָתָהּ, לָכֵן בַּעַל הָרַחֲמִים יַסְתִּירָהּ בְּסֵתֶר כְּנָפָיו לְעוֹלָמִים וְיִצְרֹר בִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים אֶת נִשְׁמָתָהּ יְהֹוָה הוּא נַחֲלָתָהּ וְתָנוּחַ בְּשָּׁלוֹם עַל מִשְׁכָּבָהּ וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','en','May God remember the soul of my mother, my teacher, (Mention her Hebrew name and that of her father) daughter of who has gone to her world. because I pledge [without vowing] to donate charity for her sake. In this merit, may her soul be bound up in the bond of life, with the souls of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov, Sarah, Rivkah, Rachel, and Leah, and with the other righteous men and women who are in Gan Eden (Paradise) and let us say, Amein.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-shabbat-morning-services-prayer-for-deceased','transliteration','El maleh rachamim shochen bameromim hametzeh menucha nechona al kanfei hashechina b''ma''alot k''doshim utehorim k''zohar harakia mazhirim et nishmat (fvf") shehalecha leolamah ba''avur (shflvny) nadav litzdaka b''ad hazkarat nishmatah,
lachen ba''al harachamim yastirah b''seter k''nafav leolamim ve yitzror bitzror hachayim et nishmatah Adonai hu nachalatah ve tanuach b''shalom al mishkavah ve nomar amen.','Siddur Sefard, Shabbat Morning Services, Prayer for Deceased'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:0:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הושענות ליו"ט ראשון ולחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:0:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Hoshanot for the First Day Holiday and the Intermediate Days','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשַׁע נָא','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:1:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hosha na','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For Your sake, our God, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:2:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Lema''ancha Eloheinu hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ בּוֹרְאֵנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Creator, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:3:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Lema''ancha bore''enu hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ גּוֹאֲלֵנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Redeemer, please save;','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:4:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Lema''ancha goalenu hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַנְךָ דּוֹרְשֵׁנוּ הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','for Your sake, our Seeker, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:5:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Lema''ancha doreshenu hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:6:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליו"ט ראשון למעט כשחל בשבת שאז אומרים זה ביום א'', א'' דחוה"מ:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:6:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the first day holiday, except when it falls out on Shabbat. In that case, we say this on Sunday, the first day of the intermediate days of the festival:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','לְמַעַן אֲמִתָּךְ. לְמַעַן בְרִיתָךְ. לְמַעַן גָּדְלָךְ וְתִפְאַרְתָּךְ. לְמַעַן דָּתָךְ. לְמַעַן הוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן וִעוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן זִכְרָךְ. לְמַעַן חַסְדָּךְ. לְמַעַן טוּבָךְ. לְמַעַן יִחוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן כְּבוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן לִמּוּדָךְ. לְמַעַן מַלְכוּתָךְ. לְמַעַן נִצְחָךְ. לְמַעַן סוֹדָךְ. לְמַעַן עֻזָךְ. לְמַעַן פְּאֵרָךְ. לְמַעַן צִדְקָתָךְ. לְמַעַן קְדֻשָּׁתָךְ. לְמַעַן רַחֲמֶיךָ הָרַבִּים. לְמַעַן שְׁכִינָתָךְ. הוֹשַׁע נָא: לְמַעַן תְּהִלָּתָךְ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the sake of Your truth; for the sake of Your covenant; for the sake of Your greatness and harmony; for the sake of Your doctrine; for the sake of Your majesty; for the sake of Your assembly; for the sake of Your mention; for the sake of Your kindness; for the sake of Your goodness; for the sake of Your unity; for the sake of Your glory; for the sake of Your teaching; for the sake of Your kingdom; for the sake of Your eternity; for the sake of Your secret; for the sake of Your might; for the sake of Your splendor; for the sake of Your righteousness; for the sake of Your holiness; for the sake of Your great mercy; for the sake of Your Divine Presence, please save! For the sake of Your praise, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:7:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Lema''an amitach.
Lema''an ve ritach.
Lema''an godlach ve tifartach.
Lema''an datach.
Lema''an hodach.
Lema''an viudach.
Lema''an zichrach.
Lema''an chasdach.
Lema''an tuvach.
Lema''an yichudach.
Lema''an k''vodach.
