('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:8:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:9:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','K''hoshata elim b''lud imach.
B''tzetecha leyesha amach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata goy velohim.
Derushim leyesha Elohim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata hamon tzivot.
Ve imam malachei tzevaot.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata zakim mibeit avadim.
Chanun b''yadam ma''avidim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata tevuim b''tzul gezarim.
Yekarecha imam ma''avirim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata kana meshoreret vayosha.
Legochah metzuyenet vayivasha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata ma''amar ve hotzeti etchem.
Nakuv ve hutzeti itechem.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata sovevei mizbeach.
Omesei arava lehakif mizbeach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata pilei aron k''hufsha.
Tzier peleshet bacharon af ve nosha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata k''hilot bavela shalachta.
Rachum lema''anam shulachta.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata shevut shivtei Yaakov.
Tashuv ve tashiv shevut oholei Yaakov ve hoshia na.
K''hoshata shomerei mitzvot ve chochei yeshuot el lemoshaot.
Ve hoshia na.
Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:10:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hoshia et amecha uvarech et nachalatecha ure''em ve nase''em ad ha''olam.
Ve yihyu devarai eleh asher hitchananti lifnei Adonai k''rovim el Adonai Eloheinu yomam valayela la''asot mishpat avdo umishpat amo Yisrael devar yom b''yomo.
Lema''an da''at kol amei ha''aretz ki Adonai hu haelohim ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:11:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליום א'' דחוה"מ למעט כשיו"ט חל בשבת אז יאמרו זה ביום ג'', ג'' דחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:11:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For the first day of the intermediate days of the festival, except when the holiday falls out on Shabbat. In that case, we say this on Tuesday, the third day of the intermediate days:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֶבֶן שְׁתִיָּה. בֵּית הַבְּחִירָה. גּוֹרֶן אָרְנָן. דְּבִיר הַמּוּצְנָע. הַר הַמּוֹרִיָּה. וְהַר יֵרָאֶה. זְבוּל תִּפְאַרְתֶּךָ. חָנָה דָוִד. טוֹב הַלְּבָנוֹן. יְפֵה נוֹף מְשׂוֹשׂ כָּל הָאָרֶץ. כְּלִילַת יוֹפִי. לִינַת הַצֶּדֶק. מָכוֹן לְשִׁבְתֶּךָ. נָוֶה שַׁאֲנָן. סֻכַּת שָׁלֵם. עֲלִיַּת שְׁבָטִים. פִּנַת יִקְרַת. צִיּוֹן הַמְצֻיֶּנֶת. קֹדֶשׁ הַקֳּדָשִׁים. רָצוּף אַהֲבָה. שְׁכִינַת כְּבוֹדֶךָ. תֵּל תַּלְפִּיּוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Foundation stone, chosen house, threshing floor of Ornan, hidden sanctuary, Mount Moriah, Mount of He is Seen, palace of Your splendor, residence of David, goodly ridge, beautifully placed, joy of all the earth, most beautiful bride, resting place of justice, place of Your dwelling, tranquil habitation, complete sukkah, pilgrimage of the tribes, precious corner, excellent Zion, holy of holies, inlaid with love, dwelling place of Your glory - please save! Hill of magnificence, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:12:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Even shetiya.
Beit habechira.
Goren arenan.
Devir hamutzena.
Har hamoriya.
Ve har yeraeh.
Zevul tifartecha.
Chana David.
Tov halevanon.
Yefeh nof mesos kol ha''aretz.
K''lilat yofi.
Linat hatzedek.
Machon leshivtecha.
Naveh sha''anan.
Sukat shalem.
Aliyat shevatim.
Pinat yikrat.
Tziyon hametzuyenet.
Kodesh hakodashim.
Ratzuf ahava.
Shechinat k''vodecha.
Tel talpiyot.
Hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:13:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
