K''hoshata ma''amar ve hotzeti etchem.
Nakuv ve hutzeti itechem.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata sovevei mizbeach.
Omesei arava lehakif mizbeach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata pilei aron k''hufsha.
Tzier peleshet bacharon af ve nosha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata k''hilot bavela shalachta.
Rachum lema''anam shulachta.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata shevut shivtei Yaakov.
Tashuv ve tashiv shevut oholei Yaakov ve hoshia na.
K''hoshata shomerei mitzvot ve chochei yeshuot el lemoshaot.
Ve hoshia na.
Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:15:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hoshia et amecha uvarech et nachalatecha ure''em ve nase''em ad ha''olam.
Ve yihyu devarai eleh asher hitchananti lifnei Adonai k''rovim el Adonai Eloheinu yomam valayela la''asot mishpat avdo umishpat amo Yisrael devar yom b''yomo.
Lema''an da''at kol amei ha''aretz ki Adonai hu haelohim ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:16:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','ליום ה'', ג'' דחוה"מ רק כשיו"ט חל ביום שני','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:16:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','For Thursday, the third day of the intermediate days of the festival, only when the holiday falls out on Monday:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אוֹם אֲנִי חוֹמָה. בָּרָה כַּחַמָּה. גּוֹלָה וְסוּרָה. דָּמְתָה לְתָמָר. הַהֲרוּגָה עָלֶיךָ. וְנֶחֱשֶׁבֶת כְּצֹאן טִבְחָה. זְרוּיָה בֵּין מַכְעִיסֶיהָ. חֲבוּקָה וּדְבוּקָה בָּךְ. טוֹעֶנֶת עֻלָּךְ. יְחִידָה לְיַחֲדָךְ. כְּבוּשָׁה בַגּוֹלָה. לוֹמֶדֶת יִרְאָתָךְ. מְרוּטַת לֶחִי. נְתוּנָה לְמַכִּים. סוֹבֶלֶת סִבְלָךְ. עֲנִיָּה סֹעֲרָה. פְּדוּיַת טוֹבִיָּה. צֹאן קָדָשִׁים. קְהִלּוֹת יַעֲקֹב. רְשׁוּמִים בִּשְׁמֶךָ. שׁוֹאֲגִים הוֹשַׁע נָא: תְּמוּכִים עָלֶיךָ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','The nation - ''I am a wall,'' bright as the sun, exiled and turned away, compared to a date palm, the one killed for You and considered like sheep for slaughter; scattered among its angerers, hugging and clinging to You, seeking Your yoke, alone to unify You, trampled in the exile, studying Your awe, pulled of cheek, given to be paupers, bearing Your burden, ship in a storm, redeemed of Tuviah (Moses), holy sheep, congregations of Jacob, marked with Your name - roars, "Please save!" [They are] dependent upon You, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:17:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Om ani choma.
Bara kachama.
Gola ve sura.
Dameta letamar.
Haharuga aleicha.
Ve necheshevet k''tzon tivcha.
Zeruya bein machiseiha.
Chavuka udevuka bach.
Toenet ulach.
Yechida leyachadach.
K''vusha vagola.
Lomedet yiratach.
Merutat lechi.
Netuna lemakim.
Sovelet sivlach.
Aniya soara.
Peduyat toviya.
Tzon kadashim.
K''hilot Yaakov.
Reshumim bishmecha.
Shoagim hosha na.
Temuchim aleicha.
Hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:18:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:19:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','K''hoshata elim b''lud imach.
B''tzetecha leyesha amach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata goy velohim.
Derushim leyesha Elohim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata hamon tzivot.
Ve imam malachei tzevaot.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata zakim mibeit avadim.
Chanun b''yadam ma''avidim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata tevuim b''tzul gezarim.
Yekarecha imam ma''avirim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata kana meshoreret vayosha.
Legochah metzuyenet vayivasha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata ma''amar ve hotzeti etchem.
Nakuv ve hutzeti itechem.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata sovevei mizbeach.
Omesei arava lehakif mizbeach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata pilei aron k''hufsha.
Tzier peleshet bacharon af ve nosha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata k''hilot bavela shalachta.
Rachum lema''anam shulachta.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata shevut shivtei Yaakov.
Tashuv ve tashiv shevut oholei Yaakov ve hoshia na.
K''hoshata shomerei mitzvot ve chochei yeshuot el lemoshaot.
Ve hoshia na.
Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:20:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hoshia et amecha uvarech et nachalatecha ure''em ve nase''em ad ha''olam.
Ve yihyu devarai eleh asher hitchananti lifnei Adonai k''rovim el Adonai Eloheinu yomam valayela la''asot mishpat avdo umishpat amo Yisrael devar yom b''yomo.
Lema''an da''at kol amei ha''aretz ki Adonai hu haelohim ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:21:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום א'', ה'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום ג'', ה'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ה'', ה'' דחוה"מ.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:21:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Sunday, the fifth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday comes out on Thursday, we say this on Tuesday, the fifth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday comes out on Shabbat, we say this on Thursday, the fifth day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אָדוֹן הַמּוֹשִׁיעַ. בִּלְתְּךָ אֵין לְהוֹשִׁיעַ. גִּבּוֹר וְרַב לְהוֹשִׁיעַ. דַּלּוֹתִי וְלִי יְהוֹשִׁיעַ. הָאֵל הַמּוֹשִׁיעַ. וּמַצִּיל וּמוֹשִׁיעַ. זוֹעֲקֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. חוֹכֶיךָ הוֹשִׁיעַ. טְלָאֶיךָ תַּשְׂבִּיעַ. יְבוּל לְהַשְׁפִּיעַ. כָּל שִׂיחַ תַּדְשֵׁא וְתוֹשִׁיעַ. לְגֵיא בַּל תַּרְשִׁיעַ. מְגָדִים תַּמְתִּיק וְתוֹשִׁיעַ. נְשִׂיאִים לְהַסִּיעַ. שְׂעִירִים לְהָנִיעַ. עֲנָנִים מִלְּהַמְנִיעַ. פּוֹתֵחַ יָד וּמַשְׂבִּיעַ. צְמֵאֶיךָ תַּשְׂבִּיעַ. קוֹרְאֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. רְחוּמֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. שׁוֹחֲרֶיךָ הוֹשִׁיעַ. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תְּמִימֶיךָ תּוֹשִׁיעַ. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','The Master who brings salvation - without You there is no salvation, mighty One and great in saving, ''I became indigent and He will bring me salvation,'' the saving God who rescues and brings salvation - bring salvation to those who cry to You; bring salvation to those that wait for You, to satiate your sheep, to give produce bountifully, make every shrub grow, and bring salvation. Do not do bad to the valley - sweeten the delicacies and bring salvation, to carry the clouds, to move the rains. Restrain the clouds, open the hand and satiate - satiate Your thirsty ones. Bring salvation to those that call to You, bring salvation to the ones You pity, bring salvation to the ones who seek You, please save! Bring salvation to Your blameless ones, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:22:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Adon hamoshia.
Biltecha ein lehoshia.
Gibor ve rav lehoshia.
Daloti ve li yehoshia.
Hael hamoshia.
Umatzil umoshia.
