('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:23:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:24:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','K''hoshata elim b''lud imach.
B''tzetecha leyesha amach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata goy velohim.
Derushim leyesha Elohim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata hamon tzivot.
Ve imam malachei tzevaot.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata zakim mibeit avadim.
Chanun b''yadam ma''avidim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata tevuim b''tzul gezarim.
Yekarecha imam ma''avirim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata kana meshoreret vayosha.
Legochah metzuyenet vayivasha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata ma''amar ve hotzeti etchem.
Nakuv ve hutzeti itechem.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata sovevei mizbeach.
Omesei arava lehakif mizbeach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata pilei aron k''hufsha.
Tzier peleshet bacharon af ve nosha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata k''hilot bavela shalachta.
Rachum lema''anam shulachta.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata shevut shivtei Yaakov.
Tashuv ve tashiv shevut oholei Yaakov ve hoshia na.
K''hoshata shomerei mitzvot ve chochei yeshuot el lemoshaot.
Ve hoshia na.
Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:25:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hoshia et amecha uvarech et nachalatecha ure''em ve nase''em ad ha''olam.
Ve yihyu devarai eleh asher hitchananti lifnei Adonai k''rovim el Adonai Eloheinu yomam valayela la''asot mishpat avdo umishpat amo Yisrael devar yom b''yomo.
Lema''an da''at kol amei ha''aretz ki Adonai hu haelohim ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:26:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ב'' יאמרו זה ביום ד'', ב'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום ה'', ב'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום א'', ג'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ו בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ב'', ב'' דחוה"מ','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:26:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Monday, we say this on Thursday, the second day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Thursday, the second day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֶעֱרוֹךְ שׁוּעִי. בְּבֵית שַׁוְעִי. גִּלִּיתִי בַצּוֹם פִּשְׁעִי. דְּרַשְׁתִּיךָ בּוֹ לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. הַקְשִׁיבָה לְקוֹל שַׁוְעִי. וְקוּמָה וְהוֹשִׁיעִי. זְכוֹר וְרַחֵם מוֹשִׁיעִי. חַי כֵּן תְּשַׁעְשְׁעִי. טוֹב בְּאֶנֶק שְׁעִי. יוּחַשׁ מוֹשִׁיעִי. כַּלֵּה מַרְשִׁיעִי. לְבַל עוֹד תַּרְשִׁיעִי. מַהֵר אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׁעִי. נֶצַח לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. שָׂא נָא עֲוֹן רִשְׁעִי. עֲבוֹר עַל פִּשְׁעִי. פְּנֵה נָא לְהוֹשִׁיעִי. צוּר צַדִּיק מוֹשִׁיעִי. קַבֵּל נָא שַׁוְעִי. רוֹמֵם קֶרֶן יִשְׁעִי. שַׁדַּי מוֹשִׁיעִי. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תּוֹפִיעַ וְתוֹשִׁיעִי. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','I shall set up my prayer in the house of my prayer: I have revealed my rebellion on the fast (Yom Kippur); I sought You then to save me. Listen to the voice of my prayer, and arise and bring me salvation. My Savior, remember and have mercy. Living One, indeed make me rejoice; Goodly One, in groaning, answer me - may my Savior be quick. Destroy the one who does evil to me (Satan), so that he not continue to make me evil. Quickly, God of my salvation, eternally to save me. Please lift up the iniquity of my evil, pass over my rebellion; please turn to me to bring me salvation. Rock, my righteous Savior, please accept my prayer. Lift up the horn of my salvation; Omnipresent, my Savior, please save! Appear and bring me salvation, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:27:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','E''eroch shui.
B''veit shavi.
Giliti vatzom pishi.
Derashticha bo lehoshi''i.
Hakshiva lekol shavi.
Ve kuma ve hoshi''i.
Zechor ve rachem moshi''i.
Chai ken teshashei.
Tov b''enek shei.
Yuchash moshi''i.
Kaleh marshi''i.
Leval od tarshi''i.
Maher Elohei yishi.
Netzach lehoshi''i.
Sa na avon rishi.
Avor al pishi.
Peneh na lehoshi''i.
Tzur tzadik moshi''i.
Kabel na shavi.
Romem keren yishi.
Shadai moshi''i.
Hosha na.
Tofia ve toshi''i.
Hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:28:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ אֵלִים בְּלוּד עִמָּךְ. בְּצֵאתְךָ לְיֵשַׁע עַמָּךְ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ גּוֹי וֵאלֹהִים. דְרוּשִׁים לְיֵשַׁע אֱלֹהִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ הֲמוֹן צִבְאוֹת. וְעִמָּם מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ זַכִּים מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים. חַנּוּן בְּיָדָם מַעֲבִידִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ טְבוּעִים בְּצוּל גְּזָרִים. יְקָרְךָ עִמָּם מַעֲבִירִים. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ כַּנָּה מְשׁוֹרֶרֶת וַיּוֹשַׁע. לְגוֹחָהּ מְצֻיֶּנֶת וַיִּוָּשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ מַאֲמַר וְהוֹצֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם. נָקוּב וְהוּצֵאתִי אִתְּכֶם. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ סוֹבְבֵי מִזְבֵּחַ. עוֹמְסֵי עֲרָבָה לְהַקִּיף מִזְבֵּחַ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ פִּלְאֵי אָרוֹן כְּהֻפְשַׁע. צִעֵר פְּלֶשֶׁת בַּחֲרוֹן אַף וְנוֹשַׁע. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ קְהִלּוֹת בָּבֶלָה שָׁלַחְתָּ. רַחוּם לְמַעֲנָם שֻׁלַּחְתָּ. כֵּן הוֹשַׁע נָא: כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שְׁבוּת שִׁבְטֵי יַעֲקֹב. תָּשׁוּב וְתָשִׁיב שְׁבוּת אָהֳלֵי יַעֲקֹב וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא. כְּהוֹשַׁעְתָּ שׁוֹמְרֵי מִצְוֹת וְחוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. וְהוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא: אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Like You saved the great ones in Lud (the son of Mitzrayim, Egypt''s namesake) with You, when You went out to save Your people, so too please save! Like You saved ''a nation and its leaders'' needing the salvation of God, so too please save! Like You saved many legions and, with them, hosts of angels, so too please save! Like You saved the pure ones from a house of bondage [when] they subjugated the Compassionate One with their hands, so too please save! Like You saved the drowning ones in the depths of the shreds [when] they were transporting Your glory with them, so too please save! Like You saved the base, singing (Exodus 13:40), "and He saved," [when] the One bursting out was indicated as saved, so too please save! Like You saved [with] the statement (Exodus 6:6), "and I will take you (etchem)," [but] it is designated, ''and I will go out with you (itchem),'' so too please save! Like You saved the ones that went around the altar, loaded with the willow to circle the altar, so too please save! Like You saved the wonders of the ark when it was sullied - He distraught Philistia with burning anger and it was saved - so too please save! Like You saved the congregations You sent to Babylonia - Merciful One, You [too] were sent for their sake - so too please save! You saved the return of the tribes of Jacob - return and bring back the return of the tents of Jacob and, so too, please save! Like You saved the keepers of the commandments and those awaiting salvations - You are the ''God of salvations'' - so, so too please bring salvation! Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:29:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','K''hoshata elim b''lud imach.
B''tzetecha leyesha amach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata goy velohim.
Derushim leyesha Elohim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata hamon tzivot.
Ve imam malachei tzevaot.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata zakim mibeit avadim.
Chanun b''yadam ma''avidim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata tevuim b''tzul gezarim.
Yekarecha imam ma''avirim.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata kana meshoreret vayosha.
Legochah metzuyenet vayivasha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata ma''amar ve hotzeti etchem.
Nakuv ve hutzeti itechem.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata sovevei mizbeach.
Omesei arava lehakif mizbeach.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata pilei aron k''hufsha.
Tzier peleshet bacharon af ve nosha.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata k''hilot bavela shalachta.
Rachum lema''anam shulachta.
Ken hosha na.
K''hoshata shevut shivtei Yaakov.
Tashuv ve tashiv shevut oholei Yaakov ve hoshia na.
K''hoshata shomerei mitzvot ve chochei yeshuot el lemoshaot.
Ve hoshia na.
Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','הוֹשִׁיעָה אֶת עַמֶּךָ וּבָרֵךְ אֶת נַחֲלָתֶךָ וּרְעֵם וְנַשְּׂאֵם עַד הָעוֹלָם: וְיִהְיוּ דְּבָרַי אֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר הִתְחַנַּנְתִּי לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה קְרוֹבִים אֶל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ יוֹמָם וָלָיְלָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפַּט עַבְדּוֹ וּמִשְׁפַּט עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר יוֹם בְּיוֹמוֹ: לְמַעַן דַּעַת כָּל עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים אֵין עוֹד:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Deliver and bless Your people; tend them and sustain them forever (Psalms 28:9). And may these words of mine, which I have offered in supplication before the Lord, be close to the Lord our God day and night, that He may provide for His servant and for His people Israel, according to each day’s needs. In order that all the peoples of the earth may know that the Lord alone is God, there is no other (I Kings 8:59-60).','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:30:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Hoshia et amecha uvarech et nachalatecha ure''em ve nase''em ad ha''olam.
Ve yihyu devarai eleh asher hitchananti lifnei Adonai k''rovim el Adonai Eloheinu yomam valayela la''asot mishpat avdo umishpat amo Yisrael devar yom b''yomo.
Lema''an da''at kol amei ha''aretz ki Adonai hu haelohim ein od.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:31:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','כשחל יו"ט ביום ב'' יאמרו זה ביום ו'', ד'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ג'' יאמרו זה ביום ו'', ג'' דחוה"מ. כשחל יו"ט ביום ה'' יאמרו זה ביום ב'', ד'' דחוה"מ, כשחל יו"ט בש"ק יאמרו זה ביום ד'', ד'' דחוה"מ.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:31:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','When the holiday falls out on Monday, we say this on Friday, the fourth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Tuesday, we say this on Friday, the third day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Thursday, we say this on Monday, the fourth day of the intermediate days. When the holiday falls out on Shabbat, we say this on Wednesday the fourth day of the intermediate days.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֵל לְמוֹשָׁעוֹת. בְּאַרְבַּע שָׁבוּעוֹת. גָּשִׁים בְּשַׁוְעוֹת. דּוֹפְקֵי עֶרֶךְ שׁוּעוֹת. (נ"א שְׁעוֹת) הוֹגֵי שַׁעְשְׁעוֹת. וְחִידוֹתָם מִשְׁתַּעְשְׁעוֹת. זוֹעֲקִים לְהַשְׁעוֹת. חוֹכֵי יְשׁוּעוֹת. טְפוּלִים בְּךָ שְׁעוֹת. יוֹדְעֵי בִין שָׁעוֹת. כּוֹרְעֶיךָ בְּשַׁוְעוֹת. לְהָבִין שְׁמוּעוֹת. מִפִּיךָ נִשְׁמָעוֹת. נוֹתֵן תְּשׁוּעוֹת. סְפוּרוֹת מַשְׁמָעוֹת. (נ"א מְשַׁמְעוֹת) עֵדוּת מַשְׁמִיעוֹת. פּוֹעֵל יְשׁוּעוֹת. צַדִּיק נוֹשָׁעוֹת. קִרְיַת (נ"א קָרֵב) תְּשׁוּעוֹת. רֶגֶשׁ תְּשׁוּאוֹת. שָׁלשׁ שָׁעוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא: תָּחִישׁ לִתְשׁוּעוֹת. הוֹשַׁע נָא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','''God of salvations'' - with four oaths, they approach with prayers, knock with the arrangement of prayers, meditate upon the enjoyments (the Torah) and enjoy their riddles; they yell out for salvations, those that await salvations with You in their prayers, knowing the understanding of the hours, bending down in their prayers to understand the traditions that were heard from Your mouth - Giver of salvations - recounters of heard things, the ones that give over [the] testimony - Doer of salvations, Righteous One of salvation - the town of salvation, [with] emotional cheers [in] three hours, please save! Be quick for salvations, please save!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:32:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','El lemoshaot.
B''arba shavuot.
Gashim b''shavot.
Dofekei erech shuot.
(n" sheot) hogei shasheot.
Ve chidotam mishtasheot.
Zoakim lehashot.
Chochei yeshuot.
Tefulim b''cha sheot.
Yode''ei vin shaot.
Kore''eicha b''shavot.
Lehavin shemuot.
Mipicha nishmaot.
Noten teshuot.
Sefurot mashmaot.
(n" meshamot) edut mashmiot.
Poel yeshuot.
Tzadik noshaot.
Kiryat (n" karev) teshuot.
Regesh teshuot.
Shalsh shaot.
Hosha na.
Tachish litshuot.
Hosha na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:he','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','he','אֲנִי וָהוֹ הוֹשִׁיעָה נָּא:','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:en','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','en','Ani Vaho, please bring salvation!','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
('sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed:33:transliteration','sefaria-siddur-sefard-sukkot-first-day-chol-hamoed','transliteration','Ani vaho hoshia na.','Siddur Sefard, Sukkot, First Day & Chol HaMoed'),
