('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בשבת מתחילין:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','On Shabbat, begin here:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','וַיְהִי־עֶרֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי. וַיְכֻלּוּ הַשָּׁמַיִם וְהָאָרֶץ וְכָל־צְבָאָם. וַיְכַל אֱלֹהִים בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה וַיִּשְׁבֹּת בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה. וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אוֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','And there was evening and there was morning, the sixth day. And the heaven and the earth were finished, and all their host. And on the seventh day God finished His work which He had done; and He rested on the seventh day from all His work which He had done. And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it; because He rested on it from all of His work which God created in doing (Genesis 1:31-2:3).','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Vayehi erev vayehi voker yom hashishi.
Vayechulu hashamayim ve ha''aretz ve chol tzeva''am.
Vayechal Elohim bayom hashevi''i melachto asher asa vayishbot bayom hashevi''i mikol melachto asher asa.
Vayevarech Elohim et yom hashevi''i vayekadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol melachto asher bara Elohim la''asot.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בחול מתחילין:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','On weekdays, begin here:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','סַבְרִי מָרָנָן וְרַבָּנָן וְרַבּוֹתַי. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, בּוֹרֵא פְּרִי הַגָּפֶן.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who creates the fruit of the vine.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Savri maranan ve rabanan ve rabotai.
Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
boreh peri hagafen.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר בָּחַר בָּנוּ מִכָּל־עָם וְרוֹמְמָנוּ מִכָּל־לָשׁוֹן וְקִדְּשָׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו. וַתִּתֶּן לָנוּ יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ בְּאַהֲבָה (לשבת: שַׁבָּתוֹת לִמְנוּחָה וּ)מוֹעֲדִים לְשִׂמְחָה, חַגִּים וּזְמַנִּים לְשָׂשׂוֹן, (לשבת: אֶת יוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת הַזֶּה וְ)אֶת יוֹם חַג הַמַּצּוֹת הַזֶּה זְמַן חֵרוּתֵנוּ, (לשבת: בְּאַהֲבָה) מִקְרָא קֹדֶשׁ זֵכֶר לִיצִיאַת מִצְרָיִם. כִּי בָנוּ בָחַרְתָּ וְאוֹתָנוּ קִדַּשְׁתָּ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים, (לשבת: וְשַׁבָּת) וּמוֹעֲדֵי קָדְשֶׁךָ (לשבת: בְּאַהֲבָה וּבְרָצוֹן) בְּשִׂמְחָה וּבְשָׂשׂוֹן הִנְחַלְתָּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who has chosen us from all peoples and has raised us above all tongues and has sanctified us with His commandments. And You have given us, Lord our God, [Sabbaths for rest], appointed times for happiness, holidays and special times for joy, [this Sabbath day, and] this Festival of Matsot, our season of freedom [in love] a holy convocation in memory of the Exodus from Egypt. For You have chosen us and sanctified us above all peoples. In Your gracious love, You granted us Your [holy Sabbath, and] special times for happiness and joy.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
elheinu melech ha''olam asher bachar banu mikol am ve romemanu mikol lashon ve kidshanu b''mitzvotav.
Vatiten lanu yeya Eloheinu b''ahava (lshvt.
Shabatot limnucha umoadim) lesimcha,
chagim uzemanim lesason,
(lshvt.
Et yom hashabat hazeh ve et) yom chag hamatzot hazeh zeman cherutenu,
(lshvt.
B''ahava) mikra kodesh zecher litziat mitzrayim.
Ki vanu vacharta ve otanu kidashta mikol ha''amim,
(lshvt.
Ve shabat) umoadei kodshecha (lshvt.
B''ahava uveratzon) b''simcha uvesason hinchaltanu.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:7:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, מְקַדֵּשׁ (לשבת: הַשַׁבָּת וְ)יִשְׂרָאֵל וְהַזְּמַנִּים.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:7:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, O Lord, who sanctifies [the Sabbath,] Israel, and the appointed times.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:7:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
mekadesh (lshvt.
Hashabat ve Yisrael) ve hazemanim.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:8:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בּמוצאי שבת מוסיפים:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:8:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','On Saturday night add the following two paragraphs:','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:9:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, בּוֹרֵא מְאוֹרֵי הָאֵשׁ. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, הַמַּבְדִיל בֵּין קֹדֶשׁ לְחֹל, בֵּין אוֹר לְחשֶׁךְ, בֵּין יִשְׂרָאֵל לָעַמִּים, בֵּין יוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי לְשֵׁשֶׁת יְמֵי הַמַּעֲשֶׂה. בֵּין קְדֻשַּׁת שַׁבָּת לִקְדֻשַּׁת יוֹם טוֹב הִבְדַּלְתָּ, וְאֶת־יוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי מִשֵּׁשֶׁת יְמֵי הַמַּעֲשֶׂה קִדַּשְׁתָּ. הִבְדַּלְתָּ וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ אֶת־עַמְּךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּקְדֻשָּׁתֶךָ.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:9:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who creates the light of the fire. Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who distinguishes between the holy and the profane, between light and darkness, between Israel and the nations, between the seventh day and the six working days. You have distinguished between the holiness of the Sabbath and the holiness of the Festival, and You have sanctified the seventh day above the six working days. You have distinguished and sanctified Your people Israel with Your holiness.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:9:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
boreh meorei haesh.
Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
hamavdil bein kodesh lechol,
bein or lechshech,
bein Yisrael la''amim,
bein yom hashevi''i lesheshet yemei hama''aseh.
Bein k''dushat shabat likdushat yom tov hivdalta,
ve et yom hashevi''i misheshet yemei hama''aseh kidashta.
Hivdalta ve kidashta et amecha Yisrael bikdushatecha.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:10:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, הַמַּבְדִיל בֵּין קֹדֶשׁ לְקֹדֶשׁ.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:10:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, O Lord, who distinguishes between the holy and the holy.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:10:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
hamavdil bein kodesh lekodesh.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:11:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, שֶׁהֶחֱיָנוּ וְקִיְּמָנוּ וְהִגִּיעָנוּ לַזְּמַן הַזֶּה.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:11:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who has granted us life and sustenance and permitted us to reach this season.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:11:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
shehecheyanu ve kiyemanu ve higianu lazeman hazeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:12:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','he','שותה בהסיבת שמאל ואינו מברך ברכה אחרונה.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh:12:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-kadesh','en','Drink while reclining to the left and do not recite a blessing after drinking.','Pesach Haggadah, Kadesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','he','כַּרְפַּס','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','en','Greens.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','transliteration','Karpas','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','he','לוקח מן הכרפס פחות מכזית – כדי שלא יתחייב בברכה אחרונה – טובל במי מלח, מברך "בורא פרי האדמה", ומכווין לפטור בברכה גם את המרור. אוכל בלא הסבה.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','en','Take from the greens less than a kazayit - so that you will not need to say the blessing after eating it; dip it into the salt water; say the blessing "who creates the fruit of the earth;" and have in mind that this blessing will also be for the bitter herbs. Eat without reclining.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, בּוֹרֵא פְּרִי הָאֲדָמָה.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','en','Blessed are you, Lord our God, King of the universe, who creates the fruit of the earth.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-karpas','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
boreh peri ha''adama.','Pesach Haggadah, Karpas'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz','he','יַחַץ','Pesach Haggadah, Yachatz'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz','en','Break','Pesach Haggadah, Yachatz'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz','transliteration','Yachatz','Pesach Haggadah, Yachatz'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz','he','חותך את המצה האמצעית לשתים, ומצפין את הנתח הגדול לאפיקומן','Pesach Haggadah, Yachatz'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-yachatz','en','Split the middle matsah in two, and conceal the larger piece to use it for the afikoman.','Pesach Haggadah, Yachatz'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','he','מַגִּיד','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','en','The Recitation [of the exodus story]','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','transliteration','Magid','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','he','מגלה את המצות, מגביה את הקערה ואומר בקול רם:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','en','The leader uncovers the matsot, raises the Seder plate, and says out loud:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','he','הָא לַחְמָא עַנְיָא דִּי אֲכָלוּ אַבְהָתָנָא בְּאַרְעָא דְמִצְרָיִם. כָּל דִכְפִין יֵיתֵי וְיֵיכֹל, כָּל דִצְרִיךְ יֵיתֵי וְיִפְסַח. הָשַּׁתָּא הָכָא, לְשָׁנָה הַבָּאָה בְּאַרְעָא דְיִשְׂרָאֵל. הָשַּׁתָּא עַבְדֵי, לְשָׁנָה הַבָּאָה בְּנֵי חוֹרִין.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','en','This is the bread of destitution that our ancestors ate in the land of Egypt. Anyone who is famished should come and eat, anyone who is in need should come and partake of the Pesach sacrifice. Now we are here, next year we will be in the land of Israel; this year we are slaves, next year we will be free people.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-ha-lachma-anya','transliteration','Ha lachma anya di achalu avhatana b''ara demitzrayim.
Kol dichfin yeitei ve yeichol,
kol ditzrich yeitei ve yifsach.
Hashata hacha,
leshana haba''a b''ara deyisrael.
Hashata avdei,
leshana haba''a b''nei chorin.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Ha Lachma Anya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions','he','מסיר את הקערה מעל השולחן. מוזגין כוס שני. הבן שואל:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Four Questions'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions','en','He removes the plate from the table. We pour a second cup of wine. The son then asks:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Four Questions'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions','he','מַה נִּשְׁתַּנָּה הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה מִכָּל הַלֵּילוֹת? שֶׁבְּכָל הַלֵּילוֹת אָנוּ אוֹכְלִין חָמֵץ וּמַצָּה, הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה – כֻּלּוֹ מַצָּה. שֶׁבְּכָל הַלֵּילוֹת אָנוּ אוֹכְלִין שְׁאָר יְרָקוֹת – הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה (כֻּלּוֹ) מָרוֹר. שֶׁבְּכָל הַלֵּילוֹת אֵין אָנוּ מַטְבִּילִין אֲפִילוּ פַּעַם אֶחָת – הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה שְׁתֵּי פְעָמִים. שֶׁבְּכָל הַלֵּילוֹת אָנוּ אוֹכְלִין בֵּין יוֹשְׁבִין וּבֵין מְסֻבִּין – הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה כֻּלָּנוּ מְסֻבִּין.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Four Questions'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions','en','What differentiates this night from all [other] nights? On all [other] nights we eat chamets and matsa; this night, only matsa? On all [other] nights we eat other vegetables; tonight (only) marror. On all [other] nights, we don''t dip [our food], even one time; tonight [we dip it] twice. On [all] other nights, we eat either sitting or reclining; tonight we all recline.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Four Questions'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-four-questions','transliteration','Mah nishtana halayla hazeh mikol haleilot?
Shebechal haleilot anu ochelin chametz umatza,
halayla hazeh – kulo matza.
Shebechal haleilot anu ochelin shear yerakot – halayla hazeh (kulo) maror.
Shebechal haleilot ein anu matbilin afilu pa''am echat – halayla hazeh shetei feamim.
Shebechal haleilot anu ochelin bein yoshevin uvein mesubin – halayla hazeh kulanu mesubin.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Four Questions'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','he','מַעֲשֶׂה בְרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר וְרַבִּי יְהוֹשֻׁעַ וְרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בֶּן־עֲזַרְיָה וְרַבִּי עֲקִיבָא וְרַבִּי טַרְפוֹן שֶׁהָיוּ מְסֻבִּין בִּבְנֵי־בְרַק וְהָיוּ מְסַפְּרִים בִּיצִיאַת מִצְרַיִם כָּל־אוֹתוֹ הַלַּיְלָה, עַד שֶׁבָּאוּ תַלְמִידֵיהֶם וְאָמְרוּ לָהֶם רַבּוֹתֵינוּ הִגִּיעַ זְמַן קְרִיאַת שְׁמַע שֶׁל שַׁחֲרִית.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','en','It happened once [on Pesach] that Rabbi Eliezer, Rabbi Yehoshua, Rabbi Elazar ben Azariah, Rabbi Akiva and Rabbi Tarfon were reclining in Bnei Brak and were telling the story of the exodus from Egypt that whole night, until their students came and said to them, "The time of [reciting] the morning Shema has arrived."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','transliteration','Ma''aseh ve rabi eliezer ve rabi yehoshua ve rabi elazar ben azarya ve rabi akiva ve rabi tarfon shehayu mesubin bivnei ve rak ve hayu mesaperim bitziat mitzrayim kol oto halayla,
ad shebau talmideihem ve ameru lahem raboteinu higia zeman k''riat shema shel shacharit.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','he','אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בֶּן־עֲזַרְיָה הֲרֵי אֲנִי כְּבֶן שִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה וְלֹא זָכִיתִי שֶׁתֵּאָמֵר יְצִיאַת מִצְרַיִם בַּלֵּילוֹת עַד שֶׁדְּרָשָׁהּ בֶּן זוֹמָא, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר, לְמַעַן תִּזְכֹּר אֶת יוֹם צֵאתְךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ. יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ הַיָּמִים. כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ הַלֵּילוֹת. וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ הָעוֹלָם הַזֶּה. כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ לְהָבִיא לִימוֹת הַמָּשִׁיחַ:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','en','Rabbi Elazar ben Azariah said, "Behold I am like a man of seventy years and I have not merited [to understand why] the exodus from Egypt should be said at night until Ben Zoma explicated it, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 16:3), ''In order that you remember the day of your going out from the land of Egypt all the days of your life;'' ''the days of your life'' [indicates that the remembrance be invoked during] the days, ''all the days of your life'' [indicates that the remembrance be invoked also during] the nights." But the Sages say, "''the days of your life'' [indicates that the remembrance be invoked in] this world, ''all the days of your life'' [indicates that the remembrance be invoked also] in the days of the Messiah."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-story-of-the-five-rabbis','transliteration','Amar rabi elazar ben azarya harei ani k''ven shivim shana ve lo zachiti sheteamer yetziat mitzrayim baleilot ad shederashah ben zoma,
shene''emar,
lema''an tizkor et yom tzetecha me''eretz mitzrayim kol yemei chayeicha.
Yemei chayeicha hayamim.
Kol yemei chayeicha haleilot.
Vachachamim omerim yemei chayeicha ha''olam hazeh.
Kol yemei chayeicha lehavi limot hamashiach.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Story of the Five Rabbis'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','he','בָּרוּךְ הַמָּקוֹם, בָּרוּךְ הוּא, בָּרוּךְ שֶׁנָּתַן תּוֹרָה לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל, בָּרוּךְ הוּא. כְּנֶגֶד אַרְבָּעָה בָנִים דִּבְּרָה תוֹרָה: אֶחָד חָכָם, וְאֶחָד רָשָׁע, וְאֶחָד תָּם, וְאֶחָד שֶׁאֵינוֹ יוֹדֵעַ לִשְׁאוֹל.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','en','Blessed be the Place [of all], Blessed be He; Blessed be the One who Gave the Torah to His people Israel, Blessed be He. Corresponding to four sons did the Torah speak; one [who is] wise, one [who is] evil, one who is innocent and one who doesn''t know to ask.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','transliteration','Baruch hamakom,
baruch hu,
baruch shenatan torah leamo Yisrael,
baruch hu.
K''neged arba''a vanim dibera torah.
Echad chacham,
ve echad rasha,
ve echad tam,
ve echad she''eino yodea lishol.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','he','חָכָם מָה הוּא אוֹמֵר? מָה הָעֵדוֹת וְהַחֻקִּים וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִים אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ אֶתְכֶם. וְאַף אַתָּה אֱמוֹר לוֹ כְּהִלְכוֹת הַפֶּסַח: אֵין מַפְטִירִין אַחַר הַפֶּסַח אֲפִיקוֹמָן:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','en','What does the wise [son] say? "''What are these testimonies, statutes and judgments that the Lord our God commanded you?'' (Deuteronomy 6:20)" And accordingly you will say to him, as per the laws of the Pesach sacrifice, "We may not eat an afikoman [a dessert or other foods eaten after the meal] after [we are finished eating] the Pesach sacrifice (Mishnah Pesachim 10:8)."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','transliteration','Chacham ma hu omer?
Ma haedot ve hachukim ve hamishpatim asher tziva yeya Eloheinu etchem.
Ve af atah emor lo k''hilchot hapesach.
Ein maftirin achar hapesach afikoman.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','he','רָשָׁע מָה הוּא אוֹמֵר? מָה הָעֲבוֹדָה הַזּאֹת לָכֶם. לָכֶם – וְלֹא לוֹ. וּלְפִי שֶׁהוֹצִיא אֶת עַצְמוֹ מִן הַכְּלָל כָּפַר בְּעִקָּר. וְאַף אַתָּה הַקְהֵה אֶת שִׁנָּיו וֶאֱמוֹר לוֹ: "בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְיָ לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם". לִי וְלֹא־לוֹ. אִלּוּ הָיָה שָׁם, לֹא הָיָה נִגְאָל:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','en','What does the evil [son] say? "''What is this worship to you?'' (Exodus 12:26)" ''To you'' and not ''to him.'' And since he excluded himself from the collective, he denied a principle [of the Jewish faith]. And accordingly, you will blunt his teeth and say to him, "''For the sake of this, did the Lord do [this] for me in my going out of Egypt'' (Exodus 13:8)." ''For me'' and not ''for him.'' If he had been there, he would not have been saved.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','transliteration','Rasha ma hu omer?
Ma ha''avoda hazot lachem.
Lachem – ve lo lo.
Ulefi shehotzi et atzmo min hakelal kafar b''ikar.
Ve af atah hakheh et shinav ve''emor lo.
"ba''avur zeh asa yeya li b''tzeti mimitzrayim".
Li ve lo lo.
Ilu haya sham,
lo haya nigal.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','he','תָּם מָה הוּא אוֹמֵר? מַה זּאֹת. וְאָמַרְתָּ אֵלָיו "בְּחוֹזֶק יָד הוֹצִיאָנוּ יְיָ מִמִּצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים".','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','en','What does the innocent [son] say? "''What is this?'' (Exodus 13:14)" And you will say to him, "''With the strength of [His] hand did the Lord take us out from Egypt, from the house of slaves'' (Exodus 13:14).''"','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','transliteration','Tam ma hu omer?
Mah zot.
Ve amarta elav "b''chozek yad hotzianu yeya mimitzrayim mibeit avadim".','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','he','וְשֶׁאֵינוֹ יוֹדֵעַ לִשְׁאוֹל – אַתְּ פְּתַח לוֹ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר, וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא לֵאמֹר, בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְיָ לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','en','And [regarding] the one who doesn''t know to ask, you will open [the conversation] for him. As it is stated (Exodus 13:8), "And you will speak to your son on that day saying, for the sake of this, did the Lord do [this] for me in my going out of Egypt."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-the-four-sons','transliteration','Ve she''eino yodea lishol – at petach lo,
shene''emar,
ve higadta levincha bayom hahu lemor,
ba''avur zeh asa yeya li b''tzeti mimitzrayim.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, The Four Sons'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh','he','יָכוֹל מֵראשׁ חֹדֶשׁ? תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא. אִי בַיּוֹם הַהוּא יָכוֹל מִבְּעוֹד יוֹם? תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה – בַּעֲבוּר זֶה לֹא אָמַרְתִּי, אֶלָּא בְּשָׁעָה שֶׁיֵּשׁ מַצָּה וּמָרוֹר מֻנָּחִים לְפָנֶיךָ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Yechol Me''rosh Chodesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh','en','It could be from Rosh Chodesh [that one would have to discuss the Exodus. However] we learn [otherwise, since] it is stated, "on that day." If it is [written] "on that day," it could be from while it is still day [before the night of the fifteenth of Nissan. However] we learn [otherwise, since] it is stated, "for the sake of this." I didn''t say ''for the sake of this'' except [that it be observed] when [this] matsa and maror are resting in front of you [meaning, on the night of the fifteenth].','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Yechol Me''rosh Chodesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-yechol-me-rosh-chodesh','transliteration','Yachol mersh chodesh?
Talmud lomar bayom hahu.
Ee vayom hahu yachol mibeod yom?
Talmud lomar ba''avur zeh – ba''avur zeh lo amarti,
ela b''sha''a sheyesh matza umaror munachim lefanecha.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Yechol Me''rosh Chodesh'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','he','מִתְּחִלָּה עוֹבְדֵי עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה הָיוּ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ, וְעַכְשָׁיו קֵרְבָנוּ הַמָּקוֹם לַעֲבוֹדָתוֹ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וַיֹאמֶר יְהוֹשֻעַ אֶל־כָּל־הָעָם, כֹּה אָמַר יְיָ אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, בְּעֵבֶר הַנָּהָר יָשְׁבוּ אֲבוֹתֵיכֶם מֵעוֹלָם, תֶּרַח אֲבִי אַבְרָהָם וַאֲבִי נָחוֹר, וַיַּעַבְדוּ אֱלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','en','From the beginning, our ancestors were idol worshipers. And now, the Place [of all] has brought us close to His worship, as it is stated (Joshua 24:2-4), "Yehoshua said to the whole people, so said the Lord, God of Israel, ''Over the river did your ancestors dwell from always, Terach the father of Avraham and the father of Nachor, and they worshiped other gods.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','transliteration','Mitechila ovedei avoda zara hayu avoteinu,
ve achshav kerevanu hamakom la''avodato,
shene''emar.
Vayomer yehoshua el kol ha''am,
koh amar yeya Elohei Yisrael,
b''ever hanahar yashevu avoteichem meolam,
terach avi Avraham va''avi nachor,
vaya''avdu Elohim acherim.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','he','וָאֶקַּח אֶת־אֲבִיכֶם אֶת־אַבְרָהָם מֵעֵבֶר הַנָּהָר וָאוֹלֵךְ אוֹתוֹ בְּכָל־אֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן, וָאַרְבֶּה אֶת־זַרְעוֹ וָאֶתֶּן־לוֹ אֶת־יִצְחָק. וָאֶתֵּן לְיִצְחָק אֶת־יַעֲקֹב וְאֶת־עֵשָׂו, וָאֶתֵּן לְעֵשָׂו אֶת־הַר שֵּׂעִיר לָרֶשֶׁת אוֹתוֹ, וְיַעֲקֹב וּבָנָיו יָרְדוּ מִצְרָיִם.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','en','And I took your father, Avraham, from over the river and I made him walk in all the land of Canaan and I increased his seed and I gave him Yitschak. And I gave to Yitschak, Ya''akov and Esav; and I gave to Esav, Mount Seir [in order that he] inherit it; and Yaakov and his sons went down to Egypt.''"','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','transliteration','Vaekach et avichem et Avraham me''ever hanahar vaolech oto b''chol eretz k''na''an,
va''arbeh et zaro vaeten lo et Yitzchak.
Vaeten leYitzchak et Yaakov ve et esav,
vaeten le''esav et har seir lareshet oto,
ve Yaakov uvanav yaredu mitzrayim.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','he','בָּרוּךְ שׁוֹמֵר הַבְטָחָתוֹ לְיִשְׂרָאֵל, בָּרוּךְ הוּא. שֶׁהַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא חִשַּׁב אֶת־הַקֵּץ, לַעֲשׂוֹת כְּמוֹ שֶּׁאָמַר לְאַבְרָהָם אָבִינוּ בִּבְרִית בֵּין הַבְּתָרִים, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וַיֹּאמֶר לְאַבְרָם, יָדֹעַ תֵּדַע כִּי־גֵר יִהְיֶה זַרְעֲךָ בְּאֶרֶץ לֹא לָהֶם, וַעֲבָדוּם וְעִנּוּ אֹתָם אַרְבַּע מֵאוֹת שָׁנָה. וְגַם אֶת־הַגּוֹי אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹדוּ דָּן אָנֹכִי וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן יֵצְאוּ בִּרְכֻשׁ גָּדוֹל.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','en','Blessed be the One who keeps His promise to Israel, blessed be He; since the Holy One, blessed be He, calculated the end [of the exile,] to do as He said to Avraham, our father, in the Covenant between the Pieces, as it is stated (Genesis 15:13-14), "And He said to Avram, ''you should surely know that your seed will be a stranger in a land that is not theirs, and they will enslave them and afflict them four hundred years. And also that nation for which they shall toil will I judge, and afterwards they will go out with much property.''"','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','transliteration','Baruch shomer havtachato leYisrael,
baruch hu.
Shehakadosh baruch hu chishav et haketz,
la''asot k''mo sheamar leAvraham avinu bivrit bein habetarim,
shene''emar.
Vayomer leavram,
yadoa teda ki ger yihyeh zaracha b''eretz lo lahem,
va''avadum ve inu otam arba meot shana.
Ve gam et hagoy asher ya''avodu dan anochi ve acharei chen yetzeu birchush gadol.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','he','מכסה המצה ומגביה את הכוס בידו, ואומר:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','en','He covers the matsa and lifts up the cup and says:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','he','וְהִיא שֶׁעָמְדָה לַאֲבוֹתֵינוּ וְלָנוּ. שֶׁלֹּא אֶחָד בִּלְבַד עָמַד עָלֵינוּ לְכַלּוֹתֵנוּ, אֶלָּא שֶׁבְּכָל דּוֹר וָדוֹר עוֹמְדִים עָלֵינוּ לְכַלוֹתֵנוּ, וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא מַצִּילֵנוּ מִיָּדָם.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','en','And it is this that has stood for our ancestors and for us; since it is not [only] one [person or nation] that has stood [against] us to destroy us, but rather in each generation, they stand [against] us to destroy us, but the Holy One, blessed be He, rescues us from their hand.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-in-the-beginning-our-fathers-were-idol-worshipers','transliteration','Ve hi sheameda la''avoteinu ve lanu.
Shelo echad bilvad amad aleinu lechalotenu,
ela shebechal dor vador omedim aleinu lechalotenu,
ve hakadosh baruch hu matzilenu miyadam.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, In the Beginning Our Fathers Were Idol Worshipers'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','כַּמָה מַעֲלוֹת טוֹבוֹת לַמָּקוֹם עָלֵינוּ!','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','How many degrees of good did the Place [of all bestow] upon us!','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Kama ma''alot tovot lamakom aleinu!','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ הוֹצִיאָנוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם וְלֹא עָשָׂה בָהֶם שְׁפָטִים, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had taken us out of Egypt and not made judgements on them; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu hotzianu mimitzrayim ve lo asa vahem shefatim,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ עָשָׂה בָהֶם שְׁפָטִים, וְלֹא עָשָׂה בֵאלֹהֵיהֶם, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had made judgments on them and had not made [them] on their gods; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu asa vahem shefatim,
ve lo asa veloheihem,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ עָשָׂה בֵאלֹהֵיהֶם, וְלֹא הָרַג אֶת־בְּכוֹרֵיהֶם, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had made [them] on their gods and had not killed their firstborn; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu asa veloheihem,
ve lo harag et b''choreihem,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ הָרַג אֶת־בְּכוֹרֵיהֶם וְלֹא נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־מָמוֹנָם, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had killed their firstborn and had not given us their money; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu harag et b''choreihem ve lo natan lanu et mamonam,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־מָמוֹנָם וְלֹא קָרַע לָנוּ אֶת־הַיָּם, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had given us their money and had not split the Sea for us; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu natan lanu et mamonam ve lo kara lanu et hayam,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ קָרַע לָנוּ אֶת־הַיָּם וְלֹא הֶעֱבִירָנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ בֶּחָרָבָה, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had split the Sea for us and had not taken us through it on dry land; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu kara lanu et hayam ve lo he''eviranu ve tocho becharava,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:7:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ הֶעֱבִירָנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ בֶּחָרָבָה וְלֹא שִׁקַּע צָרֵנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:7:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had taken us through it on dry land and had not pushed down our enemies in [the Sea]; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:7:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu he''eviranu ve tocho becharava ve lo shika tzarenu ve tocho dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:8:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ שִׁקַּע צָרֵנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ וְלֹא סִפֵּק צָרְכֵּנוּ בַּמִדְבָּר אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:8:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had pushed down our enemies in [the Sea] and had not supplied our needs in the wilderness for forty years; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:8:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu shika tzarenu ve tocho ve lo sipek tzorkenu bamidbar arbaim shana dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:9:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ סִפֵּק צָרְכֵּנוּ בַּמִּדְבָּר אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה וְלֹא הֶאֱכִילָנוּ אֶת־הַמָּן דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:9:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had supplied our needs in the wilderness for forty years and had not fed us the manna; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:9:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu sipek tzorkenu bamidbar arbaim shana ve lo he''echilanu et haman dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:10:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ הֶאֱכִילָנוּ אֶת־הַמָּן וְלֹא נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:10:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had fed us the manna and had not given us the Shabbat; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:10:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu he''echilanu et haman ve lo natan lanu et hashabat,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:11:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת, וְלֹא קֵרְבָנוּ לִפְנֵי הַר סִינַי, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:11:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had given us the Shabbat and had not brought us close to Mount Sinai; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:11:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu natan lanu et hashabat,
ve lo kerevanu lifnei har sinai,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:12:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ קֵרְבָנוּ לִפְנֵי הַר סִינַי, וְלא נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַתּוֹרָה. דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:12:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had brought us close to Mount Sinai and had not given us the Torah; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:12:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu kerevanu lifnei har sinai,
vel natan lanu et hatora.
Dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:13:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ נָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַתּוֹרָה וְלֹא הִכְנִיסָנוּ לְאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל, דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:13:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had given us the Torah and had not brought us into the land of Israel; [it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:13:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu natan lanu et hatora ve lo hichnisanu le''eretz Yisrael,
dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:14:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','אִלּוּ הִכְנִיסָנוּ לְאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל וְלֹא בָנָה לָּנוּ אֶת־בֵּית הַבְּחִירָה דַּיֵּנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:14:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','If He had brought us into the land of Israel and had not built us the ''Chosen House'' [the Temple; it would have been] enough for us.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:14:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Ilu hichnisanu le''eretz Yisrael ve lo vana lanu et beit habechira dayenu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:15:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','he','עַל אַחַת, כַּמָה וְכַמָה, טוֹבָה כְפוּלָה וּמְכֻפֶּלֶת לַמָּקוֹם עָלֵינוּ: שֶׁהוֹצִיאָנוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם, וְעָשָׂה בָהֶם שְׁפָטִים, וְעָשָׂה בֵאלֹהֵיהֶם, וְהָרַג אֶת־בְּכוֹרֵיהֶם, וְנָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־מָמוֹנָם, וְקָרַע לָנוּ אֶת־הַיָּם, וְהֶעֱבִירָנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ בֶּחָרָבָה, וְשִׁקַּע צָרֵנוּ בְתוֹכוֹ, וְסִפֵּק צָרְכֵּנוּ בַּמִדְבָּר אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה, וְהֶאֱכִילָנוּ אֶת־הַמָּן, וְנָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת, וְקֵרְבָנוּ לִפְנֵי הַר סִינַי, וְנָתַן לָנוּ אֶת־הַתּוֹרָה, וְהִכְנִיסָנוּ לְאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל, וּבָנָה לָּנוּ אֶת־בֵּית הַבְּחִירָה לְכַפֵּר עַל־כָּל־עֲוֹנוֹתֵינוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:15:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','en','How much more so is the good that is doubled and quadrupled that the Place [of all bestowed] upon us [enough for us]; since he took us out of Egypt, and made judgments with them, and made [them] with their gods, and killed their firstborn, and gave us their money, and split the Sea for us, and brought us through it on dry land, and pushed down our enemies in [the Sea], and supplied our needs in the wilderness for forty years, and fed us the manna, and gave us the Shabbat, and brought us close to Mount Sinai, and gave us the Torah, and brought us into the land of Israel and built us the ''Chosen House'' [the Temple] to atone upon all of our sins.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu:15:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-dayenu','transliteration','Al achat,
kama ve chama,
tova chefula umechupelet lamakom aleinu.
Shehotzianu mimitzrayim,
ve asa vahem shefatim,
ve asa veloheihem,
ve harag et b''choreihem,
ve natan lanu et mamonam,
ve kara lanu et hayam,
ve he''eviranu ve tocho becharava,
ve shika tzarenu ve tocho,
ve sipek tzorkenu bamidbar arbaim shana,
ve he''echilanu et haman,
ve natan lanu et hashabat,
ve kerevanu lifnei har sinai,
ve natan lanu et hatora,
ve hichnisanu le''eretz Yisrael,
uvana lanu et beit habechira lechaper al kol avonoteinu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Dayenu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','רַבָּן גַּמְלִיאֵל הָיָה אוֹמֵר: כָּל שֶׁלֹּא אָמַר שְׁלֹשָׁה דְּבָרִים אֵלּוּ בַּפֶּסַח, לֹא יָצָא יְדֵי חוֹבָתוֹ, וְאֵלּוּ הֵן: פֶּסַח, מַצָּה, וּמָרוֹר.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','Rabban Gamliel was accustomed to say, Anyone who has not said these three things on Pesach has not fulfilled his obligation, and these are them: the Pesach sacrifice, matsa and marror.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','transliteration','Raban gamliel haya omer.
Kol shelo amar shelosha devarim elu bapesach,
lo yatza yedei chovato,
ve elu hen.
Pesach,
matza,
umaror.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','פֶּסַח שֶׁהָיוּ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ אוֹכְלִים בִּזְמַן שֶׁבֵּית הַמִּקְדָּשׁ הָיָה קַיָּם, עַל שׁוּם מָה? עַל שׁוּם שֶׁפָּסַח הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא עַל בָּתֵּי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ בְּמִצְרַיִם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וַאֲמַרְתֶּם זֶבַח־פֶּסַח הוּא לַייָ, אֲשֶׁר פָּסַח עַל־בָּתֵּי בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּמִצְרַיִם בְּנָגְפּוֹ אֶת־מִצְרַיִם, וְאֶת־בָּתֵּינוּ הִצִּיל, וַיִּקֹּד הָעָם וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲווּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','The Pesach [passover] sacrifice that our ancestors were accustomed to eating when the Temple existed, for the sake of what [was it]? For the sake [to commemorate] that the Holy One, blessed be He, passed over the homes of our ancestors in Egypt, as it is stated (Exodus 12:27); "And you shall say: ''It is the passover sacrifice to the Lord, for that He passed over the homes of the Children of Israel in Egypt, when He smote the Egyptians, and our homes he saved.’ And the people bowed the head and bowed."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','transliteration','Pesach shehayu avoteinu ochelim bizman shebeit hamikdash haya kayam,
al shum ma?
Al shum shepasach hakadosh baruch hu al batei avoteinu b''mitzrayim,
shene''emar.
Va''amartem zevach pesach hu layya,
asher pasach al batei ve nei Yisrael b''mitzrayim b''nagepo et mitzrayim,
ve et bateinu hitzil,
vayikod ha''am vayishtachavu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','אוחז המצה בידו ומראה אותה למסובין:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','He holds the matsa in his hand and shows it to the others there.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','מַצָּה זוֹ שֶׁאָנוּ אוֹכְלִים, עַל שׁוּם מַה? עַל שׁוּם שֶׁלֹּא הִסְפִּיק בְּצֵקָם שֶׁל אֲבוֹתֵינוּ לְהַחֲמִיץ עַד שֶׁנִּגְלָה עֲלֵיהֶם מֶלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים, הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, וּגְאָלָם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וַיֹּאפוּ אֶת־הַבָּצֵק אֲשֶׁר הוֹצִיאוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם עֻגֹת מַצּוֹת, כִּי לֹא חָמֵץ, כִּי גֹרְשׁוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם וְלֹא יָכְלוּ לְהִתְמַהְמֵהַּ, וְגַם־צֵדָה לֹא־עָשׂוּ לָהֶם.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','This matsa that we are eating, for the sake of what [is it]? For the sake [to commemorate] that our ancestors'' dough was not yet able to rise, before the King of the kings of kings, the Holy One, blessed be He, revealed [Himself] to them and redeemed them, as it is stated (Exodus 12:39); "And they baked the dough which they brought out of Egypt into matsa cakes, since it did not rise; because they were expelled from Egypt, and could not tarry, neither had they made for themselves provisions."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','transliteration','Matza zo sheanu ochelim,
al shum mah?
Al shum shelo hispik b''tzekam shel avoteinu lehachamitz ad shenigla aleihem melech malchei hamelachim,
hakadosh baruch hu,
ugealam,
shene''emar.
Vayofu et habatzek asher hotziu mimitzrayim ugot matzot,
ki lo chametz,
ki goreshu mimitzrayim ve lo yachelu lehitmahmeah,
ve gam tzeda lo asu lahem.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','אוחז המרור בידו ומראה אותו למסובין:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','He holds the marror in his hand and shows it to the others there.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','מָרוֹר זֶה שֶׁאָנוּ אוֹכְלִים, עַל שׁוּם מַה? עַל שׁוּם שֶׁמֵּרְרוּ הַמִּצְרִים אֶת־חַיֵּי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ בְּמִצְרַיִם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וַיְמָרְרוּ אֶת־חַיֵּיהם בַּעֲבֹדָה קָשָה, בְּחֹמֶר וּבִלְבֵנִים וּבְכָל־עֲבֹדָה בַּשָּׂדֶה אֶת כָּל עֲבֹדָתָם אֲשֶׁר־עָבְדוּ בָהֶם בְּפָרֶךְ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','This marror [bitter greens] that we are eating, for the sake of what [is it]? For the sake [to commemorate] that the Egyptians embittered the lives of our ancestors in Egypt, as it is stated (Exodus 1:14); "And they made their lives bitter with hard service, in mortar and in brick, and in all manner of service in the field; in all their service, wherein they made them serve with rigor."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','transliteration','Maror zeh sheanu ochelim,
al shum mah?
Al shum shemereru hamitzrim et chayei avoteinu b''mitzrayim,
shene''emar.
Vayemareru et chayeihm ba''avoda kasha,
b''chomer uvilvenim uvechol avoda basadeh et kol avodatam asher avedu vahem b''farech.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','he','בְּכָל־דּוֹר וָדוֹר חַיָּב אָדָם לִרְאוֹת אֶת־עַצְמוֹ כְּאִלּוּ הוּא יָצָא מִמִּצְרַיִם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא לֵאמֹר, בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְיָ לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרַיִם. לֹא אֶת־אֲבוֹתֵינוּ בִּלְבַד גָּאַל הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, אֶלָּא אַף אוֹתָנוּ גָּאַל עִמָּהֶם, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: וְאוֹתָנוּ הוֹצִיא מִשָּׁם, לְמַעַן הָבִיא אוֹתָנוּ, לָתֶת לָנוּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לַאֲבֹתֵינוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','en','In each and every generation, a person is obligated to see himself as if he left Egypt, as it is stated (Exodus 13:8); "And you shall explain to your son on that day: For the sake of this, did the Lord do [this] for me in my going out of Egypt." Not only our ancestors did the Holy One, blessed be He, redeem, but rather also us [together] with them did He redeem, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 6:23); "And He took us out from there, in order to bring us in, to give us the land which He swore unto our fathers."','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-rabban-gamliel-s-three-things','transliteration','B''chol dor vador chayav adam lirot et atzmo k''ilu hu yatza mimitzrayim,
shene''emar.
Ve higadta levincha bayom hahu lemor,
ba''avur zeh asa yeya li b''tzeti mimitzrayim.
Lo et avoteinu bilvad ga''al hakadosh baruch hu,
ela af otanu ga''al imahem,
shene''emar.
Ve otanu hotzi misham,
lema''an havi otanu,
latet lanu et ha''aretz asher nishba la''avoteinu.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Rabban Gamliel''s Three Things'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','he','יאחז הכוס בידו ויכסה המצות ויאמר:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','en','He holds the cup in his hand and and he covers the matsa and says:','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','he','לְפִיכָךְ אֲנַחְנוּ חַיָּבִים לְהוֹדוֹת, לְהַלֵּל, לְשַׁבֵּחַ, לְפָאֵר, לְרוֹמֵם, לְהַדֵּר, לְבָרֵךְ, לְעַלֵּה, וּלְקַלֵּס לְמִי שֶׁעָשָׂה לַאֲבוֹתֵינוּ וְלָנוּ אֶת־כָּל־הַנִסִּים הָאֵלּוּ: הוֹצִיאָנוּ מֵעַבְדוּת לְחֵרוּת, מִיָּגוֹן לְשִׂמְחָה, וּמֵאֵבֶל לְיוֹם טוֹב, וּמֵאֲפֵלָה לְאוֹר גָּדוֹל, וּמִשִּׁעְבּוּד לִגְאֻלָּה. וְנֹאמַר לְפָנָיו שִׁירָה חֲדָשָׁה: הַלְלוּ יָהּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','en','Therefore we are obligated to thank, praise, laud, glorify, exalt, lavish, bless, raise high, and acclaim He who made all these miracles for our ancestors and for us: He brought us out from slavery to freedom, from sorrow to joy, from mourning to [celebration of] a festival, from darkness to great light, and from servitude to redemption. And let us say a new song before Him, Halleluyah!','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','transliteration','Lefichach anachnu chayavim lehodot,
lehalel,
leshabeach,
lefaer,
leromem,
lehader,
levarech,
lealeh,
ulekales lemi sheasa la''avoteinu ve lanu et kol hanisim haelu.
Hotzianu meavdut lecherut,
miyagon lesimcha,
ume''evel leyom tov,
umeafela leor gadol,
umishibud ligula.
Ve nomar lefanav shira chadasha.
Halelu yah.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','he','הַלְלוּ יָהּ הַלְלוּ עַבְדֵי יְיָ, הַלְלוּ אֶת־שֵׁם יְיָ. יְהִי שֵׁם יְיָ מְבֹרָךְ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד־עוֹלָם. מִמִּזְרַח־שֶׁמֶשׁ עַד־מְבוֹאוֹ מְהֻלָּל שֵׁם יְיָ. רָם עַל־כָּל־גּוֹיִם יְיָ, עַל הַשָּׁמַיִם כְּבוֹדוֹ. מִי כַּייָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ הַמַּגְבִּיהִי לָשָׁבֶת. הַמַּשְׁפִּילִי לִרְאוֹת בַּשָּׁמַיִם וּבָאָרֶץ. מְקִימִי מֵעָפָר דָּל, מֵאַשְׁפֹּת יָרִים אֶבְיוֹן. לְהוֹשִׁיבִי עִם־נְדִיבִים, עִם נְדִיבֵי עַמּוֹ. מוֹשִׁיבִי עֲקֶרֶת הַבַּיִת, אֵם־הַבָּנִים שְׂמֵחָה, הַלְלוּ־יָהּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','en','Halleluyah! Praise, servants of the Lord, praise the name of the Lord. May the Name of the Lord be blessed from now and forever. From the rising of the sun in the East to its setting, the name of the Lord is praised. Above all nations is the Lord, His honor is above the heavens. Who is like the Lord, our God, Who sits on high; Who looks down upon the heavens and the earth? He brings up the poor out of the dirt; from the refuse piles, He raises the destitute. To seat him with the nobles, with the nobles of his people. He seats a barren woman in a home, a happy mother of children. Halleluyah! (Psalms 113)','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','transliteration','Halelu yah halelu avdei yeya,
halelu et shem yeya.
Yehi shem yeya mevorach meatah ve ad olam.
Mimizrach shemesh ad mevo''o mehulal shem yeya.
Ram al kol goyim yeya,
al hashamayim k''vodo.
Mi kayya Eloheinu hamagbihi lashavet.
Hamashpili lirot bashamayim uva''aretz.
Mekimi meafar dal,
meashpot yarim evyon.
Lehoshivi im nedivim,
im nedivei amo.
Moshivi akeret habayit,
em habanim semecha,
halelu yah.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','he','בְּצֵאת יִשְׂרָאֵל מִמִּצְרַיִם, בֵּית יַעֲקֹב מֵעַם לֹעֵז. הָיְתָה יְהוּדָה לְקָדְשׁוֹ, יִשְׂרָאֵל מַמְשְׁלוֹתָיו. הַיָּם רָאָה וַיָּנֹס, הַיַּרְדֵּן יִסֹּב לְאָחוֹר. הֶהָרִים רָקְדוּ כְאֵילִים, גְּבָעוֹת כִּבְנֵי צֹאן. מַה־לְּךָ הַיָּם כִּי תָנוּס, הַיַּרְדֵּן – תִּסֹּב לְאָחוֹר. הֶהָרִים – תִּרְקְדוּ כְאֵילִים, גְּבָעוֹת כִּבְנֵי־צֹאן. מִלְּפְנֵי אָדוֹן חוּלִי אָרֶץ, מִלְּפְנֵי אֱלוֹהַּ יַעֲקֹב. הַהֹפְכִי הַצּוּר אֲגַם־מָיִם, חַלָּמִיש לְמַעְיְנוֹ־מָיִם.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','en','In Israel''s going out from Egypt, the house of Ya''akov from a people of foreign speech. Yehudah became His -holy one, Israel, His dominion. The Sea saw and fled, the Jordan turned to the rear. The mountains danced like rams, the hills like young sheep. What is happening to you, O Sea, that you are fleeing, O Jordan that you turn to the rear; O mountains that you dance like rams, O hills like young sheep? From before the Master, tremble O earth, from before the Lord of Ya''akov. He who turns the boulder into a pond of water, the flint into a spring of water. (Psalms 114)','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-first-half-of-hallel','transliteration','B''tzet Yisrael mimitzrayim,
beit Yaakov meam loez.
Hayeta Yehudah lekodsho,
Yisrael mamshelotav.
Hayam ra''a vayanos,
hayarden yisov leachor.
Heharim rakedu che''eilim,
gevaot kivnei tzon.
Mah lecha hayam ki tanus,
hayarden – tisov leachor.
Heharim – tirkedu che''eilim,
gevaot kivnei tzon.
Milefenei adon chuli aretz,
milefenei eloah Yaakov.
Hahofechi hatzur agam mayim,
chalamish lemayeno mayim.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, First Half of Hallel'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','he','מגביהים את הכוס עד גאל ישראל.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','en','We raise the cup until we reach "who redeemed Israel"','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, אֲשֶׁר גְּאָלָנוּ וְגָאַל אֶת־אֲבוֹתֵינוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם, וְהִגִּיעָנוּ הַלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה לֶאֱכָל־בּוֹ מַצָּה וּמָרוֹר. כֵּן יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ יַגִּיעֵנוּ לְמוֹעֲדִים וְלִרְגָלִים אֲחֵרִים הַבָּאִים לִקְרָאתֵנוּ לְשָׁלוֹם, שְׂמֵחִים בְּבִנְיַן עִירֶךָ וְשָׂשִׂים בַּעֲבוֹדָתֶךָ. וְנֹאכַל שָׁם מִן הַזְּבָחִים וּמִן הַפְּסָחִים אֲשֶׁר יַגִּיעַ דָּמָם עַל קִיר מִזְבַּחֲךָ לְרָצוֹן, וְנוֹדֶה לְךָ שִׁיר חָדָש עַל גְּאֻלָּתֵנוּ וְעַל פְּדוּת נַפְשֵׁנוּ. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, גָּאַל יִשְׂרָאֵל.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who redeemed us and redeemed our ancestors from Egypt, and brought us on this night to eat matsa and marror; so too, Lord our God, and God of our ancestors, bring us to other appointed times and holidays that will come to greet us in peace, joyful in the building of Your city and happy in Your worship; that we shall eat there from the offerings and from the Pesach sacrifices, the blood of which shall reach the wall of Your altar for favor, and we shall thank You with a new song upon our redemption and upon the restoration of our souls. Blessed are you, Lord, who redeemed Israel.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
asher gealanu ve ga''al et avoteinu mimitzrayim,
ve higianu halayla hazeh le''echol bo matza umaror.
Ken yeya Eloheinu velohei avoteinu yagienu lemoadim ve lirgalim acherim habaim likratenu leshalom,
semechim b''vinyan irecha ve sasim ba''avodatecha.
Ve nochal sham min hazevachim umin hapesachim asher yagia damam al kir mizbachacha leratzon,
ve nodeh lecha shir chadash al geulatenu ve al pedut nafshenu.
Baruch atah yeya,
ga''al Yisrael.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','he','שותים את הכוס בהסבת שמאל.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','en','We say the blessing below and drink the cup while reclining to the left','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם בּוֹרֵא פְּרִי הַגָּפֶן.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, who creates the fruit of the vine.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-magid-second-cup-of-wine','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam boreh peri hagafen.','Pesach Haggadah, Magid, Second Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','he','רָחְצָה','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','en','Washing','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','transliteration','Rachetza','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','he','נוטלים את הידים ומברכים:','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','en','We wash the hands and make the blessing.','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, אֲשֶׁר קִדְּשָׁנוּ בְמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ עַל נְטִילַת יָדַיִם.','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the Universe, who has sanctified us with His commandments and has commanded us on the washing of the hands.','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-rachtzah','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
asher kidshanu ve mitzvotav ve tzivanu al netilat yadayim.','Pesach Haggadah, Rachtzah'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech','he','שֻׁלְחָן עוֹרֵךְ','Pesach Haggadah, Shulchan Orech'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech','en','The Set Table','Pesach Haggadah, Shulchan Orech'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech','transliteration','Shulchan orech','Pesach Haggadah, Shulchan Orech'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech','he','אוכלים ושותים.','Pesach Haggadah, Shulchan Orech'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-shulchan-orech','en','We eat and drink.','Pesach Haggadah, Shulchan Orech'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֱלֹהֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם, בּוֹרֵא פְּרִי הַגָּפֶן.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Third Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine','en','Blessed are You, Lord our God, King of the universe, who creates the fruit of the vine.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Third Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine','transliteration','Baruch atah yeya,
Eloheinu melech ha''olam,
boreh peri hagafen.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Third Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine','he','ושותים בהסיבה ואינו מברך ברכה אחרונה.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Third Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-third-cup-of-wine','en','We drink while reclining and do not say a blessing afterwards.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Third Cup of Wine'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath','he','מוזגים כוס של אליהו ופותחים את הדלת:','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Pour Out Thy Wrath'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath','en','We pour the cup of Eliyahu and open the door.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Pour Out Thy Wrath'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath','he','שְׁפֹךְ חֲמָתְךָ אֶל־הַגּוֹיִם אֲשֶׁר לֹא יְדָעוּךָ וְעַל־מַמְלָכוֹת אֲשֶׁר בְּשִׁמְךָ לֹא קָרָאוּ. כִּי אָכַל אֶת־יַעֲקֹב וְאֶת־נָוֵהוּ הֵשַׁמּוּ. שְׁפָךְ־עֲלֵיהֶם זַעֲמֶךָ וַחֲרוֹן אַפְּךָ יַשִּׂיגֵם. תִּרְדֹף בְּאַף וְתַשְׁמִידֵם מִתַּחַת שְׁמֵי יְיָ.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Pour Out Thy Wrath'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath','en','Pour your wrath upon the nations that did not know You and upon the kingdoms that did not call upon Your Name! Since they have consumed Ya''akov and laid waste his habitation (Psalms 79:6-7). Pour out Your fury upon them and the fierceness of Your anger shall reach them (Psalms 69:25)! You shall pursue them with anger and eradicate them from under the skies of the Lord (Lamentations 3:66).','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Pour Out Thy Wrath'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-barech-pour-out-thy-wrath','transliteration','Shefoch chamatecha el hagoyim asher lo yedaucha ve al mamlachot asher b''shimcha lo karau.
Ki achal et Yaakov ve et navehu heshamu.
Shefach aleihem za''amecha vacharon apecha yasigem.
Tirdof b''af ve tashmidem mitachat shemei yeya.','Pesach Haggadah, Barech, Pour Out Thy Wrath'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','הוֹדוּ לַייָ כִּי־טוֹב כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. הוֹדוּ לֵאלֹהֵי הָאֱלֹהִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. הוֹדוּ לַאֲדֹנֵי הָאֲדֹנִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְעֹשֵׂה נִפְלָאוֹת גְדֹלוֹת לְבַדּוֹ כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְעֹשֵׂה הַשָּׁמַיִם בִּתְבוּנָה כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְרוֹקַע הָאָרֶץ עַל־הַמָּיִם כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְעֹשֵׂה אוֹרִים גְּדֹלִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. אֶת־הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ לְמֶמְשֶׁלֶת בַּיּוֹם כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. אֶת־הַיָּרֵחַ וְכוֹכָבִים לְמֶמְשְׁלוֹת בַּלַּיְלָה כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְמַכֵּה מִצְרַיִם בִּבְכוֹרֵיהֶם כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וַיּוֹצֵא יִשְׂרָאֵל מִתּוֹכָם כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. בְּיָד חֲזָקָה וּבִזְרוֹעַ נְטוּיָה כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְגֹזֵר־יַם סוּף לִגְזָרִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וְהֶעֱבִיר יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּתוֹכוֹ כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וְנִעֵר פַּרְעֹה וְחֵילוֹ בְיַם־סוּף כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְמוֹלִיךְ עַמּוֹ בַּמִּדְבָּר כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְמַכֵּה מְלָכִים גְּדֹלִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וַיַּהֲרֹג מְלָכִים אַדִּירִים כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. לְסִיחוֹן מֶלֶךְ הָאֱמֹרִי כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וּלְעוֹג מֶלֶךְ הַבָּשָׁן כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וָנָתַן אַרְצָם לְנַחֲלָה כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. נַחֲלָה לְיִשְׂרָאֵל עַבְדוֹ כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. שֶׁבְּשִׁפְלֵנוּ זָכַר לָנוּ כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. וַיִפְרְקֵנוּ מִצָּרֵינוּ כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. נֹתֵן לֶחֶם לְכָל־בָּשָׂר כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ. הוֹדוּ לְאֵל הַשָּׁמַיִם כִּי לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','Thank the Lord, since He is good, since His kindness is forever. Thank the Power of powers since His kindness is forever. To the Master of masters, since His kindness is forever. To the One who alone does wondrously great deeds, since His kindness is forever. To the one who made the Heavens with discernment, since His kindness is forever. To the One who spread the earth over the waters, since His kindness is forever. To the One who made great lights, since His kindness is forever. The sun to rule in the day, since His kindness is forever. The moon and the stars to rule in the night, since His kindness is forever. To the One that smote Egypt through their firstborn, since His kindness is forever. And He took Israel out from among them, since His kindness is forever. With a strong hand and an outstretched forearm, since His kindness is forever. To the One who cut up the Reed Sea into strips, since His kindness is forever. And He made Israel to pass through it, since His kindness is forever. And He jolted Pharaoh and his troop in the Reed Sea, since His kindness is forever. To the One who led his people in the wilderness, since His kindness is forever. To the One who smote great kings, since His kindness is forever. And he killed mighty kings, since His kindness is forever. Sichon, king of the Amorite, since His kindness is forever. And Og, king of the Bashan, since His kindness is forever. And he gave their land as an inheritance, since His kindness is forever. An inheritance for Israel, His servant, since His kindness is forever. That in our lowliness, He remembered us, since His kindness is forever. And he delivered us from our adversaries, since His kindness is forever. He gives bread to all flesh, since His kindness is forever. Thank the Power of the heavens, since His kindness is forever. (Psalms 136)','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Hodu layya ki tov ki le''olam chasdo.
Hodu lelohei haelohim ki le''olam chasdo.
Hodu la''adonei ha''adonim ki le''olam chasdo.
Leoseh niflaot gedolot levado ki le''olam chasdo.
Leoseh hashamayim bitvuna ki le''olam chasdo.
Leroka ha''aretz al hamayim ki le''olam chasdo.
Leoseh orim gedolim ki le''olam chasdo.
Et hashemesh lememshelet bayom ki le''olam chasdo.
Et hayareach ve chochavim lememshelot balayla ki le''olam chasdo.
Lemakeh mitzrayim bivchoreihem ki le''olam chasdo.
Vayotzeh Yisrael mitocham ki le''olam chasdo.
B''yad chazaka uvizroa netuya ki le''olam chasdo.
Legozer yam suf ligzarim ki le''olam chasdo.
Ve he''evir Yisrael b''tocho ki le''olam chasdo.
Ve nier paroh ve cheilo ve yam suf ki le''olam chasdo.
Lemolich amo bamidbar ki le''olam chasdo.
Lemakeh melachim gedolim ki le''olam chasdo.
Vayaharog melachim adirim ki le''olam chasdo.
Lesichon melech haemori ki le''olam chasdo.
Uleog melech habashan ki le''olam chasdo.
Vanatan artzam lenachala ki le''olam chasdo.
Nachala leYisrael avdo ki le''olam chasdo.
Shebeshiflenu zachar lanu ki le''olam chasdo.
Vayifrekenu mitzareinu ki le''olam chasdo.
Noten lechem lechol basar ki le''olam chasdo.
Hodu le''el hashamayim ki le''olam chasdo.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','נִשְׁמַת כָּל חַי תְּבָרֵךְ אֶת שִׁמְךָ, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ, וְרוּחַ כָּל בָּשָׂר תְּפָאֵר וּתְרוֹמֵם זִכְרְךָ, מַלְכֵּנוּ, תָּמִיד. מִן הָעוֹלָם וְעַד הָעוֹלָם אַתָּה אֵל, וּמִבַּלְעָדֶיךָ אֵין לָנוּ מֶלֶךְ גּוֹאֵל וּמוֹשִיעַ, פּוֹדֶה וּמַצִּיל וּמְפַרְנֵס וּמְרַחֵם בְּכָל עֵת צָרָה וְצוּקָה. אֵין לָנוּ מֶלֶךְ אֶלָּא אַתָּה. אֱלֹהֵי הָרִאשׁוֹנִים וְהָאַחֲרוֹנִים, אֱלוֹהַּ כָּל בְּרִיּוֹת, אֲדוֹן כָּל תּוֹלָדוֹת, הַמְּהֻלָּל בְּרֹב הַתִּשְׁבָּחוֹת, הַמְּנַהֵג עוֹלָמוֹ בְּחֶסֶד וּבְרִיּוֹתָיו בְּרַחֲמִים. וַייָ לֹא יָנוּם וְלא יִישָׁן – הַמְּעוֹרֵר יְשֵׁנִים וְהַמֵּקִיץ נִרְדָּמִים, וְהַמֵּשִׂיחַ אִלְּמִים וְהַמַּתִּיר אֲסוּרִים וְהַסּוֹמֵךְ נוֹפְלִים וְהַזּוֹקֵף כְּפוּפִים. לְךָ לְבַדְּךָ אֲנַחְנוּ מוֹדִים.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','The soul of every living being shall bless Your Name, Lord our God; the spirit of all flesh shall glorify and exalt Your remembrance always, our King. From the world and until the world, You are the Power, and other than You we have no king, redeemer, or savior, restorer, rescuer, provider, and merciful one in every time of distress and anguish; we have no king, besides You! God of the first ones and the last ones, God of all creatures, Master of all Generations, Who is praised through a multitude of praises, Who guides His world with kindness and His creatures with mercy. The Lord neither slumbers nor sleeps. He who rouses the sleepers and awakens the dozers; He who makes the mute speak, and frees the captives, and supports the falling, and straightens the bent. We thank You alone.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Nishmat kol chai tevarech et shimcha,
yeya Eloheinu,
ve ruach kol basar tefaer uteromem zichrecha,
malkenu,
tamid.
Min ha''olam ve ad ha''olam atah el,
umibaladeicha ein lanu melech goel umoshia,
podeh umatzil umefarnes umerachem b''chol et tzara ve tzuka.
Ein lanu melech ela atah.
Elohei harishonim ve ha''acharonim,
eloah kol b''riyot,
adon kol toladot,
hamehulal b''rov hatishbachot,
hamenaheg olamo b''chesed uveriyotav b''rachamim.
Vayya lo yanum vel yishan – hameorer yeshenim ve hamekitz nirdamim,
ve hamesiach ilemim ve hamatir asurim ve hasomech nofelim ve hazokef k''fufim.
Lecha levadecha anachnu modim.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','אִלּוּ פִינוּ מָלֵא שִׁירָה כַיָּם, וּלְשׁוֹנֵנוּ רִנָּה כֲּהַמוֹן גַּלָּיו, וְשִׂפְתוֹתֵינוּ שֶׁבַח כְּמֶרְחֲבֵי רָקִיעַ, וְעֵינֵינוּ מְאִירוֹת כַּשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְכַיָּרֵחַ, וְיָדֵינוּ פְרוּשׂות כְּנִשְׁרֵי שָׁמַיִם, וְרַגְלֵינוּ קַלּוֹת כָּאַיָּלוֹת – אֵין אֲנַחְנוּ מַסְפִּיקִים לְהוֹדוֹת לְךָ, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ, וּלְבָרֵךְ אֶת שִׁמְךָ עַל אַחַת מֵאֶלֶף, אַלְפֵי אֲלָפִים וְרִבֵּי רְבָבוֹת פְּעָמִים הַטּוֹבוֹת שֶׁעָשִׂיתָ עִם אֲבוֹתֵינוּ וְעִמָּנוּ. מִמִּצְרַים גְּאַלְתָּנוּ, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ, וּמִבֵּית עֲבָדִים פְּדִיתָנוּ, בְּרָעָב זַנְתָּנוּ וּבְשָׂבָע כִּלְכַּלְתָּנוּ, מֵחֶרֶב הִצַּלְתָּנוּ וּמִדֶּבֶר מִלַּטְתָּנוּ, וּמֵחֳלָיִם רָעִים וְנֶאֱמָנִים דִּלִּיתָנוּ.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','Were our mouth as full of song as the sea, and our tongue as full of joyous song as its multitude of waves, and our lips as full of praise as the breadth of the heavens, and our eyes as sparkling as the sun and the moon, and our hands as outspread as the eagles of the sky and our feet as swift as deers - we still could not thank You sufficiently, Lord our God and God of our ancestors, and to bless Your Name for one thousandth of the thousand of thousands of thousands, and myriad myriads, of goodnesses that You performed for our ancestors and for us. From Egypt, Lord our God, did you redeem us and from the house of slaves you restored us. In famine You nourished us, and in plenty you sustained us. From the sword you saved us, and from plague you spared us; and from severe and enduring diseases you delivered us.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Ilu finu maleh shira chayam,
uleshonenu rina kahamon galav,
ve siftoteinu shevach k''merchavei rakia,
ve eineinu meirot kashemesh ve chayareach,
ve yadeinu ferusvt k''nishrei shamayim,
ve ragleinu kalot ka''ayalot – ein anachnu maspikim lehodot lecha,
yeya Eloheinu velohei avoteinu,
ulevarech et shimcha al achat me''elef,
alfei alafim ve ribei revavot peamim hatovot sheasita im avoteinu ve imanu.
Mimitzraym gealtanu,
yeya Eloheinu,
umibeit avadim peditanu,
b''ra''av zantanu uvesava kilkaltanu,
mecherev hitzaltanu umidever milattanu,
umecholayim raim ve ne''emanim dilitanu.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','עַד הֵנָּה עֲזָרוּנוּ רַחֲמֶיךָ וְלֹא עֲזָבוּנוּ חֲסָדֶיךָ, וְאַל תִּטְּשֵׁנוּ, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ, לָנֶצַח. עַל כֵּן אֵבָרִים שֶׁפִּלַּגְתָּ בָּנוּ וְרוּחַ וּנְשָׁמָה שֶׁנָּפַחְתָּ בְּאַפֵּינוּ וְלָשׁוֹן אֲשֶׁר שַׂמְתָּ בְּפִינוּ – הֵן הֵם יוֹדוּ וִיבָרְכוּ וִישַׁבְּחוּ וִיפָאֲרוּ וִירוֹמְמוּ וְיַעֲרִיצוּ וְיַקְדִּישׁוּ וְיַמְלִיכוּ אֶת שִׁמְךָ מַלְכֵּנוּ. כִּי כָל פֶּה לְךָ יוֹדֶה, וְכָל לָשׁוֹן לְךָ תִּשָּׁבַע, וְכָל בֶּרֶךְ לְךָ תִכְרַע, וְכָל קוֹמָה לְפָנֶיךָ תִשְׁתַּחֲוֶה, וְכָל לְבָבוֹת יִירָאוּךָ, וְכָל קֶרֶב וּכְלָיּוֹת יְזַמֵּרוּ לִשְמֶךָ. כַּדָּבָר שֶׁכָּתוּב, כָּל עַצְמֹתַי תֹּאמַרְנָה, יְיָ מִי כָמוֹךָ מַצִּיל עָנִי מֵחָזָק מִמֶּנוּ, וְעָנִי וְאֶבְיוֹן מִגֹּזְלוֹ. מִי יִדְמֶה לָּךְ וּמִי יִשְׁוֶה לָּךְ וּמִי יַעֲרֹךְ לָךְ הָאֵל הַגָּדוֹל, הַגִּבּוֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא, אֵל עֶלְיוֹן, קֹנֵה שָׁמַיִם וָאָרֶץ. נְהַלֶּלְךָ וּנְשַׁבֵּחֲךָ וּנְפָאֶרְךָ וּנְבָרֵךְ אֶת שֵׁם קָדְשֶׁךָ, כָּאָמוּר: לְדָוִד, בָּרְכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְיָ וְכָל־קְרָבַי אֶת שֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ. הָאֵל בְּתַעֲצֻמוֹת עֻזֶּךָ, הַגָּדוֹל בִּכְבוֹד שְׁמֶךָ, הַגִּבּוֹר לָנֶצַח וְהַנּוֹרָא בְּנוֹרְאוֹתֶיךָ, הַמֶּלֶךְ הַיּוֹשֵׁב עַל כִּסֵּא רָם וְנִשָׂא. שׁוֹכֵן עַד מָרוֹם וְקָדוֹשׁ שְׁמוֹ. וְכָתוּב: רַנְּנוּ צַדִּיקִים בַּייָ, לַיְשָׁרִים נָאוָה תְהִלָּה. בְּפִי יְשָׁרִים תִּתְהַלָּל, וּבְדִבְרֵי צַדִּיקִים תִּתְבָּרַךְ, וּבִלְשׁוֹן חֲסִידִים תִּתְרוֹמָם, וּבְקֶרֶב קְדוֹשִׁים תִּתְקַדָּשׁ.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','Until now Your mercy has helped us, and Your kindness has not forsaken us; and do not abandon us, Lord our God, forever. Therefore, the limbs that You set within us and the spirit and soul that You breathed into our nostrils, and the tongue that You placed in our mouth - verily, they shall thank and bless and praise and glorify, and exalt and revere, and sanctify and coronate Your name, our King. For every mouth shall offer thanks to You; and every tongue shall swear allegiance to You; and every knee shall bend to You; and every upright one shall prostrate himself before You; all hearts shall fear You; and all innermost feelings and thoughts shall sing praises to Your name, as the matter is written (Psalms 35:10), "All my bones shall say, ‘Lord, who is like You? You save the poor man from one who is stronger than he, the poor and destitute from the one who would rob him.''" Who is similar to You and who is equal to You and who can be compared to You, O great, strong and awesome Power, O highest Power, Creator of the heavens and the earth. We shall praise and extol and glorify and bless Your holy name, as it is stated (Psalms 103:1), " [A Psalm] of David. Bless the Lord, O my soul; and all that is within me, His holy name." The Power, in Your powerful boldness; the Great, in the glory of Your name; the Strong One forever; the King who sits on His high and elevated throne. He who dwells always; lofty and holy is His name. And as it is written (Psalms 33:10), "Sing joyfully to the Lord, righteous ones, praise is beautiful from the upright." By the mouth of the upright You shall be praised; By the lips of the righteous shall You be blessed; By the tongue of the devout shall You be exalted; And among the holy shall You be sanctified.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Ad hena azarunu rachameicha ve lo azavunu chasadeicha,
ve al titeshenu,
yeya Eloheinu,
lanetzach.
Al ken evarim shepilagta banu ve ruach uneshama shenafachta b''apeinu ve lashon asher samta b''finu – hen hem yodu vivarechu vishabechu vifa''aru viromemu ve ya''aritzu ve yakdishu ve yamlichu et shimcha malkenu.
Ki chol peh lecha yodeh,
ve chol lashon lecha tishava,
ve chol berech lecha tichra,
ve chol koma lefanecha tishtachaveh,
ve chol levavot yiraucha,
ve chol kerev uchelayot yezameru lishmecha.
Kadavar shekatuv,
kol atzmotai tomarna,
yeya mi chamocha matzil ani mechazak mimenu,
ve ani ve evyon migozelo.
Mi yidmeh lach umi yishveh lach umi ya''aroch lach hael hagadol,
hagibor ve hanora,
el elyon,
koneh shamayim va''aretz.
Nehalelcha uneshabechacha unefaercha unevarech et shem kodshecha,
ka''amur.
LeDavid,
barechi nafshi et yeya ve chol k''ravai et shem kodsho.
Hael b''ta''atzumot uzecha,
hagadol bichvod shemecha,
hagibor lanetzach ve hanora b''noreoteicha,
hamelech hayoshev al kiseh ram ve nisa.
Shochen ad marom ve kadosh shemo.
Ve chatuv.
Ranenu tzadikim bayya,
laysharim nava tehila.
B''fi yesharim tithalal,
uvedivrei tzadikim titbarach,
uvilshon chasidim titromam,
uvekerev k''doshim titkadash.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','וּבְמַקְהֲלוֹת רִבְבוֹת עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּרִנָּה יִתְפָּאֵר שִׁמְךָ, מַלְכֵּנוּ, בְּכָל דּוֹר וָדוֹר, שֶׁכֵּן חוֹבַת כָּל הַיְצוּרִים לְפָנֶיךָ, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ, לְהוֹדוֹת לְהַלֵּל לְשַׁבֵּחַ, לְפָאֵר לְרוֹמֵם לְהַדֵּר לְבָרֵךְ, לְעַלֵּה וּלְקַלֵּס עַל כָּל דִּבְרֵי שִׁירוֹת וְתִשְׁבְּחוֹת דָּוִד בֶּן יִשַׁי עַבְדְּךָ מְשִׁיחֶךָ.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','And in the assemblies of the myriads of Your people, the House of Israel, in joyous song will Your name be glorified, our King, in each and every generation; as it is the duty of all creatures, before You, Lord our God, and God of our ancestors, to thank, to praise, to extol, to glorify, to exalt, to lavish, to bless, to raise high and to acclaim - beyond the words of the songs and praises of David, the son of Yishai, Your servant, Your anointed one.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Uvemakhalot rivvot amecha beit Yisrael b''rina yitpaer shimcha,
malkenu,
b''chol dor vador,
sheken chovat kol hayetzurim lefanecha,
yeya Eloheinu velohei avoteinu,
lehodot lehalel leshabeach,
lefaer leromem lehader levarech,
lealeh ulekales al kol divrei shirot ve tishbechot David ben yishai avdecha meshichecha.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','he','יִשְׁתַּבַּח שִׁמְךָ לָעַד מַלְכֵּנוּ, הָאֵל הַמֶלֶךְ הַגָּדוֹל וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ בַּשָּׁמַיִם וּבָאָרֶץ, כִּי לְךָ נָאֶה, יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ, שִׁיר וּשְׁבָחָה, הַלֵּל וְזִמְרָה, עֹז וּמֶמְשָׁלָה, נֶצַח, גְּדֻלָּה וּגְבוּרָה, תְּהִלָּה וְתִפְאֶרֶת, קְדֻשָּׁה וּמַלְכוּת, בְּרָכוֹת וְהוֹדָאוֹת מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ, אֵל מֶלֶךְ גָּדוֹל בַּתִּשְׁבָּחוֹת, אֵל הַהוֹדָאוֹת, אֲדוֹן הַנִפְלָאוֹת, הַבּוֹחֵר בְּשִׁירֵי זִמְרָה, מֶלֶךְ אֵל חֵי הָעוֹלָמִים.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','en','May Your name be praised forever, our King, the Power, the Great and holy King - in the heavens and in the earth. Since for You it is pleasant - O Lord our God and God of our ancestors - song and lauding, praise and hymn, boldness and dominion, triumph, greatness and strength, psalm and splendor, holiness and kingship, blessings and thanksgivings, from now and forever. Blessed are You Lord, Power, King exalted through laudings, Power of thanksgivings, Master of Wonders, who chooses the songs of hymn - King, Power of the life of the worlds.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-hallel-songs-of-praise-and-thanks','transliteration','Yishtabach shimcha la''ad malkenu,
hael hamelech hagadol ve hakadosh bashamayim uva''aretz,
ki lecha naeh,
yeya Eloheinu velohei avoteinu,
shir ushevacha,
halel ve zimra,
oz umemshala,
netzach,
gedula ugevura,
tehila ve tiferet,
k''dusha umalchut,
b''rachot ve hodaot meatah ve ad olam.
Baruch atah yeya,
el melech gadol batishbachot,
el hahodaot,
adon haniflaot,
habocher b''shirei zimra,
melech el chei haolamim.','Pesach Haggadah, Hallel, Songs of Praise and Thanks'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','he','נִרְצָה','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','en','Accepted','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','transliteration','Nirtza','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','he','חֲסַל סִדּוּר פֶּסַח כְּהִלְכָתוֹ, כְּכָל מִשְׁפָּטוֹ וְחֻקָּתוֹ. כַּאֲשֶׁר זָכִינוּ לְסַדֵּר אוֹתוֹ כֵּן נִזְכֶּה לַעֲשׂוֹתוֹ. זָךְ שׁוֹכֵן מְעוֹנָה, קוֹמֵם קְהַל עֲדַת מִי מָנָה. בְּקָרוֹב נַהֵל נִטְעֵי כַנָּה פְּדוּיִם לְצִיּוֹן בְּרִנָּה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','en','Completed is the Seder of Pesach according to its law, according to all its judgement and statute. Just as we have merited to arrange it, so too, may we merit to do [its sacrifice]. Pure One who dwells in the habitation, raise up the congregation of the community, which whom can count. Bring close, lead the plantings of the sapling, redeemed, to Zion in joy.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chasal-siddur-pesach','transliteration','Chasal sidur pesach k''hilchato,
k''chal mishpato ve chukato.
Ka''asher zachinu lesader oto ken nizkeh la''asoto.
Zach shochen meona,
komem k''hal adat mi mana.
B''karov nahel nitei chana peduyim letziyon b''rina.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chasal Siddur Pesach'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa','he','לְשָׁנָה הַבָּאָה בִּירוּשָלַיִם הַבְּנוּיָה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, L''Shana HaBaa'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa','en','Next year, let us be in the built Jerusalem!','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, L''Shana HaBaa'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-l-shana-habaa','transliteration','Leshana haba''a birushalayim habenuya.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, L''Shana HaBaa'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','אַדִּיר בִּמְלוּכָה, בָּחוּר כַּהֲלָכָה, גְּדוּדָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Mighty in rulership, properly chosen, his troops shall say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Adir bimlucha,
bachur kahalacha,
gedudav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','דָּגוּל בִּמְלוּכָה, הָדוּר כַּהֲלָכָה, וָתִיקָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Noted in rulership, properly splendid, His distinguished ones will say to him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Dagul bimlucha,
hadur kahalacha,
vatikav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','זַכַּאי בִּמְלוּכָה, חָסִין כַּהֲלָכָה טַפְסְרָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Meritorious in rulership, properly robust, His scribes shall say to him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Zakai bimlucha,
chasin kahalacha tafserav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','יָחִיד בִּמְלוּכָה, כַּבִּיר כַּהֲלָכָה לִמּוּדָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Unique in rulership, properly powerful, His wise ones say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Yachid bimlucha,
kabir kahalacha limudav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','מוֹשֵׁל בִּמְלוּכָה, נוֹרָא כַּהֲלָכָה סְבִיבָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Reigning in rulership, properly awesome, those around Him say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Moshel bimlucha,
nora kahalacha sevivav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','עָנָיו בִּמְלוּכָה, פּוֹדֶה כַּהֲלָכָה, צַדִּיקָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Humble in rulership, properly restoring, His righteous ones say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Anav bimlucha,
podeh kahalacha,
tzadikav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:7:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','קָדּוֹשׁ בִּמְלוּכָה, רַחוּם כַּהֲלָכָה שִׁנְאַנָּיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:7:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Holy in rulership, properly merciful, His angels say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:7:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Kadosh bimlucha,
rachum kahalacha shinanav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:8:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','he','תַּקִיף בִּמְלוּכָה, תּוֹמֵךְ כַּהֲלָכָה תְּמִימָיו יֹאמְרוּ לוֹ: לְךָ וּלְךָ, לְךָ כִּי לְךָ, לְךָ אַף לְךָ, לְךָ יְיָ הַמַּמְלָכָה, כִּי לוֹ נָאֶה, כִּי לוֹ יָאֶה.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:8:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','en','Dynamic in rulership, properly supportive, His innocent ones say to Him, "Yours and Yours, Yours since it is Yours, Yours and even Yours, Yours, Lord is the kingdom; since for Him it is pleasant, for Him it is suited."','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e:8:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-ki-lo-na-e','transliteration','Takif bimlucha,
tomech kahalacha temimav yomeru lo.
Lecha ulecha,
lecha ki lecha,
lecha af lecha,
lecha yeya hamamlacha,
ki lo naeh,
ki lo yaeh.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Ki Lo Na''e'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:0:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','אַדִּיר הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:0:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Mighty is He, may He build His house soon. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:0:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Adir hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:1:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','בָּחוּר הוּא, גָּדוֹל הוּא, דָּגוּל הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:1:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Chosen is He, great is He, noted is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:1:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Bachur hu,
gadol hu,
dagul hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:2:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','הָדוּר הוּא, וָתִיק הוּא, זַכַּאי הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:2:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Splendid is He, distinguished is He, meritorious is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:2:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Hadur hu,
vatik hu,
zakai hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:3:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','חָסִיד הוּא, טָהוֹר הוּא, יָחִיד הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:3:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Pious is He, pure is He, unique is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:3:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Chasid hu,
tahor hu,
yachid hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:4:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','כַּבִּיר הוּא, לָמוּד הוּא, מֶלֶךְ הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:4:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Powerful is He, wise is He, A king is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:4:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Kabir hu,
lamud hu,
melech hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:5:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','נוֹרָא הוּא, סַגִּיב הוּא, עִזּוּז הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:5:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Awesome is He, exalted is He, heroic is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:5:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Nora hu,
sagiv hu,
izuz hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','פּוֹדֶה הוּא, צַדִּיק הוּא, קָּדוֹשׁ הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','A restorer is He, righteous is He, holy is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Podeh hu,
tzadik hu,
kadosh hu yivneh veito b''karov.
Bimhera,
bimhera,
b''yameinu b''karov.
El b''neh,
el b''neh,
b''neh veitecha b''karov.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:7:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','he','רַחוּם הוּא, שַׁדַּי הוּא, תַּקִּיף הוּא יִבְנֶה בֵיתוֹ בְּקָרוֹב. בִּמְהֵרָה, בִּמְהֵרָה, בְּיָמֵינוּ בְּקָרוֹב. אֵל בְּנֵה, אֵל בְּנֵה, בְּנֵה בֵיתְךָ בְּקָרוֹב.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:7:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','en','Merciful is He, the Omnipotent is He, dynamic is He. Quickly, quickly, in our days, soon. God build, God build, build Your house soon.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Adir Hu'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu:7:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-adir-hu','transliteration','Rachum hu,
shadai hu,
takif hu yivneh veito b''karov.
