('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:6:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','he','וְאָתָא תוֹרָא וְשָׁתָה לְמַיָא, דְּכָבָה לְנוּרָא, דְּשָׂרַף לְחוּטְרָא, דְּהִכָּה לְכַלְבָּא, דְּנָשַׁךְ לְשׁוּנְרָא, דְּאַָכְלָה לְגַדְיָא, דְּזַבִּין אַבָּא בִּתְרֵי זוּזֵי. חַד גַּדְיָא, חַד גַּדְיָא.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:6:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','en','Then came a bull and drank the water, that extinguished the fire, that burnt the stick, that hit the dog, that bit the cat, that ate the kid that my father bought for two zuz, one kid, one kid.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:6:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','transliteration','Ve atah torah ve shata lemaya,
dechava lenura,
desaraf lechutera,
dehika lechalba,
denashach leshunera,
dea''achla legadya,
dezabin aba bitrei zuzei.
Chad gadya,
chad gadya.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:7:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','he','וְאָתָא הַשׁוֹחֵט וְשָׁחַט לְתוֹרָא, דְּשָׁתָה לְמַיָא, דְּכָבָה לְנוּרָא, דְּשָׂרַף לְחוּטְרָא, דְּהִכָּה לְכַלְבָּא, דְּנָשַׁךְ לְשׁוּנְרָא, דְּאַָכְלָה לְגַדְיָא, דְּזַבִּין אַבָּא בִּתְרֵי זוּזֵי. חַד גַּדְיָא, חַד גַּדְיָא.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:7:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','en','Then came the schochet and slaughtered the bull, that drank the water, that extinguished the fire, that burnt the stick, that hit the dog, that bit the cat, that ate the kid that my father bought for two zuz, one kid, one kid.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:7:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','transliteration','Ve atah hashochet ve shachat letorah,
deshata lemaya,
dechava lenura,
desaraf lechutera,
dehika lechalba,
denashach leshunera,
dea''achla legadya,
dezabin aba bitrei zuzei.
Chad gadya,
chad gadya.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:8:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','he','וְאָתָא מַלְאָךְ הַמָּוֶת וְשָׁחַט לְשׁוֹחֵט, דְּשָׁחַט לְתוֹרָא, דְּשָׁתָה לְמַיָא, דְּכָבָה לְנוּרָא, דְּשָׂרַף לְחוּטְרָא, דְּהִכָּה לְכַלְבָּא, דְּנָשַׁךְ לְשׁוּנְרָא, דְּאַָכְלָה לְגַדְיָא, דְּזַבִּין אַבָּא בִּתְרֵי זוּזֵי. חַד גַּדְיָא, חַד גַּדְיָא.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:8:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','en','Then came the angel of death and slaughtered the schochet, who slaughtered the bull, that drank the water, that extinguished the fire, that burnt the stick, that hit the dog, that bit the cat, that ate the kid that my father bought for two zuz, one kid, one kid.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:8:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','transliteration','Ve atah malach hamavet ve shachat leshochet,
deshachat letorah,
deshata lemaya,
dechava lenura,
desaraf lechutera,
dehika lechalba,
denashach leshunera,
dea''achla legadya,
dezabin aba bitrei zuzei.
Chad gadya,
chad gadya.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:9:he','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','he','וְאָתָא הַקָּדושׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא וְשָׁחַט לְמַלְאַךְ הַמָּוֶת, דְּשָׁחַט לְשׁוֹחֵט, דְּשָׁחַט לְתוֹרָא, דְּשָׁתָה לְמַיָא, דְּכָבָה לְנוּרָא, דְּשָׂרַף לְחוּטְרָא, דְּהִכָּה לְכַלְבָּא, דְּנָשַׁךְ לְשׁוּנְרָא, דְּאַָכְלָה לְגַדְיָא, דְּזַבִּין אַבָּא בִּתְרֵי זוּזֵי. חַד גַּדְיָא, חַד גַּדְיָא.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:9:en','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','en','Then came the Holy One, blessed be He and slaughtered the angel of death, who slaughtered the schochet, who slaughtered the bull, that drank the water, that extinguished the fire, that burnt the stick, that hit the dog, that bit the cat, that ate the kid that my father bought for two zuz, one kid, one kid.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya:9:transliteration','sefaria-pesach-haggadah-nirtzah-chad-gadya','transliteration','Ve atah hakadvsh baruch hu ve shachat lemalach hamavet,
deshachat leshochet,
deshachat letorah,
deshata lemaya,
dechava lenura,
desaraf lechutera,
dehika lechalba,
denashach leshunera,
dea''achla legadya,
dezabin aba bitrei zuzei.
Chad gadya,
chad gadya.','Pesach Haggadah, Nirtzah, Chad Gadya'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא מִן כָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha for Erev Rosh Hashana, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and or all Yisrael, and say, Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha for Erev Rosh Hashana, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.
Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela min kol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh shalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha for Erev Rosh Hashana, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה הַשָּׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Maariv, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; far above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes the peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and or all Yisrael, and say, Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Maariv, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-maariv-mourner-s-kaddish','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.
Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela ule''ela mikol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh hashalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Maariv, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּשָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּֽנוּ עַל נְטִילַת יָדָֽיִם:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us concerning the washing of hands.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu al netilat yadayim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר יָצַר אֶת הָאָדָם בְּחָכְמָה וּבָֽרָא בוֹ נְקָבִים נְקָבִים חֲלוּלִים חֲלוּלִים גָּלוּי וְיָדֽוּעַ לִפְנֵי כִסֵּא כְבוֹדֶֽךָ שֶׁאִם יִפָּתֵֽחַ אֶחָד מֵהֶם אוֹ יִסָּתֵם אֶחָד מֵהֶם אִי אֶפְשַׁר לְהִתְקַיֵּם וְלַעֲמֹד לְפָנֶֽיךָ אֲפִילוּ שָׁעָה אֶחָת. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה רוֹפֵא כָל בָּשָׂר וּמַפְלִיא לַעֲשׂוֹת:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy, our God, King of the Universe, Who formed man with wisdom and created within him openings and hollows. It is obvious and known in the presence of Your glorious throne that if one of them were ruptured, or if one of them were blocked, it would be impossible to exist and stand in Your Presence even for a short while. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who heals all flesh and performs wonders.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher yatzar et ha''adam b''chochma uvara vo nekavim nekavim chalulim chalulim galuy ve yadua lifnei chiseh chevodecha she''im yipateach echad mehem o yisatem echad mehem ee efshar lehitkayem ve la''amod lefanecha afilu sha''a echat.
Baruch atah Adonai rofeh chol basar umafli la''asot.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','he','אֱלֹהַי, נְשָׁמָה שֶׁנָּתַֽתָּ בִּי טְהוֹרָה הִיא אַתָּה בְרָאתָהּ אַתָּה יְצַרְתָּהּ אַתָּה נְפַחְתָּהּ בִּי וְאַתָּה מְשַׁמְּרָהּ בְּקִרְבִּי וְאַתָּה עָתִיד לִטְּלָהּ מִמֶּֽנִּי וּלְהַחֲזִירָהּ בִּי לֶעָתִיד לָבֹא, כָּל זְמַן שֶׁהַנְּשָׁמָה בְקִרְבִּי מוֹדֶה אֲנִי לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהַי וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתַי רִבּוֹן כָּל הַמַּעֲשִׂים אֲדוֹן כָּל הַנְּשָׁמוֹת: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמַּחֲזִיר נְשָׁמוֹת לִפְגָרִים מֵתִים:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','en','My God! the soul which You bestowed in me is pure; You created it, You formed it, You breathed it into me and You preserve it within me. You will eventually take it from me, and restore it in me in the time to come. So long as the soul is within me I give thanks to You, Adonoy my God, and God of my fathers, Lord of all creatures, Master of all souls. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Who restores souls to dead bodies.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-upon-arising','transliteration','Elohai,
neshama shenatata bee tehora hi atah ve ratah atah yetzartah atah nefachtah bee ve atah meshamerah b''kirbi ve atah atid litelah mimeni ulehachazirah bee leatid lavo,
kol zeman shehaneshama ve kirbi modeh ani lefanecha Adonai Elohai velohei avotai ribon kol hama''asim adon kol haneshamot.
Baruch atah Adonai hamachazir neshamot lifgarim metim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings Upon Arising'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּשָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּֽנוּ לַעֲסֹק בְּדִבְרֵי תוֹרָה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy, our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us to be engrossed in the words of Torah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu la''asok b''divrei torah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','וְהַעֲרֶב נָא יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֶת דִּבְרֵי תוֹרָתְךָ בְּפִֽינוּ וּבְפִי עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִהְיֶה אֲנַֽחְנוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵֽינוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵי עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל כֻּלָּֽנוּ יוֹדְעֵי שְׁמֶֽךָ וְלוֹמְדֵי תוֹרָתֶֽךָ לִשְׁמָהּ: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה הַמְלַמֵּד תּוֹרָה לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','Adonoy our God, please make pleasant the words of Your Torah in our mouths and in the mouths of Your people Yisrael. And may we and our descendants and the descendants of Your people the House of Yisrael, all be perceivers of Your Name and students of Your Torah for its own sake. Blessed are You, Adonoy Who teaches Torah to His people, Yisrael.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Ve ha''arev na Adonai Eloheinu et divrei toratecha b''finu uvefi amecha beit Yisrael ve nihyeh anachenu ve tze''etzaeinu ve tze''etzaei amecha beit Yisrael kulanu yode''ei shemecha ve lomedei toratecha lishmah.
Baruch atah Adonai hamelamed torah leamo Yisrael.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר בָּֽחַר בָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים וְנָֽתַן לָֽנוּ אֶת תּוֹרָתוֹ: בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה נוֹתֵן הַתּוֹרָה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe Who chose us from among all the peoples and gave us His Torah. Blessed are You, Adonoy, Giver of the Torah!','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher bachar banu mikol ha''amim ve natan lanu et torato.
Baruch atah Adonai noten hatora.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:3:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהֹוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶֽךָ: יָאֵר יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וִיחֻנֶּֽךָּ: יִשָּׂא יְהֹוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶֽיךָ וְיָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:3:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','May Adonoy bless you and guard you. May Adonoy shine His countenance upon you and be gracious unto you. May Adonoy turn His countenance toward you and grant you peace.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:3:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Yevarechcha Adonai ve yishmerecha.
Yaer Adonai panav eleicha vichuneka.
Yisa Adonai panav eleicha ve yasem lecha shalom.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:4:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','אֵֽלּוּ דְבָרִים שֶׁאֵין לָהֶם שִׁעוּר הַפֵּאָה וְהַבִּכּוּרִים וְהָרְאָיוֹן וּגְמִילוּת חֲסָדִים וְתַלְמוּד תּוֹרָה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:4:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','These are precepts for which no fixed measure is prescribed: [leaving] the corner [of a field unharvested], [the offering of] the first fruits, the appearance-offering, [performing] deeds of kindness, and the study of Torah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:4:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Elu devarim she''ein lahem shiur hapea ve habikurim ve hareayon ugemilut chasadim ve talmud torah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:5:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','he','אֵֽלּוּ דְבָרִים שֶׁאָדָם אוֹכֵל פֵּרוֹתֵיהֶם בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְהַקֶּֽרֶן קַיֶּֽמֶת לוֹ לָעוֹלָם הַבָּא, וְאֵֽלּוּ הֵן כִּבּוּד אָב וָאֵם וּגְמִילוּת חֲסָדִים וְהַשְׁכָּמַת בֵּית הַמִּדְרָשׁ שַׁחֲרִית וְעַרְבִית וְהַכְנָסַת אוֹרְחִים וּבִקּוּר חוֹלִים וְהַכְנָסַת כַּלָּה וּלְוָיַת הַמֵּת וְעִיּוּן תְּפִלָּה וַהֲבָאַת שָׁלוֹם בֵּין אָדָם לַחֲבֵרוֹ וְתַלְמוּד תּוֹרָה כְּנֶֽגֶד כֻּלָּם:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:5:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','en','These are precepts, the fruits of which man enjoys in this world, [while] the principal [reward] is preserved for him in the World-to-Come. They are: honoring father and mother, [performing] deeds of kindness, early attendance in the House of Study morning and evening, providing hospitality to guests, visiting the sick, participating in making a wedding, accompanying the dead [to the grave], concentrating on the meaning of prayers, making peace between fellow men and the study of Torah is equal to them all.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah:5:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-blessings-of-the-torah','transliteration','Elu devarim sheadam ochel peroteihem baolam hazeh ve hakeren kayemet lo laolam haba,
ve elu hen kibud av vaem ugemilut chasadim ve hashkamat beit hamidrash shacharit ve arvit ve hachnasat orechim uvikur cholim ve hachnasat kala ulevayat hamet ve iyun tefilah vahava''at shalom bein adam lachavero ve talmud torah k''neged kulam.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Blessings of the Torah'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה הַשָּׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; far above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes the peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and or all Yisrael, and say, Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-mourner-s-kaddish','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.
Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela ule''ela mikol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh hashalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','he','הַמֶּֽלֶךְ יּוֹשֵׁב עַל כִּסֵּא רָם וְנִשָּׂא:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','en','The King Who sits on a throne [that is] exalted and uplifted.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','transliteration','Hamelech yoshev al kiseh ram ve nisa.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','he','שׁוֹכֵן עַד מָרוֹם וְקָדוֹשׁ שְׁמוֹ. וְכָתוּב רַנְּנוּ צַדִּיקִים בַּיהוָֹה. לַיְשָׁרִים נָאוָה תְהִלָּה: בְּפִי יְשָׁרִים תִּתְרוֹמָם. וּבְדִבְרֵי צַדִּיקִים תִּתְבָּרַךְ. וּבִלְשׁוֹן חֲסִידִים תִּתְקַדָּשׁ. וּבְקֶֽרֶב קְדוֹשִׁים תִּתְהַלָּל:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','en','He Who dwells in eternity, exalted and holy is His Name. And it is written: “Joyfully exult in God, [you] righteous ones, for the upright, praise is fitting. Through the mouth of the upright, You are exalted, and with the words of the righteous You are blessed; and by the tongue of the pious, You are sanctified; and in the midst of the holy, You are extolled.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','transliteration','Shochen ad marom ve kadosh shemo.
Ve chatuv ranenu tzadikim ba''adonai.
Laysharim nava tehila.
B''fi yesharim titromam.
Uvedivrei tzadikim titbarach.
Uvilshon chasidim titkadash.
Uvekerev k''doshim tithalal.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','he','וּבְמַקְהֲלוֹת רִבְבוֹת עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל. בְּרִנָּה יִתְפָּאַר שִׁמְךָ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ בְּכָל דּוֹר וָדוֹר. שֶׁכֵּן חוֹבַת כָּל הַיְצוּרִים לְפָנֶֽיךָ. יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ. וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ חזן: לְהוֹדוֹת לְהַלֵּל לְשַׁבֵּחַ. לְפָאֵר לְרוֹמֵם לְהַדֵּר לְבָרֵךְ לְעַלֵּה וּלְקַלֵּס עַל כָּל דִּבְרֵי שִׁירוֹת וְתִשְׁבְּחוֹת דָּוִד בֶּן יִשַׁי. עַבְדְּךָ מְשִׁיחֶֽךָ:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','en','And in the assemblies of myriads of Your people, the House of Yisrael; with joyful song glorified will be Your Name, our King, in every generation. For it is the duty of all beings, before You, Adonoy, our God and God of our fathers, to thank, to extol, and to praise; to glorify, to exalt, and to honor; to bless, to elevate, and to acclaim [You,] even beyond all the words of song and praise of Dovid, son of Yishai, Your servant, Your anointed.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-the-king','transliteration','Uvemakhalot rivvot amecha beit Yisrael.
B''rina yitpa''ar shimcha malkenu b''chol dor vador.
Sheken chovat kol hayetzurim lefanecha.
Adonai Eloheinu.
Velohei avoteinu chzn.
Lehodot lehalel leshabeach.
Lefaer leromem lehader levarech lealeh ulekales al kol divrei shirot ve tishbechot David ben yishai.
Avdecha meshichecha.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, The King'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אַתָּה בְחַרְתָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים. אָהַֽבְתָּ אוֹתָֽנוּ וְרָצִֽיתָ בָּֽנוּ. וְרוֹמַמְתָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הַלְּשׁוֹנוֹת. וְקִדַּשְׁתָּֽנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתֶֽיךָ. וְקֵרַבְתָּֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ לַעֲבוֹדָתֶֽךָ. וְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ עָלֵֽינוּ קָרָֽאתָ:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','You chose us from [among] all the peoples; You loved us and took pleasure in us; You exalted us above all tongues, and You sanctified us with Your commandments; You drew us near, our King, to Your servitude and Your great and Holy Name, You have pronounced upon us.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Atah ve chartanu mikol ha''amim.
Ahaveta otanu ve ratzita banu.
Ve romamtanu mikol haleshonot.
Ve kidashtanu b''mitzvoteicha.
Ve keravtanu malkenu la''avodatecha.
Ve shimcha hagadol ve hakadosh aleinu karata.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','וַתִּתֶּן לָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בְּאַהֲבָה (אֶת־יוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת הַזֶּה וְ) אֶת־יוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן הַזֶּה. יוֹם (זִכְרוֹן) תְּרוּעָה (בְּאַהֲבָה) מִקְרָא קֹֽדֶשׁ זֵֽכֶר לִיצִיאַת מִצְרָֽיִם:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','And You gave us Adonoy, our God, in love, On Shabbos add: (this Shabbos Day and) this day of Remembrance a day for On Shabbos add: (the remembrance of) sounding the shofar On Shabbos add: (with love) a day of holy assembly commemorating the exodus from Mitzrayim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Vatiten lanu Adonai Eloheinu b''ahava (et yom hashabat hazeh v) et yom hazikaron hazeh.
Yom (zichron) terua (b''ahava) mikra kodesh zecher litziat mitzrayim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ יַעֲלֶה וְיָבֹא וְיַגִּֽיעַ וְיֵרָאֶה וְיֵרָצֶה וְיִשָּׁמַע וְיִפָּקֵד וְיִזָּכֵר זִכְרוֹנֵֽנוּ וּפִקְדוֹנֵֽנוּ וְזִכְרוֹן אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ וְזִכְרוֹן מָשִֽׁיחַ בֶּן דָּוִד עַבְדֶּֽךָ וְזִכְרוֹן יְרוּשָׁלַֽיִם עִיר קָדְשֶֽׁךָ וְזִכְרוֹן כָּל עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל לְפָנֶֽיךָ. לִפְלֵיטָה לְטוֹבָה לְחֵן וּלְחֶֽסֶד וּלְרַחֲמִים לְחַיִּים וּלְשָׁלוֹם בְּיוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן הַזֶּה. זָכְרֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בּוֹ לְטוֹבָה. וּפָקְדֵֽנוּ בוֹ לִבְרָכָה. וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ בוֹ לְחַיִּים. וּבִדְבַר יְשׁוּעָה וְרַחֲמִים חוּס וְחָנֵּֽנוּ. וְרַחֵם עָלֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ. כִּי אֵלֶֽיךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ. כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','Our God and God of our fathers, may there ascend, come, and reach, appear, be desired, and heard, counted and recalled our remembrance and reckoning; the remembrance of our fathers; the remembrance of the Messiah the son of Dovid, Your servant; the remembrance of Yerushalayim, city of Your Sanctuary and the remembrance of Your entire people, the House of Yisrael, before You for survival, for well-being, for favor, kindliness, compassion, for life and peace on this day of Remembrance. Remember us Adonoy, our God on this day for well-being; be mindful of us on this day for blessing, and deliver us for life. In accord with the promise of deliverance and compassion, spare us and favor us, have compassion on us and deliver us; for to You our eyes are directed because You are the Almighty, Who is King, Gracious and Merciful.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Eloheinu velohei avoteinu ya''aleh ve yavo ve yagia ve yeraeh ve yeratzeh ve yishama ve yipaked ve yizacher zichronenu ufikdonenu ve zichron avoteinu ve zichron mashiach ben David avdecha ve zichron Yerushalayim ir kodshecha ve zichron kol amecha beit Yisrael lefanecha.
Lifleita letova lechen ulechesed ulerachamim lechayim uleshalom b''yom hazikaron hazeh.
Zacherenu Adonai Eloheinu bo letova.
Ufakedenu vo livracha.
Ve hoshienu vo lechayim.
Uvidvar yeshua ve rachamim chus ve chanenu.
Ve rachem aleinu ve hoshienu.
Ki eleicha eineinu.
Ki el melech chanun ve rachum atah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ. מְלוֹךְ עַל כָּל הָעוֹלָם כֻּלּוֹ בִּכְבוֹדֶֽךָ וְהִנָּשֵׂא עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בִּיקָרֶֽךָ וְהוֹפַע בַּהֲדַר גְּאוֹן עֻזֶּֽךָ עַל כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי תֵבֵל אַרְצֶֽךָ. וְיֵדַע כָּל פָּעוּל כִּי אַתָּה פְעַלְתּוֹ וְיָבִין כָּל יְצוּר כִּי אַתָּה יְצַרְתּוֹ וְיֹאמַר כֹּל אֲשֶׁר נְשָׁמָה בְאַפּוֹ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֶֽלֶךְ וּמַלְכוּתוֹ בַּכֹּל מָשָֽׁלָה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','Our God and God of our fathers, reign over the entire world with Your glory, and be uplifted over all the earth with Your honor, and appear in the splendor of Your majestic might over all who dwell in the inhabited world of Your earth; so everything that has been made will know that You have made it, and it will be understood by everything that was formed that You formed it, And they will say, everyone who has breath in his nostrils, “Adonoy, God of Yisrael is King and His Kingship rules over all.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Eloheinu velohei avoteinu.
Meloch al kol ha''olam kulo bichvodecha ve hinaseh al kol ha''aretz bikarecha ve hofa bahadar geon uzecha al kol yoshevei tevel artzecha.
Ve yeda kol paul ki atah fealto ve yavin kol yetzur ki atah yetzarto ve yomar kol asher neshama ve apo Adonai Elohei Yisrael melech umalchuto bakol mashala.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:4:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','(אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ רְצֵה בִמְנוּחָתֵֽנוּ) קַדְּשֵֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתֶֽיךָ וְתֵן חֶלְקֵֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ שַׂבְּעֵֽנוּ מִטּוּבֶֽךָ וְשַׂמְּחֵֽנוּ בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ: (וְהַנְחִילֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בְּאַהֲבָה וּבְרָצוֹן שַׁבַּת קָדְשֶֽׁךָ וְיָנֽוּחוּ בוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל מְקַדְּשֵׁי שְׁמֶֽךָ) וְטַהֵר לִבֵּֽנוּ לְעָבְדְּךָ בֶּאֱמֶת כִּי אַתָּה אֱלֹהִים אֱמֶת וּדְבָרְךָ אֱמֶת וְקַיָּם לָעַד. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ מְקַדֵּשׁ (הַשַּׁבָּת וְ) יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:4:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','On Shabbos add: (Our God and God of our fathers, be pleased with our rest) Sanctify us with Your commandments and give us our share in Your Torah; satisfy us from Your goodness and gladden us with Your deliverance, On Shabbos add: (And give us as our inheritance Adonoy our God with love and with pleasure Your holy Sabbath; and may Yisrael rest thereon— [they who are] sanctifiers of Your Name) and purify our hearts to serve You in truth, for You are the true God, and Your word is true and enduring forever. Blessed are You, Adonoy, King over all the earth, Sanctifier On Shabbos add: (of the Sabbath and) of Yisrael and the Day of Remembrance.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:4:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','(Eloheinu velohei avoteinu retzeh vimnuchatenu) kadeshenu b''mitzvoteicha ve ten chelkenu b''toratecha sabe''enu mituvecha ve samechenu bishuatecha.
(ve hanchilenu Adonai Eloheinu b''ahava uveratzon shabat kodshecha ve yanuchu vo Yisrael mekadeshei shemecha) ve taher libenu leavedecha be''emet ki atah Elohim emet udevarecha emet ve kayam la''ad.
Baruch atah Adonai melech al kol ha''aretz mekadesh (hashabat v) Yisrael ve yom hazikaron.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אַתָּה בְחַרְתָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הָעַמִּים. אָהַֽבְתָּ אוֹתָֽנוּ וְרָצִֽיתָ בָּֽנוּ. וְרוֹמַמְתָּֽנוּ מִכָּל הַלְּשׁוֹנוֹת. וְקִדַּשְׁתָּֽנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתֶֽיךָ. וְקֵרַבְתָּֽנוּ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ לַעֲבוֹדָתֶֽךָ. וְשִׁמְךָ הַגָּדוֹל וְהַקָּדוֹשׁ עָלֵֽינוּ קָרָֽאתָ:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','You chose us from [among] all the peoples; You loved us and took pleasure in us; You exalted us above all tongues, and You sanctified us with Your commandments; You drew us near, our King, to Your servitude and Your great and Holy Name, You have pronounced upon us.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Atah ve chartanu mikol ha''amim.
Ahaveta otanu ve ratzita banu.
Ve romamtanu mikol haleshonot.
Ve kidashtanu b''mitzvoteicha.
Ve keravtanu malkenu la''avodatecha.
Ve shimcha hagadol ve hakadosh aleinu karata.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','וַתִּתֶּן לָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בְּאַהֲבָה אֶת־יוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן הַזֶּה. יוֹם תְּרוּעָה מִקְרָא קֹֽדֶשׁ זֵֽכֶר לִיצִיאַת מִצְרָֽיִם:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','And You gave us Adonoy, our God, in love, this day of Remembrance a day for sounding the shofar a day of holy assembly commemorating the exodus from Mitzrayim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Vatiten lanu Adonai Eloheinu b''ahava et yom hazikaron hazeh.
Yom terua mikra kodesh zecher litziat mitzrayim.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ יַעֲלֶה וְיָבֹא וְיַגִּֽיעַ וְיֵרָאֶה וְיֵרָצֶה וְיִשָּׁמַע וְיִפָּקֵד וְיִזָּכֵר זִכְרוֹנֵֽנוּ וּפִקְדוֹנֵֽנוּ וְזִכְרוֹן אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ וְזִכְרוֹן מָשִֽׁיחַ בֶּן דָּוִד עַבְדֶּֽךָ וְזִכְרוֹן יְרוּשָׁלַֽיִם עִיר קָדְשֶֽׁךָ וְזִכְרוֹן כָּל עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל לְפָנֶֽיךָ. לִפְלֵיטָה לְטוֹבָה לְחֵן וּלְחֶֽסֶד וּלְרַחֲמִים לְחַיִּים וּלְשָׁלוֹם בְּיוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן הַזֶּה. זָכְרֵֽנוּ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ בּוֹ לְטוֹבָה. וּפָקְדֵֽנוּ בוֹ לִבְרָכָה. וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ בוֹ לְחַיִּים. וּבִדְבַר יְשׁוּעָה וְרַחֲמִים חוּס וְחָנֵּֽנוּ. וְרַחֵם עָלֵֽינוּ וְהוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ. כִּי אֵלֶֽיךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ. כִּי אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם אָֽתָּה:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','Our God and God of our fathers, may there ascend, come, and reach, appear, be desired, and heard, counted and recalled our remembrance and reckoning; the remembrance of our fathers; the remembrance of the Messiah the son of Dovid, Your servant; the remembrance of Yerushalayim, city of Your Sanctuary and the remembrance of Your entire people, the House of Yisrael, before You for survival, for well-being, for favor, kindliness, compassion, for life and peace on this day of Remembrance. Remember us Adonoy, our God on this day for well-being; be mindful of us on this day for blessing, and deliver us for life. In accord with the promise of deliverance and compassion, spare us and favor us, have compassion on us and deliver us; for to You our eyes are directed because You are the Almighty, Who is King, Gracious and Merciful.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Eloheinu velohei avoteinu ya''aleh ve yavo ve yagia ve yeraeh ve yeratzeh ve yishama ve yipaked ve yizacher zichronenu ufikdonenu ve zichron avoteinu ve zichron mashiach ben David avdecha ve zichron Yerushalayim ir kodshecha ve zichron kol amecha beit Yisrael lefanecha.
Lifleita letova lechen ulechesed ulerachamim lechayim uleshalom b''yom hazikaron hazeh.
Zacherenu Adonai Eloheinu bo letova.
Ufakedenu vo livracha.
Ve hoshienu vo lechayim.
Uvidvar yeshua ve rachamim chus ve chanenu.
Ve rachem aleinu ve hoshienu.
Ki eleicha eineinu.
Ki el melech chanun ve rachum atah.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','he','אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ. מְלוֹךְ עַל כָּל הָעוֹלָם כֻּלּוֹ בִּכְבוֹדֶֽךָ וְהִנָּשֵׂא עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בִּיקָרֶֽךָ וְהוֹפַע בַּהֲדַר גְּאוֹן עֻזֶּֽךָ עַל כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי תֵבֵל אַרְצֶֽךָ. וְיֵדַע כָּל פָּעוּל כִּי אַתָּה פְעַלְתּוֹ וְיָבִין כָּל יְצוּר כִּי אַתָּה יְצַרְתּוֹ וְיֹאמַר כֹּל אֲשֶׁר נְשָׁמָה בְאַפּוֹ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֶֽלֶךְ וּמַלְכוּתוֹ בַּכֹּל מָשָֽׁלָה: קַדְּשֵֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתֶֽיךָ וְתֵן חֶלְקֵֽנוּ בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ שַׂבְּעֵֽנוּ מִטּוּבֶֽךָ וְשַׂמְּחֵֽנוּ בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ: וְטַהֵר לִבֵּֽנוּ לְעָבְדְּךָ בֶּאֱמֶת כִּי אַתָּה אֱלֹהִים אֱמֶת וּדְבָרְךָ אֱמֶת וְקַיָּם לָעַד. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה מֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ מְקַדֵּשׁ יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיוֹם הַזִּכָּרוֹן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','en','Our God and God of our fathers, reign over the entire world with Your glory, and be uplifted over all the earth with Your honor, and appear in the splendor of Your majestic might over all who dwell in the inhabited world of Your earth; so everything that has been made will know that You have made it, and it will be understood by everything that was formed that You formed it, And they will say, everyone who has breath in his nostrils, “Adonoy, God of Yisrael is King and His Kingship rules over all.” Sanctify us with Your commandments and give us our share in Your Torah; satisfy us from Your goodness and gladden us with Your deliverance, and purify our hearts to serve You in truth, for You are the true God, and Your word is true and enduring forever. Blessed are You, Adonoy, King over all the earth, Sanctifier of Yisrael and the Day of Remembrance.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day:3:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-the-morning-prayers-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-sancification-of-the-day','transliteration','Eloheinu velohei avoteinu.
Meloch al kol ha''olam kulo bichvodecha ve hinaseh al kol ha''aretz bikarecha ve hofa bahadar geon uzecha al kol yoshevei tevel artzecha.
Ve yeda kol paul ki atah fealto ve yavin kol yetzur ki atah yetzarto ve yomar kol asher neshama ve apo Adonai Elohei Yisrael melech umalchuto bakol mashala.
Kadeshenu b''mitzvoteicha ve ten chelkenu b''toratecha sabe''enu mituvecha ve samechenu bishuatecha.
Ve taher libenu leavedecha be''emet ki atah Elohim emet udevarecha emet ve kayam la''ad.
Baruch atah Adonai melech al kol ha''aretz mekadesh Yisrael ve yom hazikaron.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, The Morning Prayers, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Sancification of the Day'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','he','יְקוּם פֻּרְקָן מִן שְׁמַיָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמֵי וְחַיֵּי אֲרִיכֵי וּמְזוֹנֵי רְוִיחֵי וְסִיַּעְתָּא דִשְׁמַיָּא וּבַרְיוּת גּוּפָא וּנְהוֹרָא מַעַלְיָא. זַרְעָא חַיָּא וְקַיָּמָא. זַרְעָא דִּי לָא יִפְסוֹק וְדִי לָא יִבְטוֹל מִפִּתְגָּמֵי אוֹרַיְתָא: לְמָרָנָן וְרַבָּנָן חֲבוּרָתָא קַדִּישָׁתָא. דִּי בְאַרְעָא דְיִשְׂרָאֵל וְדִי בְּבָבֶל. לְרֵישֵׁי כַלֵּי וּלְרֵישֵׁי גַלְוָתָא וּלְרֵישֵׁי מְתִיבָתָא וּלְדַיָּנֵי דִי בָבָא: לְכָל תַּלְמִידֵיהוֹן וּלְכָל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן וּלְכָל מָאן דְּעָסְקִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא. מַלְכָּא דְעָלְמָא יְבָרֵךְ יַתְהוֹן יַפִּישׁ חַיֵּיהוֹן וְיַסְגֵּא יוֹמֵיהוֹן וְיִתֵּן אַרְכָּא לִשְׁנֵיהוֹן וְיִתְפָּרְקוּן וְיִשְׁתֵּזְבוּן מִן כָּל עָקָא וּמִן כָּל מַרְעִין בִּישִׁין. מָרָן דִּי בִשְׁמַיָּא יְהֵא בְסַעְדְּהוֹן כָּל זְמַן וְעִדָּן. וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','en','May there arise deliverance from Heaven— favor, kindliness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance, Heavenly assistance, physical health, good vision, and living, thriving children, children who will not interrupt nor desist from studying the words of the Torah— For our masters, and our sages, the holy fellowships, in the land of Yisrael and in Babylonia. For the heads of Torah assemblies, for the heads of the communities in exile, for the heads of the yeshivos, and for the judges in the gateways; for all their disciples, and for all the disciples of their disciples, and for all who occupy themselves with Torah, the King of the Universe will bless them, prolong their lifespans, increase their days, and give length to their years. And they will be delivered and saved from all distress and from all severe illness. The Master in heaven, will help them at all times and at every season. And let us say Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','transliteration','Yekum purkan min shemaya china ve chisda ve rachamei ve chayei arichei umezonei revichei ve siyata dishmaya uvaryut gufa unehora ma''alya.
Zara chaya ve kayama.
Zara di la yifsok ve di la yivtol mipitgamei orayta.
Lemaranan ve rabanan chavurata kadishata.
Di ve ara deyisrael ve di b''vavel.
Lereishei chalei ulereishei galvata ulereishei metivata uledayanei di vava.
Lechol talmideihon ulechal talmidei talmideihon ulechal man deasekin b''orayta.
Malka dealema yevarech yathon yapish chayeihon ve yasgeh yomeihon ve yiten arka lishneihon ve yitparekun ve yishtezevun min kol aka umin kol marin bishin.
Maran di vishmaya yeheh ve sadehon kol zeman ve idan.
Ve nomar amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','he','יְקוּם פֻּרְקָן מִן שְׁמַיָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמֵי וְחַיֵּי אֲרִיכֵי וּמְזוֹנֵי רְוִיחֵי וְסִיַּעְתָּא דִשְׁמַיָּא וּבַרְיוּת גּוּפָא וּנְהוֹרָא מַעַלְיָא. זַרְעָא חַיָּא וְקַיָּמָא זַרְעָא דִּי לָא יִפְסוֹק וְדִי לָא יִבְטוֹל מִפִּתְגָּמֵי אוֹרַיְתָא: לְכָל קְהָלָא קַדִּישָׁא הָדֵין רַבְרְבַיָּא עִם זְעֵרַיָּא טַפְלָא וּנְשַׁיָּא. מַלְכָּא דְעָלְמָא יְבָרֵךְ יַתְכוֹן יַפִּישׁ חַיֵּיכוֹן וְיַסְגֵּא יוֹמֵיכוֹן וְיִתֵּן אַרְכָּא לִשְׁנֵיכוֹן וְתִתְפָּרְקוּן וְתִשְׁתֵּזְבוּן מִן כָּל עָקָא וּמִן כָּל מַרְעִין בִּישִׁין. מָרָן דִּי בִשְׁמַיָא יְהֵא בְסַעְדְּכוֹן כָּל זְמַן וְעִדָּן. וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','en','May there arise deliverance from Heaven— favor, kindliness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance, Heavenly assistance, physical health, good vision, and living, thriving children, children who will not interrupt nor desist from studying the words of Torah— for this entire holy congregation, adults, and children, infants and women. The King of the Universe will bless you, prolong your lifespans, increase your days, and give length to your years. And you will be delivered and saved from all distress and severe illness. The Master in heaven, will help you at all times and at every season and let us say Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','transliteration','Yekum purkan min shemaya china ve chisda ve rachamei ve chayei arichei umezonei revichei ve siyata dishmaya uvaryut gufa unehora ma''alya.
Zara chaya ve kayama zara di la yifsok ve di la yivtol mipitgamei orayta.
Lechol k''hala kadisha hadein ravrevaya im ze''eraya tafla uneshaya.
Malka dealema yevarech yatchon yapish chayeichon ve yasgeh yomeichon ve yiten arka lishneichon ve titparekun ve tishtezevun min kol aka umin kol marin bishin.
Maran di vishmaya yeheh ve sadechon kol zeman ve idan.
Ve nomar amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:2:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','he','מִי שֶׁבֵּרַךְ אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב. הוּא יְבָרֵךְ אֶת כָּל הַקָּהָל הַקָּדוֹשׁ הַזֶּה עִם כָּל קְהִלּוֹת הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ. הֵם וּנְשֵׁיהֶם וּבְנֵיהֶם וּבְנוֹתֵיהֶם וְכָל אֲשֶׁר לָהֶם וּמִי שֶׁמְּיַחֲדִים בָּתֵּי כְנֵסִיּוֹת לִתְפִלָּה. וּמִי שֶׁבָּאִים בְּתוֹכָם לְהִתְפַּלֵּל. וּמִי שֶׁנּוֹתְנִים נֵר לַמָּאוֹר וְיַֽיִן לְקִדּוּשׁ וּלְהַבְדָּלָה וּפַת לָאוֹרְחִים וּצְדָקָה לָעֲנִיִּים. חזן: וְכָל מִי שֶׁעוֹסְקִים בְּצָרְכֵי צִבּוּר בֶּאֱמוּנָה. הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא יְשַׁלֵּם שְׂכָרָם וְיָסִיר מֵהֶם כָּל מַחֲלָה וְיִרְפָּא לְכָל גּוּפָם וְיִסְלַח לְכָל עֲו‍ֹנָם. וְיִשְׁלַח בְּרָכָה וְהַצְלָחָה בְּכָל מַעֲשֵׂה יְדֵיהֶם עִם כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל אֲחֵיהֶם. וְנֹאמַר אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:2:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','en','He Who blessed our fathers, Avraham, Yitzchak and Yaakov, will bless this entire holy congregation together with all the holy congregations, them, their wives and their sons and their daughters, and all that belong to them. Whoever dedicates synagogues for prayer, and whoever enters them to pray, and whoever donates lamps for lighting, wine for Kiddush and Havdalah, food for wayfarers, charity for the poor; and whoever occupies himself with the needs of the community— in a faithful manner— The Holy One, blessed is He, will pay them their reward, remove from them all sickness, heal their entire body, pardon all their iniquities, and send blessing, and success upon all the work of their hands, together with all of Yisrael, their brethren, and let us say, Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon:2:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-reading-of-the-torah-yekum-purkon','transliteration','Mi sheberach avoteinu Avraham Yitzchak ve Yaakov.
Hu yevarech et kol hakahal hakadosh hazeh im kol k''hilot hakodesh.
Hem unesheihem uveneihem uvenoteihem ve chol asher lahem umi shemeyachadim batei chenesiyot litfila.
Umi shebaim b''tocham lehitpalel.
Umi shenotenim ner lamaor ve yayin lekidush ulehavdala ufat laorechim utzedaka la''aniyim.
Chzn.
Ve chol mi sheosekim b''tzarechei tzibur be''emuna.
Hakadosh baruch hu yeshalem secharam ve yasir mehem kol machala ve yirpa lechol gufam ve yislach lechol avonam.
Ve yishlach b''racha ve hatzlacha b''chol ma''aseh yedeihem im kol Yisrael acheihem.
Ve nomar amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Reading of the Torah, Yekum Purkon'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עַל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעַל רַבָּנָן וְעַל תַּלְמִידֵיהוֹן וְעַל כָּל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן, וְעַל כָּל מָאן דְּעָסְקִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא, דִּי בְאַתְרָא הָדֵין וְדִי בְכָל אֲתַר וַאֲתַר, יְהֵא לְהוֹן וּלְכוֹן שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמִין וְחַיִּין אֲרִיכִין וּמְזוֹנֵי רְוִיחֵי וּפוּרְקָנָא מִן קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דְבִשְׁמַיָּא וְאַרְעָא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה הַשָּׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה בְרַחֲמָיו שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future — and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; far above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. Upon Yisrael, and upon our Sages, and upon their disciples, and upon all the disciples of their disciples, and upon all those who engage in Torah study in this land and in every land. May there be unto them and unto you abundant peace, favor, kindness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance and redemption from their Father Who is in heaven and on earth, —and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and a good life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes the peace in His high heavens may He, in His mercy, make peace for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela ule''ela mikol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Al Yisrael ve al rabanan ve al talmideihon ve al kol talmidei talmideihon,
ve al kol man deasekin b''orayta,
di ve atra hadein ve di ve chal atar va''atar,
yeheh lehon ulechon shelama rabah china ve chisda ve rachamin ve chayin arichin umezonei revichei ufurekana min kodam avuhon devishmaya ve ara ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim tovim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh hashalom bimromav hu ya''aseh ve rachamav shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּלִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְעִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁכִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְהֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And You shall know this day and take into your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia,
va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu,
shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz,
umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al,
ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim,
hu Eloheinu ein od,
emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','he','עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁמֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁעֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְעוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְבוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּלוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עוֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְמֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: חזן: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-first-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','transliteration','Al ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha,
lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz,
yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu,
ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu,
vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha,
ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed,
ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod,
kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Chzn.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, First Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עַל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעַל רַבָּנָן וְעַל תַּלְמִידֵיהוֹן וְעַל כָּל תַּלְמִידֵי תַלְמִידֵיהוֹן, וְעַל כָּל מָאן דְּעָסְקִין בְּאוֹרַיְתָא, דִּי בְאַתְרָא הָדֵין וְדִי בְכָל אֲתַר וַאֲתַר, יְהֵא לְהוֹן וּלְכוֹן שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא חִנָּא וְחִסְדָּא וְרַחֲמִין וְחַיִּין אֲרִיכִין וּמְזוֹנֵי רְוִיחֵי וּפוּרְקָנָא מִן קֳדָם אֲבוּהוֹן דְבִשְׁמַיָּא וְאַרְעָא וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים טוֹבִים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה הַשָּׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה בְרַחֲמָיו שָׁלוֹם עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future — and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; far above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. Upon Yisrael, and upon our Sages, and upon their disciples, and upon all the disciples of their disciples, and upon all those who engage in Torah study in this land and in every land. May there be unto them and unto you abundant peace, favor, kindness, compassion, long life, ample sustenance and redemption from their Father Who is in heaven and on earth, —and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and a good life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes the peace in His high heavens may He, in His mercy, make peace for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-kaddish-d-rabanan','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela ule''ela mikol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Al Yisrael ve al rabanan ve al talmideihon ve al kol talmidei talmideihon,
ve al kol man deasekin b''orayta,
di ve atra hadein ve di ve chal atar va''atar,
yeheh lehon ulechon shelama rabah china ve chisda ve rachamin ve chayin arichin umezonei revichei ufurekana min kodam avuhon devishmaya ve ara ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim tovim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh hashalom bimromav hu ya''aseh ve rachamav shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Kaddish d''Rabanan'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּלִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְעִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁכִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְהֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And You shall know this day and take into your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia,
va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu,
shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz,
umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al,
ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim,
hu Eloheinu ein od,
emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','he','עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁמֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁעֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְעוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְבוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּלוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עוֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְמֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: חזן: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-musaf-second-day-of-rosh-hashana-aleinu','transliteration','Al ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha,
lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz,
yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu,
ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu,
vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha,
ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed,
ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod,
kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Chzn.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Musaf, Second Day of Rosh Hashana, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','he','עָלֵֽינוּ לְשַׁבֵּֽחַ לַאֲדוֹן הַכֹּל לָתֵת גְּדֻלָּה לְיוֹצֵר בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁלֹּא עָשָֽׂנוּ כְּגוֹיֵי הָאֲרָצוֹת וְלֹא שָׂמָֽנוּ כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה שֶׁלֹּא שָׂם חֶלְקֵֽנוּ כָּהֶם וְגוֹרָלֵֽנוּ כְּכָל הֲמוֹנָם: שֶׁהֵם מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לָהֶֽבֶל וָרִיק וּמִתְפַּלְּלִים אֶל אֵל לֹא יוֹשִֽׁיעַ, וַאֲנַֽחְנוּ כּוֹרְעִים וּמִשְׁתַּחֲוִים וּמוֹדִים לִפְנֵי מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא, שֶׁהוּא נוֹטֶה שָׁמַֽיִם וְיוֹסֵד אָֽרֶץ, וּמוֹשַׁב יְקָרוֹ בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל, וּשְׁכִינַת עֻזּוֹ בְּגָבְהֵי מְרוֹמִים, הוּא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ אֵין עוֹד, אֱמֶת מַלְכֵּֽנוּ אֶֽפֶס זוּלָתוֹ כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתוֹ וְיָדַעְתָּ הַיּוֹם וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶֽךָ כִּי יְהֹוָה הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַֽיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּֽחַת אֵין עוֹד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','en','It is our obligation to praise the Master of all, to ascribe greatness to the Creator of the [world in the] beginning: that He has not made us like the nations of the lands, and has not positioned us like the families of the earth; that He has not assigned our portion like theirs, nor our lot like that of all their multitudes. For they prostrate themselves to vanity and nothingness, and pray to a god that cannot deliver. But we bow, prostrate ourselves, and offer thanks before the Supreme King of kings, the Holy One blessed is He, Who spreads the heavens, and establishes the earth, and the seat of His glory is in heaven above, and the abode of His invincible might is in the loftiest heights. He is our God, there is nothing else. Our King is true, all else is insignificant, as it is written in His Torah: “And You shall know this day and take into your heart that Adonoy is God in the heavens above and upon the earth below; there is nothing else.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','transliteration','Aleinu leshabeach la''adon hakol latet gedula leyotzer b''reshit shelo asanu k''goyei ha''aratzot ve lo samanu k''mishpechot ha''adama shelo sam chelkenu kahem ve goralenu k''chal hamonam.
Shehem mishtachavim lahevel varik umitpalelim el el lo yoshia,
va''anachenu koreim umishtachavim umodim lifnei melech malchei hamelachim hakadosh baruch hu,
shehu noteh shamayim ve yosed aretz,
umoshav yekaro bashamayim mima''al,
ushechinat uzo b''govhei meromim,
hu Eloheinu ein od,
emet malkenu efes zulato kakatuv b''torato ve yadata hayom vahashevota el levavecha ki Adonai hu haelohim bashamayim mima''al ve al ha''aretz mitachat ein od.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:1:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','he','עַל כֵּן נְקַוֶּה לְךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ לִרְאוֹת מְהֵרָה בְּתִפְאֶֽרֶת עֻזֶּֽךָ לְהַעֲבִיר גִּלּוּלִים מִן הָאָֽרֶץ וְהָאֱלִילִים כָּרוֹת יִכָּרֵתוּן לְתַקֵּן עוֹלָם בְּמַלְכוּת שַׁדַּי וְכָל בְּנֵי בָשָׂר יִקְרְאוּ בִשְׁמֶֽךָ, לְהַפְנוֹת אֵלֶֽיךָ כָּל רִשְׁעֵי אָֽרֶץ, יַכִּֽירוּ וְיֵדְעוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי תֵבֵל כִּי לְךָ תִכְרַע כָּל בֶּֽרֶךְ תִּשָּׁבַע כָּל לָשׁוֹן: לְפָנֶֽיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִכְרְעוּ וְיִפֹּֽלוּ, וְלִכְבוֹד שִׁמְךָ יְקָר יִתֵּֽנוּ, וִיקַבְּלוּ כֻלָּם אֶת עוֹל מַלְכוּתֶֽךָ, וְתִמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם מְהֵרָה לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד, כִּי הַמַּלְכוּת שֶׁלְּךָ הִיא וּלְעֽוֹלְמֵי עַד תִּמְלוֹךְ בְּכָבוֹד, כַּכָּתוּב בְּתוֹרָתֶֽךָ יְהֹוָה יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד: חזן: וְנֶאֱמַר וְהָיָה יְהֹוָה לְמֶֽלֶךְ עַל כָּל הָאָֽרֶץ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא יִהְיֶה יְהֹוָה אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:1:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','en','We therefore put our hope in You, Adonoy our God, to soon behold the glory of Your might in banishing idolatry from the earth, and the false gods will be utterly exterminated to perfect the world as the kingdom of Shadai. And all mankind will invoke Your Name, to turn back to You, all the wicked of the earth. They will realize and know, all the inhabitants of the world, that to You, every knee must bend, every tongue must swear [allegiance to You]. Before You, Adonoy, our God, they will bow and prostrate themselves, and to the glory of Your Name give honor. And they will all accept [upon themselves] the yoke of Your kingdom, and You will reign over them, soon, forever and ever. For the kingdom is Yours, and to all eternity You will reign in glory, as it is written in Your Torah: “Adonoy will reign forever and ever.” And it is said: “And Adonoy will be King over the whole earth; on that day Adonoy will be One and His Name One.”','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu:1:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-aleinu','transliteration','Al ken nekaveh lecha Adonai Eloheinu lirot mehera b''tiferet uzecha leha''avir gilulim min ha''aretz ve haelilim karot yikaretun letaken olam b''malchut shadai ve chol b''nei vasar yikreu vishmecha,
lehafnot eleicha kol rishei aretz,
yakiru ve yedeu kol yoshevei tevel ki lecha tichra kol berech tishava kol lashon.
Lefanecha Adonai Eloheinu yichreu ve yipolu,
ve lichvod shimcha yekar yitenu,
vikabelu chulam et ol malchutecha,
ve timloch aleihem mehera le''olam vaed,
ki hamalchut shelecha hi uleolemei ad timloch b''chavod,
kakatuv b''toratecha Adonai yimloch le''olam vaed.
Chzn.
Ve ne''emar ve haya Adonai lemelech al kol ha''aretz bayom hahu yihyeh Adonai echad ushemo echad.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Aleinu'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא בְּעָלְמָא דִּי בְרָא כִרְעוּתֵהּ וְיַמְלִיךְ מַלְכוּתֵהּ בְּחַיֵּיכוֹן וּבְיוֹמֵיכוֹן וּבְחַיֵּי דְכָל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, בַּעֲגָלָא וּבִזְמַן קָרִיב וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא מְבָרַךְ לְעָלַם וּלְעָלְמֵי עָלְמַיָּא: יִתְבָּרַךְ וְיִשְׁתַּבַּח וְיִתְפָּאַר וְיִתְרוֹמַם וְיִתְנַשֵּׂא וְיִתְהַדָּר וְיִתְעַלֶּה וְיִתְהַלָּל שְׁמֵהּ דְקוּדְשָׁא, בְּרִיךְ הוּא לְעֵֽלָּא וּלְעֵֽלָּא מִכָּל בִּרְכָתָא וְשִׁירָתָא, תֻּשְׁבְּחָתָא וְנֶחֱמָתָא, דַּאֲמִירָן בְּעָלְמָא, וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: יְהֵא שְׁלָמָא רַבָּא מִן שְׁמַיָּא וְחַיִּים עָלֵֽינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן: עוֹשֶׂה הַשָּׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו הוּא יַעֲשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם עָלֵינוּ וְעַל כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאִמְרוּ אָמֵן:','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name in the world which He created according to His will; and may He rule His Kingdom in your lifetime and in your days, and in the lifetime of the entire House of Yisrael, speedily and in the near future— and say Amein. May His great Name be blessed forever and for all eternity. Blessed and praised, glorified, and exalted and uplifted, honored and elevated and extolled be the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He; far above all the blessings and hymns, praises and consolations which we utter in the world—and say Amein. May there be abundant peace from heaven and life for us and for all Yisrael, —and say Amein. He Who makes the peace in His high heavens may He, make peace for us and or all Yisrael, and say, Amein.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish:0:transliteration','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-mincha-mourner-s-kaddish','transliteration','Yitgadal ve yitkadash shemeh rabah b''alema di ve ra chiruteh ve yamlich malchuteh b''chayeichon uveyomeichon uvechayei dechal beit Yisrael,
ba''agala uvizman kariv ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shemeh rabah mevarach lealam ulealemei alemaya.
Yitbarach ve yishtabach ve yitpa''ar ve yitromam ve yitnaseh ve yithadar ve yitaleh ve yithalal shemeh dekudesha,
b''rich hu le''ela ule''ela mikol birchata ve shirata,
tushbechata ve nechemata,
da''amiran b''alema,
ve''imru amen.
Yeheh shelama rabah min shemaya ve chayim aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.
Oseh hashalom bimromav hu ya''aseh shalom aleinu ve al kol Yisrael ve''imru amen.','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz, Mincha, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-linear-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish:0:he','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-linear-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish','he','יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz Linear, Mincha for Erev Rosh Hashana, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
('sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-linear-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish:0:en','sefaria-machzor-rosh-hashanah-ashkenaz-linear-mincha-for-erev-rosh-hashana-mourner-s-kaddish','en','Exalted and sanctified be His great Name','Machzor Rosh Hashanah Ashkenaz Linear, Mincha for Erev Rosh Hashana, Mourner''s Kaddish'),
