('research-habakkuk-3:11:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','Thou marchest through the earth in indignation, Thou threshest the nations in anger.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:11:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','B''za''am titzad aretz b''af tadush goyim','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:12:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','יָצָ֙אתָ֙ לְיֵ֣שַׁע עַמֶּ֔ךָ לְיֵ֖שַׁע אֶת־מְשִׁיחֶ֑ךָ מָחַ֤צְתָּ רֹּאשׁ֙ מִבֵּ֣ית רָשָׁ֔ע עָר֛וֹת יְס֥וֹד עַד־צַוָּ֖אר סֶֽלָה׃ (פ)','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:12:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','Thou art come forth for the deliverance of Thy people, for the deliverance of Thine anointed; Thou woundest the head out of the house of the wicked, uncovering the foundation even unto the neck. Selah','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:12:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Yatzata leyesha amecha leyesha et meshichecha machatzta rosh mibeit rasha arot yesod ad tzavar sela (f)','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:13:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','נָקַ֤בְתָּ בְמַטָּיו֙ רֹ֣אשׁ פרזו [פְּרָזָ֔יו] יִסְעֲר֖וּ לַהֲפִיצֵ֑נִי עֲלִ֣יצֻתָ֔ם כְּמוֹ־לֶאֱכֹ֥ל עָנִ֖י בַּמִּסְתָּֽר׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:13:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','Thou hast stricken through with his own rods the head of his rulers, that come as a whirlwind to scatter me; whose rejoicing is as to devour the poor secretly.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:13:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Nakavta ve matav rosh perazav yisaru lahafitzeni alitzutam k''mo le''echol ani bamistar','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:14:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','דָּרַ֥כְתָּ בַיָּ֖ם סוּסֶ֑יךָ חֹ֖מֶר מַ֥יִם רַבִּֽים׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:14:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','Thou hast trodden the sea with Thy horses, the foaming of mighty waters.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:14:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Darachta vayam suseicha chomer mayim rabim','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:15:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','שָׁמַ֣עְתִּי ׀ וַתִּרְגַּ֣ז בִּטְנִ֗י לְקוֹל֙ צָלֲל֣וּ שְׂפָתַ֔י יָב֥וֹא רָקָ֛ב בַּעֲצָמַ֖י וְתַחְתַּ֣י אֶרְגָּ֑ז אֲשֶׁ֤ר אָנ֙וּחַ֙ לְי֣וֹם צָרָ֔ה לַעֲל֖וֹת לְעַ֥ם יְגוּדֶֽנּוּ׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:15:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','When I heard, mine inward parts trembled, My lips quivered at the voice; Rottenness entereth into my bones, And I tremble where I stand; that I should wait for the day of trouble, when he cometh up against the people that he invadeth.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:15:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Shamati vatirgaz bitni lekol tzalalu sefatai yavo rakav ba''atzamai ve tachtai ergaz asher anuach leyom tzara la''alot leam yegudenu','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:16:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','כִּֽי־תְאֵנָ֣ה לֹֽא־תִפְרָ֗ח וְאֵ֤ין יְבוּל֙ בַּגְּפָנִ֔ים כִּחֵשׁ֙ מַעֲשֵׂה־זַ֔יִת וּשְׁדֵמ֖וֹת לֹא־עָ֣שָׂה אֹ֑כֶל גָּזַ֤ר מִמִּכְלָה֙ צֹ֔אן וְאֵ֥ין בָּקָ֖ר בָּרְפָתִֽים׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:16:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','For though the fig-tree shall not blossom, neither shall fruit be in the vines; the labour of the olive shall fail, And the fields shall yield no food; The flock shall be cut off from the fold, and there shall be no herd in the stalls;','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:16:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Ki te''ena lo tifrach ve ein yevul bagefanim kichesh ma''aseh zayit ushedemot lo asa ochel gazar mimichla tzon ve ein bakar barefatim','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:17:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','וַאֲנִ֖י בַּיהוָ֣ה אֶעְל֑וֹזָה אָגִ֖ילָה בֵּאלֹהֵ֥י יִשְׁעִֽי׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:17:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I will exult in the God of my salvation.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:17:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Va''ani ba''adonai eloza agila belohei yishi','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:18:he','research-habakkuk-3','he','יְהוִ֤הּ אֲדֹנָי֙ חֵילִ֔י וַיָּ֤שֶׂם רַגְלַי֙ כָּֽאַיָּל֔וֹת וְעַ֥ל בָּמוֹתַ֖י יַדְרִכֵ֑נִי לַמְנַצֵּ֖חַ בִּנְגִינוֹתָֽי׃','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:18:en','research-habakkuk-3','en','God, the Lord, is my strength, And He maketh my feet like hinds’feet, And He maketh me to walk upon my high places. For the Leader. With my string-music.','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-habakkuk-3:18:transliteration','research-habakkuk-3','transliteration','Elohim adonai cheili vayasem raglai ka''ayalot ve al bamotai yadricheni lamnatzeach binginotai','Habakkuk 3'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:0:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וָֽאֶתְפַּֽלְלָ֛ה לַיהוָ֥ה אֱלֹהַ֖י וָאֶתְוַדֶּ֑ה וָאֹֽמְרָ֗ה אָנָּ֤א אֲדֹנָי֙ הָאֵ֤ל הַגָּדוֹל֙ וְהַנּוֹרָ֔א שֹׁמֵ֤ר הַבְּרִית֙ וְֽהַחֶ֔סֶד לְאֹהֲבָ֖יו וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י מִצְוֺתָֽיו׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:0:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','And I prayed unto the LORD my God, and made confession, and said: ‘O Lord, the great and awful God, who keepest covenant and mercy with them that love Thee and keep Thy commandments,','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:0:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Vaetpalela laAdonai Elohai vaetvadeh vaomera ana adonai hael hagadol ve hanora shomer haberit ve hachesed leohavav uleshomerei mitzvotav','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:1:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','חָטָ֥אנוּ וְעָוִ֖ינוּ והרשענו [הִרְשַׁ֣עְנוּ] וּמָרָ֑דְנוּ וְס֥וֹר מִמִּצְוֺתֶ֖ךָ וּמִמִּשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:1:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','we have sinned, and have dealt iniquitously, and have done wickedly, and have rebelled, and have turned aside from Thy commandments and from Thine ordinances;','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:1:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Chatanu ve avinu hirshanu umaradenu ve sor mimitzvotecha umimishpateicha','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:2:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וְלֹ֤א שָׁמַ֙עְנוּ֙ אֶל־עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים אֲשֶׁ֤ר דִּבְּרוּ֙ בְּשִׁמְךָ֔ אֶל־מְלָכֵ֥ינוּ שָׂרֵ֖ינוּ וַאֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ וְאֶ֖ל כָּל־עַ֥ם הָאָֽרֶץ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:2:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','neither have we hearkened unto Thy servants the prophets, that spoke in Thy name to our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and to all the people of the land.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:2:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ve lo shamanu el avadeicha hanevi''im asher diberu b''shimcha el melacheinu sareinu va''avoteinu ve el kol am ha''aretz','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:3:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','לְךָ֤ אֲדֹנָי֙ הַצְּדָקָ֔ה וְלָ֛נוּ בֹּ֥שֶׁת הַפָּנִ֖ים כַּיּ֣וֹם הַזֶּ֑ה לְאִ֤ישׁ יְהוּדָה֙ וּלְיוֹשְׁבֵ֣י יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם וּֽלְכָל־יִשְׂרָאֵ֞ל הַקְּרֹבִ֣ים וְהָרְחֹקִ֗ים בְּכָל־הָֽאֲרָצוֹת֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר הִדַּחְתָּ֣ם שָׁ֔ם בְּמַעֲלָ֖ם אֲשֶׁ֥ר מָֽעֲלוּ־בָֽךְ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:3:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','Unto Thee, O Lord, belongeth righteousness, but unto us confusion of face, as at this day; to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and unto all Israel, that are near, and that are far off, through all the countries whither Thou hast driven them, because they dealt treacherously with Thee.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:3:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Lecha adonai hatzedaka ve lanu boshet hapanim kayom hazeh leish Yehudah uleyoshevei yerushalaim ulechol Yisrael hakerovim ve harechokim b''chol ha''aratzot asher hidachtam sham b''ma''alam asher ma''alu vach','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:4:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','יְהוָ֗ה לָ֚נוּ בֹּ֣שֶׁת הַפָּנִ֔ים לִמְלָכֵ֥ינוּ לְשָׂרֵ֖ינוּ וְלַאֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ אֲשֶׁ֥ר חָטָ֖אנוּ לָֽךְ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:4:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','O LORD, to us belongeth confusion of face, to our kings, to our princes, and to our fathers, because we have sinned against Thee.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:4:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Adonai lanu boshet hapanim limlacheinu lesareinu ve la''avoteinu asher chatanu lach','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:5:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','לַֽאדֹנָ֣י אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ הָרַחֲמִ֖ים וְהַסְּלִח֑וֹת כִּ֥י מָרַ֖דְנוּ בּֽוֹ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:5:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','To the Lord our God belong compassions and forgivenesses; for we have rebelled against Him;','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:5:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ladonai Eloheinu harachamim ve haselichot ki maradnu bo','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:6:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וְלֹ֣א שָׁמַ֔עְנוּ בְּק֖וֹל יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ לָלֶ֤כֶת בְּתֽוֹרֹתָיו֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר נָתַ֣ן לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ בְּיַ֖ד עֲבָדָ֥יו הַנְּבִיאִֽים׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:6:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','neither have we hearkened to the voice of the LORD our God, to walk in His laws, which He set before us by His servants the prophets. .','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:6:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ve lo shamanu b''kol Adonai Eloheinu lalechet b''torotav asher natan lefaneinu b''yad avadav hanevi''im','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:7:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וְכָל־יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל עָֽבְרוּ֙ אֶת־תּ֣וֹרָתֶ֔ךָ וְס֕וֹר לְבִלְתִּ֖י שְׁמ֣וֹעַ בְּקֹלֶ֑ךָ וַתִּתַּ֨ךְ עָלֵ֜ינוּ הָאָלָ֣ה וְהַשְּׁבֻעָ֗ה אֲשֶׁ֤ר כְּתוּבָה֙ בְּתוֹרַת֙ מֹשֶׁ֣ה עֶֽבֶד־הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים כִּ֥י חָטָ֖אנוּ לֽוֹ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:7:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','Yea, all Israel have transgressed Thy law, and have turned aside, so as not to hearken to Thy voice; and so there hath been poured out upon us the curse and the oath that is written in the Law of Moses the servant of God; for we have sinned against Him.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:7:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ve chol Yisrael averu et toratecha ve sor levilti shemoa b''kolecha vatitach aleinu ha''ala ve hashevua asher k''tuva b''torat Moshe eved haelohim ki chatanu lo','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:8:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וַיָּ֜קֶם אֶת־דבריו [דְּבָר֣וֹ ׀] אֲשֶׁר־דִּבֶּ֣ר עָלֵ֗ינוּ וְעַ֤ל שֹֽׁפְטֵ֙ינוּ֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר שְׁפָט֔וּנוּ לְהָבִ֥יא עָלֵ֖ינוּ רָעָ֣ה גְדֹלָ֑ה אֲשֶׁ֣ר לֹֽא־נֶעֶשְׂתָ֗ה תַּ֚חַת כָּל־הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר נֶעֶשְׂתָ֖ה בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:8:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','And He hath confirmed His word, which He spoke against us, and against our judges that judged us, by bringing upon us a great evil; so that under the whole heaven hath not been done as hath been done upon Jerusalem.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:8:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Vayakem edevaro asher diber aleinu ve al shofeteinu asher shefatunu lehavi aleinu ra''a gedola asher lo ne''esta tachat kol hashamayim ka''asher ne''esta birushalaim','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:9:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר כָּתוּב֙ בְּתוֹרַ֣ת מֹשֶׁ֔ה אֵ֛ת כָּל־הָרָעָ֥ה הַזֹּ֖את בָּ֣אָה עָלֵ֑ינוּ וְלֹֽא־חִלִּ֜ינוּ אֶת־פְּנֵ֣י ׀ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ לָשׁוּב֙ מֵֽעֲוֺנֵ֔נוּ וּלְהַשְׂכִּ֖יל בַּאֲמִתֶּֽךָ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:9:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','As it is written in the Law of Moses, all this evil is come upon us; yet have we not entreated the favour of the LORD our God, that we might turn from our iniquities, and have discernment in Thy truth.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:9:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ka''asher katuv b''torat Moshe et kol hara''a hazot ba''a aleinu ve lo chilinu et penei Adonai Eloheinu lashuv meavonenu ulehaskil ba''amitecha','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:10:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וַיִּשְׁקֹ֤ד יְהוָה֙ עַל־הָ֣רָעָ֔ה וַיְבִיאֶ֖הָ עָלֵ֑ינוּ כִּֽי־צַדִּ֞יק יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ עַל־כָּל־מַֽעֲשָׂיו֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשָׂ֔ה וְלֹ֥א שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ בְּקֹלֽוֹ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:10:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','And so the LORD hath watched over the evil, and brought it upon us; for the LORD our God is righteous in all His works which He hath done, and we have not hearkened to His voice.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:10:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Vayishkod Adonai al hara''a vayevieha aleinu ki tzadik Adonai Eloheinu al kol ma''asav asher asa ve lo shamanu b''kolo','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:11:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וְעַתָּ֣ה ׀ אֲדֹנָ֣י אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ אֲשֶׁר֩ הוֹצֵ֨אתָ אֶֽת־עַמְּךָ֜ מֵאֶ֤רֶץ מִצְרַ֙יִם֙ בְּיָ֣ד חֲזָקָ֔ה וַתַּֽעַשׂ־לְךָ֥ שֵׁ֖ם כַּיּ֣וֹם הַזֶּ֑ה חָטָ֖אנוּ רָשָֽׁעְנוּ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:11:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','And now, O Lord our God, that hast brought Thy people forth out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and hast gotten Thee renown, as at this day; we have sinned, we have done wickedly.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:11:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ve atah adonai Eloheinu asher hotzeta et amecha me''eretz mitzrayim b''yad chazaka vata''as lecha shem kayom hazeh chatanu rashaenu','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:12:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','אֲדֹנָ֗י כְּכָל־צִדְקֹתֶ֙ךָ֙ יָֽשָׁב־נָ֤א אַפְּךָ֙ וַחֲמָ֣תְךָ֔ מֵעִֽירְךָ֥ יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם הַר־קָדְשֶׁ֑ךָ כִּ֤י בַחֲטָאֵ֙ינוּ֙ וּבַעֲוֺנ֣וֹת אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ יְרוּשָׁלִַ֧ם וְעַמְּךָ֛ לְחֶרְפָּ֖ה לְכָל־סְבִיבֹתֵֽינוּ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:12:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','O Lord, according to all Thy righteousness, let Thine anger and Thy fury, I pray Thee, be turned away from Thy city Jerusalem, Thy holy mountain; because for our sins, and for the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and Thy people are become a reproach to all that are about us.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:12:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Adonai k''chol tzidkotecha yashav na apecha vachamatecha meirecha yerushalaim har kodshecha ki vachataeinu uva''avonot avoteinu yerushalaim ve amecha lecherpa lechol sevivoteinu','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:13:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','וְעַתָּ֣ה ׀ שְׁמַ֣ע אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ אֶל־תְּפִלַּ֤ת עַבְדְּךָ֙ וְאֶל־תַּ֣חֲנוּנָ֔יו וְהָאֵ֣ר פָּנֶ֔יךָ עַל־מִקְדָּשְׁךָ֖ הַשָּׁמֵ֑ם לְמַ֖עַן אֲדֹנָֽי׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:13:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','Now therefore, O our God, hearken unto the prayer of Thy servant, and to his supplications, and cause Thy face to shine upon Thy sanctuary that is desolate, for the Lord’s sake.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:13:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Ve atah shema Eloheinu el tefilat avdecha ve el tachanunav ve haer paneicha al mikdashecha hashamem lema''an adonai','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:14:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','הַטֵּ֨ה אֱלֹהַ֥י ׀ אָזְנְךָ֮ וּֽשֲׁמָע֒ פקחה [פְּקַ֣ח] עֵינֶ֗יךָ וּרְאֵה֙ שֹֽׁמְמֹתֵ֔ינוּ וְהָעִ֕יר אֲשֶׁר־נִקְרָ֥א שִׁמְךָ֖ עָלֶ֑יהָ כִּ֣י ׀ לֹ֣א עַל־צִדְקֹתֵ֗ינוּ אֲנַ֨חְנוּ מַפִּילִ֤ים תַּחֲנוּנֵ֙ינוּ֙ לְפָנֶ֔יךָ כִּ֖י עַל־רַחֲמֶ֥יךָ הָרַבִּֽים׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:14:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','O my God, incline Thine ear, and hear; open Thine eyes, and behold our desolations, and the city upon which Thy name is called; for we do not present our supplications before Thee because of our righteousness, but because of Thy great compassions.','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:14:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Hateh Elohai oznecha ushama pekach eineicha ure''eh shomemoteinu ve hair asher nikra shimcha aleiha ki lo al tzidkoteinu anachnu mapilim tachanuneinu lefanecha ki al rachameicha harabim','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:15:he','research-daniel-9-4-19','he','אֲדֹנָ֤י ׀ שְׁמָ֙עָה֙ אֲדֹנָ֣י ׀ סְלָ֔חָה אֲדֹנָ֛י הַֽקֲשִׁ֥יבָה וַעֲשֵׂ֖ה אַל־תְּאַחַ֑ר לְמַֽעֲנְךָ֣ אֱלֹהַ֔י כִּֽי־שִׁמְךָ֣ נִקְרָ֔א עַל־עִירְךָ֖ וְעַל־עַמֶּֽךָ׃','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:15:en','research-daniel-9-4-19','en','O Lord, hear, O Lord, forgive, O Lord, attend and do, defer not; for Thine own sake, O my God, because Thy name is called upon Thy city and Thy people.’','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-daniel-9-4-19:15:transliteration','research-daniel-9-4-19','transliteration','Adonai shema''a adonai selacha adonai hakashiva va''aseh al teachar lema''ancha Elohai ki shimcha nikra al irecha ve al amecha','Daniel 9:4-19'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:0:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','וָאֹמְרָ֗ה אֱלֹהַי֙ בֹּ֣שְׁתִּי וְנִכְלַ֔מְתִּי לְהָרִ֧ים אֱלֹהַ֛י פָּנַ֖י אֵלֶ֑יךָ כִּ֣י עֲוֺנֹתֵ֤ינוּ רָבוּ֙ לְמַ֣עְלָה רֹּ֔אשׁ וְאַשְׁמָתֵ֥נוּ גָדְלָ֖ה עַ֥ד לַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:0:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','and I said: ‘O my God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face to Thee, my God; for our iniquities are increased over our head, and our guiltiness is grown up unto the heavens.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:0:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Vaomera Elohai bosheti ve nichlamti leharim Elohai panai eleicha ki avonoteinu ravu lemala rosh ve ashmatenu godla ad lashamayim','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:1:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','מִימֵ֣י אֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙ בְּאַשְׁמָ֣ה גְדֹלָ֔ה עַ֖ד הַיּ֣וֹם הַזֶּ֑ה וּבַעֲוֺנֹתֵ֡ינוּ נִתַּ֡נּוּ אֲנַחְנוּ֩ מְלָכֵ֨ינוּ כֹהֲנֵ֜ינוּ בְּיַ֣ד ׀ מַלְכֵ֣י הָאֲרָצ֗וֹת בַּחֶ֜רֶב בַּשְּׁבִ֧י וּבַבִּזָּ֛ה וּבְבֹ֥שֶׁת פָּנִ֖ים כְּהַיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:1:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','Since the days of our fathers we have been exceeding guilty unto this day; and for our iniquities have we, our kings, and our priests, been delivered into the hand of the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, and to spoiling, and to confusion of face, as it is this day.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:1:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Mimei avoteinu anachnu b''ashma gedola ad hayom hazeh uva''avonoteinu nitanu anachnu melacheinu chohaneinu b''yad malchei ha''aratzot bacherev bashevi uvabiza uvevoshet panim k''hayom hazeh','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:2:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','וְעַתָּ֡ה כִּמְעַט־רֶגַע֩ הָיְתָ֨ה תְחִנָּ֜ה מֵאֵ֣ת ׀ יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ לְהַשְׁאִ֥יר לָ֙נוּ֙ פְּלֵיטָ֔ה וְלָתֶת־לָ֥נוּ יָתֵ֖ד בִּמְק֣וֹם קָדְשׁ֑וֹ לְהָאִ֤יר עֵינֵ֙ינוּ֙ אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ וּלְתִתֵּ֛נוּ מִֽחְיָ֥ה מְעַ֖ט בְּעַבְדֻתֵֽנוּ׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:2:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','And now for a little moment grace hath been shown from the LORD our God, to leave us a remnant to escape, and to give us a nail in His holy place, that our God may lighten our eyes, and give us a little reviving in our bondage.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:2:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Ve atah kimat rega hayeta techina me''et Adonai Eloheinu lehashir lanu peleita ve latet lanu yated bimkom kodsho lehair eineinu Eloheinu uletitenu micheya meat b''avdutenu','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:3:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','כִּֽי־עֲבָדִ֣ים אֲנַ֔חְנוּ וּבְעַבְדֻ֔תֵנוּ לֹ֥א עֲזָבָ֖נוּ אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ וַֽיַּט־עָלֵ֣ינוּ חֶ֡סֶד לִפְנֵי֩ מַלְכֵ֨י פָרַ֜ס לָֽתֶת־לָ֣נוּ מִֽחְיָ֗ה לְרוֹמֵ֞ם אֶת־בֵּ֤ית אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙ וּלְהַעֲמִ֣יד אֶת־חָרְבֹתָ֔יו וְלָֽתֶת־לָ֣נוּ גָדֵ֔ר בִּֽיהוּדָ֖ה וּבִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ (ס)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:3:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','For we are bondmen; yet our God hath not forsaken us in our bondage, but hath extended mercy unto us in the sight of the kings of Persia, to give us a reviving, to set up the house of our God, and to repair the ruins thereof, and to give us a fence in Judah and in Jerusalem.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:3:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Ki avadim anachnu uveavdutenu lo azavanu Eloheinu vayat aleinu chesed lifnei malchei faras latet lanu micheya leromem et beit Eloheinu uleha''amid et chorvotav ve latet lanu gader bihuda uvirushalaim (s)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:4:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','וְעַתָּ֛ה מַה־נֹּאמַ֥ר אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ אַֽחֲרֵי־זֹ֑את כִּ֥י עָזַ֖בְנוּ מִצְוֺתֶֽיךָ׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:4:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','And now, O our God, what shall we say after this? for we have forsaken Thy commandments,','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:4:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Ve atah mah nomar Eloheinu acharei zot ki azavnu mitzvoteicha','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:5:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','אֲשֶׁ֣ר צִוִּ֗יתָ בְּיַ֨ד עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ הַנְּבִיאִים֮ לֵאמֹר֒ הָאָ֗רֶץ אֲשֶׁ֨ר אַתֶּ֤ם בָּאִים֙ לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ אֶ֤רֶץ נִדָּה֙ הִ֔יא בְּנִדַּ֖ת עַמֵּ֣י הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת בְּתוֹעֲבֹֽתֵיהֶ֗ם אֲשֶׁ֥ר מִלְא֛וּהָ מִפֶּ֥ה אֶל־פֶּ֖ה בְּטֻמְאָתָֽם׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:5:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','which Thou hast commanded by Thy servants the prophets, saying: The land, unto which ye go to possess it, is an unclean land through the uncleanness of the peoples of the lands, through their abominations, wherewith they have filled it from one end to another with their filthiness.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:5:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Asher tzivita b''yad avadeicha hanevi''im lemor ha''aretz asher atem baim lerishtah eretz nida hi b''nidat amei ha''aratzot b''toavoteihem asher miluha mipeh el peh b''tumatam','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:6:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','וְ֠עַתָּה בְּֽנוֹתֵיכֶ֞ם אַל־תִּתְּנ֣וּ לִבְנֵיהֶ֗ם וּבְנֹֽתֵיהֶם֙ אַל־תִּשְׂא֣וּ לִבְנֵיכֶ֔ם וְלֹֽא־תִדְרְשׁ֧וּ שְׁלֹמָ֛ם וְטוֹבָתָ֖ם עַד־עוֹלָ֑ם לְמַ֣עַן תֶּחֶזְק֗וּ וַאֲכַלְתֶּם֙ אֶת־ט֣וּב הָאָ֔רֶץ וְהוֹרַשְׁתֶּ֥ם לִבְנֵיכֶ֖ם עַד־עוֹלָֽם׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:6:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','Now therefore give not your daughters unto their sons, neither take their daughters unto your sons, nor seek their peace or their prosperity for ever; that ye may be strong, and eat the good of the land, and leave it for an inheritance to your children for ever.','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:6:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Ve atah b''noteichem al titenu livneihem uvenoteihem al tisu livneichem ve lo tidreshu shelomam ve tovatam ad olam lema''an techezku va''achaltem et tuv ha''aretz ve horashtem livneichem ad olam','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:7:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','וְאַֽחֲרֵי֙ כָּל־הַבָּ֣א עָלֵ֔ינוּ בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֙ינוּ֙ הָרָעִ֔ים וּבְאַשְׁמָתֵ֖נוּ הַגְּדֹלָ֑ה כִּ֣י ׀ אַתָּ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ חָשַׂ֤כְתָּֽ לְמַ֙טָּה֙ מֵֽעֲוֺנֵ֔נוּ וְנָתַ֥תָּה לָּ֛נוּ פְּלֵיטָ֖ה כָּזֹֽאת׃','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:7:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','And after all that is come upon us for our evil deeds, and for our great guilt, seeing that Thou our God hast punished us less than our iniquities deserve, and hast given us such a remnant,','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:7:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Ve acharei kol haba aleinu b''ma''aseinu haraim uveashmatenu hagedola ki atah Eloheinu chasachta lemata meavonenu ve natata lanu peleita kazot','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:8:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','הֲנָשׁוּב֙ לְהָפֵ֣ר מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ וּ֨לְהִתְחַתֵּ֔ן בְּעַמֵּ֥י הַתֹּעֵב֖וֹת הָאֵ֑לֶּה הֲל֤וֹא תֶֽאֱנַף־בָּ֙נוּ֙ עַד־כַּלֵּ֔ה לְאֵ֥ין שְׁאֵרִ֖ית וּפְלֵיטָֽה׃ (פ)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:8:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','shall we again break Thy commandments, and make marriages with the peoples that do these abominations? wouldest not Thou be angry with us till Thou hadst consumed us, so that there should be no remnant, nor any to escape?','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:8:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Hanashuv lehafer mitzvoteicha ulehitchaten b''amei hatoevot haeleh halo te''enaf banu ad kaleh le''ein she''erit ufeleita (f)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:9:he','research-ezra-9-6-15','he','יְהוָ֞ה אֱלֹהֵ֤י יִשְׂרָאֵל֙ צַדִּ֣יק אַ֔תָּה כִּֽי־נִשְׁאַ֥רְנוּ פְלֵיטָ֖ה כְּהַיּ֣וֹם הַזֶּ֑ה הִנְנ֤וּ לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙ בְּאַשְׁמָתֵ֔ינוּ כִּ֣י אֵ֥ין לַעֲמ֛וֹד לְפָנֶ֖יךָ עַל־זֹֽאת׃ (פ)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:9:en','research-ezra-9-6-15','en','O LORD, the God of Israel, Thou art righteous; for we are left a remnant that is escaped, as it is this day; behold, we are before Thee in our guiltiness; for none can stand before Thee because of this.’','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-ezra-9-6-15:9:transliteration','research-ezra-9-6-15','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Yisrael tzadik atah ki nisharnu feleita k''hayom hazeh hinnu lefanecha b''ashmateinu ki ein la''amod lefanecha al zot (f)','Ezra 9:6-15'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:0:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','וָאֹמַ֗ר אָֽנָּ֤א יְהוָה֙ אֱלֹהֵ֣י הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם הָאֵ֥ל הַגָּד֖וֹל וְהַנּוֹרָ֑א שֹׁמֵ֤ר הַבְּרִית֙ וָחֶ֔סֶד לְאֹהֲבָ֖יו וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י מִצְוֺתָֽיו׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:0:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','and said: ‘I beseech Thee, O LORD, the God of heaven, the great and awful God, that keepeth covenant and mercy with them that love Him and keep His commandments;','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:0:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Vaomar ana Adonai Elohei hashamayim hael hagadol ve hanora shomer haberit vachesed leohavav uleshomerei mitzvotav','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:1:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','תְּהִ֣י נָ֣א אָזְנְךָֽ־קַשֶּׁ֣בֶת וְֽעֵינֶ֪יךָ פְתֻוּח֟וֹת לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ אֶל־תְּפִלַּ֣ת עַבְדְּךָ֡ אֲשֶׁ֣ר אָנֹכִי֩ מִתְפַּלֵּ֨ל לְפָנֶ֤יךָ הַיּוֹם֙ יוֹמָ֣ם וָלַ֔יְלָה עַל־בְּנֵ֥י יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ וּמִתְוַדֶּ֗ה עַל־חַטֹּ֤אות בְּנֵֽי־יִשְׂרָאֵל֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר חָטָ֣אנוּ לָ֔ךְ וַאֲנִ֥י וּבֵית־אָבִ֖י חָטָֽאנוּ׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:1:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','let Thine ear now be attentive, and Thine eyes open, that Thou mayest hearken unto the prayer of Thy servant, which I pray before Thee at this time, day and night, for the children of Israel Thy servants, while I confess the sins of the children of Israel, which we have sinned against Thee; yea, I and my father’s house have sinned.','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:1:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Tehi na oznecha kashevet ve eineicha fetuvchot lishmoa el tefilat avdecha asher anochi mitpalel lefanecha hayom yomam valayla al b''nei Yisrael avadeicha umitvadeh al chatovt b''nei Yisrael asher chatanu lach va''ani uveit avi chatanu','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:2:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','חֲבֹ֖ל חָבַ֣לְנוּ לָ֑ךְ וְלֹא־שָׁמַ֣רְנוּ אֶת־הַמִּצְוֺ֗ת וְאֶת־הַֽחֻקִּים֙ וְאֶת־הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים אֲשֶׁ֥ר צִוִּ֖יתָ אֶת־מֹשֶׁ֥ה עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:2:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','We have dealt very corruptly against Thee, and have not kept the commandments, nor the statutes, nor the ordinances which Thou didst command Thy servant Moses.','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:2:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Chavol chavalnu lach ve lo shamarnu et hamitzvot ve et hachukim ve et hamishpatim asher tzivita et Moshe avdecha','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:3:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','זְכָר־נָא֙ אֶת־הַדָּבָ֔ר אֲשֶׁ֥ר צִוִּ֛יתָ אֶת־מֹשֶׁ֥ה עַבְדְּךָ֖ לֵאמֹ֑ר אַתֶּ֣ם תִּמְעָ֔לוּ אֲנִ֕י אָפִ֥יץ אֶתְכֶ֖ם בָּעַמִּֽים׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:3:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','Remember, I beseech Thee, the word that Thou didst command Thy servant Moses, saying: If ye deal treacherously, I will scatter you abroad among the peoples;','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:3:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Zechar na et hadavar asher tzivita et Moshe avdecha lemor atem timalu ani afitz etchem ba''amim','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:4:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','וְשַׁבְתֶּ֣ם אֵלַ֔י וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙ מִצְוֺתַ֔י וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם אֹתָ֑ם אִם־יִהְיֶ֨ה נִֽדַּחֲכֶ֜ם בִּקְצֵ֤ה הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙ מִשָּׁ֣ם אֲקַבְּצֵ֔ם והבואתים [וַהֲבִֽיאוֹתִים֙] אֶל־הַמָּק֔וֹם אֲשֶׁ֣ר בָּחַ֔רְתִּי לְשַׁכֵּ֥ן אֶת־שְׁמִ֖י שָֽׁם׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:4:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','but if ye return unto Me, and keep My commandments and do them, though your dispersed were in the uttermost part of the heaven, yet will I gather them from thence, and will bring them unto the place that I have chosen to cause My name to dwell there.','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:4:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Ve shavtem elai ushemartem mitzvotai va''asitem otam im yihyeh nidachachem biktzeh hashamayim misham akabetzem vahaviotim el hamakom asher bacharti leshaken et shemi sham','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:5:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','וְהֵ֥ם עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ וְעַמֶּ֑ךָ אֲשֶׁ֤ר פָּדִ֙יתָ֙ בְּכֹחֲךָ֣ הַגָּד֔וֹל וּבְיָדְךָ֖ הַחֲזָקָֽה׃','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:5:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','Now these are Thy servants and Thy people, whom Thou hast redeemed by Thy great power, and by Thy strong hand.','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:5:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Ve hem avadeicha ve amecha asher padita b''chochacha hagadol uveyadecha hachazaka','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:6:he','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','he','אָנָּ֣א אֲדֹנָ֗י תְּהִ֣י נָ֣א אָזְנְךָֽ־קַ֠שֶּׁבֶת אֶל־תְּפִלַּ֨ת עַבְדְּךָ֜ וְאֶל־תְּפִלַּ֣ת עֲבָדֶ֗יךָ הַֽחֲפֵצִים֙ לְיִרְאָ֣ה אֶת־שְׁמֶ֔ךָ וְהַצְלִֽיחָה־נָּ֤א לְעַבְדְּךָ֙ הַיּ֔וֹם וּתְנֵ֣הוּ לְרַחֲמִ֔ים לִפְנֵ֖י הָאִ֣ישׁ הַזֶּ֑ה וַאֲנִ֛י הָיִ֥יתִי מַשְׁקֶ֖ה לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ (פ)','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:6:en','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','en','O Lord, I beseech Thee, let now Thine ear be attentive to the prayer of Thy servant, and to the prayer of Thy servants, who delight to fear Thy name; and prosper, I pray Thee, Thy servant this day, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.’ Now I was cupbearer to the king.','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-1-5-11:6:transliteration','research-nehemiah-1-5-11','transliteration','Ana adonai tehi na oznecha kashevet el tefilat avdecha ve el tefilat avadeicha hachafetzim leyira et shemecha ve hatzlicha na leavdecha hayom utenehu lerachamim lifnei haish hazeh va''ani hayiti mashkeh lamelech (f)','Nehemiah 1:5-11'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:0:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ הַלְוִיִּ֡ם יֵשׁ֣וּעַ וְ֠קַדְמִיאֵל בָּנִ֨י חֲשַׁבְנְיָ֜ה שֵׁרֵֽבְיָ֤ה הֽוֹדִיָּה֙ שְׁבַנְיָ֣ה פְתַֽחְיָ֔ה ק֗וּמוּ בָּרֲכוּ֙ אֶת־יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם מִן־הָעוֹלָ֖ם עַד־הָעוֹלָ֑ם וִיבָֽרְכוּ֙ שֵׁ֣ם כְּבוֹדֶ֔ךָ וּמְרוֹמַ֥ם עַל־כָּל־בְּרָכָ֖ה וּתְהִלָּֽה׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:0:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Then the Levites, Jeshua, and Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah, said: ‘Stand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting; and let them say: Blessed be Thy glorious Name, that is exalted above all blessing and praise.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:0:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vayomeru haleviyim yeshua ve kadmiel bani chashavneya shereveya hodiya shevanya fetacheya kumu barachu et Adonai Elohechem min ha''olam ad ha''olam vivarechu shem k''vodecha umeromam al kol b''racha utehila','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:1:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','אַתָּה־ה֣וּא יְהוָה֮ לְבַדֶּךָ֒ את [אַתָּ֣ה] עָשִׂ֡יתָ אֶֽת־הַשָּׁמַיִם֩ שְׁמֵ֨י הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם וְכָל־צְבָאָ֗ם הָאָ֜רֶץ וְכָל־אֲשֶׁ֤ר עָלֶ֙יהָ֙ הַיַּמִּים֙ וְכָל־אֲשֶׁ֣ר בָּהֶ֔ם וְאַתָּ֖ה מְחַיֶּ֣ה אֶת־כֻּלָּ֑ם וּצְבָ֥א הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם לְךָ֥ מִשְׁתַּחֲוִֽים׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:1:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Thou art the LORD, even Thou alone; Thou hast made heaven, the heaven of heavens, with all their host, the earth and all things that are thereon, the seas and all that is in them, and Thou preservest them all; and the host of heaven worshippeth Thee.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:1:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Atah hu Adonai levadecha atah asita et hashamayim shemei hashamayim ve chol tzeva''am ha''aretz ve chol asher aleiha hayamim ve chol asher bahem ve atah mechayeh et kulam utzeva hashamayim lecha mishtachavim','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:2:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','אַתָּה־הוּא֙ יְהוָ֣ה הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים אֲשֶׁ֤ר בָּחַ֙רְתָּ֙ בְּאַבְרָ֔ם וְהוֹצֵאת֖וֹ מֵא֣וּר כַּשְׂדִּ֑ים וְשַׂ֥מְתָּ שְּׁמ֖וֹ אַבְרָהָֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:2:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Thou art the LORD the God, who didst choose Abram, and broughtest him forth out of Ur of the Chaldees, and gavest him the name of Abraham;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:2:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Atah hu Adonai haelohim asher bacharta b''avram ve hotzeto meur kasdim ve samta shemo Avraham','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:3:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּמָצָ֣אתָ אֶת־לְבָבוֹ֮ נֶאֱמָ֣ן לְפָנֶיךָ֒ וְכָר֨וֹת עִמּ֜וֹ הַבְּרִ֗ית לָתֵ֡ת אֶת־אֶרֶץ֩ הַכְּנַעֲנִ֨י הַחִתִּ֜י הָאֱמֹרִ֧י וְהַפְּרִזִּ֛י וְהַיְבוּסִ֥י וְהַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֖י לָתֵ֣ת לְזַרְע֑וֹ וַתָּ֙קֶם֙ אֶת־דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ כִּ֥י צַדִּ֖יק אָֽתָּה׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:3:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and foundest his heart faithful before Thee, and madest a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Amorite, and the Perizzite, and the Jebusite, and the Girgashite, even to give it unto his seed, and hast performed Thy words; for Thou art righteous;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:3:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Umatzata et levavo ne''eman lefanecha ve charot imo haberit latet et eretz hakena''ani hachiti haemori ve haperizi ve hayevusi ve hagirgashi latet lezaro vatakem et devareicha ki tzadik atah','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:4:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַתֵּ֛רֶא אֶת־עֳנִ֥י אֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם וְאֶת־זַעֲקָתָ֥ם שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ עַל־יַם־סֽוּף׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:4:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','And Thou sawest the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, and heardest their cry by the Red Sea;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:4:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vatereh et oni avoteinu b''mitzrayim ve et za''akatam shamata al yam suf','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:5:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַ֠תִּתֵּן אֹתֹ֨ת וּמֹֽפְתִ֜ים בְּפַרְעֹ֤ה וּבְכָל־עֲבָדָיו֙ וּבְכָל־עַ֣ם אַרְצ֔וֹ כִּ֣י יָדַ֔עְתָּ כִּ֥י הֵזִ֖ידוּ עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם וַתַּֽעַשׂ־לְךָ֥ שֵׁ֖ם כְּהַיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:5:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and didst show signs and wonders upon Pharaoh, and on all his servants, and on all the people of his land; for Thou knewest that they dealt proudly against them; and didst get Thee a name, as it is this day.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:5:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vatiten otot umofetim b''faroh uvechol avadav uvechol am artzo ki yadata ki hezidu aleihem vata''as lecha shem k''hayom hazeh','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:6:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְהַיָּם֙ בָּקַ֣עְתָּ לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם וַיַּֽעַבְר֥וּ בְתוֹךְ־הַיָּ֖ם בַּיַּבָּשָׁ֑ה וְֽאֶת־רֹ֨דְפֵיהֶ֜ם הִשְׁלַ֧כְתָּ בִמְצוֹלֹ֛ת כְּמוֹ־אֶ֖בֶן בְּמַ֥יִם עַזִּֽים׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:6:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','And Thou didst divide the sea before them, so that they went through the midst of the sea on the dry land; and their pursuers Thou didst cast into the depths, as a stone into the mighty waters.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:6:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve hayam bakata lifneihem vaya''avru ve toch hayam bayabasha ve et rodefeihem hishlachta vimtzolot k''mo even b''mayim azim','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:7:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּבְעַמּ֣וּד עָנָ֔ן הִנְחִיתָ֖ם יוֹמָ֑ם וּבְעַמּ֥וּד אֵשׁ֙ לַ֔יְלָה לְהָאִ֣יר לָהֶ֔ם אֶת־הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ אֲשֶׁ֥ר יֵֽלְכוּ־בָֽהּ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:7:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Moreover in a pillar of cloud Thou didst lead them by day; and in a pillar of fire by night, to give them light in the way wherein they should go.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:7:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Uveamud anan hinchitam yomam uveamud esh layla lehair lahem et haderech asher yelechu vah','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:8:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְעַ֤ל הַר־סִינַי֙ יָרַ֔דְתָּ וְדַבֵּ֥ר עִמָּהֶ֖ם מִשָּׁמָ֑יִם וַתִּתֵּ֨ן לָהֶ֜ם מִשְׁפָּטִ֤ים יְשָׁרִים֙ וְתוֹר֣וֹת אֱמֶ֔ת חֻקִּ֥ים וּמִצְוֺ֖ת טוֹבִֽים׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:8:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Thou camest down also upon mount Sinai, and spokest with them from heaven, and gavest them right ordinances and laws of truth, good statutes and commandments;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:8:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve al har sinai yaradta ve daber imahem mishamayim vatiten lahem mishpatim yesharim ve torot emet chukim umitzvot tovim','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:9:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְאֶת־שַׁבַּ֥ת קָדְשְׁךָ֖ הוֹדַ֣עַתָ לָהֶ֑ם וּמִצְו֤וֹת וְחֻקִּים֙ וְתוֹרָ֔ה צִוִּ֣יתָ לָהֶ֔ם בְּיַ֖ד מֹשֶׁ֥ה עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:9:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and madest known unto them Thy holy sabbath, and didst command them commandments, and statutes, and a law, by the hand of Moses Thy servant;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:9:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve et shabat kodshecha hoda''ata lahem umitzvot ve chukim ve torah tzivita lahem b''yad Moshe avdecha','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:10:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְ֠לֶחֶם מִשָּׁמַ֜יִם נָתַ֤תָּה לָהֶם֙ לִרְעָבָ֔ם וּמַ֗יִם מִסֶּ֛לַע הוֹצֵ֥אתָ לָהֶ֖ם לִצְמָאָ֑ם וַתֹּ֣אמֶר לָהֶ֗ם לָבוֹא֙ לָרֶ֣שֶׁת אֶת־הָאָ֔רֶץ אֲשֶׁר־נָשָׂ֥אתָ אֶת־יָדְךָ֖ לָתֵ֥ת לָהֶֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:10:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and gavest them bread from heaven for their hunger, and broughtest forth water for them out of the rock for their thirst, and didst command them that they should go in to possess the land which Thou hadst lifted up Thy hand to give them.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:10:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve lechem mishamayim natata lahem liravam umayim misela hotzeta lahem litzma''am vatomer lahem lavo lareshet et ha''aretz asher nasata et yadecha latet lahem','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:11:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְהֵ֥ם וַאֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ הֵזִ֑ידוּ וַיַּקְשׁוּ֙ אֶת־עָרְפָּ֔ם וְלֹ֥א שָׁמְע֖וּ אֶל־מִצְוֺתֶֽיךָ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:11:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','But they and our fathers dealt proudly, and hardened their neck, and hearkened not to Thy commandments,','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:11:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve hem va''avoteinu hezidu vayakshu et orpam ve lo shameu el mitzvoteicha','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:12:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַיְמָאֲנ֣וּ לִשְׁמֹ֗עַ וְלֹא־זָכְר֤וּ נִפְלְאֹתֶ֙יךָ֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשִׂ֣יתָ עִמָּהֶ֔ם וַיַּקְשׁוּ֙ אֶת־עָרְפָּ֔ם וַיִּתְּנוּ־רֹ֛אשׁ לָשׁ֥וּב לְעַבְדֻתָ֖ם בְּמִרְיָ֑ם וְאַתָּה֩ אֱל֨וֹהַּ סְלִיח֜וֹת חַנּ֧וּן וְרַח֛וּם אֶֽרֶךְ־אַפַּ֥יִם וְרַב־וחסד [חֶ֖סֶד] וְלֹ֥א עֲזַבְתָּֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:12:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and refused to hearken, neither were mindful of Thy wonders that Thou didst among them; but hardened their neck, and in their rebellion appointed a captain to return to their bondage; but Thou art a God ready to pardon, gracious and full of compassion, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy, and forsookest them not.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:12:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vayema''anu lishmoa ve lo zacheru nifleoteicha asher asita imahem vayakshu et orpam vayitenu rosh lashuv leavdutam b''miryam ve atah eloah selichot chanun ve rachum erech apayim ve rachesed ve lo azavtam','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:13:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','אַ֗ף כִּֽי־עָשׂ֤וּ לָהֶם֙ עֵ֣גֶל מַסֵּכָ֔ה וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ זֶ֣ה אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ אֲשֶׁ֥ר הֶעֶלְךָ֖ מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֔וּ נֶאָצ֖וֹת גְּדֹלֽוֹת׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:13:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Yea, when they had made them a molten calf, and said: ‘This is thy God that brought thee up out of Egypt, and had wrought great provocations;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:13:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Af ki asu lahem egel masecha vayomeru zeh Elohecha asher he''elcha mimitzrayim vaya''asu neatzot gedolot','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:14:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְאַתָּה֙ בְּרַחֲמֶ֣יךָ הָֽרַבִּ֔ים לֹ֥א עֲזַבְתָּ֖ם בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר אֶת־עַמּ֣וּד הֶ֠עָנָן לֹא־סָ֨ר מֵעֲלֵיהֶ֤ם בְּיוֹמָם֙ לְהַנְחֹתָ֣ם בְּהַדֶּ֔רֶךְ וְאֶת־עַמּ֨וּד הָאֵ֤שׁ בְּלַ֙יְלָה֙ לְהָאִ֣יר לָהֶ֔ם וְאֶת־הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ אֲשֶׁ֥ר יֵֽלְכוּ־בָֽהּ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:14:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','yet Thou in Thy manifold mercies forsookest them not in the wilderness; the pillar of cloud departed not from over them by day, to lead them in the way; neither the pillar of fire by night, to show them light, and the way wherein they should go.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:14:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve atah b''rachameicha harabim lo azavtam bamidbar et amud heanan lo sar mealeihem b''yomam lehanchotam b''haderech ve et amud haesh b''layla lehair lahem ve et haderech asher yelechu vah','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:15:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְרוּחֲךָ֨ הַטּוֹבָ֔ה נָתַ֖תָּ לְהַשְׂכִּילָ֑ם וּמַנְךָ֙ לֹא־מָנַ֣עְתָּ מִפִּיהֶ֔ם וּמַ֛יִם נָתַ֥תָּה לָהֶ֖ם לִצְמָאָֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:15:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Thou gavest also Thy good spirit to instruct them, and withheldest not Thy manna from their mouth, and gavest them water for their thirst.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:15:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve ruchacha hatova natata lehaskilam umancha lo manata mipihem umayim natata lahem litzma''am','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:16:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים שָׁנָ֛ה כִּלְכַּלְתָּ֥ם בַּמִּדְבָּ֖ר לֹ֣א חָסֵ֑רוּ שַׂלְמֹֽתֵיהֶם֙ לֹ֣א בָל֔וּ וְרַגְלֵיהֶ֖ם לֹ֥א בָצֵֽקוּ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:16:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Yea, forty years didst Thou sustain them in the wilderness, and they lacked nothing; their clothes waxed not old, and their feet swelled not.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:16:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve arbaim shana kilkaltam bamidbar lo chaseru salmoteihem lo valu ve ragleihem lo vatzeku','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:17:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַתִּתֵּ֨ן לָהֶ֤ם מַמְלָכוֹת֙ וַעֲמָמִ֔ים וַֽתַּחְלְקֵ֖ם לְפֵאָ֑ה וַיִּֽירְשׁ֞וּ אֶת־אֶ֣רֶץ סִיח֗וֹן וְאֶת־אֶ֙רֶץ֙ מֶ֣לֶךְ חֶשְׁבּ֔וֹן וְאֶת־אֶ֖רֶץ ע֥וֹג מֶֽלֶךְ־הַבָּשָֽׁן׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:17:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Moreover Thou gavest them kingdoms and peoples, which Thou didst allot quarter by quarter; so they possessed the land of Sihon, even the land of the king of Heshbon, and the land of Og king of Bashan.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:17:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vatiten lahem mamlachot va''amamim vatachlekem lefea vayireshu et eretz sichon ve et eretz melech cheshbon ve et eretz og melech habashan','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:18:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּבְנֵיהֶ֣ם הִרְבִּ֔יתָ כְּכֹכְבֵ֖י הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם וַתְּבִיאֵם֙ אֶל־הָאָ֔רֶץ אֲשֶׁר־אָמַ֥רְתָּ לַאֲבֹתֵיהֶ֖ם לָב֥וֹא לָרָֽשֶׁת׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:18:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Their children also didst Thou multiply as the stars of heaven, and didst bring them into the land, concerning which Thou didst say to their fathers, that they should go in to possess it.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:18:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Uveneihem hirbita k''chochevei hashamayim vateviem el ha''aretz asher amarta la''avoteihem lavo larashet','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:19:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ הַבָּנִים֙ וַיִּֽירְשׁ֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֔רֶץ וַתַּכְנַ֨ע לִפְנֵיהֶ֜ם אֶת־יֹשְׁבֵ֤י הָאָ֙רֶץ֙ הַכְּנַ֣עֲנִ֔ים וַֽתִּתְּנֵ֖ם בְּיָדָ֑ם וְאֶת־מַלְכֵיהֶם֙ וְאֶת־עַֽמְמֵ֣י הָאָ֔רֶץ לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת בָּהֶ֖ם כִּרְצוֹנָֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:19:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','So the children went in and possessed the land, and Thou didst subdue before them the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, and gavest them into their hands, with their kings, and the peoples of the land, that they might do with them as they would.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:19:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vayavou habanim vayireshu et ha''aretz vatachna lifneihem et yoshevei ha''aretz hakena''anim vatitenem b''yadam ve et malcheihem ve et amemei ha''aretz la''asot bahem kirtzonam','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:20:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַֽיִּלְכְּד֞וּ עָרִ֣ים בְּצֻרוֹת֮ וַאֲדָמָ֣ה שְׁמֵנָה֒ וַיִּֽירְשׁ֡וּ בָּתִּ֣ים מְלֵֽאִים־כָּל־ט֠וּב בֹּר֨וֹת חֲצוּבִ֜ים כְּרָמִ֧ים וְזֵיתִ֛ים וְעֵ֥ץ מַאֲכָ֖ל לָרֹ֑ב וַיֹּאכְל֤וּ וַֽיִּשְׂבְּעוּ֙ וַיַּשְׁמִ֔ינוּ וַיִּֽתְעַדְּנ֖וּ בְּטוּבְךָ֥ הַגָּדֽוֹל׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:20:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','And they took fortified cities, and a fat land, and possessed houses full of all good things, cisterns hewn out, vineyards, and oliveyards, and fruit-trees in abundance; so they did eat, and were filled, and became fat, and luxuriated in Thy great goodness.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:20:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vayilkedu arim b''tzurot va''adama shemena vayireshu batim meleim kol tuv borot chatzuvim k''ramim ve zeitim ve etz ma''achal larov vayochelu vayisbeu vayashminu vayiteadenu b''tuvecha hagadol','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:21:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַיַּמְר֨וּ וַֽיִּמְרְד֜וּ בָּ֗ךְ וַיַּשְׁלִ֤כוּ אֶת־תּוֹרָֽתְךָ֙ אַחֲרֵ֣י גַוָּ֔ם וְאֶת־נְבִיאֶ֣יךָ הָרָ֔גוּ אֲשֶׁר־הֵעִ֥ידוּ בָ֖ם לַהֲשִׁיבָ֣ם אֵלֶ֑יךָ וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֔וּ נֶאָצ֖וֹת גְּדוֹלֹֽת׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:21:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Nevertheless they were disobedient, and rebelled against Thee, and cast Thy law behind their back, and slew Thy prophets that did forewarn them to turn them back unto Thee, and they wrought great provocations.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:21:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vayamru vayimredu bach vayashlichu et toratecha acharei gavam ve et nevieicha haragu asher heidu vam lahashivam eleicha vaya''asu neatzot gedolot','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:22:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַֽתִּתְּנֵם֙ בְּיַ֣ד צָֽרֵיהֶ֔ם וַיָּצֵ֖רוּ לָהֶ֑ם וּבְעֵ֤ת צָֽרָתָם֙ יִצְעֲק֣וּ אֵלֶ֔יךָ וְאַתָּה֙ מִשָּׁמַ֣יִם תִּשְׁמָ֔ע וּֽכְרַחֲמֶ֣יךָ הָֽרַבִּ֗ים תִּתֵּ֤ן לָהֶם֙ מֽוֹשִׁיעִ֔ים וְיוֹשִׁיע֖וּם מִיַּ֥ד צָרֵיהֶֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:22:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Therefore Thou didst deliver them into the hand of their adversaries, who distressed them; and in the time of their trouble, when they cried unto Thee, Thou heardest from heaven; and according to Thy manifold mercies Thou gavest them saviours who might save them out of the hand of their adversaries.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:22:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vatitenem b''yad tzareihem vayatzeru lahem uve''et tzaratam yitzaku eleicha ve atah mishamayim tishma ucherachameicha harabim titen lahem moshi''im ve yoshium miyad tzareihem','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:23:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּכְנ֣וֹחַ לָהֶ֔ם יָשׁ֕וּבוּ לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת רַ֖ע לְפָנֶ֑יךָ וַתַּֽעַזְבֵ֞ם בְּיַ֤ד אֹֽיְבֵיהֶם֙ וַיִּרְדּ֣וּ בָהֶ֔ם וַיָּשׁ֙וּבוּ֙ וַיִּזְעָק֔וּךָ וְאַתָּ֞ה מִשָּׁמַ֧יִם תִּשְׁמַ֛ע וְתַצִּילֵ֥ם כְּֽרַחֲמֶ֖יךָ רַבּ֥וֹת עִתִּֽים׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:23:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','But after they had rest, they did evil again before Thee; therefore didst Thou leave them in the hand of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them; yet when they returned, and cried unto Thee, many times didst Thou hear from heaven, and deliver them according to Thy mercies;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:23:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Uchenoach lahem yashuvu la''asot ra lefanecha vata''azvem b''yad oyeveihem vayirdu vahem vayashuvu vayizakucha ve atah mishamayim tishma ve tatzilem k''rachameicha rabot itim','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:24:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַתָּ֨עַד בָּהֶ֜ם לַהֲשִׁיבָ֣ם אֶל־תּוֹרָתֶ֗ךָ וְהֵ֨מָּה הֵזִ֜ידוּ וְלֹא־שָׁמְע֤וּ לְמִצְוֺתֶ֙יךָ֙ וּבְמִשְׁפָּטֶ֣יךָ חָֽטְאוּ־בָ֔ם אֲשֶׁר־יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה אָדָ֖ם וְחָיָ֣ה בָהֶ֑ם וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ כָתֵף֙ סוֹרֶ֔רֶת וְעָרְפָּ֥ם הִקְשׁ֖וּ וְלֹ֥א שָׁמֵֽעוּ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:24:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','and didst forewarn them, that Thou mightest bring them back unto Thy law; yet they dealt proudly, and hearkened not unto Thy commandments, but sinned against Thine ordinances, which if a man do, he shall live by them, and presented a stubborn shoulder, and hardened their neck, and would not hear.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:24:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vata''ad bahem lahashivam el toratecha ve hema hezidu ve lo shameu lemitzvoteicha uvemishpateicha chateu vam asher ya''aseh adam ve chaya vahem vayitenu chatef soreret ve orpam hikshu ve lo shameu','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:25:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וַתִּמְשֹׁ֤ךְ עֲלֵיהֶם֙ שָׁנִ֣ים רַבּ֔וֹת וַתָּ֨עַד בָּ֧ם בְּרוּחֲךָ֛ בְּיַד־נְבִיאֶ֖יךָ וְלֹ֣א הֶאֱזִ֑ינוּ וַֽתִּתְּנֵ֔ם בְּיַ֖ד עַמֵּ֥י הָאֲרָצֹֽת׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:25:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Yet many years didst Thou extend mercy unto them, and didst forewarn them by Thy spirit through Thy prophets; yet would they not give ear; therefore gavest Thou them into the hand of the peoples of the lands.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:25:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Vatimshoch aleihem shanim rabot vata''ad bam b''ruchacha b''yad nevieicha ve lo he''ezinu vatitenem b''yad amei ha''aratzot','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:26:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּֽבְרַחֲמֶ֧יךָ הָרַבִּ֛ים לֹֽא־עֲשִׂיתָ֥ם כָּלָ֖ה וְלֹ֣א עֲזַבְתָּ֑ם כִּ֛י אֵֽל־חַנּ֥וּן וְרַח֖וּם אָֽתָּה׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:26:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Nevertheless in Thy manifold mercies Thou didst not utterly consume them, nor forsake them; for Thou art a gracious and merciful God.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:26:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Uverachameicha harabim lo asitam kala ve lo azavtam ki el chanun ve rachum atah','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:27:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְעַתָּ֣ה אֱ֠לֹהֵינוּ הָאֵ֨ל הַגָּד֜וֹל הַגִּבּ֣וֹר וְהַנּוֹרָא֮ שׁוֹמֵ֣ר הַבְּרִ֣ית וְהַחֶסֶד֒ אַל־יִמְעַ֣ט לְפָנֶ֡יךָ אֵ֣ת כָּל־הַתְּלָאָ֣ה אֲֽשֶׁר־מְ֠צָאַתְנוּ לִמְלָכֵ֨ינוּ לְשָׂרֵ֧ינוּ וּלְכֹהֲנֵ֛ינוּ וְלִנְבִיאֵ֥נוּ וְלַאֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ וּלְכָל־עַמֶּ֑ךָ מִימֵי֙ מַלְכֵ֣י אַשּׁ֔וּר עַ֖ד הַיּ֥וֹם הַזֶּֽה׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:27:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Now therefore, our God, the great, the mighty, and the awful God, who keepest covenant and mercy, let not all the travail seem little before Thee, that hath come upon us, on our kings, on our princes, and on our priests, and on our prophets, and on our fathers, and on all Thy people, since the time of the kings of Assyria unto this day.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:27:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve atah Eloheinu hael hagadol hagibor ve hanora shomer haberit ve hachesed al yimat lefanecha et kol hatela''a asher metza''atnu limlacheinu lesareinu ulechohaneinu ve linvienu ve la''avoteinu ulechol amecha mimei malchei ashur ad hayom hazeh','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:28:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְאַתָּ֣ה צַדִּ֔יק עַ֖ל כָּל־הַבָּ֣א עָלֵ֑ינוּ כִּֽי־אֱמֶ֥ת עָשִׂ֖יתָ וַאֲנַ֥חְנוּ הִרְשָֽׁעְנוּ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:28:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Howbeit Thou art just in all that is come upon us; for Thou hast dealt truly, but we have done wickedly;','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:28:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve atah tzadik al kol haba aleinu ki emet asita va''anachnu hirshaenu','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:29:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְאֶת־מְלָכֵ֤ינוּ שָׂרֵ֙ינוּ֙ כֹּהֲנֵ֣ינוּ וַאֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ לֹ֥א עָשׂ֖וּ תּוֹרָתֶ֑ךָ וְלֹ֤א הִקְשִׁ֙יבוּ֙ אֶל־מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ וּלְעֵ֣דְוֺתֶ֔יךָ אֲשֶׁ֥ר הַעִידֹ֖תָ בָּהֶֽם׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:29:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','neither have our kings, our princes, our priests, nor our fathers, kept Thy law, nor hearkened unto Thy commandments and Thy testimonies, wherewith Thou didst testify against them.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:29:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve et melacheinu sareinu kohaneinu va''avoteinu lo asu toratecha ve lo hikshivu el mitzvoteicha ule''edevoteicha asher haidota bahem','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:30:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וְהֵ֣ם בְּמַלְכוּתָם֩ וּבְטוּבְךָ֨ הָרָ֜ב אֲשֶׁר־נָתַ֣תָּ לָהֶ֗ם וּבְאֶ֨רֶץ הָרְחָבָ֧ה וְהַשְּׁמֵנָ֛ה אֲשֶׁר־נָתַ֥תָּ לִפְנֵיהֶ֖ם לֹ֣א עֲבָד֑וּךָ וְֽלֹא־שָׁ֔בוּ מִמַּֽעַלְלֵיהֶ֖ם הָרָעִֽים׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:30:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','For they have not served Thee in their kingdom, and in Thy great goodness that Thou gavest them, and in the large and fat land which Thou gavest before them, neither turned they from their wicked works.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:30:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Ve hem b''malchutam uvetuvecha harav asher natata lahem uve''eretz harechava ve hashemena asher natata lifneihem lo avaducha ve lo shavu mima''alleihem haraim','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:31:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','הִנֵּ֛ה אֲנַ֥חְנוּ הַיּ֖וֹם עֲבָדִ֑ים וְהָאָ֜רֶץ אֲשֶׁר־נָתַ֣תָּה לַאֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ לֶאֱכֹ֤ל אֶת־פִּרְיָהּ֙ וְאֶת־טוּבָ֔הּ הִנֵּ֛ה אֲנַ֥חְנוּ עֲבָדִ֖ים עָלֶֽיהָ׃','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:31:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','Behold, we are servants this day, and as for the land that Thou gavest unto our fathers to eat the fruit thereof and the good thereof, behold, we are servants in it.','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:31:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Hineh anachnu hayom avadim ve ha''aretz asher natata la''avoteinu le''echol et piryah ve et tuvah hineh anachnu avadim aleiha','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:32:he','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','he','וּתְבוּאָתָ֣הּ מַרְבָּ֗ה לַמְּלָכִ֛ים אֲשֶׁר־נָתַ֥תָּה עָלֵ֖ינוּ בְּחַטֹּאותֵ֑ינוּ וְעַ֣ל גְּ֠וִיֹּתֵינוּ מֹשְׁלִ֤ים וּבִבְהֶמְתֵּ֙נוּ֙ כִּרְצוֹנָ֔ם וּבְצָרָ֥ה גְדוֹלָ֖ה אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃ (פ)','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:32:en','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','en','And it yieldeth much increase unto the kings whom Thou hast set over us because of our sins; also they have power over our bodies, and over our cattle, at their pleasure, and we are in great distress.’','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-nehemiah-9-5-37:32:transliteration','research-nehemiah-9-5-37','transliteration','Utevuatah marba lamelachim asher natata aleinu b''chatovteinu ve al geviyoteinu moshelim uvivhemtenu kirtzonam uvetzara gedola anachenu (f)','Nehemiah 9:5-37'),
('research-i-chronicles-4-10:0:he','research-i-chronicles-4-10','he','וַיִּקְרָ֣א יַ֠עְבֵּץ לֵאלֹהֵ֨י יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל לֵאמֹ֗ר אִם־בָּרֵ֨ךְ תְּבָרֲכֵ֜נִי וְהִרְבִּ֤יתָ אֶת־גְּבוּלִי֙ וְהָיְתָ֤ה יָדְךָ֙ עִמִּ֔י וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ מֵּרָעָ֖ה לְבִלְתִּ֣י עָצְבִּ֑י וַיָּבֵ֥א אֱלֹהִ֖ים אֵ֥ת אֲשֶׁר־שָׁאָֽל׃','I Chronicles 4:10'),
('research-i-chronicles-4-10:0:en','research-i-chronicles-4-10','en','And Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying: ‘Oh that Thou wouldest bless me indeed, and enlarge my border, and that Thy hand might be with me, and that Thou wouldest work deliverance from evil, that it may not pain me! ’ And God granted him that which he requested.','I Chronicles 4:10'),
('research-i-chronicles-4-10:0:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-4-10','transliteration','Vayikra yabetz lelohei Yisrael lemor im barech tevaracheni ve hirbita et gevuli ve hayeta yadecha imi ve asita mera''a levilti atzebi vayaveh Elohim et asher sha''al','I Chronicles 4:10'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:0:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וַיְבָ֤רֶךְ דָּוִיד֙ אֶת־יְהוָ֔ה לְעֵינֵ֖י כָּל־הַקָּהָ֑ל וַיֹּ֣אמֶר דָּוִ֗יד בָּר֨וּךְ אַתָּ֤ה יְהוָה֙ אֱלֹהֵי֙ יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל אָבִ֔ינוּ מֵעוֹלָ֖ם וְעַד־עוֹלָֽם׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:0:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','Wherefore David blessed the LORD before all the congregation; and David said: ‘Blessed be Thou, O LORD, the God of Israel our father, for ever and ever.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:0:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Vayevarech David et Adonai le''einei kol hakahal vayomer David baruch atah Adonai Elohei Yisrael avinu meolam ve ad olam','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:1:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','לְךָ֣ יְ֠הוָה הַגְּדֻלָּ֨ה וְהַגְּבוּרָ֤ה וְהַתִּפְאֶ֙רֶת֙ וְהַנֵּ֣צַח וְהַה֔וֹד כִּי־כֹ֖ל בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם וּבָאָ֑רֶץ לְךָ֤ יְהוָה֙ הַמַּמְלָכָ֔ה וְהַמִּתְנַשֵּׂ֖א לְכֹ֥ל ׀ לְרֹֽאשׁ׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:1:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','Thine, O LORD, is the greatness, and the power, and the glory, and the victory, and the majesty; for all that is in the heaven and in the earth is Thine; Thine is the kingdom, O LORD, and Thou art exalted as head above all.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:1:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Lecha Adonai hagedula ve hagevura ve hatiferet ve hanetzach ve hahod ki chol bashamayim uva''aretz lecha Adonai hamamlacha ve hamitnaseh lechol lerosh','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:2:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וְהָעֹ֤שֶׁר וְהַכָּבוֹד֙ מִלְּפָנֶ֔יךָ וְאַתָּה֙ מוֹשֵׁ֣ל בַּכֹּ֔ל וּבְיָדְךָ֖ כֹּ֣חַ וּגְבוּרָ֑ה וּבְיָ֣דְךָ֔ לְגַדֵּ֥ל וּלְחַזֵּ֖ק לַכֹּֽל׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:2:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','Both riches and honour come of Thee, and Thou rulest over all; and in Thy hand is power and might; and in Thy hand it is to make great, and to give strength unto all.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:2:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ve haosher ve hakavod milefaneicha ve atah moshel bakol uveyadecha koach ugevura uveyadecha legadel ulechazek lakol','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:3:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וְעַתָּ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ מוֹדִ֥ים אֲנַ֖חְנוּ לָ֑ךְ וּֽמְהַֽלְלִ֖ים לְשֵׁ֥ם תִּפְאַרְתֶּֽךָ׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:3:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','Now therefore, our God, we thank Thee, and praise Thy glorious name.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:3:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ve atah Eloheinu modim anachnu lach umehalelim leshem tifartecha','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:4:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וְכִ֨י מִ֤י אֲנִי֙ וּמִ֣י עַמִּ֔י כִּֽי־נַעְצֹ֣ר כֹּ֔חַ לְהִתְנַדֵּ֖ב כָּזֹ֑את כִּֽי־מִמְּךָ֣ הַכֹּ֔ל וּמִיָּדְךָ֖ נָתַ֥נּוּ לָֽךְ׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:4:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','But who am I, and what is my people, that we should be able to offer so willingly after this sort? for all things come of Thee, and of Thine own have we given Thee.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:4:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ve chi mi ani umi ami ki natzor koach lehitnadev kazot ki mimecha hakol umiyadecha natanu lach','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:5:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','כִּֽי־גֵרִ֨ים אֲנַ֧חְנוּ לְפָנֶ֛יךָ וְתוֹשָׁבִ֖ים כְּכָל־אֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ כַּצֵּ֧ל ׀ יָמֵ֛ינוּ עַל־הָאָ֖רֶץ וְאֵ֥ין מִקְוֶֽה׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:5:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','For we are strangers before Thee, and sojourners, as all our fathers were: our days on the earth are as a shadow, and there is no abiding.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:5:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ki gerim anachnu lefanecha ve toshavim k''chol avoteinu katzel yameinu al ha''aretz ve ein mikveh','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:6:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ כֹּ֣ל הֶהָמ֤וֹן הַזֶּה֙ אֲשֶׁ֣ר הֲכִינֹ֔נוּ לִבְנֽוֹת־לְךָ֥ בַ֖יִת לְשֵׁ֣ם קָדְשֶׁ֑ךָ מִיָּדְךָ֥ היא [ה֖וּא] וּלְךָ֥ הַכֹּֽל׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:6:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','O LORD our God, all this store that we have prepared to build Thee a house for Thy holy name cometh of Thy hand, and is all Thine own.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:6:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Adonai Eloheinu kol hehamon hazeh asher hachinonu livnot lecha vayit leshem kodshecha miyadecha hu ulecha hakol','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:7:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וְיָדַ֣עְתִּי אֱלֹהַ֔י כִּ֤י אַתָּה֙ בֹּחֵ֣ן לֵבָ֔ב וּמֵישָׁרִ֖ים תִּרְצֶ֑ה אֲנִ֗י בְּיֹ֤שֶׁר לְבָבִי֙ הִתְנַדַּ֣בְתִּי כָל־אֵ֔לֶּה וְעַתָּ֗ה עַמְּךָ֙ הַנִּמְצְאוּ־פֹ֔ה רָאִ֥יתִי בְשִׂמְחָ֖ה לְהִֽתְנַדֶּב־לָֽךְ׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:7:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','I know also, my God, that Thou triest the heart, and hast pleasure in uprightness. As for me, in the uprightness of my heart I have willingly offered all these things; and now have I seen with joy Thy people, that are present here, offer willingly unto Thee.','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:7:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ve yadati Elohai ki atah bochen levav umeisharim tirtzeh ani b''yosher levavi hitnadavti chol eleh ve atah amecha hanimtzeu foh raiti ve simcha lehitenadev lach','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:8:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','יְהוָ֗ה אֱ֠לֹהֵי אַבְרָהָ֞ם יִצְחָ֤ק וְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙ אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ שֳׁמְרָה־זֹּ֣את לְעוֹלָ֔ם לְיֵ֥צֶר מַחְשְׁב֖וֹת לְבַ֣ב עַמֶּ֑ךָ וְהָכֵ֥ן לְבָבָ֖ם אֵלֶֽיךָ׃','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:8:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','O LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, our fathers, keep this for ever, even the imagination of the thoughts of the heart of Thy people, and direct their heart unto Thee;','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:8:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Adonai Elohei Avraham Yitzchak ve Yisrael avoteinu shomra zot le''olam leyetzer machshevot levav amecha ve hachen levavam eleicha','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:9:he','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','he','וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה בְנִ֗י תֵּ֚ן לֵבָ֣ב שָׁלֵ֔ם לִשְׁמוֹר֙ מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ עֵדְוֺתֶ֖יךָ וְחֻקֶּ֑יךָ וְלַעֲשׂ֣וֹת הַכֹּ֔ל וְלִבְנ֖וֹת הַבִּירָ֥ה אֲשֶׁר־הֲכִינֽוֹתִי׃ (פ)','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:9:en','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','en','and give unto Solomon my son a whole heart, to keep Thy commandments, Thy testimonies, and Thy statutes, and to do all these things, and to build the palace, for which I have made, provision.’','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-i-chronicles-29-10-19:9:transliteration','research-i-chronicles-29-10-19','transliteration','Ve lishlomoh ve ni ten levav shalem lishmor mitzvoteicha edevoteicha ve chukeicha ve la''asot hakol ve livnot habira asher hachinoti (f)','I Chronicles 29:10-19'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:0:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','וַיֹּאמַ֗ר יְהוָ֞ה אֱלֹהֵ֤י אֲבֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙ הֲלֹ֨א אַתָּֽה־ה֤וּא אֱלֹהִים֙ בַּשָּׁמַ֔יִם וְאַתָּ֣ה מוֹשֵׁ֔ל בְּכֹ֖ל מַמְלְכ֣וֹת הַגּוֹיִ֑ם וּבְיָדְךָ֙ כֹּ֣חַ וּגְבוּרָ֔ה וְאֵ֥ין עִמְּךָ֖ לְהִתְיַצֵּֽב׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:0:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','and he said: ‘O LORD, the God of our fathers, art not Thou alone God in heaven? and art not Thou ruler over all the kingdoms of the nations? and in Thy hand is power and might, so that none is able to withstand Thee.','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:0:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Vayomar Adonai Elohei avoteinu halo atah hu Elohim bashamayim ve atah moshel b''chol mamlechot hagoyim uveyadecha koach ugevura ve ein imecha lehityatzev','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:1:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','הֲלֹ֣א ׀ אַתָּ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ הוֹרַ֙שְׁתָּ֙ אֶת־יֹשְׁבֵי֙ הָאָ֣רֶץ הַזֹּ֔את מִלִּפְנֵ֖י עַמְּךָ֣ יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל וַֽתִּתְּנָ֗הּ לְזֶ֛רַע אַבְרָהָ֥ם אֹֽהַבְךָ֖ לְעוֹלָֽם׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:1:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','Didst not Thou, O our God, drive out the inhabitants of this land before Thy people Israel, and gavest it to the seed of Abraham Thy friend for ever?','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:1:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Halo atah Eloheinu horashta et yoshevei ha''aretz hazot milifnei amecha Yisrael vatitenah lezera Avraham ohavcha le''olam','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:2:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ־בָ֑הּ וַיִּבְנ֨וּ לְךָ֧ ׀ בָּ֛הּ מִקְדָּ֖שׁ לְשִׁמְךָ֥ לֵאמֹֽר׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:2:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','And they dwelt therein, and have built Thee a sanctuary therein for Thy name, saying:','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:2:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Vayeshevu vah vayivnu lecha bah mikdash leshimcha lemor','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:3:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','אִם־תָּב֨וֹא עָלֵ֜ינוּ רָעָ֗ה חֶרֶב֮ שְׁפוֹט֮ וְדֶ֣בֶר וְרָעָב֒ נַֽעַמְדָ֞ה לִפְנֵ֨י הַבַּ֤יִת הַזֶּה֙ וּלְפָנֶ֔יךָ כִּ֥י שִׁמְךָ֖ בַּבַּ֣יִת הַזֶּ֑ה וְנִזְעַ֥ק אֵלֶ֛יךָ מִצָּרָתֵ֖נוּ וְתִשְׁמַ֥ע וְתוֹשִֽׁיעַ׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:3:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','If evil come upon us, the sword, judgment, or pestilence, or famine, we will stand before this house, and before Thee—for Thy name is in this house—and cry unto Thee in our affliction, and Thou wilt hear and save.','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:3:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Im tavo aleinu ra''a cherev shefot ve dever ve ra''av na''amda lifnei habayit hazeh ulefanecha ki shimcha babayit hazeh ve nizak eleicha mitzaratenu ve tishma ve toshia','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:4:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','וְעַתָּ֡ה הִנֵּה֩ בְנֵֽי־עַמּ֨וֹן וּמוֹאָ֜ב וְהַר־שֵׂעִ֗יר אֲ֠שֶׁר לֹֽא־נָתַ֤תָּה לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙ לָב֣וֹא בָהֶ֔ם בְּבֹאָ֖ם מֵאֶ֣רֶץ מִצְרָ֑יִם כִּ֛י סָ֥רוּ מֵעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם וְלֹ֥א הִשְׁמִידֽוּם׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:4:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','And now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and mount Seir, whom Thou wouldest not let Israel invade, when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned aside from them, and destroyed them not;','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:4:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Ve atah hineh ve nei amon umoav ve har seir asher lo natata leYisrael lavo vahem b''voam me''eretz mitzrayim ki saru mealeihem ve lo hishmidum','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:5:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','וְהִ֨נֵּה־הֵ֔ם גֹּמְלִ֖ים עָלֵ֑ינוּ לָבוֹא֙ לְגָ֣רְשֵׁ֔נוּ מִיְּרֻשָּׁתְךָ֖ אֲשֶׁ֥ר הֽוֹרַשְׁתָּֽנוּ׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:5:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','behold, they render unto us [evil], to come to cast us out of Thy possession, which Thou hast given us to inherit.','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:5:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Ve hineh hem gomelim aleinu lavo legareshenu miyerushatecha asher horashtanu','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:6:he','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','he','אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙ הֲלֹ֣א תִשְׁפָּט־בָּ֔ם כִּ֣י אֵ֥ין בָּ֙נוּ֙ כֹּ֔חַ לִ֠פְנֵי הֶהָמ֥וֹן הָרָ֛ב הַזֶּ֖ה הַבָּ֣א עָלֵ֑ינוּ וַאֲנַ֗חְנוּ לֹ֤א נֵדַע֙ מַֽה־נַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה כִּ֥י עָלֶ֖יךָ עֵינֵֽינוּ׃','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:6:en','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','en','O our God, wilt Thou not execute judgment on them? for we have no might against this great multitude that cometh against us; neither know we what to do; but our eyes are upon Thee.’','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12:6:transliteration','research-ii-chronicles-20-6-12','transliteration','Eloheinu halo tishpat bam ki ein banu koach lifnei hehamon harav hazeh haba aleinu va''anachnu lo neda mah na''aseh ki aleicha eineinu','II Chronicles 20:6-12'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:0:he','research-proverbs-30-7-9','he','שְׁ֭תַּיִם שָׁאַ֣לְתִּי מֵאִתָּ֑ךְ אַל־תִּמְנַ֥ע מִ֝מֶּ֗נִּי בְּטֶ֣רֶם אָמֽוּת׃','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:0:en','research-proverbs-30-7-9','en','Two things have I asked of Thee; Deny me them not before I die:','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:0:transliteration','research-proverbs-30-7-9','transliteration','Shetayim sha''alti meitach al timna mimeni b''terem amut','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:1:he','research-proverbs-30-7-9','he','שָׁ֤וְא ׀ וּֽדְבַר־כָּזָ֡ב הַרְחֵ֬ק מִמֶּ֗נִּי רֵ֣אשׁ וָ֭עֹשֶׁר אַל־תִּֽתֶּן־לִ֑י הַ֝טְרִיפֵ֗נִי לֶ֣חֶם חֻקִּֽי׃','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:1:en','research-proverbs-30-7-9','en','Remove far from me falsehood and lies; Give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with mine allotted bread;','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:1:transliteration','research-proverbs-30-7-9','transliteration','Shav udevar kazav harchek mimeni resh vaosher al titen li hatrifeni lechem chuki','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:2:he','research-proverbs-30-7-9','he','פֶּ֥ן אֶשְׂבַּ֨ע ׀ וְכִחַשְׁתִּי֮ וְאָמַ֗רְתִּי מִ֥י יְה֫וָ֥ה וּפֶֽן־אִוָּרֵ֥שׁ וְגָנַ֑בְתִּי וְ֝תָפַ֗שְׂתִּי שֵׁ֣ם אֱלֹהָֽי׃ (פ)','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:2:en','research-proverbs-30-7-9','en','Lest I be full, and deny, and say: ‘Who is the LORD?’ Or lest I be poor, and steal, And profane the name of my God.','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('research-proverbs-30-7-9:2:transliteration','research-proverbs-30-7-9','transliteration','Pen esba ve chichashti ve amarti mi Adonai ufen ivaresh ve ganavti ve tafasti shem Elohai (f)','Proverbs 30:7-9'),
('tefillin:0:he','tefillin','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּ֒שָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ לְהָנִיחַ תְּפִלִּין:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:0:en','tefillin','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us to put on tefillin.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:0:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu lehaniach tefillin.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:1:he','tefillin','he','בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ מֶֽלֶךְ הָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר קִדְּ֒שָֽׁנוּ בְּמִצְוֹתָיו וְצִוָּנוּ עַל מִצְוַת תְּפִלִּין:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:1:en','tefillin','en','Blessed are You, Adonoy our God, King of the Universe, Who sanctified us with His commandments, and commanded us concerning the mitzvoh of tefillin.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:1:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Baruch atah Adonai Eloheinu melech ha''olam asher kidshanu b''mitzvotav ve tzivanu al mitzvat tefillin.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:2:he','tefillin','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:2:en','tefillin','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:2:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Baruch shem k''vod malchuto le''olam vaed.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:3:he','tefillin','he','וּמֵחָכְמָתְ֒ךָ אֵל עֶלְיוֹן תַּאֲצִיל עָלַי וּמִבִּינָתְ֒ךָ תְּבִינֵֽנִי וּבְחַסְדְּ֒ךָ תַּגְדִּיל עָלַי וּבִגְבוּרָתְ֒ךָ תַּצְמִית אוֹיְ֒בַי וְקָמַי וְשֶׁמֶן הַטּוֹב תָּרִיק עַל שִׁבְעָה קְנֵי הַמְּ֒נוֹרָה לְהַשְׁפִּֽיעַ טוּבְ֒ךָ לִבְרִיּוֹתֶֽיךָ: פּוֹתֵחַ אֶת־יָדֶֽךָ וּמַשְׂבִּֽיעַ לְכָל־חַי רָצוֹן:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:3:en','tefillin','en','And may You impart from Your wisdom to me, God most high; and give me understanding from Your understanding. With Your lovingkindness, do great things with me. With Your merit, cut off my enemies and opponents. Pour bountiful oil upon the seven branches of the menorah, in order to cause goodness to flow to Your creatures. Open Your hand and fulfill the will of every living thing.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:3:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Umechochmatecha el elyon ta''atzil alai umibinatecha tevineni uvechasdecha tagdil alai uvigvuratecha tatzmit oyevai ve kamai ve shemen hatov tarik al shiva k''nei hamenora lehashpia tuvecha livriyoteicha.
Poteach et yadecha umasbia lechol chai ratzon.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:4:he','tefillin','he','וְאֵרַשְׂתִּיךְ לִי לְעוֹלָם, וְאֵרַשְׂתִּיךְ לִי בְּצֶֽדֶק וּבְמִשְׁפָּט וּבְחֶֽסֶד וּבְרַחֲמִים: וְאֵרַשְׂתִּיךְ לִי בֶּאֱמוּנָה, וְיָדַֽעַתְּ אֶת־יְהֹוָה:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:4:en','tefillin','en','And I will betrothe you to Me forever; and I will betrothe you to Me in righteousness, in justice, in kindliness and in mercy. And I will betrothe you to Me in faithfulness and you shall know Adonoy.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:4:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Ve erastich li le''olam,
ve erastich li b''tzedek uvemishpat uvechesed uverachamim.
Ve erastich li be''emuna,
ve yada''at et Adonai.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:5:he','tefillin','he','וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: קַדֶּשׁ־לִי כָל־בְּכוֹר פֶּֽטֶר כָּל־רֶֽחֶם בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בָּאָדָם וּבַבְּ֒הֵמָה לִי הוּא: וַיֹּֽאמֶר משֶׁה אֶל־הָעָם זָכוֹר אֶת־הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה אֲשֶׁר יְצָאתֶם מִמִּצְרַֽיִם מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים כִּי בְּחֹֽזֶק יָד הוֹצִיא יְהֹוָה אֶתְכֶם מִזֶּה וְלֹא יֵאָכֵל חָמֵץ: הַיּוֹם אַתֶּם יֹצְ֒אִים בְּחֹֽדֶשׁ הָאָבִיב: וְהָיָה כִי־יְבִיאֲךָ יְהֹוָה אֶל־אֶֽרֶץ הַכְּ֒נַעֲנִי וְהַחִתִּי וְהָאֱמֹרִי וְהַחִוִּי וְהַיְבוּסִי אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ לָֽתֶת לָךְ אֶֽרֶץ זָבַת חָלָב וּדְבָשׁ וְעָבַדְתָּ אֶת־הָעֲבֹדָה הַזֹּאת בַּחֹֽדֶשׁ הַזֶּה: שִׁבְעַת יָמִים תֹּאכַל מַצֹּת וּבַיּוֹם הַשְּׁ֒בִיעִי חַג לַיהוָֹה: מַצּוֹת יֵאָכֵל אֵת שִׁבְעַת הַיָּמִים וְלֹא־יֵרָאֶה לְךָ חָמֵץ וְלֹא־יֵרָאֶה לְךָ שְׂאֹר בְּכָל־גְּבֻלֶֽךָ: וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא לֵאמֹר בַּֽעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהֹוָה לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָֽיִם: וְהָיָה לְךָ לְאוֹת עַל־יָדְ֒ךָ וּלְזִכָּרוֹן בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ לְמַֽעַן תִּֽהְיֶה תּוֹרַת יְהֹוָה בְּפִֽיךָ כִּי בְּיָד חֲזָקָה הוֹצִאֲךָ יְהֹוָה מִמִּצְרָֽיִם: וְשָׁמַרְתָּ אֶת־הַחֻקָּה הַזֹּאת לְמוֹעֲדָהּ מִיָּמִים יָמִֽימָה:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:5:en','tefillin','en','Adonoy spoke to Moses, saying: “Sanctify unto Me all the firstborn, whatsoever opens the womb among the Children of Israel, both of man and beast is Mine.” And Moses said to the people: “Remember this day on which you came out of Egypt, out of the house of bondage, for with a strong hand Adonoy brought you out from here, and [therefore] you must not eat chametz. This day you are departing, in the month of springtime. And it will be when Adonoy will bring you to the land of the Canaanites and the Hittites, and the Emorites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, which He swore to your fathers to give you, a land flowing with milk and honey, you shall perform this service in this month. Seven days, you shall eat matzos, and on the seventh day there shall be a festival [dedicated] to Adonoy. Matzos shall be eaten during these seven days, and no chametz and no leaven shall be seen in your possession within all your boundaries. And you shall relate to your son on that day, saying: ‘Because of this Adonoy acted on my behalf when I came out of Egypt. And it shall be for a sign upon your arm and for a reminder between your eyes so that Adonoy’s teaching will be [the words of] your mouth; for with a strong hand Adonoy brought you out of Egypt. And you shall keep this ordinance in its appointed time from year to year.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:5:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Vayedaber Adonai el Moshe lemor.
Kadesh li chol b''chor peter kol rechem bivnei Yisrael ba''adam uvabehema li hu.
Vayomer Moshe el ha''am zachor et hayom hazeh asher yetzatem mimitzrayim mibeit avadim ki b''chozek yad hotzi Adonai etchem mizeh ve lo yeachel chametz.
Hayom atem yotzeim b''chodesh ha''aviv.
Ve haya chi yeviacha Adonai el eretz hakena''ani ve hachiti ve haemori ve hachivi ve hayevusi asher nishba la''avoteicha latet lach eretz zavat chalav udevash ve avadta et ha''avoda hazot bachodesh hazeh.
Shivat yamim tochal matzot uvayom hashevi''i chag laAdonai.
Matzot yeachel et shivat hayamim ve lo yeraeh lecha chametz ve lo yeraeh lecha seor b''chol gevulecha.
Ve higadta levincha bayom hahu lemor ba''avur zeh asa Adonai li b''tzeti mimitzrayim.
Ve haya lecha leot al yadecha ulezikaron bein eineicha lema''an tiheyeh torat Adonai b''ficha ki b''yad chazaka hotziacha Adonai mimitzrayim.
Ve shamarta et hachuka hazot lemoadah miyamim yamima.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:6:he','tefillin','he','וְהָיָה כִּי־יְבִאֲךָ יְהֹוָה אֶל־אֶֽרֶץ הַכְּ֒נַעֲנִי כַּאֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לְךָ וְלַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ וּנְתָנָהּ לָךְ: וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ כָל־פֶּֽטֶר־רֶֽחֶם לַֽיהוָֹה וְכָל פֶּֽטֶר שֶֽׁגֶר בְּהֵמָה אֲשֶׁר יִהְיֶה לְךָ הַזְּ֒כָרִים לַיהוָֹה: וְכָל־פֶּֽטֶר חֲמֹר תִּפְדֶּה בְשֶׂה וְאִם־לֹא תִפְדֶּה וַעֲרַפְתּוֹ וְכֹל בְּכוֹר אָדָם בְּבָנֶֽיךָ תִּפְדֶּה: וְהָיָה כִּי־יִשְׁאָלְ֒ךָ בִנְךָ מָחָר לֵאמֹר מַה־זֹּאת וְאָמַרְתָּ אֵלָיו בְּחֹֽזֶק יָד הוֹצִיאָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה מִמִּצְרַֽיִם מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים: וַיְהִי כִּי־הִקְשָׁה פַרְעֹה לְשַׁלְּ֒חֵנוּ וַיַּהֲרֹג יְהֹוָה כָּל־בְּכוֹר בְּאֶֽרֶץ מִצְרַֽיִם מִבְּֽ֒כֹר אָדָם וְעַד־בְּכוֹר בְּהֵמָה עַל־כֵּן אֲנִי זֹבֵֽחַ לַֽיהוָֹה כָּל־פֶּֽטֶר רֶֽחֶם הַזְּ֒כָרִים וְכָל־בְּכוֹר בָּנַי אֶפְדֶּה: וְהָיָה לְאוֹת עַל־יָדְ֒כָה וּלְטוֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ כִּי בְּחֹֽזֶק יָד הוֹצִיאָֽנוּ יְהֹוָה מִמִּצְרָֽיִם:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:6:en','tefillin','en','And it will be, when Adonoy will bring you to the land of the Canaanites as He swore unto you and to your fathers, and will have given it to you. Then you shall bring to Adonoy every one that opens the womb, and every firstling that is dropped by cattle that belong to you, the males shall belong to Adonoy, The firstling of a donkey you shall redeem with a lamb; and if you do not redeem it, then you must kill it by breaking its neck. You must redeem every firstborn of man among your children. And it will be when your son asks you in future times, saying: ‘What is this?’ You shall say to him: ‘With a strong hand Adonoy brought us out of Egypt, out of the house of bondage. And it was when Pharaoh unyieldingly refused to let us go, that Adonoy killed all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, from the firstborn of man, to the firstborn of beast; therefore I sacrifice to Adonoy all that opens the womb that are males, and every firstborn of my sons, I redeem.’ And it shall be a sign upon your arm, and for totafos between your eyes, for with a strong hand, Adonoy brought us out of Egypt.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:6:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Ve haya ki yeviacha Adonai el eretz hakena''ani ka''asher nishba lecha ve la''avoteicha unetanah lach.
Ve ha''avarta chol peter rechem laAdonai ve chol peter sheger b''hema asher yihyeh lecha hazecharim laAdonai.
Ve chol peter chamor tifdeh ve seh ve im lo tifdeh va''arafto ve chol b''chor adam b''vaneicha tifdeh.
Ve haya ki yishalecha vincha machar lemor mah zot ve amarta elav b''chozek yad hotzianu Adonai mimitzrayim mibeit avadim.
Vayehi ki hiksha faroh leshalechenu vayaharog Adonai kol b''chor b''eretz mitzrayim mibechor adam ve ad b''chor b''hema al ken ani zoveach laAdonai kol peter rechem hazecharim ve chol b''chor banai efdeh.
Ve haya leot al yadecha uletotafot bein eineicha ki b''chozek yad hotzianu Adonai mimitzrayim.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:7:he','tefillin','he','אֵל מֶֽלֶךְ נֶאֱמָן:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:7:en','tefillin','en','(Almighty, faithful King)','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:7:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','El melech ne''eman.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:8:he','tefillin','he','שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יְהֹוָה אֶחָד:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:8:en','tefillin','en','Hear, Israel: Adonoy is our God, Adonoy is One.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:8:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Shema Yisrael Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echad.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:9:he','tefillin','he','בָּרוּךְ שֵׁם כְּבוֹד מַלְכוּתוֹ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:9:en','tefillin','en','Blessed [is His] Name, Whose glorious kingdom is forever and ever.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:9:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Baruch shem k''vod malchuto le''olam vaed.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:10:he','tefillin','he','וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ בְּכָל֯־לְ֯בָבְ֒ךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁ֒ךָ וּבְכָל־מְאֹדֶֽךָ: וְהָיוּ הַדְּ֒בָרִים הָאֵֽלֶּה אֲשֶׁר֯ אָ֯נֹכִי מְצַוְּ֒ךָ הַיּוֹם עַל֯־לְ֯בָבֶֽךָ: וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶֽיךָ וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ וּבְלֶכְתְּ֒ךָ בַדֶּֽרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּ֒ךָ וּבְקוּמֶֽךָ: וּקְשַׁרְתָּם לְאוֹת עַל֯־יָ֯דֶֽךָ וְהָיוּ לְטֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֶֽיךָ: וּכְתַבְתָּם עַל־מְזֻזוֹת בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּבִשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:10:en','tefillin','en','And you shall love Adonoy your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your possessions. And these words which I command you today, shall be upon your heart. And you shall teach them sharply to your children. And you shall discuss them when you sit in your house, and when you travel on the road, and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand, and they shall be for totafos between your eyes. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:10:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Ve''ahavta et Adonai Elohecha b''chal levavecha uvechol nafshecha uvechol meodecha.
Ve hayu hadevarim haeleh asher anochi metzavecha hayom al levavecha.
Ve shinantam levaneicha ve dibarta bam b''shivtecha b''veitecha uvelechtecha vaderech uveshachebecha uvekumecha.
Ukeshartam leot al yadecha ve hayu letotafot bein eineicha.
Uchetavtam al mezuzot beitecha uvishareicha.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:11:he','tefillin','he','וְהָיָה אִם־שָׁמֹֽעַ תִּשְׁמְ֒עוּ אֶל־מִצְוֹתַי אֲשֶׁר֯ אָ֯נֹכִי מְצַוֶּה אֶתְכֶם הַיּוֹם לְאַהֲבָה אֶת־יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם וּלְעָבְדוֹ בְּכָל֯־לְ֯בַבְכֶם וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁ֒כֶם: וְנָתַתִּי מְטַר֯־אַ֯רְצְ֒כֶם בְּעִתּוֹ֯ י֯וֹרֶה וּמַלְקוֹשׁ וְאָסַפְתָּ דְגָנֶֽךָ וְתִירשְׁ֒ךָ וְיִצְהָרֶֽךָ: וְנָתַתִּי עֵֽשֶׂב֯ בְּ֯שָׂדְ֒ךָ לִבְהֶמְתֶּֽךָ וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָֽעְתָּ: הִשָּׁמְ֒רוּ לָכֶם פֶּן֯־יִ֯פְתֶּה לְבַבְכֶם וְסַרְתֶּם וַעֲבַדְתֶּם אֱלֹהִים֯ אֲ֯חֵרִים וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶם לָהֶם: וְחָרָה אַף־יְהֹוָה בָּכֶם וְעָצַר֯ אֶ֯ת־הַשָּׁמַֽיִם וְלֹא֯־יִ֯הְיֶה מָטָר וְהָאֲדָמָה לֹא תִתֵּן אֶת֯־יְ֯בוּלָהּ וַאֲבַדְתֶּם֯ מְ֯הֵרָה מֵעַל הָאָֽרֶץ הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר֯ יְ֯הֹוָה נֹתֵן לָכֶם: וְשַׂמְתֶּם֯ אֶ֯ת־דְּבָרַי֯ אֵֽ֯לֶּה עַל֯־לְ֯בַבְכֶם וְעַל־נַפְשְׁ֒כֶם וּקְשַׁרְתֶּם֯ אֹ֯תָם לְאוֹת עַל֯־יֶ֯דְכֶם וְהָיוּ לְטוֹטָפֹת בֵּין עֵינֵיכֶם: וְלִמַּדְתֶּם֯ אֹ֯תָם אֶת־בְּנֵיכֶם לְדַבֵּר בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּ֒ךָ בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ וּבְלֶכְתְּ֒ךָ בַדֶּֽרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּ֒ךָ וּבְקוּמֶֽךָ: וּכְתַבְתָּם עַל־מְזוּזוֹת בֵּיתֶֽךָ וּבִשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ: לְמַֽעַן֯ יִ֯רְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם וִימֵי בְנֵיכֶם עַל הָאֲדָמָה אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע יְהֹוָה לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶם לָתֵת לָהֶם כִּימֵי הַשָּׁמַֽיִם עַל־הָאָֽרֶץ:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:11:en','tefillin','en','And it will be— if you vigilantly obey My commandments which I command you this day, to love Adonoy your God, and serve Him with your entire hearts and with your entire souls— that I will give rain for your land in its proper time, the early (autumn) rain and the late (spring) rain; and you will harvest your grain and your wine and your oil. And I will put grass in your fields for your cattle, and you will eat and be satisfied. Beware lest your hearts be swayed and you turn astray, and you worship alien gods and bow to them. And Adonoy’s fury will blaze among you, and He will close off the heavens and there will be no rain and the earth will not yield its produce; and you will perish swiftly from the good land which Adonoy gives you. Place these words of Mine upon your hearts and upon your souls,— and bind them for a sign upon your hands, and they shall be for totafos between your eyes. And you shall teach them to your sons, to speak them when you sit in your house, and when you travel on the road, and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways. In order that your days be prolonged, and the days of your children, upon the land which Adonoy swore to your fathers to give them [for as long] as the heavens are above the earth.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:11:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Ve haya im shamoa tishmeu el mitzvotai asher anochi metzaveh etchem hayom leahava et Adonai Elohechem uleavedo b''chal levavchem uvechol nafshechem.
Ve natati metar artzechem b''ito yoreh umalkosh ve asafta deganecha ve tirshecha ve yitzharecha.
Ve natati esev b''sadecha livhemtecha ve achalta ve savaeta.
Hishameru lachem pen yifteh levavchem ve sartem va''avadtem Elohim acherim ve hishtachavitem lahem.
Ve chara af Adonai bachem ve atzar et hashamayim ve lo yihyeh matar ve ha''adama lo titen et yevulah va''avadtem mehera meal ha''aretz hatova asher Adonai noten lachem.
Ve samtem et devarai eleh al levavchem ve al nafshechem ukeshartem otam leot al yedchem ve hayu letotafot bein eineichem.
Ve limadtem otam et b''neichem ledaber bam b''shivtecha b''veitecha uvelechtecha vaderech uveshachebecha uvekumecha.
Uchetavtam al mezuzot beitecha uvishareicha.
Lema''an yirbu yemeichem vimei ve neichem al ha''adama asher nishba Adonai la''avoteichem latet lahem kimei hashamayim al ha''aretz.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:12:he','tefillin','he','וַֽיֹּאמֶר֯ יְ֯הֹוָה֯ אֶ֯ל־משֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: דַּבֵּר֯ אֶ֯ל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם וְעָשׂוּ לָהֶם צִיצִת עַל־כַּנְפֵי בִגְ֒דֵיהֶם לְדֹרֹתָם וְנָתְ֒נוּ עַל־צִיצִת הַכָּנָף֯ פְּ֯תִיל תְּכֵֽלֶת: וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם֯ אֹ֯תוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם֯ אֶ֯ת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת֯ יְ֯הֹוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם֯ אֹ֯תָם וְלֹא תָתֽוּרוּ אַחֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲשֶׁר֯־אַ֯תֶּם זֹנִים֯ אַ֯חֲרֵיהֶם: לְמַֽעַן תִּזְכְּ֒רוּ וַעֲשִׂיתֶם֯ אֶ֯ת־כָּל־מִצְוֹתָי וִהְיִיתֶם קְדשִׁים לֵאלֹהֵיכֶם: אֲנִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם֯ אֲ֯שֶׁר הוֹצֵֽאתִי אֶתְכֶם֯ מֵ֯אֶֽרֶץ מִצְרַֽיִם לִהְיוֹת לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים֯ אֲ֯נִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם֯:','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:12:en','tefillin','en','And Adonoy spoke to Moses saying: Speak to the children of Israel, and tell them to make for themselves fringes on the corners of their garments throughout their generations; and they will place with the fringes of each corner a thread of blue. And it will be to you for fringes, and you will look upon it and you will remember all the commandments of Adonoy, and you will perform them; and you will not turn aside after your hearts and after your eyes which cause you to go astray. In order that you will remember and perform all My commandments; and you will be holy unto your God. I am Adonoy, your God, Who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be your God: I am Adonoy, your God—','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:12:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Vayomer Adonai el Moshe lemor.
Daber el b''nei Yisrael ve amarta alehem ve asu lahem tzitzit al kanfei vigdeihem ledorotam ve natenu al tzitzit hakanaf petil techelet.
Ve haya lachem letzitzit ureitem oto uzechartem et kol mitzvot Adonai va''asitem otam ve lo taturu acharei levavchem ve acharei eineichem asher atem zonim achareihem.
Lema''an tizkeru va''asitem et kol mitzvotai vihyitem k''dshim leloheichem.
Ani Adonai Elohechem asher hotzeti etchem me''eretz mitzrayim lihyot lachem lelohim ani Adonai Elohechem.','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:13:he','tefillin','he','אֱ֯מֶת','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:13:en','tefillin','en','—is true—','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin'),
('tefillin:13:transliteration','tefillin','transliteration','Emet','Siddur Ashkenaz, Weekday, Shacharit, Preparatory Prayers, Tefillin');
create or replace function private.require_active_prayer() returns trigger
language plpgsql security definer set search_path='' as $$
begin
 if not exists(select 1 from private.catalog where id=new.prayer_id and active) then
  raise exception 'This prayer is not in the current research catalog.';
 end if;
 return new;
end $$;
revoke all on function private.require_active_prayer() from public;
drop trigger if exists active_prayer on private.sessions;
create trigger active_prayer before insert on private.sessions for each row execute function private.require_active_prayer();
drop trigger if exists active_prayer on public.circle_activity;
create trigger active_prayer before insert or update on public.circle_activity for each row execute function private.require_active_prayer();
commit;
